// Auto-generated for the Unit Board (Zone 5: Verbal Advantage Lv.6–10 / 字彙的力量2)
window.VA2_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit": 26, "level": 6, "cards": [{"w": "depravity", "p": "n.", "d": "Moral corruption; extreme wickedness.", "c": "墮落；邪惡", "s": "In the Victorian novel the class studied, the miser's depravity is revealed gradually: he cheats orphans, betrays his only friend, and finally lets an innocent clerk go to prison for a crime he himself committed.", "t": "在全班研讀的那本維多利亞時期小說中，守財奴的墮落是逐步揭露的：他欺騙孤兒、背叛唯一的朋友，最後甚至讓一名無辜的職員為他自己犯下的罪行入獄。", "as": "Historians who once vilified the emperor as a monster of depravity now argue that his reputation was shaped by the calumny of rivals eager to justify their own machinations.", "at": "曾把那位皇帝詆毀為墮落惡魔的歷史學家，如今主張他的名聲是由急於為自身陰謀辯護的對手所散播的毀謗塑造而成。"}, {"w": "presumptuous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Overconfident and too bold in taking liberties.", "c": "冒昧的；放肆的", "s": "It seemed presumptuous for the first-year intern to rewrite the senior editor's headline without asking, especially since she had been at the newspaper for only three days and had never met the editor.", "t": "這位第一年的實習生未經詢問就改寫資深編輯的標題，似乎太過冒昧，尤其她才到報社三天，而且從未見過那位編輯。", "as": "The young senator's presumptuous speech, in which he pontificated about foreign policy after only a week in office, struck veteran colleagues as both callow and impertinent.", "at": "這位年輕參議員上任才一週，就對外交政策高談闊論，他那番冒昧的演說讓資深同僚覺得既幼稚又無禮。"}, {"w": "grandiose", "p": "adj.", "d": "Impressive in size or scope, often pretentiously so.", "c": "宏偉的；浮誇的", "s": "The mayor unveiled a grandiose plan to build a glass dome over the entire downtown, but engineers quietly noted that the city could not even afford to repair its crumbling bridges.", "t": "市長公布了一項在整個市中心上方興建玻璃穹頂的浮誇計畫，但工程師們私下指出，市政府甚至連修繕搖搖欲墜的橋梁都負擔不起。", "as": "The dictator's grandiose monuments, each more ostentatious than the last, stood in stark contrast to the squalid housing in which most of his citizens were forced to live.", "at": "這位獨裁者浮誇的紀念碑一座比一座更鋪張炫耀，與大多數國民被迫居住的骯髒破舊住宅形成強烈對比。"}, {"w": "disseminate", "p": "v.", "d": "To spread information or ideas widely.", "c": "散播；傳播", "s": "Public health officials used radio broadcasts, posters, and text messages to disseminate clear, accurate information about the vaccine, hoping to reach rural villages where rumors had spread faster than the facts.", "t": "公共衛生官員利用廣播、海報和簡訊來傳播清楚且正確的疫苗資訊，希望觸及那些謠言傳得比事實還快的偏遠村莊。", "as": "Before the printing press, monks laboriously copied texts by hand, so scholars could disseminate new ideas only slowly; Gutenberg's invention was truly a seminal and epochal moment.", "at": "在印刷術問世之前，僧侶們費力地手抄文本，因此學者只能緩慢地傳播新思想；古騰堡的發明確實是具有深遠影響、劃時代的一刻。"}, {"w": "eclectic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Drawing from many different sources or styles.", "c": "兼容並蓄的；折衷的", "s": "The café's eclectic playlist moved from Baroque harpsichord pieces to Taiwanese folk songs to modern jazz, reflecting the owner's belief that good music can come from any era or culture.", "t": "這家咖啡館兼容並蓄的播放清單從巴洛克大鍵琴曲、台灣民謠一路播到現代爵士樂，反映出店主認為好音樂可以來自任何時代或文化的信念。", "as": "The architect's eclectic designs combine Gothic arches with Japanese gardens, a juxtaposition that critics once derided but now praise as proof of her inimitable style.", "at": "這位建築師兼容並蓄的設計將哥德式拱門與日式庭園結合，這種並置手法曾遭評論家嘲笑，如今卻被讚譽為她無可模仿之風格的證明。"}, {"w": "servile", "p": "adj.", "d": "Excessively eager to obey or please others.", "c": "奴性的；卑躬屈膝的", "s": "The courtiers' servile behavior toward the king, bowing low at every word and praising even his worst decisions, disgusted the visiting foreign ambassador, who always valued honest advice over empty flattery.", "t": "朝臣們對國王卑躬屈膝的舉止——對他說的每句話都深深鞠躬，連他最糟的決定都讚不絕口——令來訪的外國大使感到厭惡，因為他一向重視誠實的建言，而非空洞的奉承。", "as": "Tired of his servile assistants, the director hired a contrarian who would gainsay his ideas rather than offer the obsequious praise he had grown to distrust.", "at": "厭倦了身邊卑躬屈膝的助理，這位導演聘請了一位愛唱反調的人，此人會反駁他的想法，而不是提供他已逐漸不信任的諂媚讚美。"}, {"w": "voracious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having a huge appetite; extremely eager for something.", "c": "貪吃的；渴求的", "s": "A voracious reader since childhood, the novelist finished three or four books a week, borrowing so many from the local library that the librarians eventually agreed to raise her borrowing limit.", "t": "這位小說家從小就是個如飢似渴的讀者，每週讀完三、四本書，從當地圖書館借的書多到館員最後同意提高她的借閱上限。", "as": "The voracious caterpillar will gormandize on milkweed for about two weeks before forming a protective chrysalis, from which it emerges transformed into a beautiful monarch butterfly.", "at": "這隻貪吃的毛毛蟲會狼吞虎嚥地啃食馬利筋約兩週，然後結成保護性的蛹，最後從中蛻變為一隻美麗的帝王斑蝶。"}, {"w": "convoluted", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely complicated and difficult to follow.", "c": "錯綜複雜的；費解的", "s": "The tax form's instructions were so convoluted, with exceptions to exceptions and footnotes referring to other footnotes, that even the accountant had to read them three times before she understood them.", "t": "那份稅表的說明錯綜複雜，例外之中還有例外、註腳又指向其他註腳，連會計師都得讀三遍才看懂。", "as": "The lawyer's convoluted argument, full of circumlocution and abstruse terminology, failed to persuade the jury, who much preferred the prosecutor's brief and lucid summary of the evidence.", "at": "律師那套錯綜複雜的論點充滿拐彎抹角的說法和深奧難懂的術語，未能說服陪審團；他們更喜歡檢察官對證據簡短而清晰的總結。"}, {"w": "rant", "p": "v.", "d": "To speak or shout at length in a wild, angry way.", "c": "咆哮；大聲斥責", "s": "Instead of calmly explaining his objections to the new parking rules, the frustrated resident began to rant at the city council for twenty minutes, shouting until the chairperson finally turned off his microphone.", "t": "這位沮喪的居民沒有冷靜說明他對新停車規定的反對意見，反而對市議會咆哮了二十分鐘，一直喊到主席終於關掉他的麥克風。", "as": "Whenever the coach would rant about the referees, his players exchanged weary glances, knowing that such a tirade would only earn another penalty and further nettle the officials.", "at": "每當教練對裁判大聲咆哮時，球員們就會疲憊地互看一眼，因為他們知道這種長篇怒罵只會換來另一次判罰，進一步激怒裁判。"}, {"w": "stratagem", "p": "n.", "d": "A clever plan or trick to outwit an opponent.", "c": "計謀；策略", "s": "The Trojan Horse remains legend's most famous stratagem: unable to break through the city walls, the Greeks hid soldiers inside a giant wooden statue and pretended to sail away in defeat.", "t": "特洛伊木馬至今仍是傳說中最著名的計謀：希臘人無法攻破城牆，便將士兵藏在一座巨大的木雕像中，並假裝戰敗航行離去。", "as": "The general's stratagem was simple but adroit: he feigned a retreat, lured the enemy into a labyrinthine valley, and forced their commander to capitulate within hours.", "at": "這位將軍的計謀簡單卻高明：他佯裝撤退，把敵軍誘入迷宮般的山谷，在數小時內就迫使敵方指揮官投降。"}, {"w": "emaciated", "p": "adj.", "d": "Abnormally thin and weak from hunger or illness.", "c": "憔悴的；消瘦的", "s": "When the rescue team finally reached the stranded hikers after two weeks, they found them emaciated and exhausted, having survived only on a few energy bars and water from a nearby stream.", "t": "兩週後救援隊終於找到受困的登山客時，發現他們骨瘦如柴、精疲力竭，僅靠幾條能量棒和附近溪流的水存活下來。", "as": "The emaciated prisoners released after the war were too lethargic to walk, and doctors warned that only a slow, judicious diet could gradually restore their health.", "at": "戰後獲釋的戰俘骨瘦如柴，虛弱得無法行走，醫師警告只有緩慢而審慎的飲食才能逐步恢復他們的健康。"}, {"w": "misgiving", "p": "n.", "d": "A feeling of doubt or worry about something.", "c": "疑慮；擔憂", "s": "Although the board approved the merger, one director expressed a serious misgiving about it, warning that combining two companies with such different cultures could lead to conflict and the loss of talented employees.", "t": "雖然董事會批准了這項合併案，但一位董事對此表達了嚴重的疑慮，警告說將兩家文化如此不同的公司合併，可能導致衝突並流失優秀員工。", "as": "Despite her misgivings about the deal, the ambassador chose to acquiesce, hoping that a temporary rapprochement would preclude a wider and far more devastating war between the two rival nations.", "at": "儘管對這項協議心存疑慮，這位大使仍選擇默許，希望暫時的和解能避免兩個敵對國家之間爆發更大規模、更具毀滅性的戰爭。"}, {"w": "adulation", "p": "n.", "d": "Excessive admiration or praise.", "c": "奉承；過度崇拜", "s": "After scoring the winning goal in the final, the young striker returned home to a hero's welcome, but the constant adulation from fans and reporters soon made it difficult for him to stay humble and focused.", "t": "這位年輕前鋒在決賽踢進致勝球後，回到家鄉受到英雄式的歡迎，但球迷和記者不斷的過度崇拜，很快使他難以保持謙遜和專注。", "as": "The pop star basked in the adulation of millions, yet in interviews she seemed pensive, admitting that fame was ephemeral and that true friends were a rare boon.", "at": "這位流行巨星沐浴在數百萬人的崇拜之中，然而在訪談中她似乎若有所思，坦言名聲轉瞬即逝，真正的朋友則是難得的恩賜。"}, {"w": "devotee", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who is extremely enthusiastic about something.", "c": "愛好者；熱衷者", "s": "A lifelong devotee of classical opera, the retired physician has attended almost every performance at the National Theater for thirty years and can sing entire arias from Puccini and Verdi from memory.", "t": "這位退休醫師是古典歌劇的終身愛好者，三十年來幾乎看遍國家戲劇院的每一場演出，還能憑記憶唱出普契尼和威爾第的整首詠嘆調。", "as": "Though a devotee of the philosopher's ideas, the young scholar refused to venerate him uncritically, noting that some of his most famous arguments about ethics were clearly fallacious.", "at": "雖然這位年輕學者熱衷於那位哲學家的思想，但他拒絕盲目地崇敬他，並指出他一些最著名的倫理論證顯然是謬誤的。"}, {"w": "vivacious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lively, spirited, and full of energy.", "c": "活潑的；有朝氣的", "s": "The new tour guide was so vivacious, telling jokes, asking questions, and bouncing from one exhibit to the next, that even the tired students at the back of the group began to pay attention.", "t": "新來的導覽員活潑有朝氣，一邊講笑話、一邊提問，在展品之間輕快地穿梭，就連隊伍後面疲倦的學生也開始專心聽講。", "as": "Her vivacious personality and jovial humor made her the most popular hostess in the city, yet beneath that ebullience lay a remarkably keen and perspicacious mind.", "at": "她活潑的個性和愉快的幽默感使她成為城裡最受歡迎的女主人，但在那份熱情洋溢之下，藏著一顆極為敏銳、洞察入微的心。"}, {"w": "anachronistic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Out of its proper time; belonging to an earlier era.", "c": "時代錯置的；不合時宜的", "s": "Film critics laughed when they noticed a wristwatch on a Roman soldier in the expensive historical epic, an anachronistic detail that revealed how carelessly the costume department had actually researched the period.", "t": "影評人發現那部耗資不菲的歷史史詩片中一名羅馬士兵戴著手錶時都笑了，這個時代錯置的細節暴露出服裝部門對那個時期的考究有多麼草率。", "as": "Some critics call the monarchy an anachronistic institution, a vestigial remnant of feudal hierarchy, while its defenders argue that such tradition provides stability amid the vicissitudes of politics.", "at": "一些評論家稱君主制是時代錯置的體制，是封建階級制度殘留下來的遺跡；而擁護者則主張，這樣的傳統能在政治的興衰變遷中提供穩定。"}, {"w": "garish", "p": "adj.", "d": "Unpleasantly bright and showy; gaudy.", "c": "俗豔的；過分花俏的", "s": "The hotel's new owners painted the elegant nineteenth-century lobby in garish shades of neon pink and lime green, a choice that horrified preservationists who had fought to protect the building's original character.", "t": "飯店的新業主把典雅的十九世紀大廳漆成俗豔的螢光粉紅與萊姆綠，這個選擇讓曾努力保護建築原有特色的古蹟保存人士大為震驚。", "as": "The newly rich banker's mansion was filled with garish chandeliers and gold-plated baubles, an ostentatious display that the city's old aristocratic families quietly found risible.", "at": "那位新富銀行家的豪宅裡擺滿俗豔的水晶吊燈和鍍金的小玩意兒，這種炫耀排場讓城裡的老貴族家庭暗自覺得可笑。"}, {"w": "qualm", "p": "n.", "d": "An uneasy feeling of doubt or guilty conscience.", "c": "疑慮；良心不安", "s": "The ruthless businessman felt not a single qualm about firing hundreds of loyal workers by email the week before the holidays, insisting that his only responsibility was to increase profits for shareholders.", "t": "那位冷酷的商人在假期前一週以電子郵件解雇數百名忠誠員工，卻毫無一絲良心不安，堅稱他唯一的責任就是為股東增加利潤。", "as": "Having no qualms about plagiarism, the mendacious author passed off another writer's ideas as his own, an act of turpitude that ended his promising career almost overnight.", "at": "這位滿口謊言的作家毫無顧忌地抄襲，把別人的想法冒充成自己的，這種卑劣行徑幾乎在一夜之間斷送了他前途看好的事業。"}, {"w": "consummate", "p": "adj.", "d": "Showing great skill; complete or perfect.", "c": "技藝高超的；完美的", "s": "A consummate professional, the violinist performed the entire concerto flawlessly even after one of her strings snapped in the middle of the second movement, calmly switching instruments with the concertmaster without missing a single note.", "t": "這位小提琴家是技藝精湛的專業人士，即使在第二樂章中途斷了一根弦，仍完美地演奏完整首協奏曲，她冷靜地與樂團首席交換樂器，沒有漏掉任何一個音符。", "as": "The consummate diplomat could mollify even the most irascible negotiators at the summit, defusing tense disputes with a felicitous phrase before they escalated into open hostility.", "at": "這位手腕高超的外交官能安撫峰會上最暴躁的談判代表，在緊張的爭端演變成公開敵對之前，用一句恰到好處的話化解危機。"}, {"w": "impertinent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Rude and disrespectful, especially toward someone in authority.", "c": "無禮的；魯莽的", "s": "When the student interrupted the visiting professor's lecture to ask how much money she earned and why her clothes looked so old, the principal apologized for the impertinent question and spoke with him afterward.", "t": "那名學生打斷來訪教授的演講，問她賺多少錢、為什麼衣服看起來那麼舊，校長為這個無禮的問題致歉，並在事後找他談話。", "as": "The impertinent apprentice dared to castigate his elderly master in the crowded public square, and his churlish remarks soon led the guild to ostracize him entirely.", "at": "那名無禮的學徒竟敢在擁擠的廣場上公開斥責年邁的師傅，而他粗魯的言論很快就讓公會將他完全排擠出去。"}]}, {"unit": 27, "level": 6, "cards": [{"w": "ramification", "p": "n.", "d": "A complex consequence that results from an action.", "c": "後果；衍生影響", "s": "Before voting to cut the school's music budget, board members were urged to consider every ramification of the decision, including lower student morale, fewer college scholarships, and the loss of experienced teachers.", "t": "在投票刪減學校音樂預算之前，委員們被敦促考慮這項決定的每一個後果，包括學生士氣低落、大學獎學金減少，以及失去經驗豐富的教師。", "as": "The economist warned that the tariff's ramifications would be deleterious and far-reaching, and that policymakers who ignored them were being dangerously myopic about global trade.", "at": "這位經濟學家警告，關稅的衍生影響將是有害且深遠的，忽視這些影響的決策者在全球貿易問題上目光短淺得危險。"}, {"w": "elucidate", "p": "v.", "d": "To make something clear by explaining it.", "c": "闡明；解釋清楚", "s": "Confused by the poem's strange imagery, the students asked their teacher to elucidate the meaning of the final stanza, so she drew a diagram connecting each symbol to events in the poet's life.", "t": "學生們對那首詩奇特的意象感到困惑，便請老師闡明最後一節的意義，於是她畫了一張圖，把每個象徵與詩人生平的事件連結起來。", "as": "The professor's gift was to elucidate abstruse theories in lucid, simple language, so that even a neophyte could grasp the essential ideas of quantum mechanics.", "at": "這位教授的天賦在於能用清晰簡單的語言闡明深奧的理論，讓即使是初學者也能掌握量子力學的基本概念。"}, {"w": "adage", "p": "n.", "d": "A traditional saying expressing a common truth.", "c": "格言；諺語", "s": "Her grandmother often repeated the old adage \"slow and steady wins the race,\" reminding her that consistent daily practice would help her master the piano more surely than occasional marathon sessions.", "t": "她的祖母常重複那句古老的格言「穩紮穩打才能贏得比賽」，提醒她每天持之以恆地練習，會比偶爾的馬拉松式練習更能確實掌握鋼琴。", "as": "The candidate's speech relied almost entirely on hackneyed adages and empty platitudes about hard work, and the commentators who heard it quickly dismissed it as banal rather than inspiring.", "at": "這位候選人的演說幾乎完全依賴陳腔濫調的格言和關於努力工作的空洞老生常談，聽過的評論員們很快就認為它平庸乏味，而非鼓舞人心。"}, {"w": "besotted", "p": "adj.", "d": "Strongly infatuated, so that one's judgment is muddled.", "c": "迷戀的；昏了頭的", "s": "Completely besotted with the charming stranger he had met in Paris, the young poet in the novel abandons his studies, sells his books, and follows her across Europe despite his family's warnings.", "t": "小說中的年輕詩人完全迷戀上他在巴黎遇見的迷人陌生人，不顧家人的警告，放棄學業、賣掉書本，跟著她走遍歐洲。", "as": "Besotted with his own reputation, the overweening general ignored every urgent warning from his scouts about the enemy's position, and his hubris led directly to a humiliating defeat.", "at": "這位傲慢自負的將軍迷戀自己的名聲，忽視斥候關於敵軍位置的每一次緊急警告，而他的狂妄直接導致了一場屈辱的敗仗。"}, {"w": "rueful", "p": "adj.", "d": "Expressing regret or sorrow, often in a gentle way.", "c": "懊悔的；悔恨的", "s": "With a rueful smile, the former champion admitted that skipping training to attend parties had cost him the gold medal, and he urged younger athletes not to repeat his mistake.", "t": "這位前冠軍帶著懊悔的微笑承認，翹掉訓練去參加派對讓他失去了金牌，並勸年輕選手不要重蹈他的覆轍。", "as": "In his rueful apologia, the disgraced mayor expressed genuine contrition for his nepotism, admitting that he had appointed relatives who were plainly unqualified for their jobs.", "at": "在他那份懊悔的自我辯白中，名譽掃地的市長對自己任人唯親表示由衷懊悔，承認他任命了顯然不適任的親戚。"}, {"w": "spasmodic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Occurring in sudden, brief, irregular bursts.", "c": "斷斷續續的；痙攣性的", "s": "Because the village's internet connection was spasmodic, working for a few minutes and then failing for an hour, the students had to download their homework at the library in town.", "t": "由於村裡的網路連線斷斷續續，一會兒能用、一會兒又斷線一小時，學生們只好到鎮上的圖書館下載作業。", "as": "The team's spasmodic efforts at reform were ultimately bootless; without a sustained plan, each brief burst of enthusiasm quickly gave way to lethargy and complacency.", "at": "這支團隊斷斷續續的改革努力最終徒勞無功；由於缺乏持續的計畫，每一陣短暫的熱情很快就被懶散和自滿取代。"}, {"w": "detritus", "p": "n.", "d": "Waste, debris, or fragments left after something breaks down.", "c": "碎屑；殘骸", "s": "After the typhoon passed, hundreds of volunteers spent several days clearing the detritus from the beach, collecting broken branches, plastic bottles, tangled fishing nets, and pieces of metal roofs torn from nearby houses by the powerful winds.", "t": "颱風過後，數百名志工花了好幾天清理海灘上的殘骸，撿拾斷枝、塑膠瓶、糾結的漁網，以及被強風從附近房屋扯下的鐵皮屋頂碎片。", "as": "Archaeologists patiently sifted through the detritus of the ancient city, where moldering wooden beams, copious fragments of pottery, and rusted tools attested to a once prosperous community.", "at": "考古學家耐心地篩檢古城的殘骸，那裡正在腐朽的木樑、大量陶器碎片和生鏽的工具證明這裡曾是一個繁榮的社群。"}, {"w": "awry", "p": "adv.", "d": "Away from the expected course; wrong.", "c": "出差錯地；歪斜地", "s": "The engineers had carefully tested the rocket for months, but something went awry just seconds after launch, and the vehicle veered sharply off course before exploding high above the ocean in a ball of flame.", "t": "工程師們已經仔細測試這枚火箭好幾個月，但發射後短短幾秒就出了差錯，火箭急遽偏離航道，在海洋上空高處爆炸成一團火球。", "as": "When the elaborate museum heist went awry, the miscreants immediately began blaming one another, and their bitter recrimination gave detectives enough evidence to incriminate the entire gang.", "at": "當這場精心策劃的博物館搶案出了差錯，這群惡棍立刻開始互相指責，而他們之間激烈的互相推諉讓警探掌握了足以將整個幫派定罪的證據。"}, {"w": "encumber", "p": "v.", "d": "To burden or hinder someone or something.", "c": "阻礙；拖累", "s": "The hikers decided not to encumber themselves with heavy camping stoves and extra clothing, choosing instead to carry only water, snacks, and a light rain jacket for the steep climb.", "t": "登山客們決定不讓沉重的露營爐和多餘衣物拖累自己，而是只攜帶水、點心和一件輕便雨衣去攀登陡峭的山路。", "as": "Encumbered by onerous regulations and a hidebound bureaucracy, the small company struggled for years to survive before patient investors finally helped it streamline its operations and expand overseas.", "at": "這家小公司受到繁重法規和墨守成規的官僚體制拖累，為了生存苦撐多年，直到有耐心的投資者終於協助它精簡營運並拓展海外市場。"}, {"w": "blemish", "p": "n.", "d": "A small mark or flaw that spoils appearance or reputation.", "c": "瑕疵；污點", "s": "The jeweler examined the diamond carefully under a powerful magnifying glass and found a tiny blemish near its edge, a flaw that, though invisible to the naked eye, lowered the stone's value by thousands of dollars.", "t": "珠寶商用高倍放大鏡仔細檢查這顆鑽石，在邊緣附近發現一個微小的瑕疵，這個缺陷雖然肉眼看不見，卻使寶石的價值降低了數千美元。", "as": "The judge's long career of impeccable probity had only one blemish: a minor peccadillo from her university days that her political opponents tried, quite unsuccessfully, to exaggerate.", "at": "這位法官漫長而廉潔無瑕的職涯只有一個污點：她大學時代的一個小過失，而她的政敵曾試圖誇大此事，卻完全未能得逞。"}, {"w": "impediment", "p": "n.", "d": "Something that blocks or hinders progress.", "c": "障礙；阻礙", "s": "For many immigrant families, the language barrier is the greatest impediment to finding good jobs, so the community center now offers free evening English classes and help with job applications.", "t": "對許多移民家庭來說，語言隔閡是找到好工作的最大障礙，因此社區中心現在提供免費的夜間英語課程，並協助填寫求職申請。", "as": "Lack of funding was the main impediment to the project, but the indefatigable director continued to importune donors until a munificent foundation finally agreed to help.", "at": "缺乏資金是這項計畫的主要障礙，但不屈不撓的主任持續懇求捐款人，直到一個慷慨的基金會終於同意提供協助。"}, {"w": "modicum", "p": "n.", "d": "A small amount of something.", "c": "少量；一點點", "s": "Even a modicum of preparation would have helped the team; instead, they arrived at the debate tournament without notes, research, or any idea of which side of the topic they would argue.", "t": "就算只有一點點準備也會對這支隊伍有幫助；但他們卻在沒有筆記、沒有研究，也不知道自己要辯論哪一方的情況下來到辯論賽。", "as": "The critic conceded that the novel showed a modicum of talent but found its prose prolix and its characters so vapid that she could not finish it.", "at": "這位評論家承認這部小說展現了些許才華，但認為其文筆冗長累贅、角色空洞乏味，以至於她讀不完。"}, {"w": "dossier", "p": "n.", "d": "A collection of documents about a person or subject.", "c": "檔案；卷宗", "s": "Before the final round of job interviews, the hiring committee carefully reviewed a thick dossier on each candidate, containing transcripts, recommendation letters, writing samples, and summaries of previous research projects.", "t": "在最後一輪面試前，招聘委員會仔細審閱了每位應徵者的厚厚一疊檔案，其中包含成績單、推薦信、寫作樣本，以及先前研究計畫的摘要。", "as": "Over two years, the investigative reporter compiled a dossier detailing the senator's surreptitious meetings with lobbyists, evidence that seemed to corroborate long-standing rumors of a secret cabal.", "at": "這位調查記者花了兩年整理出一份檔案，詳述該參議員與遊說人士的秘密會面，這些證據似乎證實了長久以來有關一個秘密小集團的傳聞。"}, {"w": "alliteration", "p": "n.", "d": "Repetition of the same initial sound in nearby words.", "c": "頭韻", "s": "Advertisers often rely on alliteration to make brand names memorable, which is why so many products have names like Coca-Cola, Dunkin' Donuts, and Best Buy that repeat the same beginning sound.", "t": "廣告商常依賴頭韻讓品牌名稱容易記住，這就是為什麼有那麼多產品名稱，例如可口可樂、唐恩都樂和百思買，都重複相同的開頭音。", "as": "The poet's fondness for alliteration, as in the line \"sibilant serpents slithering silently,\" gives her verse a mellifluous, almost musical quality that readers and critics alike find hard to forget.", "at": "這位詩人偏愛頭韻，例如「嘶嘶作響的蛇悄悄蜿蜒滑行」這一句，使她的詩句帶有悅耳甚至近乎音樂般的特質，讓讀者和評論家都難以忘懷。"}, {"w": "rectitude", "p": "n.", "d": "Moral correctness and honesty in behavior.", "c": "正直；清廉", "s": "The senior accountant's rectitude was legendary throughout the firm; she once politely rejected a large bribe from a wealthy client and immediately reported the offer to the company's ethics committee.", "t": "這位資深會計師的正直在全公司是出了名的；她曾禮貌地拒絕一位富有客戶的鉅額賄賂，並立即向公司的倫理委員會舉報此事。", "as": "Admired for his rectitude and stoic calm, the chief justice was considered incorruptible, a paragon whom even his fiercest political opponents could not credibly impugn or malign.", "at": "這位首席大法官因正直和沉著冷靜而受人敬仰，被認為廉潔不阿，是連最激烈的政敵都無法可信地抹黑的典範。"}, {"w": "vexatious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Causing annoyance, frustration, or worry.", "c": "惱人的；令人煩惱的", "s": "The landlord filed one vexatious lawsuit after another against his tenants, not because he expected to win, but because he hoped the endless legal costs would force them to move out.", "t": "這位房東接二連三地對房客提起惱人的訴訟，並不是因為他預期會勝訴，而是希望無止盡的訴訟費用能迫使他們搬走。", "as": "The planning committee found the local gadfly's vexatious complaints tiresome and repetitive, yet his captious objections occasionally revealed real and serious flaws in its proposals for the new park.", "at": "規劃委員會覺得這位地方上牛虻式批評者的惱人抱怨既煩人又重複，但他吹毛求疵的反對意見偶爾也揭露出新公園提案中真正且嚴重的缺陷。"}, {"w": "epithet", "p": "n.", "d": "A descriptive word or phrase, often insulting, applied to someone.", "c": "稱號；綽號；侮辱性字眼", "s": "The Macedonian ruler Alexander earned the epithet \"the Great\" through his vast military conquests, while England's King Richard I became widely known as \"the Lionheart\" for his remarkable courage in battle.", "t": "馬其頓統治者亞歷山大因廣大的軍事征服而贏得「大帝」的稱號，而英格蘭國王理查一世則因在戰場上的過人勇氣而廣為人知為「獅心王」。", "as": "Rather than answer the reporter's questions, the demagogue hurled crude epithets at the press, a churlish display of invective that alienated many of his former supporters.", "at": "那位煽動者沒有回答記者的問題，反而對媒體丟出粗鄙的侮辱字眼，這種粗魯的謾罵表現疏離了許多以前的支持者。"}, {"w": "travesty", "p": "n.", "d": "A shocking, absurd distortion or imitation of something.", "c": "拙劣的模仿；歪曲", "s": "Human rights groups called the trial a travesty of justice, pointing out that the defendant was denied a lawyer, the witnesses were paid, and the verdict was announced before any evidence was presented.", "t": "人權團體稱這場審判是對正義的嘲弄，指出被告被拒絕聘請律師、證人收受金錢，而且判決在任何證據提出前就已宣布。", "as": "The director's adaptation was a travesty of the beloved novel, replacing its poignant ending with a garish chase scene and reducing its wise heroine to a vapid stereotype.", "at": "導演的改編是對這部受喜愛小說的拙劣歪曲，把它動人的結局換成俗豔的追逐場面，並將睿智的女主角貶成空洞的刻板形象。"}, {"w": "wane", "p": "v.", "d": "To decrease gradually in size, strength, or power.", "c": "衰退；逐漸減少", "s": "As the semester went on, the students' enthusiasm for the new online platform began to wane, and by December only a handful were still logging in to complete the optional exercises.", "t": "隨著學期推進，學生們對這個新線上平台的熱情開始逐漸消退，到了十二月只剩少數幾人仍會登入完成選修練習。", "as": "As the empire's influence slowly waned, its once indomitable armies grew torpid and undisciplined, and its moribund economy could no longer support the lavish court in the capital.", "at": "隨著帝國的影響力慢慢衰退，它那曾經不可征服的軍隊變得遲緩無力、紀律鬆散，奄奄一息的經濟也再無法支撐首都奢華的宮廷。"}, {"w": "hubris", "p": "n.", "d": "Excessive pride or self-confidence that leads to downfall.", "c": "狂妄自大；傲慢", "s": "In classical Greek tragedy, the hero's hubris often leads to his ruin; believing himself equal to the gods, he ignores every warning from prophets and friends until fate finally punishes him for his arrogance.", "t": "在古典希臘悲劇中，英雄的狂妄自大常導致他的毀滅；他自認與眾神平起平坐，無視先知和朋友的每一個警告，直到命運終於懲罰他的傲慢。", "as": "The CEO's hubris blinded him to the company's precarious finances, and his megalomania, together with the sycophants who flattered him, ultimately drove the once-thriving firm into bankruptcy.", "at": "這位執行長的狂妄自大使他看不見公司岌岌可危的財務狀況，而他的自大狂，加上那些奉承他的馬屁精，最終讓這家曾經興盛的公司走向破產。"}]}, {"unit": 28, "level": 6, "cards": [{"w": "vicarious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Experienced through imagining another person's actions or feelings.", "c": "間接感受的；感同身受的", "s": "Unable to travel because of her illness, the elderly woman took vicarious pleasure in her grandson's adventures, reading every email he sent from Peru and studying the photographs of mountains she would never climb herself.", "t": "這位年長的婦人因病無法旅行，便從孫子的冒險中獲得間接的樂趣，她閱讀他從秘魯寄來的每一封電子郵件，細細端詳那些她自己永遠無法攀登的山峰照片。", "as": "Many readers enjoy the vicarious thrill of picaresque novels, following roguish heroes through perilous adventures while remaining safely ensconced in their own comfortable armchairs at home.", "at": "許多讀者喜歡流浪漢小說帶來的間接刺激，跟隨調皮搗蛋的主角經歷驚險的冒險，同時自己卻安穩舒適地窩在家中的扶手椅裡。"}, {"w": "stipulate", "p": "v.", "d": "To demand or specify something as part of an agreement.", "c": "規定；明定", "s": "The scholarship's rules stipulate that every recipient must maintain at least a B average and complete forty hours of community service each year, or the funding will be withdrawn for the following semester.", "t": "這項獎學金的規定明定，每位獲獎者都必須維持至少 B 的平均成績，並每年完成四十小時的社區服務，否則下學期的資助將被撤回。", "as": "The treaty stipulated that both nations would abrogate their old military alliances and refrain from any act that might militate against lasting peace in the region.", "at": "這項條約規定，兩國將廢除舊有的軍事同盟，並避免採取任何可能妨礙該地區持久和平的行動。"}, {"w": "despotic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Ruling with absolute, cruel, and unchecked power.", "c": "專制的；暴虐的", "s": "Under the despotic regime, newspapers were shut down, peaceful protesters were jailed without trial, and anyone who criticized the ruler in public risked losing their job, their home, or even their life.", "t": "在那個專制政權之下，報社被查封，和平抗議者未經審判就被關押，任何公開批評統治者的人都可能失去工作、家園，甚至性命。", "as": "The despotic king's imperious decrees grew so harsh and arbitrary that even his once servile ministers began to plot against him in secret, eventually forcing him into exile.", "at": "這位專制國王專橫的法令變得極為嚴苛又任意妄為，連他那些曾經卑躬屈膝的大臣都開始暗中密謀反對他，最終迫使他流亡海外。"}, {"w": "unsavory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Morally offensive or disreputable; unpleasant.", "c": "令人反感的；名聲不好的", "s": "Investigators discovered that the charity's director had unsavory connections to several known criminals, including a loan shark and a man convicted of fraud, which led donors to demand an immediate audit of its finances.", "t": "調查人員發現這家慈善機構的主任與幾名已知罪犯有不光彩的關係，其中包括一名放高利貸的人和一名詐欺罪犯，這使得捐款人要求立即稽核其財務。", "as": "The politician's unsavory alliances with venal officials and shady contractors finally came to light, and the ensuing scandal besmirched the reputation of his entire party.", "at": "這位政治人物與貪腐官員和可疑承包商之間令人反感的結盟終於曝光，隨之而來的醜聞玷污了他整個政黨的名聲。"}, {"w": "intimate", "p": "v.", "d": "To suggest or hint at something indirectly.", "c": "暗示；透露", "s": "Although the coach never said so directly, she seemed to intimate that the injured captain might not play in the championship game, mentioning several times that the team should be ready for changes.", "t": "雖然教練從未直接說出口，她似乎在暗示受傷的隊長可能不會參加冠軍賽，因為她好幾次提到球隊應該為變動做好準備。", "as": "The taciturn witness would not answer the prosecutor's questions directly, but he intimated through a few laconic remarks that the defendant's carefully constructed alibi was spurious.", "at": "那位沉默寡言的證人不肯直接回答檢察官的問題，但他透過幾句簡短的話暗示，被告精心編造的不在場證明是假的。"}, {"w": "predispose", "p": "v.", "d": "To make someone likely to behave or suffer in a certain way.", "c": "使傾向於；使易患", "s": "Doctors explained that certain genes may predispose a person to heart disease, but they emphasized that regular exercise, a balanced diet, and avoiding cigarettes can greatly reduce that inherited risk.", "t": "醫師解釋，某些基因可能使一個人容易罹患心臟病，但他們強調，規律運動、均衡飲食和避免吸菸可以大幅降低這種遺傳風險。", "as": "Her diffident upbringing seemed to predispose her toward caution, yet in moments of crisis she acted with surprising alacrity and an equanimity that impressed everyone.", "at": "她怯懦缺乏自信的成長背景似乎使她傾向於謹慎，然而在危機時刻，她卻以驚人的敏捷和令每個人印象深刻的沉著冷靜採取行動。"}, {"w": "apace", "p": "adv.", "d": "Quickly; at a fast pace.", "c": "迅速地；飛快地", "s": "Thanks to dry weather and extra night shifts, construction of the new subway line proceeded apace throughout the summer, and city officials announced that the first three stations would open several months ahead of schedule.", "t": "由於天氣乾燥加上增加夜班，新捷運路線的工程在整個夏天都迅速進行，市府官員宣布前三個車站將比預定時間提前數個月開通。", "as": "Research in artificial intelligence advances apace, and some ethicists fear that our laws are too hidebound to keep up with the inexorable progress of technology.", "at": "人工智慧研究正飛快地進展，一些倫理學家擔心我們的法律太過墨守成規，跟不上科技無可阻擋的進步。"}, {"w": "verdant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Green with lush grass or plant growth.", "c": "翠綠的；草木茂盛的", "s": "After several weeks of steady spring rain, the once dry, brown hillsides of the national park became verdant and alive with wildflowers, attracting crowds of hikers and photographers from all over the island.", "t": "經過數週持續的春雨，國家公園裡原本乾燥枯黃的山坡變得青翠茂盛，開滿了野花，吸引了來自全島各地的大批登山客和攝影師。", "as": "The poet's elegiac verses lovingly recall the verdant meadows and quiet streams of her childhood, a bucolic landscape that now lies buried beneath highways, parking lots, and shopping malls.", "at": "這位詩人哀婉的詩句深情追憶她童年時翠綠的草地與寧靜的小溪，那片田園風光如今已被埋在高速公路、停車場和購物中心底下。"}, {"w": "cajole", "p": "v.", "d": "To persuade someone gently through flattery or coaxing.", "c": "哄騙；勸誘", "s": "The little boy tried to cajole his father into buying him a new video game, promising to wash the car every weekend, finish his homework early, and never complain about vegetables again.", "t": "小男孩試圖哄父親給他買一款新的電玩遊戲，承諾每個週末都會洗車、提早寫完功課，而且再也不抱怨吃蔬菜。", "as": "Neither threats nor blandishments could cajole the obstinate old farmer into selling his land, so the developers finally had to redesign the entire shopping center.", "at": "無論是威脅還是甜言蜜語，都無法哄騙那位固執的老農夫賣掉他的土地，因此開發商最後不得不重新設計整座購物中心。"}, {"w": "bane", "p": "n.", "d": "A cause of great distress, harm, or annoyance.", "c": "禍根；災星", "s": "Mosquitoes have long been the bane of tropical communities, spreading malaria and dengue fever that kill hundreds of thousands of people every year and place enormous strain on local hospitals.", "t": "蚊子長久以來一直是熱帶社區的禍害，傳播瘧疾和登革熱，每年奪走數十萬人的性命，並對當地醫院造成巨大壓力。", "as": "Procrastination has always been the bane of the novelist's existence; she is remarkably prolific when deadlines loom, but otherwise she can languish in lethargy for weeks at a time.", "at": "拖延一直是這位小說家生活中的禍根；截止日期逼近時她產量驚人，但其他時候她可能一連好幾週都在懶散中萎靡不振。"}, {"w": "diatribe", "p": "n.", "d": "A bitter, abusive verbal attack.", "c": "抨擊；謾罵", "s": "The famous chef's angry review was less a critique than a diatribe, a two-thousand-word attack that mocked the restaurant's owner, insulted its waiters, and called the dessert an insult to civilization itself.", "t": "這位知名主廚憤怒的評論與其說是評析，不如說是一篇謾罵，這篇兩千字的抨擊嘲弄餐廳老闆、侮辱服務生，還稱甜點是對文明本身的侮辱。", "as": "The columnist's weekly diatribe against modern art was so splenetic and full of vitriol that readers began to suspect his polemical style was merely a bid for attention.", "at": "這位專欄作家每週對現代藝術的抨擊充滿怒氣與刻薄，以至於讀者開始懷疑他那種爭論性的風格只是為了博取關注。"}, {"w": "evocation", "p": "n.", "d": "The act of bringing a memory, feeling, or image to mind.", "c": "喚起；令人回想", "s": "The novel's opening chapter is a beautiful evocation of life in a 1960s Taipei alley, describing the smells of street food, the sounds of street vendors, and the laughter of children playing marbles.", "t": "這部小說的開頭章節優美地喚起了一九六〇年代台北巷弄的生活，描繪了小吃的香味、小販的叫賣聲，以及孩子們打彈珠的笑聲。", "as": "The documentary's evocation of wartime London was so poignant, with its images redolent of smoke, rubble, and air-raid sirens, that many elderly viewers who had lived through the bombing openly wept.", "at": "這部紀錄片對戰時倫敦的再現如此動人，那些令人聯想起煙霧、瓦礫和空襲警報的畫面，讓許多親身經歷過轟炸的年長觀眾公開落淚。"}, {"w": "imbue", "p": "v.", "d": "To fill or inspire someone or something with a quality.", "c": "灌輸；使充滿", "s": "The founders hoped to imbue their small school with a spirit of curiosity, encouraging students to ask questions, conduct experiments, and challenge even the textbook when the evidence seemed to point elsewhere.", "t": "創辦人希望讓這所小學校充滿好奇的精神，鼓勵學生提出問題、進行實驗，甚至在證據似乎指向其他方向時質疑課本。", "as": "The director imbued the film with a sense of quiet melancholy and ennui, perfectly capturing the ineffable loneliness of a widower who has outlived all his friends.", "at": "導演為這部電影注入一股靜謐的憂鬱與倦怠感，完美捕捉了一位比所有朋友都活得更久的鰥夫那種難以言喻的孤寂。"}, {"w": "repugnant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely distasteful; causing strong disgust.", "c": "令人厭惡的；反感的", "s": "Most citizens found the idea of testing cosmetics on puppies repugnant, and after thousands of letters of protest, the company announced it would switch to alternative methods that did not harm animals.", "t": "大多數民眾都覺得用小狗測試化妝品的想法令人厭惡，在收到數千封抗議信後，該公司宣布將改用不傷害動物的替代方法。", "as": "To the young idealist, the senator's casuistry was repugnant, a specious attempt to justify an unconscionable law that punished the poor for their own poverty.", "at": "對這位年輕的理想主義者而言，參議員的詭辯令人厭惡，那是一種似是而非的企圖，想為一條因窮人貧窮而懲罰他們、毫無良知的法律辯護。"}, {"w": "insolent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Boldly rude and disrespectful.", "c": "傲慢無禮的；目中無人的", "s": "When the referee warned him about rough play, the insolent player laughed in his face, mocked his eyesight in front of the crowd, and was immediately sent off the field for unsportsmanlike conduct.", "t": "裁判就粗暴的動作向他提出警告時，那名傲慢無禮的球員當面嘲笑他，在觀眾面前挖苦他的視力，因而立即因違反運動精神的行為被罰出場。", "as": "The insolent courtier's mocking jests eventually provoked the queen's wrath, and his churlish invective against her ministers earned him a long and humiliating banishment from the palace.", "at": "那位傲慢無禮的朝臣嘲弄的玩笑最終激怒了女王，而他對大臣們粗魯的辱罵讓他遭受了漫長而屈辱的流放，被逐出宮廷。"}, {"w": "impunity", "p": "n.", "d": "Freedom from punishment or harmful consequences.", "c": "不受懲罰；免責", "s": "For years, illegal loggers cut down protected cypress trees with impunity, knowing that the remote mountain forest had only two rangers and that the courts rarely punished anyone caught taking timber.", "t": "多年來，非法伐木者肆無忌憚地砍伐受保護的樹木，因為他們知道這片偏遠森林只有兩名巡山員，而且法院很少懲罰被抓到盜伐木材的人。", "as": "Corrupt officials who peculate public funds with impunity breed a culture of cynicism, and citizens soon conclude that probity in government is merely a quixotic dream.", "at": "肆無忌憚地盜用公款的貪官會助長一種憤世嫉俗的文化，民眾很快就會認定政府清廉只是不切實際的幻想。"}, {"w": "stagnate", "p": "v.", "d": "To stop developing, moving, or progressing.", "c": "停滯；不流動", "s": "Economists warned that wages would continue to stagnate unless the government invested in education and new industries, since most young workers had seen almost no increase in pay for a decade.", "t": "經濟學家警告，除非政府投資教育和新興產業，否則薪資將持續停滯，因為大多數年輕勞工十年來幾乎沒有加薪。", "as": "Without new ideas or young talent, the once fecund artistic movement began to stagnate, and its aging members grew complacent, merely repeating the hackneyed themes of their youth.", "at": "缺乏新想法和年輕人才，這個曾經多產的藝術運動開始停滯，其年邁的成員也變得自滿，只是不斷重複他們年輕時的陳腐主題。"}, {"w": "emblematic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Serving as a symbol or typical example of something.", "c": "象徵性的；代表性的", "s": "The bald eagle became emblematic of the United States because early leaders admired its strength and independence, and today its image appears on coins, passports, and the official presidential seal.", "t": "白頭海鵰之所以成為美國的象徵，是因為早期的領袖欣賞牠的力量與獨立，如今牠的圖像出現在硬幣、護照和總統官方印璽上。", "as": "The crumbling factory is emblematic of the town's decline, and its rusting machines are a vestigial reminder of the industrial boom that once made the region prosperous and its workers sanguine.", "at": "這座搖搖欲墜的工廠象徵著小鎮的衰落，那些生鏽的機器則是殘存的提醒，見證曾經讓這個地區繁榮、讓工人們滿懷樂觀的工業榮景。"}, {"w": "plaintive", "p": "adj.", "d": "Sounding sad and mournful.", "c": "哀傷的；悲哀的", "s": "Long after its owners had moved away, the abandoned dog sat at the gate each evening, letting out a plaintive howl that the neighbors said was the saddest sound they had ever heard.", "t": "在主人搬走很久之後，那隻被遺棄的狗每晚都坐在門口，發出哀傷的嚎叫，鄰居們說那是他們聽過最悲傷的聲音。", "as": "The plaintive melody of the erhu, with its lugubrious, sliding notes, seemed perfectly suited to the elegiac tone of the old folk tale about two separated lovers.", "at": "二胡哀傷的旋律帶著悲淒滑動的音符，似乎完美契合那則講述一對離散戀人的古老民間故事的哀婉基調。"}, {"w": "rapacious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Aggressively greedy and grasping, especially for wealth.", "c": "貪婪的；掠奪的", "s": "The rapacious landlord raised the rent three times in a single year, charged tenants for repairs he never made, and evicted an elderly couple simply because a wealthier family offered to pay more.", "t": "那位貪婪的房東在一年內調漲三次租金，向房客收取他從未進行的修繕費用，還只因一戶更有錢的家庭願意付更多錢，就把一對老夫婦趕了出去。", "as": "The rapacious colonial traders were notorious for their cupidity, stripping the Pacific islands of precious sandalwood within a few decades and leaving behind indigent communities and devastated forests.", "at": "那些貪婪的殖民商人以貪得無厭聞名，他們在短短數十年間掠奪太平洋島嶼上珍貴的檀香木，留下一貧如洗的社群和遭到摧毀的森林。"}]}, {"unit": 29, "level": 6, "cards": [{"w": "peon", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who does hard, menial, low-paid work.", "c": "苦工；地位低下的勞工", "s": "In the early years of the company, the future CEO worked as a lowly peon in the mailroom, sorting letters for twelve hours a day at minimum wage and rarely receiving a word of thanks from the executives upstairs.", "t": "在公司創立初期，這位未來的執行長在收發室當一名卑微的苦工，以最低工資每天分揀信件十二小時，幾乎從未得到樓上主管的一句感謝。", "as": "Treated as a mere peon by the officious manager, the young clerk nonetheless remained resolute, quietly mastering every task until her diligence earned an accolade from the board.", "at": "雖然被那位愛管閒事的經理當成區區一名苦工，這位年輕職員仍堅定不移，默默精通每項工作，直到她的勤奮贏得董事會的讚譽。"}, {"w": "intuit", "p": "v.", "d": "To know or understand something by instinct, without reasoning.", "c": "憑直覺得知；直覺感知", "s": "Experienced nurses often intuit that a patient is deteriorating before any monitor shows a change, relying on subtle cues such as skin color, breathing rhythm, and mood that they have learned to read over many years.", "t": "經驗豐富的護理師往往能在任何監測儀出現變化之前，就憑直覺察覺病人病情惡化，依靠的是膚色、呼吸節奏與情緒等細微線索，這些是他們多年來學會解讀的。", "as": "The astute negotiator intuited the other party's misgivings from a single pensive pause and quickly revised her proposal before anyone at the long conference table voiced an objection.", "at": "這位精明的談判者從對方一次若有所思的停頓中，直覺察覺到對方的疑慮，並在長會議桌旁任何人提出異議之前迅速修改了她的提案。"}, {"w": "opine", "p": "v.", "d": "To state or hold something as one's opinion.", "c": "發表意見；認為", "s": "During the televised panel, several commentators who had never studied economics were happy to opine at length about interest rates, while the one actual economist present cautiously reminded viewers that the data remained incomplete.", "t": "在電視轉播的座談會上，幾位從未研究過經濟學的評論員樂於針對利率長篇大論地發表意見，而現場唯一真正的經濟學家則謹慎地提醒觀眾，數據仍不完整。", "as": "Television hosts who opine on every political crisis within minutes often offer glib predictions that are rarely corroborated by later events, yet audiences continue to grant them surprising credence.", "at": "那些在幾分鐘內就對每場政治危機發表意見的電視主持人，常常提出油腔滑調的預測，而這些預測很少被後來的事件證實；然而觀眾依舊對他們抱持令人意外的信任。"}, {"w": "languish", "p": "v.", "d": "To lose strength or remain neglected in an unpleasant state.", "c": "衰弱；受冷落而停滯", "s": "Without steady funding or public attention, the promising cancer research proposal was left to languish in a government office for nearly a decade, until a new administration finally rediscovered it and approved the first clinical trials.", "t": "由於缺乏穩定經費與大眾關注，這項前景看好的癌症研究計畫在政府辦公室裡被擱置了將近十年，直到新的政府終於重新發現它，並核准了首批臨床試驗。", "as": "While the reform bill languished in committee, the dissident senators delivered one tirade after another, accusing their colleagues of complacent indifference toward millions of struggling families.", "at": "當改革法案在委員會中遭擱置停滯時，持異議的參議員們發表了一篇又一篇激烈的長篇演說，指責同僚對數百萬陷入困境的家庭抱持自滿而冷漠的態度。"}, {"w": "vestigial", "p": "adj.", "d": "Remaining as a small, useless trace of something earlier.", "c": "退化的；殘留的", "s": "Biologists point to the human tailbone as a classic example of a vestigial structure: it once supported a tail in our distant primate ancestors but now serves almost no purpose beyond anchoring a few muscles.", "t": "生物學家指出，人類的尾骨是退化結構的經典例子：它曾在我們遠古的靈長類祖先身上支撐尾巴，但如今除了固定幾條肌肉之外幾乎沒有任何作用。", "as": "Though the monarchy survives as a vestigial institution, its ceremonies still draw myriad tourists, and its defunct titles remain a source of national nostalgia rather than real power.", "at": "雖然君主制度僅以殘留的形式存續，其典禮仍吸引無數觀光客，而那些已失效的頭銜則成為國人懷舊情感的來源，而非真正的權力。"}, {"w": "somnolent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Sleepy or drowsy; tending to cause sleep.", "c": "想睡的；催眠的", "s": "After a heavy lunch in the overheated lecture hall, many students grew somnolent, their heads nodding forward as the professor's quiet, monotonous voice described the tax policies of the eighteenth-century French monarchy.", "t": "在過熱的演講廳裡吃完一頓豐盛午餐後，許多學生變得昏昏欲睡；教授輕柔而單調的聲音講述著十八世紀法國君主政體的稅收政策，他們的頭也一點一點地往前垂。", "as": "The somnolent drone of the speaker's verbose address induced such lethargy in the audience that even the most fervent supporters began to doze in their seats.", "at": "講者冗長演說那令人昏昏欲睡的單調嗡嗡聲，讓聽眾陷入極度倦怠，就連最熱情的支持者也開始在座位上打起瞌睡。"}, {"w": "supplant", "p": "v.", "d": "To take the place of, especially by force or scheming.", "c": "取代；排擠", "s": "Many music critics feared that streaming services would eventually supplant physical albums entirely, yet vinyl records have enjoyed a surprising revival as younger listeners seek out large cover art and the warm sound of analog playback.", "t": "許多樂評家擔心串流服務終將完全取代實體專輯，然而黑膠唱片卻出人意料地復興，因為年輕聽眾開始追求大幅的封面藝術以及類比播放的溫暖音色。", "as": "The ambitious general, through a series of clandestine machinations, plotted to supplant the aging king and subjugate the rebellious northern provinces before the next harvest festival.", "at": "這位野心勃勃的將軍透過一連串祕密的陰謀，計畫在下一個豐收節之前取代年邁的國王，並征服叛亂的北方諸省。"}, {"w": "euphemism", "p": "n.", "d": "A mild word used in place of a harsh or unpleasant one.", "c": "委婉語；婉轉說法", "s": "Critics complained that the company's announcement used 'rightsizing' as a euphemism for laying off nearly three thousand workers, disguising a painful reality behind a cheerful, vague term that sounded almost like a reward.", "t": "批評者抱怨，公司的公告用「規模合理化」作為裁撤近三千名員工的委婉說法，用一個聽起來幾乎像獎勵的愉悅、含糊的詞語來掩飾痛苦的現實。", "as": "The diplomat's speech was replete with euphemisms, and his ambiguous references to 'regrettable incidents' only obfuscated the brutal facts of the border conflict that had displaced thousands.", "at": "這位外交官的演說充斥著委婉語，他對「令人遺憾的事件」那些含糊的提及，只是混淆了那場造成數千人流離失所的邊境衝突的殘酷事實。"}, {"w": "visceral", "p": "adj.", "d": "Coming from deep, instinctive feelings rather than reason.", "c": "發自內心的；出於本能的", "s": "Although the statistics on ocean pollution had failed to move the audience, the documentary's single image of a sea turtle tangled in plastic provoked a visceral reaction, with several viewers gasping aloud and others turning away in distress.", "t": "雖然有關海洋污染的統計數據未能打動觀眾，但紀錄片中一隻海龜被塑膠纏住的畫面卻引發了發自內心的強烈反應，有幾位觀眾忍不住倒抽一口氣，另一些人則難過地別過頭去。", "as": "Her visceral aversion to injustice made her a fervent advocate for indigent defendants who could not afford lawyers, even when such cases brought her neither fame nor any payment.", "at": "她對不公不義發自內心的厭惡，使她成為請不起律師的貧困被告的熱忱辯護者，即使這類案件既不能為她帶來名聲，也沒有任何報酬。"}, {"w": "dispassionate", "p": "adj.", "d": "Not influenced by strong emotion; calm and impartial.", "c": "冷靜的；不偏不倚的", "s": "Judges are expected to remain dispassionate even in emotionally charged trials, weighing the evidence calmly and fairly rather than allowing sympathy for the victim or anger at the defendant to shape their final rulings.", "t": "即使在情緒激昂的審判中，法官也應保持冷靜公正，平和而公平地衡量證據，而不是讓對受害者的同情或對被告的憤怒左右最終判決。", "as": "Even amid the contentious debate, the moderator offered a dispassionate summary of each position, and her judicious tone helped mollify the angriest panelists on stage that night.", "at": "即使在爭論激烈的辯論中，主持人仍對每一方立場提出冷靜公正的摘要，而她明智審慎的語氣也幫助安撫了那晚台上最憤怒的與談人。"}, {"w": "indefatigable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Never tiring; persistent and untiring.", "c": "不知疲倦的；不屈不撓的", "s": "The indefatigable volunteer spent every weekend for fifteen years cleaning the riverbanks, hauling out tires and plastic bags in all weather, and she continued the work well into her eighties without ever asking for recognition.", "t": "這位不知疲倦的志工十五年來每個週末都去清理河岸，無論天候如何都拖出輪胎和塑膠袋，而她一直到八十多歲仍持續這項工作，從未要求任何表揚。", "as": "An indefatigable researcher, she pursued the enigma of the ancient script for decades, and her assiduous efforts finally yielded a lucid translation that scholars worldwide accepted.", "at": "身為一位不知疲倦的研究者，她數十年來鑽研那種古代文字之謎，而她勤勉不懈的努力終於產生了一份全世界學者都接受的清晰譯本。"}, {"w": "archetype", "p": "n.", "d": "An original model or a perfectly typical example.", "c": "原型；典型", "s": "Literary scholars often describe Odysseus as the archetype of the clever, wandering hero, a model whose basic traits reappear in countless later stories, from medieval romances to modern science-fiction films about lost space travelers.", "t": "文學學者常把奧德修斯形容為聰明、四處漂泊的英雄原型，他的基本特質在後來無數故事中一再出現，從中世紀傳奇到描寫迷途太空旅人的現代科幻電影皆然。", "as": "The film's villain is a hackneyed archetype, the charming yet mendacious aristocrat whose sinister smile betrays his duplicity long before the final scene reveals it to viewers.", "at": "這部電影的反派是陳腐老套的典型人物：一位迷人卻滿口謊言的貴族，早在最後一幕向觀眾揭露之前，他陰險的笑容就已洩露了他的表裡不一。"}, {"w": "veracity", "p": "n.", "d": "Truthfulness, honesty, or accuracy.", "c": "真實性；誠實", "s": "Before publishing the leaked documents, the newspaper's editors spent three weeks checking their veracity, contacting independent experts, comparing signatures, and confirming dates, because a single forged page could destroy the paper's reputation for accurate reporting.", "t": "在刊登外洩文件之前，報社編輯花了三週查證其真實性，他們聯繫獨立專家、比對簽名並確認日期，因為只要有一頁偽造，就可能毀掉報社報導準確的聲譽。", "as": "Skeptical historians questioned the veracity of the explorer's memoir, noting that its fanciful accounts of sea monsters appeared apocryphal and were never corroborated by any other traveler.", "at": "抱持懷疑的歷史學家質疑這位探險家回憶錄的真實性，指出書中關於海怪的離奇記述似乎是杜撰的，而且從未得到任何其他旅人的證實。"}, {"w": "minion", "p": "n.", "d": "A servile follower who obeys a powerful person.", "c": "嘍囉；走狗", "s": "The corrupt governor never handled bribes himself; instead, he sent a loyal minion to collect the cash from contractors, ensuring that if the scheme were ever exposed, the blame would fall on someone far less powerful.", "t": "這位貪腐的州長從不親自經手賄款；他反而派遣一名忠心的嘍囉去向承包商收取現金，確保萬一這項勾當曝光，責任會落在一個權勢遠不如他的人身上。", "as": "Surrounded by obsequious minions who never dared to remonstrate, the despotic ruler grew increasingly detached from the suffering of his people in the drought-stricken countryside.", "at": "這位專制統治者身邊圍繞著從不敢進諫、阿諛奉承的嘍囉，因而與乾旱肆虐的鄉間百姓所受的苦難日益疏離。"}, {"w": "inveterate", "p": "adj.", "d": "Firmly fixed by long habit and unlikely to change.", "c": "根深柢固的；積習難改的", "s": "An inveterate gambler for more than thirty years, the novelist borrowed money from nearly everyone he knew, and he drew on these painful experiences to write a short, powerful book about addiction and self-deception.", "t": "這位小說家三十多年來一直是積習難改的賭徒，他幾乎向每個認識的人借過錢，並以這些痛苦經歷為素材，寫了一本關於成癮與自欺的簡短而有力的書。", "as": "An inveterate procrastinator, the student habitually postponed his onerous assignments until the last night, then wrote cursory essays that his professor found vacuous and unconvincing.", "at": "這名學生是積習難改的拖延者，習慣把繁重的作業拖到最後一晚，然後寫出草率的文章，讓教授覺得內容空洞又缺乏說服力。"}, {"w": "extol", "p": "v.", "d": "To praise highly and enthusiastically.", "c": "讚揚；頌揚", "s": "Travel writers continue to extol the small island's beauty, praising its turquoise water, quiet beaches, and friendly fishing villages, though local residents now worry that all this glowing publicity will attract more tourists than the fragile environment can handle.", "t": "旅遊作家持續頌揚這座小島的美景，讚美它碧綠的海水、寧靜的海灘與友善的漁村，但當地居民如今擔心，這些熱烈的宣傳將吸引超過脆弱環境所能承受的遊客數量。", "as": "While critics extolled the composer's prolific output, a few dissenting voices disparaged her later symphonies as banal imitations of her earlier masterpieces from the 1980s.", "at": "雖然評論家盛讚這位作曲家多產的創作，但少數持不同意見的人卻貶低她後期的交響曲，認為那只是她1980年代早期傑作的平庸模仿。"}, {"w": "gaffe", "p": "n.", "d": "An embarrassing social or diplomatic blunder.", "c": "失言；失禮", "s": "The new ambassador committed an unfortunate gaffe at her first state dinner when she mistakenly toasted the host country's former rival, an error that embarrassed her staff and dominated the next day's newspaper headlines.", "t": "這位新任大使在她第一場國宴上犯了令人遺憾的失禮之舉：她誤向東道國昔日的對手國舉杯致敬，這個錯誤讓她的幕僚尷尬不已，也成了隔天報紙的頭條。", "as": "The senator's gaffe during the debate was egregious, yet his subsequent contrition seemed so genuine that most voters were willing to forgive the blunder within a week.", "at": "這位參議員在辯論中的失言極為離譜，但他隨後的悔意顯得如此真誠，以致大多數選民在一週內就願意原諒這次失誤。"}, {"w": "indoctrinate", "p": "v.", "d": "To teach someone to accept beliefs without questioning them.", "c": "灌輸（思想）；洗腦", "s": "Historians have documented how authoritarian regimes used schools to indoctrinate children, replacing open discussion with slogans and requiring students to memorize the leader's speeches rather than question them or compare them with other points of view.", "t": "歷史學家記錄了威權政權如何利用學校向兒童灌輸思想：以口號取代開放討論，並要求學生背誦領袖的演說，而不是質疑這些演說或將其與其他觀點相比較。", "as": "The cult's leaders indoctrinated gullible recruits with specious arguments, gradually convincing them to ostracize any relative who dared to question the group's teachings or its finances.", "at": "該邪教的領袖用似是而非的論點向容易受騙的新成員灌輸思想，逐漸說服他們排斥任何膽敢質疑該團體教義或其財務的親人。"}, {"w": "nuance", "p": "n.", "d": "A subtle difference in meaning, tone, or feeling.", "c": "細微差別；微妙之處", "s": "A skilled translator must capture every nuance of the original poem, noticing, for example, whether a word suggests gentle sadness or bitter regret, because even a slight change in tone can alter the reader's entire emotional experience.", "t": "一位技巧純熟的譯者必須捕捉原詩中的每一個細微差別，例如留意某個字暗示的是淡淡的哀傷還是苦澀的懊悔，因為即使語氣上些微的改變，也可能改變讀者整體的情感體驗。", "as": "Critics praised the actor's nuanced portrayal of the stoic general, whose laconic replies concealed a profound ambivalence about the war he had been ordered to fight.", "at": "評論家盛讚這位演員對那位堅忍將軍細膩入微的詮釋：將軍簡短的回答掩藏了他對奉命參與的那場戰爭深刻的矛盾心情。"}, {"w": "placate", "p": "v.", "d": "To calm someone's anger, often by making concessions.", "c": "安撫；平息（怒氣）", "s": "To placate the furious residents who had been without electricity for five days, the utility company offered each household a full month of free service and promised to bury the vulnerable power lines underground before the next storm season.", "t": "為了安撫已停電五天、怒氣沖沖的居民，電力公司提供每戶一整個月的免費用電，並承諾在下一個風暴季節來臨之前，將容易受損的電線埋入地下。", "as": "Hoping to placate the truculent union leaders, the chief executive offered a modest raise, but her conciliatory gesture was rebuffed as a mere pittance by the workers.", "at": "為了安撫態度強硬好鬥的工會領袖，執行長提出小幅加薪，但她這個和解的姿態被工人們斥為區區微薄小錢而遭到斷然拒絕。"}]}, {"unit": 30, "level": 6, "cards": [{"w": "deify", "p": "v.", "d": "To worship or treat someone as a god.", "c": "神化；奉若神明", "s": "Ancient Romans sometimes chose to deify their emperors after death, building temples in their honor and offering sacrifices, a practice that blurred the line between political leadership and religious devotion for several centuries.", "t": "古羅馬人有時會在皇帝死後將其神化，為他們興建神廟並獻上祭品；這種做法在數個世紀之間模糊了政治領導與宗教崇拜之間的界線。", "as": "Fans who deify celebrities often overlook their foibles, and this uncritical adulation can make the stars themselves surprisingly impervious to sensible advice from their closest friends.", "at": "把名人奉若神明的粉絲往往忽略他們的小缺點，而這種不加批判的過度奉承，可能使明星本身對最親近朋友的中肯建議出奇地無動於衷。"}, {"w": "recapitulate", "p": "v.", "d": "To summarize the main points of something again.", "c": "扼要重述；概括", "s": "At the end of each lecture, the chemistry professor would briefly recapitulate the key ideas of the day, listing the three main reactions on the board so that students could check whether their notes were complete.", "t": "每堂課結束時，這位化學教授都會簡要重述當天的重點，把三個主要反應列在黑板上，讓學生可以檢查自己的筆記是否完整。", "as": "Before the vote, the chair recapitulated the salient arguments on both sides, offering a terse summary that even the most verbose committee members agreed was fair.", "at": "投票之前，主席扼要重述了雙方的重要論點，提出一份簡潔的總結，就連最囉嗦的委員也同意這份總結很公正。"}, {"w": "luminary", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who is famous and inspiring in a field.", "c": "傑出人物；權威", "s": "The conference attracted every luminary in the field of climate science, including two Nobel laureates and the author of the most widely cited study on melting glaciers, so graduate students lined up for hours to hear them speak.", "t": "這場研討會吸引了氣候科學領域的每一位傑出人物，其中包括兩位諾貝爾獎得主，以及那篇被引用最多的冰川融化研究的作者，因此研究生們排隊數小時只為聆聽他們演講。", "as": "The literary luminary was known for her erudite essays, yet she remained remarkably genial and magnanimous toward young writers whose first novels were still callow and unpolished.", "at": "這位文壇巨擘以學識淵博的散文聞名，但她對處女作仍顯稚嫩、未經雕琢的年輕作家，依然格外親切而寬宏大量。"}, {"w": "confound", "p": "v.", "d": "To confuse or surprise someone by going against expectations.", "c": "使困惑；使驚訝", "s": "The tiny tardigrade continues to confound biologists, surviving boiling water, freezing temperatures, and even the vacuum of outer space, abilities that seem to defy nearly everything scientists believe about the limits of animal life.", "t": "微小的水熊蟲持續讓生物學家困惑不已，牠能在沸水、冰凍溫度，甚至外太空的真空中存活，這些能力似乎違反了科學家對動物生命極限的幾乎所有認知。", "as": "The candidate's sudden victory confounded the pundits, whose dogmatic predictions had dismissed her as a mere neophyte with only a tenuous chance of winning the primary.", "at": "這位候選人的突然勝選讓政治評論家們大感意外；他們先前武斷地預測，認為她只是個新手，贏得初選的機會微乎其微。"}, {"w": "sojourn", "p": "n.", "d": "A temporary stay in a place.", "c": "短暫停留；旅居", "s": "During her six-month sojourn in Kyoto, the American novelist studied traditional tea ceremonies and kept a detailed journal, and those observations later became the heart of her prize-winning book about cultural exchange.", "t": "這位美國小說家在京都旅居的六個月期間，學習傳統茶道並寫下詳細日記，這些觀察後來成為她那本探討文化交流的得獎作品的核心。", "as": "His brief sojourn among the itinerant herders proved edifying, teaching him to eschew the expensive comforts he had once considered essential to a happy life.", "at": "他在那群四處遷徙的牧民之間短暫停留，結果頗具啟發性，使他學會避開那些他曾認為是幸福生活所不可或缺的昂貴享受。"}, {"w": "askew", "p": "adj.", "d": "Not straight or level; crooked.", "c": "歪斜的；不正的", "s": "After the minor earthquake, residents returned home to find nearly every framed painting askew on the walls, books scattered across the floors, and one kitchen cabinet door hanging loosely by a single hinge.", "t": "小地震過後，居民返家發現牆上幾乎每一幅裱框的畫都歪斜了，書本散落一地，還有一扇廚房櫥櫃門只靠一個鉸鏈鬆鬆地掛著。", "as": "The fastidious butler could not tolerate a single fork set askew, and his punctilious inspections of the dining table bordered on the pedantic, much to the staff's amusement.", "at": "這位講究的管家無法容忍任何一支叉子擺歪，他對餐桌一絲不苟的檢查近乎迂腐，令其他員工覺得十分好笑。"}, {"w": "histrionic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Overly dramatic or theatrical in behavior.", "c": "誇張做作的；演戲般的", "s": "When the referee called a foul, the striker fell to the grass with a histrionic scream, clutching his ankle and rolling dramatically, although replays clearly showed that the defender had barely touched him.", "t": "裁判判犯規時，這名前鋒誇張地尖叫倒在草地上，抓著腳踝戲劇性地翻滾，但重播畫面清楚顯示，防守球員幾乎沒有碰到他。", "as": "The lawyer's histrionic gestures and bombastic rhetoric did little to impress the stolid judge, who preferred concise arguments grounded in demonstrable facts and clear precedent.", "at": "這位律師誇張做作的手勢與浮誇的言辭，對那位不動聲色的法官幾乎毫無影響；法官偏好以可證明的事實與明確判例為基礎的簡潔論證。"}, {"w": "coalesce", "p": "v.", "d": "To come together to form one group or whole.", "c": "聯合；合併", "s": "Over millions of years, clouds of dust and gas slowly began to coalesce under the pull of gravity, forming the first stars and planets that would eventually make up our solar system.", "t": "在數百萬年間，塵埃和氣體雲在重力牽引下慢慢開始聚合，形成最早的恆星與行星，最終構成了我們的太陽系。", "as": "Several rival factions coalesced into a single coalition, though their heterogeneous goals and lingering animosity made a lasting alliance seem rather tenuous to most observers.", "at": "數個敵對的派系聯合成單一聯盟，但它們迥異的目標與揮之不去的敵意，使得大多數觀察家認為這個聯盟難以長久維持。"}, {"w": "listless", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lacking energy, interest, or enthusiasm.", "c": "無精打采的；倦怠的", "s": "During the long heat wave, the zookeepers noticed that the polar bears had become listless, lying motionless in the shade for most of the day and showing little interest in the toys and frozen fish offered to them.", "t": "在漫長的熱浪期間，動物園管理員發現北極熊變得無精打采，大半天都一動也不動地躺在陰涼處，對提供給牠們的玩具和冷凍魚也興趣缺缺。", "as": "After weeks of monotonous tasks, the listless interns sank into a profound ennui, and even the manager's ebullient pep talks failed to rouse them from their torpor.", "at": "經過數週單調乏味的工作，這些無精打采的實習生陷入深深的倦怠，就連經理熱情洋溢的打氣演說也無法讓他們從麻木中振作起來。"}, {"w": "abate", "p": "v.", "d": "To become less strong or intense.", "c": "減弱；減輕", "s": "Ferry service between the islands was suspended for two days, and officials warned travelers that boats would not resume their normal schedule until the powerful winds began to abate and the waves returned to a safe height.", "t": "島嶼之間的渡輪服務暫停了兩天，官員警告旅客，在強風開始減弱、浪高恢復到安全程度之前，船班不會恢復正常航行。", "as": "The public's animosity toward the mayor did not abate until she issued a candid apology, accepted culpability for the scandal, and promised to redress every grievance.", "at": "直到市長坦率地道歉、承認自己在醜聞中應負的責任，並承諾矯正每一項不滿之後，民眾對她的敵意才開始減弱。"}, {"w": "ponderous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Slow, heavy, and dull or awkward.", "c": "笨重的；沉悶冗長的", "s": "Although the historian's research was impressive, reviewers complained that her ponderous writing style, full of long sentences and endless footnotes, made the nine-hundred-page biography exhausting to read from beginning to end.", "t": "雖然這位歷史學家的研究令人佩服，評論者卻抱怨她沉悶冗長的寫作風格充滿長句與無盡的註腳，使得這本九百頁的傳記從頭讀到尾令人筋疲力盡。", "as": "The professor's ponderous lectures were so prolix and pedantic that students resorted to mnemonic tricks just to stay awake and remember the dates for the exam.", "at": "這位教授沉悶冗長的講課既囉嗦又賣弄學問，學生只好藉助記憶口訣，才能保持清醒並記住考試要考的年代。"}, {"w": "consecrate", "p": "v.", "d": "To make or declare something sacred, or dedicate it formally.", "c": "使神聖；奉獻", "s": "Before the new cathedral opened to the public, the bishop arrived to consecrate the building in a solemn ceremony, blessing the altar with holy water while the choir sang hymns written especially for the occasion.", "t": "在新的大教堂對外開放之前，主教前來以莊嚴的儀式為這座建築祝聖，一邊用聖水祝福祭壇，一邊由詩班吟唱特地為此場合譜寫的聖詩。", "as": "The battlefield was consecrated as a national memorial, and its sacrosanct grounds became a place where visitors could venerate the soldiers whose sacrifice had preserved the republic.", "at": "這處戰場被奉為國家紀念地，其神聖不可侵犯的土地成為訪客能夠敬仰那些以犧牲保全共和國的士兵之處。"}, {"w": "florid", "p": "adj.", "d": "Overly elaborate or ornate; also, flushed and red.", "c": "華麗的；（臉色）紅潤的", "s": "The editor urged the young poet to cut her florid descriptions, explaining that piling up so many decorative adjectives and elaborate metaphors distracted readers from the simple, powerful emotion at the center of the poem.", "t": "編輯敦促這位年輕詩人刪減她過分華麗的描寫，並解釋說堆砌這麼多裝飾性的形容詞和繁複的隱喻，會讓讀者分心，忽略詩作核心那簡單而有力的情感。", "as": "The candidate's florid oratory was dismissed as grandiloquent by critics, who argued that his effusive phrases concealed a striking dearth of concrete, practical policy proposals on health care.", "at": "這位候選人華麗的演說被評論家斥為浮誇，他們認為他那些熱情洋溢的詞句掩蓋了在醫療保健方面具體可行政策提案的明顯匱乏。"}, {"w": "incorrigible", "p": "adj.", "d": "Unable to be corrected or reformed because of bad habits.", "c": "無可救藥的；屢教不改的", "s": "Despite years of warnings from teachers and parents, the incorrigible prankster kept hiding frogs in the science lab, and by graduation his reputation for mischief had become something of a school legend.", "t": "儘管多年來老師和家長一再警告，這個屢教不改的惡作劇者仍不斷把青蛙藏在科學實驗室裡，到畢業時，他調皮搗蛋的名聲幾乎成了學校的傳奇。", "as": "An incorrigible spendthrift, the young heir squandered his entire inheritance on lavish parties and racehorses, ignoring every warning from the family's prudent financial advisers and his worried mother.", "at": "這位年輕繼承人是個無可救藥的揮霍者，他把全部遺產浪費在奢華的派對和賽馬上，無視家族那些謹慎的理財顧問以及憂心母親的每一次警告。"}, {"w": "assail", "p": "v.", "d": "To attack violently with blows or with harsh words.", "c": "猛烈攻擊；抨擊", "s": "When the controversial report was released, rival scientists rushed to assail its methods in newspaper editorials and online forums, accusing the authors of ignoring contradictory data and exaggerating the significance of their findings.", "t": "這份具爭議性的報告發表後，與之競爭的科學家紛紛在報紙社論與網路論壇上抨擊其研究方法，指控作者忽視矛盾的數據，並誇大了研究結果的重要性。", "as": "Assailed by vitriolic critics who vilified his policies, the beleaguered minister refused to capitulate and instead delivered a trenchant defense of his reforms in parliament.", "at": "這位處境艱難的部長遭到尖刻的批評者猛烈抨擊、詆毀他的政策，但他拒絕屈服，反而在國會中為自己的改革發表了一篇犀利的辯護。"}, {"w": "elixir", "p": "n.", "d": "A magical liquid believed to cure illness or give eternal life.", "c": "萬靈藥；長生不老藥", "s": "Medieval alchemists spent their lives searching for a legendary elixir that could cure every disease and grant eternal youth, and some of their failed experiments accidentally laid the foundations of modern chemistry.", "t": "中世紀的鍊金術士窮盡一生尋找一種傳說中能治百病、賜予永恆青春的萬靈藥，而他們有些失敗的實驗卻意外為現代化學奠定了基礎。", "as": "The charlatan peddled a dubious elixir that he claimed was a panacea for every ailment, but his outrageous promises soon drew sharp criticism from local doctors and pharmacists.", "at": "這名江湖騙子兜售一種可疑的藥水，聲稱它是能治百病的萬靈丹，但他荒誕的保證很快就遭到當地醫生與藥師的嚴厲批評。"}, {"w": "impresario", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who organizes and manages concerts, operas, or shows.", "c": "（演出）經理人；主辦人", "s": "The famous impresario who brought the Russian ballet to Paris in 1909 had no talent for dancing himself, but he possessed an extraordinary gift for recruiting brilliant composers, painters, and performers to work together.", "t": "1909年將俄羅斯芭蕾帶到巴黎的那位著名演出經理人本身並沒有舞蹈天分，但他擁有非凡的才能，能招募傑出的作曲家、畫家與表演者共同合作。", "as": "The flamboyant impresario was an adroit promoter, and his uncanny ability to anticipate public taste made almost every one of his productions on Broadway extremely lucrative.", "at": "這位作風浮華的演出經理人是個精明的宣傳高手，他預測大眾品味的驚人能力，使他在百老匯製作的幾乎每一部作品都極為賺錢。"}, {"w": "sentient", "p": "adj.", "d": "Able to feel, perceive, and experience sensations.", "c": "有感覺的；有知覺的", "s": "Animal-welfare laws in several countries now recognize octopuses and crabs as sentient creatures, since research shows that these animals can experience pain and stress and should therefore be protected from unnecessary suffering.", "t": "數個國家的動物福利法如今承認章魚和螃蟹是有知覺的生物，因為研究顯示這些動物能感受疼痛與壓力，因此應受到保護，免於不必要的痛苦。", "as": "Philosophers debate whether a truly sentient machine is a chimera or an inevitable result of technology, and their discursive arguments rarely reach any unequivocal conclusion.", "at": "哲學家爭論真正具有知覺的機器究竟是虛幻的空想，還是科技發展的必然結果，而他們漫無邊際的論證鮮少得出任何明確的結論。"}, {"w": "lackluster", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lacking energy, brightness, or excitement; dull.", "c": "平淡無奇的；缺乏光彩的", "s": "After two award-winning albums, the band's third record received lackluster reviews, with critics describing the songs as tired and forgettable and noting that even loyal fans seemed only mildly interested at the release concert.", "t": "在推出兩張得獎專輯之後，這個樂團的第三張唱片得到平淡的評價，評論家形容歌曲疲乏又令人過目即忘，並指出就連忠實樂迷在發片演唱會上也只是略感興趣。", "as": "The team's lackluster performance in the final game was attributed to lethargy and complacency, and the coach's subsequent tirade in the locker room became newspaper headlines.", "at": "球隊在決賽中表現平淡乏力，被歸咎於倦怠與自滿，而教練隨後在更衣室裡的激烈訓斥也登上了報紙頭條。"}, {"w": "beneficent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Doing or producing good; generous and kind.", "c": "行善的；慈善的", "s": "The beneficent foundation spent millions of dollars building rural clinics and training local nurses, and within a decade infant mortality in the region had dropped dramatically, a change that local families still remember with deep gratitude.", "t": "這個行善的基金會花費數百萬美元興建鄉村診所並培訓當地護理師，十年之內該地區的嬰兒死亡率大幅下降，當地家庭至今仍懷著深深的感激記得這項改變。", "as": "The beneficent duchess was renowned for her philanthropic work, and her munificence toward indigent families earned her the lasting gratitude of the entire village for generations.", "at": "這位樂善好施的公爵夫人以慈善事業聞名，她對貧困家庭的慷慨贈與，贏得了整個村莊世世代代長久的感激。"}]}, {"unit": 31, "level": 7, "cards": [{"w": "tribulation", "p": "n.", "d": "Great trouble, suffering, or a cause of it.", "c": "苦難；磨難", "s": "The memoir describes every tribulation the refugee family endured on their journey across the mountains, from hunger and freezing nights to the long months spent waiting in a crowded camp for permission to cross the border.", "t": "這本回憶錄描述了這個難民家庭翻越山區途中所承受的每一項苦難，從飢餓、酷寒的夜晚，到在擁擠的營地裡苦等好幾個月才獲准越過邊界。", "as": "Despite years of tribulation, the stoic farmer never lost his equanimity, and his determined spirit became an exemplary model for the younger families struggling through the drought.", "at": "儘管歷經多年苦難，這位堅忍的農夫從未失去沉著，他堅毅的精神成為在旱災中苦撐的年輕家庭可作為楷模的榜樣。"}, {"w": "deride", "p": "v.", "d": "To mock or ridicule with contempt.", "c": "嘲笑；嘲弄", "s": "When the young painter first exhibited her bold, colorful canvases, established critics chose to deride them as childish scribbles, yet within twenty years museums around the world were competing to buy her work.", "t": "這位年輕畫家首次展出她大膽、色彩鮮明的畫作時，知名評論家選擇嘲弄它們是幼稚的塗鴉，然而不到二十年，世界各地的博物館都在爭相收購她的作品。", "as": "Iconoclastic scientists are often derided by their peers and the press, but history has repeatedly vindicated those whose heterodox ideas once seemed absurd to the scientific establishment.", "at": "打破傳統的科學家常遭同儕與媒體嘲笑，但歷史一再證明，那些非正統觀點曾讓科學界覺得荒謬的人其實是對的。"}, {"w": "nefarious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely wicked, evil, or criminal.", "c": "邪惡的；兇惡的", "s": "Investigators eventually uncovered the nefarious scheme behind the charity, which had been collecting donations for flood victims while secretly sending most of the money to offshore accounts controlled by its directors.", "t": "調查人員最終揭發了這家慈善機構背後的邪惡陰謀：它一面為水災災民募款，一面暗中把大部分款項匯入由其董事控制的境外帳戶。", "as": "The spy novel's villain hatches a nefarious plot to sabotage the summit, aided by an unscrupulous banker whose clandestine payments fund the entire operation from Geneva.", "at": "這部間諜小說的反派策劃了一項破壞高峰會的邪惡陰謀，並得到一名肆無忌憚的銀行家協助，此人從日內瓦匯出的祕密金援資助了整個行動。"}, {"w": "ideologue", "p": "n.", "d": "A person rigidly devoted to a particular set of political ideas.", "c": "意識形態信徒；空談理論家", "s": "Voters grew tired of the ideologue who refused to compromise on any issue, insisting that his party's theories were always correct even when the practical results of his policies were clearly harming the city's economy.", "t": "選民對這位意識形態信徒越來越厭倦，他在任何議題上都拒絕妥協，堅稱自己政黨的理論永遠正確，即使其政策的實際結果明顯正在傷害城市的經濟。", "as": "An inflexible ideologue, the senator remained intransigent during negotiations, and his doctrinaire refusal to consider any pragmatic compromise doomed the bipartisan bill that both parties had spent a year drafting.", "at": "這位參議員是死板的意識形態信徒，談判期間始終毫不妥協，他教條式地拒絕考慮任何務實的折衷方案，導致這項兩黨花了一年擬定的跨黨派法案注定失敗。"}, {"w": "dalliance", "p": "n.", "d": "A brief, casual, or trifling involvement with something.", "c": "（不認真的）涉獵；調情", "s": "The famous novelist's brief dalliance with acting lasted only one summer; after a single forgettable role in a local theater production, he returned to his writing desk and never stepped onto a stage again.", "t": "這位知名小說家對演戲的短暫涉獵只持續了一個夏天；在一部地方劇場作品中演出一個令人過目即忘的角色之後，他便回到書桌前，從此再也沒有站上舞台。", "as": "His youthful dalliance with radical politics proved ephemeral, and by middle age he had become a complacent banker who spoke of his former convictions with wry amusement.", "at": "他年少時對激進政治的短暫涉獵轉瞬即逝，到了中年，他已成為一名自滿的銀行家，談起過去的信念時帶著一抹揶揄的笑意。"}, {"w": "fatuous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Silly and pointless in a smug, unaware way.", "c": "愚蠢的；昏庸自滿的", "s": "During the serious debate on climate policy, one candidate made a fatuous remark about simply buying more air conditioners, and the audience groaned at how foolish and unaware the comment sounded.", "t": "在一場討論氣候政策的嚴肅辯論中，一位候選人說了一句愚蠢的話，表示只要多買幾台冷氣就好，觀眾對這句話聽起來有多麼愚昧又無知而發出不滿的嘆聲。", "as": "The talk-show host's fatuous questions revealed a vacuous understanding of the topic, and the erudite guest struggled to maintain her composure while answering such inane inquiries.", "at": "這位脫口秀主持人愚蠢的問題暴露出他對該主題空洞的理解，那位學識淵博的來賓在回答這種無聊的提問時，努力維持鎮定。"}, {"w": "meander", "p": "v.", "d": "To follow a winding course; to wander aimlessly.", "c": "蜿蜒而流；漫步閒逛", "s": "Unlike rivers in steep mountain valleys, the old river is allowed to meander slowly across the flat plain, curving back and forth in wide loops that sometimes become separated from the main channel and form small lakes.", "t": "與陡峭山谷中的河流不同，這條古老的河流得以在平坦的平原上緩緩蜿蜒，來回彎曲成寬廣的河曲，有時河曲會與主河道分離，形成小湖。", "as": "The professor's lectures tended to meander through tangential anecdotes, and his discursive style left students confused about which ideas were actually germane to the final exam.", "at": "這位教授的講課往往在離題的軼事間漫無目的地游走，他散漫的風格讓學生弄不清楚哪些觀念才真正與期末考有關。"}, {"w": "culpable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Deserving blame for a wrong or a fault.", "c": "應受譴責的；有罪的", "s": "The investigation concluded that the engineering firm was culpable for the bridge collapse, since its inspectors had ignored repeated warnings about rusting steel cables and had signed safety reports without examining the structure.", "t": "調查結論認為，這家工程公司應為橋樑倒塌負責，因為其檢查員忽視了有關鋼纜生鏽的多次警告，並在未檢查結構的情況下就簽署了安全報告。", "as": "Although the manager tried to exonerate himself, the evidence showed he was culpable, and his complicity in the fraud led to his swift dismissal last spring.", "at": "雖然這位經理試圖為自己開脫，但證據顯示他難辭其咎，而他在詐欺案中的共謀行為導致他去年春天迅速遭到解雇。"}, {"w": "sedate", "p": "adj.", "d": "Calm, quiet, and dignified; unhurried.", "c": "沉著的；穩重的", "s": "Compared with the noisy, crowded night markets of Taipei, the small mountain town offered a sedate way of life, where elderly residents strolled slowly through quiet lanes and shops closed politely at sunset.", "t": "與臺北喧鬧擁擠的夜市相比，這座山城提供了一種安穩平靜的生活方式；年長的居民在安靜的巷弄裡緩緩散步，商店也在日落時分從容地打烊。", "as": "Her sedate manner and judicious remarks contrasted sharply with the impetuous outbursts of her rival, and most voters saw her as the more circumspect leader.", "at": "她沉著穩重的舉止與明智審慎的言論，與對手衝動魯莽的爆發形成強烈對比，大多數選民因此認為她是更謹慎周到的領導者。"}, {"w": "impropriety", "p": "n.", "d": "Improper, unsuitable, or dishonest behavior.", "c": "不當行為；不妥", "s": "The judge withdrew from the case to avoid any appearance of impropriety, explaining that her brother had once worked for the defendant's company and that the public must never doubt the court's fairness.", "t": "這位法官退出該案，以避免任何看似不當的嫌疑，她解釋說她的哥哥曾在被告的公司任職，而大眾絕不能懷疑法院的公正性。", "as": "Accused of financial impropriety, the treasurer insisted on his probity, but the auditors found that he had used funds to pay for his nephew's sinecure.", "at": "被指控有財務不當行為的財務長堅稱自己廉潔正直，但查帳人員發現他挪用資金來支付他姪子那份閒差的薪水。"}, {"w": "megalomania", "p": "n.", "d": "An obsessive belief in one's own power or greatness.", "c": "自大狂；誇大妄想", "s": "Historians often point to the emperor's growing megalomania as the cause of his downfall, noting that he renamed cities after himself, ordered enormous statues of his face, and believed no army on earth could ever defeat him.", "t": "歷史學家常指出，這位皇帝日益膨脹的自大狂是他垮台的原因，並提到他以自己的名字為城市命名，下令打造巨大的頭像雕像，還相信世上沒有任何軍隊能打敗他。", "as": "The dictator's megalomania was evident in the grandiose monuments he commissioned across the capital, and his sycophantic advisers only fed his delusions of omnipotence year after year.", "at": "這位獨裁者的自大狂從他下令在首都各處興建的那些浮誇紀念碑中顯而易見，而他那些諂媚的顧問年復一年只會助長他自以為無所不能的妄想。"}, {"w": "vociferous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Expressing opinions loudly and forcefully.", "c": "大聲疾呼的；喧嚷的", "s": "The proposal to close the neighborhood library met vociferous opposition from parents and students, who packed the council meeting, chanted slogans, and delivered passionate speeches demanding that the building remain open.", "t": "關閉社區圖書館的提案遭到家長和學生的大聲反對，他們擠滿了議會會議，高喊口號，並發表慷慨激昂的演說，要求圖書館繼續開放。", "as": "The vociferous protesters denounced the new tax as odious, and their strident chants echoed through the plaza until the governor agreed to rescind the measure.", "at": "這群大聲疾呼的抗議者痛斥新稅可憎，他們刺耳的口號聲在廣場上迴盪，直到州長同意撤銷這項措施為止。"}, {"w": "contrive", "p": "v.", "d": "To plan or bring about something cleverly or deceitfully.", "c": "設法做到；策劃（詭計）", "s": "Trapped on the island without tools, the shipwrecked sailors managed to contrive a simple raft from driftwood, palm leaves, and torn sails, and they used it to reach a passing fishing boat several days later.", "t": "被困在島上又沒有工具，這些船難水手設法用漂流木、棕櫚葉和破帆拼造出一艘簡易木筏，並在幾天後靠著它抵達一艘路過的漁船。", "as": "The cunning courtier contrived an elaborate subterfuge to discredit his rival, spreading calumny about her loyalty until the queen finally banished her from the palace.", "at": "這名狡猾的朝臣策劃了一個精心設計的詭計來打擊他的對手，散播有關她忠誠度的毀謗之詞，直到女王終於將她逐出宮廷。"}, {"w": "nonplus", "p": "v.", "d": "To puzzle someone so much they don't know how to respond.", "c": "使困惑；使不知所措", "s": "The interviewer hoped to nonplus the confident candidate with an unexpected question about her greatest failure, but she answered calmly and honestly, turning a difficult moment into the most impressive part of the interview.", "t": "面試官本想用一個有關她最大失敗的意外問題讓這位自信的應徵者不知所措，但她冷靜而誠實地回答，把一個棘手的時刻轉變成整場面試中最令人印象深刻的部分。", "as": "The cryptic riddle carved on the tomb left the erudite scholars nonplussed, and even the most astute among them could only offer tentative guesses about its hidden meaning.", "at": "刻在墓上的這則隱晦謎語讓學識淵博的學者們不知所措，就連其中最精明的人也只能對它隱藏的含義提出暫時性的猜測。"}, {"w": "imperious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Arrogant and domineering; expecting to be obeyed.", "c": "專橫的；傲慢的", "s": "The imperious director snapped her fingers at assistants, demanded coffee without saying please, and expected the entire film crew to obey her commands instantly, so many talented workers refused to sign up for her next project.", "t": "這位專橫的導演對助理彈手指，要咖啡時連「請」都不說，還期望整個劇組立刻服從她的命令，因此許多有才華的工作人員拒絕參與她的下一個拍攝計畫。", "as": "The imperious aristocrat treated his servants with supercilious disdain, and his peremptory orders, shouted at all hours of the day and night, bred deep animosity throughout the household.", "at": "這位專橫的貴族以傲慢輕蔑的態度對待僕人，他那日夜隨時吼出、不容分說的命令，在整個家中滋生了深深的敵意。"}, {"w": "privation", "p": "n.", "d": "A lack of basic necessities such as food and warmth.", "c": "貧困；匱乏", "s": "Letters from soldiers during the long winter siege describe extreme privation, as troops survived on tiny portions of bread, burned furniture for warmth, and went for weeks without clean water or proper medical care.", "t": "在漫長的冬季圍城期間，士兵寄出的信件描述了極度的匱乏：部隊靠著少得可憐的麵包維生，焚燒家具取暖，並且連續數週沒有乾淨的水，也沒有適當的醫療照護。", "as": "The explorers endured months of privation in the Arctic, yet their journals reveal a remarkable equanimity and an indefatigable hope that rescue would eventually arrive.", "at": "這些探險家在北極忍受了數月的匱乏，然而他們的日誌卻展現出非凡的鎮定，以及一份認為救援終將到來的不屈不撓的希望。"}, {"w": "suffuse", "p": "v.", "d": "To spread over or through something gradually.", "c": "充滿；（光、色彩）佈滿", "s": "As the sun slowly rose over the desert, a warm golden light began to suffuse the sky, turning the dark sand dunes orange and pink while the morning air was still cool and silent.", "t": "當太陽緩緩升起於沙漠之上，溫暖的金色光芒開始佈滿天空，將黝黑的沙丘染成橙色與粉紅色，而清晨的空氣依然涼爽寂靜。", "as": "The poet's final collection is suffused with a poignant melancholy, and its elegiac verses lament the transient beauty of the seasons and of human life.", "at": "這位詩人的最後一部詩集充滿了令人心酸的憂鬱，其哀婉的詩句悲嘆四季與人生短暫易逝的美。"}, {"w": "disconsolate", "p": "adj.", "d": "Very unhappy and unable to be comforted.", "c": "鬱鬱寡歡的；無法慰藉的", "s": "After her team lost the championship on a last-second goal, the disconsolate captain sat alone on the bench for nearly an hour, refusing to speak with reporters and ignoring every teammate who tried to comfort her.", "t": "在球隊於最後一秒被射門得分而痛失冠軍之後，這位悲痛難以慰藉的隊長獨自坐在板凳上將近一小時，拒絕接受記者採訪，也不理會任何試圖安慰她的隊友。", "as": "Disconsolate after the defeat, the candidate sank into a morose silence, and not even the effusive praise of his loyal supporters could assuage his grief.", "at": "落選後鬱鬱寡歡的候選人陷入陰鬱的沉默，即使忠實支持者熱情洋溢的讚美也無法減輕他的悲傷。"}, {"w": "conundrum", "p": "n.", "d": "A confusing and difficult problem or question.", "c": "難題；謎團", "s": "Engineers faced a difficult conundrum when designing the new subway line: digging deeper would protect historic buildings above ground, but it would also double the cost and delay the project by at least five years.", "t": "工程師在設計新地鐵線時面臨一個棘手的難題：挖得更深可以保護地面上的歷史建築，但也會使成本加倍，並讓工程延誤至少五年。", "as": "The ethical conundrum confronting the hospital's doctors seemed intractable, and their protracted deliberations revealed deep ambivalence about withholding the experimental treatment from a dying young patient.", "at": "這家醫院的醫師們面臨的倫理難題似乎難以解決，他們冗長的討論顯露出對於是否停止為一位垂危年輕病患提供實驗性療法的深刻矛盾心理。"}, {"w": "dotage", "p": "n.", "d": "The period of old age when the mind weakens.", "c": "老年昏聵；年老糊塗", "s": "In Shakespeare's famous tragedy, King Lear divides his kingdom among his daughters in his dotage, a foolish decision made by a confused old man that leads to betrayal, madness, and the ruin of his entire family.", "t": "在莎士比亞著名的悲劇中，李爾王在年老昏聵之時將王國分給女兒們，這個糊塗老人所做的愚蠢決定導致了背叛、瘋狂，以及整個家族的毀滅。", "as": "In his dotage, the once trenchant critic became garrulous and sentimental, and his senescent ramblings bore little resemblance to the incisive reviews of his youth.", "at": "這位曾經犀利的評論家到了年老昏聵之時變得喋喋不休又多愁善感，他衰老的絮叨與年輕時那些一針見血的評論幾乎毫無相似之處。"}]}, {"unit": 32, "level": 7, "cards": [{"w": "vacuous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lacking thought, intelligence, or meaningful content.", "c": "空洞的；缺乏思想的", "s": "Critics dismissed the candidate's speech as vacuous, pointing out that despite forty minutes of applause lines and slogans, he never offered a single concrete proposal on health care, education, or the rising cost of housing.", "t": "評論家批評這位候選人的演說空洞無物，指出儘管他講了四十分鐘博取掌聲的台詞與口號，卻從未針對醫療、教育或日益高漲的房價提出任何具體方案。", "as": "The pundit's vacuous commentary, padded with hackneyed phrases about 'the will of the people,' offered viewers nothing but platitudes and left the complex debate over tax reform entirely unexamined.", "at": "這位名嘴空洞的評論充斥著「人民的意志」之類的陳腔濫調，帶給觀眾的只有老生常談，對稅制改革這項複雜的爭議完全沒有深入探討。"}, {"w": "intemperate", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lacking self-control; excessive, especially in drinking or speech.", "c": "無節制的；過度的", "s": "The senator later apologized for his intemperate remarks at the hearing, admitting that he had allowed his anger to override his judgment when he shouted insults at the witnesses and accused them of lying without evidence.", "t": "這位參議員事後為他在聽證會上失控的言論道歉，承認自己當時大聲辱罵證人、在毫無證據的情況下指控他們說謊，是讓怒氣凌駕了判斷力。", "as": "Biographers note that the poet's intemperate habits, from nightly drinking to reckless spending, hastened his decline, yet his letters remain lucid and poignant until the very end.", "at": "傳記作家指出，這位詩人毫無節制的習慣——從夜夜飲酒到揮霍無度——加速了他的衰敗，然而他的書信直到生命最後一刻依然清晰明澈、感人至深。"}, {"w": "stymie", "p": "v.", "d": "To prevent or hinder the progress of something.", "c": "阻礙；妨礙", "s": "A shortage of funding and laboratory equipment continued to stymie the research team's efforts, delaying their clinical trial by nearly two years and forcing several graduate students to abandon the project for better-supported labs.", "t": "經費與實驗設備的短缺持續阻礙研究團隊的努力，使他們的臨床試驗延宕將近兩年，也迫使數名研究生放棄這項計畫，轉往資源較充足的實驗室。", "as": "Bureaucratic red tape stymied the reform for years, and the minister's attempts to placate angry farmers with vague promises only deepened their animosity toward the government.", "at": "繁瑣的官僚程序使這項改革停滯多年，而部長試圖用含糊的承諾安撫憤怒農民的做法，只加深了他們對政府的敵意。"}, {"w": "ambrosia", "p": "n.", "d": "Something extremely delicious; in myth, the food of the gods.", "c": "眾神的食物；美味佳餚", "s": "In Greek mythology, the Olympian gods dined on ambrosia and nectar, a heavenly food believed to grant immortality, and any mortal who tasted it without permission risked the gods' terrible anger.", "t": "在希臘神話中，奧林帕斯諸神以神饌與神酒為食，這種天界的食物據信能賜予永生，任何未經允許就品嘗它的凡人，都可能招致眾神的可怕怒火。", "as": "To the famished explorers, a simple bowl of rice tasted like ambrosia, for after weeks of privation in the jungle, even the most prosaic meal seemed miraculous.", "at": "對飢腸轆轆的探險家來說，一碗簡單的白飯嚐起來宛如神仙佳餚，因為在叢林中困乏了數週之後，即使是最平凡的一餐也顯得不可思議。"}, {"w": "vivify", "p": "v.", "d": "To give life or energy to; to make lively.", "c": "使有生氣；使活躍", "s": "The new director hoped to vivify the sleepy local museum by adding interactive exhibits, evening concerts, and hands-on workshops that would draw young families and students back through its long-neglected doors.", "t": "新任館長希望藉由增設互動展覽、夜間音樂會與動手做工作坊，讓這間沉寂的地方博物館重新活絡起來，吸引年輕家庭與學生再次走進那扇久被冷落的大門。", "as": "The novelist vivifies her otherwise mundane suburban setting with florid descriptions of gardens and storms, turning ordinary afternoons into vivid, almost mythic scenes of quiet drama.", "at": "這位小說家以華麗的筆觸描寫花園與暴風雨，為原本平淡無奇的郊區場景注入生命，將尋常的午後化為生動、近乎神話般的靜謐戲劇場面。"}, {"w": "purloin", "p": "v.", "d": "To steal something, often in a sneaky or dishonest way.", "c": "偷竊；竊取", "s": "Investigators discovered that a trusted archivist had managed to purloin dozens of rare letters from the library's collection over several years, quietly smuggling them out in his briefcase and selling them to private collectors overseas.", "t": "調查人員發現，一名深受信任的檔案管理員多年來從圖書館館藏中竊取了數十封珍貴信件，將它們悄悄藏在公事包中帶出，再賣給海外的私人收藏家。", "as": "The clandestine operation to purloin the blueprints was a stratagem worthy of a spy novel, relying on forged badges and a guard too gullible to question them.", "at": "竊取藍圖的秘密行動是一個足以媲美間諜小說的計謀，靠的是偽造的識別證，以及一名容易受騙、根本不加盤問的警衛。"}, {"w": "bulwark", "p": "n.", "d": "A strong defense or protection against danger.", "c": "堡壘；防禦屏障", "s": "Many historians argue that an independent judiciary serves as a vital bulwark against tyranny, protecting citizens' rights even when popular leaders attempt to expand their power beyond the limits set by the constitution.", "t": "許多歷史學家認為，獨立的司法體系是對抗暴政的重要屏障，即使深受歡迎的領袖試圖將權力擴張到憲法限制之外，它仍能保護公民的權利。", "as": "A free press has long been a bulwark of democracy, yet the despotic regime denounced reporters as traitors and tried to indoctrinate schoolchildren with its own version of history.", "at": "新聞自由長久以來一直是民主的堡壘，然而這個專制政權卻把記者斥為叛徒，並試圖向學童灌輸它所編造的歷史版本。"}, {"w": "magisterial", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having or showing great authority; commanding and masterly.", "c": "權威的；威嚴的", "s": "Her magisterial three-volume history of the Ming dynasty, praised for its exhaustive research and confident analysis, quickly became the standard reference that every serious scholar of Chinese history was expected to consult.", "t": "她那部三卷本的明朝史權威鉅著，因研究詳盡、分析精闢而備受讚譽，很快便成為每一位認真研究中國歷史的學者必定參考的標準典籍。", "as": "With magisterial calm, the chief justice dismissed the lawyer's specious arguments, noting that his convoluted reasoning ignored decades of settled precedent and the plain text of the law.", "at": "首席大法官以威嚴而沉著的態度駁回了那名律師似是而非的論點，指出他迂迴曲折的推理忽略了數十年來的既定判例以及法律的明文規定。"}, {"w": "talisman", "p": "n.", "d": "An object believed to bring good luck or protection.", "c": "護身符；法寶", "s": "Before every match, the tennis champion touched a worn silver coin her grandmother had given her, treating it as a talisman that she believed would protect her from injury and bring her good fortune on the court.", "t": "每場比賽前，這位網球冠軍都會摸一摸祖母送給她的那枚磨損的銀幣，把它當作護身符，相信它能保佑她免受傷害，並在球場上帶來好運。", "as": "For the superstitious sailors, the carved whale tooth was a talisman against storms, and even the most stoic captain would not have dared to deride their faith in it.", "at": "對迷信的水手而言，那顆雕刻過的鯨齒是抵禦暴風雨的護身符，即使是最堅忍淡定的船長，也不敢嘲笑他們對它的信仰。"}, {"w": "stupefy", "p": "v.", "d": "To astonish greatly or make unable to think clearly.", "c": "使目瞪口呆；使昏沉", "s": "The sheer scale of the discovery seemed to stupefy the archaeologists, who stood in stunned silence for several minutes after uncovering a buried city whose existence had been dismissed for centuries as mere legend.", "t": "這項發現的驚人規模似乎讓考古學家們目瞪口呆；他們挖掘出一座數百年來一直被當作傳說而不予採信的地下古城後，愣在原地默然無語了好幾分鐘。", "as": "The magician's legerdemain stupefied the audience, and even the most jaded critics, who had seen every trick imaginable, sat speechless as the elephant vanished into thin air.", "at": "魔術師的戲法令觀眾目瞪口呆，就連看遍各種把戲、早已麻木無感的評論家，也在大象憑空消失時瞠目結舌、說不出話來。"}, {"w": "rancorous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Full of bitter, long-lasting resentment or hatred.", "c": "懷恨的；充滿敵意的", "s": "The rancorous dispute between the two neighboring villages over water rights had lasted for generations, and even after a fair settlement was reached, many elders refused to forgive the insults of the past.", "t": "兩個相鄰村莊之間為了水權而起的積怨糾紛已延續了好幾代，即使雙方達成了公平的和解，許多長者仍不肯原諒過去所受的羞辱。", "as": "After a rancorous campaign filled with invective and personal attacks, the newly elected mayor tried to mollify her opponents by inviting them to join a bipartisan committee.", "at": "在一場充滿謾罵與人身攻擊、火藥味十足的選戰之後，新當選的市長試圖邀請對手加入跨黨派委員會，以緩和他們的敵意。"}, {"w": "ennui", "p": "n.", "d": "A feeling of weariness and dissatisfaction caused by boredom.", "c": "倦怠；無聊", "s": "Trapped indoors during the long rainy season with no books, games, or visitors, the young poet sank into a deep ennui, complaining in his diary that each gray afternoon felt identical to the last.", "t": "漫長的雨季裡，這位年輕詩人困在屋內，沒有書、沒有遊戲，也沒有訪客，於是陷入深深的倦怠之中，在日記裡抱怨每個灰濛濛的午後都和前一天一模一樣。", "as": "The aristocrats in the novel suffer from a languid ennui; idle and listless, they drift from one monotonous party to another, longing for any diversion at all.", "at": "小說中的貴族飽受慵懶倦怠之苦；他們無所事事、無精打采，從一場單調乏味的宴會晃到另一場，渴望任何一點消遣。"}, {"w": "censorious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Severely critical of others; quick to find fault.", "c": "吹毛求疵的；苛責的", "s": "Although the young painter's work was celebrated by the public, a few censorious critics attacked every brushstroke, condemning his bright colors as vulgar and accusing him of ignoring the rules of classical composition.", "t": "雖然這位年輕畫家的作品廣受大眾喜愛，少數愛挑剔的評論家卻抨擊他的每一筆，譴責他鮮豔的用色粗俗，並指責他無視古典構圖的規則。", "as": "The censorious headmaster seemed to castigate students for the most venial offenses, treating a missing button as though it were an act of grave turpitude.", "at": "那位愛挑剔的校長似乎連最微不足道的過失都要嚴厲斥責學生，把少一顆鈕扣看得像是嚴重的敗德行為。"}, {"w": "marginalize", "p": "v.", "d": "To treat a person or group as unimportant or powerless.", "c": "使邊緣化；排斥", "s": "Historians have shown how official records tended to marginalize women scientists of the nineteenth century, crediting their discoveries to male colleagues and leaving their names out of textbooks for more than a hundred years.", "t": "歷史學家已經指出，官方紀錄往往將十九世紀的女性科學家邊緣化，把她們的發現歸功於男性同事，並使她們的名字在教科書中缺席了一百多年。", "as": "Critics argue that the new zoning law will further marginalize indigent residents, pushing them to the peripheral districts of the city where jobs and services are scarce.", "at": "批評者認為，新的分區法規將使貧困居民更加邊緣化，把他們推向工作與服務都十分匱乏的城市外圍地區。"}, {"w": "reprove", "p": "v.", "d": "To scold or correct someone, usually gently.", "c": "責備；指責", "s": "When the student interrupted his classmate for the third time, the teacher paused to reprove him quietly, reminding him that respectful discussion meant allowing everyone a chance to finish speaking.", "t": "當那名學生第三次打斷同學發言時，老師停下來輕聲責備他，提醒他尊重的討論意味著讓每個人都有機會把話說完。", "as": "The mentor gently reproved the impetuous young reporter for publishing an unverified allegation, urging her to corroborate every claim before going to print in the future.", "at": "這位導師溫和地責備那名衝動的年輕記者刊登了未經查證的指控，並勸她日後在付印前務必證實每一項說法。"}, {"w": "relegate", "p": "v.", "d": "To move someone or something to a lower position or rank.", "c": "降級；貶至次要地位", "s": "After the museum acquired several famous paintings, curators decided to relegate the lesser-known works to a basement storage room, where they remained unseen by visitors and scholars for nearly two decades.", "t": "博物館購入幾幅名畫後，策展人決定把那些較不知名的作品移到地下室的儲藏室，它們就這樣在那裡近二十年都不曾被參觀者與學者看見。", "as": "Once hailed as a seminal thinker, the philosopher was relegated to obscurity after his theories were deemed anachronistic by an impatient new generation of scholars.", "at": "這位哲學家曾被譽為開創性的思想家，但在不耐煩的新一代學者認為他的理論已經過時之後，他便被打入冷宮、默默無聞。"}, {"w": "behemoth", "p": "n.", "d": "Something enormous and powerful, such as a huge organization.", "c": "龐然大物；巨頭", "s": "The small family bookstore struggled to survive after an online retail behemoth began selling the same titles at steep discounts, delivering them to customers' doors within a day and capturing most of the local market.", "t": "自從一家網路零售巨頭開始以大幅折扣販售相同書籍，並在一天內送貨到府、奪走大部分本地市場之後，這家小小的家庭書店便苦苦掙扎、難以為繼。", "as": "The tech behemoth seemed impervious to criticism, yet a determined coalition of dissident engineers eventually forced it to redress years of careless and secretive data practices.", "at": "這家科技巨頭似乎對批評毫不在乎，然而一群堅定的異議工程師所組成的聯盟，最終迫使它糾正多年來草率又隱密的資料處理方式。"}, {"w": "incendiary", "p": "adj.", "d": "Tending to inflame anger or conflict; also, causing fires.", "c": "煽動性的；引起火災的", "s": "The radio host was suspended after broadcasting incendiary comments that blamed a minority group for the city's economic problems, remarks that police said had encouraged several violent protests in the following days.", "t": "這名電台主持人因播出煽動性言論而遭停職；他把城市的經濟問題歸咎於某個少數族群，警方表示，這番話在隨後幾天助長了數起暴力抗議。", "as": "The demagogue's incendiary rhetoric, a vitriolic mix of xenophobia and hyperbole, alarmed historians who saw in it echoes of the darkest chapters of the last century.", "at": "這名煽動家那番煽風點火的言論，夾雜著惡毒的仇外情緒與誇大其詞，令歷史學家憂心忡忡，因為他們從中聽見了上個世紀最黑暗篇章的回響。"}, {"w": "stalwart", "p": "adj.", "d": "Loyal, reliable, and firmly committed; also, strong and sturdy.", "c": "忠實的；堅定的", "s": "For more than forty years, she remained a stalwart supporter of the public library, volunteering every weekend, donating thousands of books, and defending its budget at city council meetings whenever officials proposed cuts.", "t": "四十多年來，她一直是公共圖書館忠實的支持者，每個週末都去當志工，捐贈了數千本書，並且每當官員提議刪減預算時，就在市議會上為圖書館的經費據理力爭。", "as": "Even after a bitter schism divided the party, a few stalwart members remained resolute, refusing to abandon the principles that had once united them in common cause.", "at": "即使在一場激烈的分裂使黨內四分五裂之後，少數忠貞的黨員仍堅定不移，拒絕放棄曾經讓他們團結一心的理念。"}, {"w": "enmity", "p": "n.", "d": "Deep, lasting hostility or hatred between people or groups.", "c": "敵意；仇恨", "s": "The enmity between the two rival scientists became legendary; for decades they refused to attend the same conferences, publicly ridiculed each other's theories, and even competed to name the same newly discovered dinosaur species.", "t": "這兩位敵對科學家之間的仇恨成了傳奇：數十年來，他們拒絕出席同一場研討會，公開嘲諷彼此的理論，甚至競相為同一種新發現的恐龍命名。", "as": "Centuries of enmity between the two clans finally abated when their leaders agreed to a rapprochement, sealing the peace with a marriage and a shared feast.", "at": "兩個氏族之間長達數百年的仇恨，在雙方領袖同意和解之後終於平息，他們以一場聯姻和一頓共享的盛宴為和平定下盟約。"}]}, {"unit": 33, "level": 7, "cards": [{"w": "malign", "p": "v.", "d": "To say harmful, untrue things about someone; to slander.", "c": "誹謗；中傷", "s": "The campaign was accused of hiring anonymous online accounts to malign the rival candidate, spreading false rumors that she had falsified her tax records and mistreated the staff who worked in her office.", "t": "該競選陣營被指控僱用匿名網路帳號中傷對手候選人，散布她偽造報稅紀錄、虐待辦公室員工的不實謠言。", "as": "Though rivals tried to malign the scientist with spurious charges of fraud, an independent panel exonerated her, confirming that her data were sound and her methods impeccable.", "at": "儘管對手試圖以毫無根據的造假指控誹謗這位科學家，一個獨立調查小組仍還她清白，證實她的數據可靠，研究方法也無懈可擊。"}, {"w": "libation", "p": "n.", "d": "A drink poured as an offering to a god; humorously, any drink.", "c": "奠酒；飲料", "s": "Before each battle, ancient Greek soldiers poured a libation of wine onto the ground as an offering to the gods, hoping that the ritual would win divine favor and protect them in the fighting ahead.", "t": "古希臘士兵在每場戰役之前，都會將一杯酒灑在地上作為獻給眾神的奠酒，希望這項儀式能贏得神明的眷顧，保佑他們在接下來的戰鬥中平安。", "as": "At the convivial reunion, the alumni raised their libations in honor of their old professor, an erudite and avuncular man who had taught at the college for forty years.", "at": "在歡樂的同學會上，校友們舉杯向他們的老教授致敬；這位學識淵博、慈祥和藹的長者已在這所學院任教四十年。"}, {"w": "gesticulate", "p": "v.", "d": "To make lively gestures, especially while speaking.", "c": "做手勢；比手畫腳", "s": "Unable to speak the local language, the lost tourist began to gesticulate wildly at the train schedule, pointing at the map, tapping his watch, and waving his arms until a station worker finally understood his question.", "t": "迷路的觀光客不會說當地語言，於是開始對著火車時刻表拚命比手畫腳，指著地圖、敲著手錶、揮舞雙臂，直到一名車站員工終於明白他的問題。", "as": "The histrionic actor gesticulated so vehemently during his soliloquy that critics found the performance bombastic, more a display of vanity than a sincere portrayal of grief.", "at": "這位愛誇張的演員在獨白時手勢比得過於激烈，評論家認為這場表演浮誇做作，與其說是真誠地詮釋悲傷，不如說是在展現自己的虛榮。"}, {"w": "circumlocution", "p": "n.", "d": "The use of many words where fewer would do; evasive talk.", "c": "迂迴說法；拐彎抹角", "s": "Instead of admitting that the company had lost money, the spokesman relied on circumlocution, speaking for ten minutes about 'negative growth trends' and 'challenging revenue environments' without ever stating the simple fact.", "t": "這名發言人沒有承認公司虧損，而是拐彎抹角地講了十分鐘的「負成長趨勢」和「充滿挑戰的營收環境」，卻始終不肯說出這個簡單的事實。", "as": "The diplomat's circumlocution was deliberate, for his ambiguous phrases allowed both sides to construe the agreement as a victory without anyone having to make a concession.", "at": "這位外交官的迂迴措辭是刻意為之，因為他模稜兩可的用語讓雙方都能把協議解讀為自己的勝利，而且沒有人需要讓步。"}, {"w": "besmirch", "p": "v.", "d": "To damage someone's reputation; literally, to make dirty.", "c": "玷污；詆毀（名譽）", "s": "The athlete sued the tabloid for printing false stories that sought to besmirch her reputation, arguing that its invented claims about drug use had cost her several sponsorships and the trust of her fans.", "t": "這名運動員控告那家八卦小報刊登不實報導，企圖玷污她的名聲；她主張該報捏造的用藥指控讓她失去了幾份贊助合約與球迷的信任。", "as": "The scandal besmirched the senator's once-unblemished name, and no amount of public contrition could ever restore the probity that voters had long associated with him.", "at": "這起醜聞玷污了這位參議員原本清白無瑕的名聲，無論他如何公開懺悔，都再也無法挽回選民長久以來對他正直廉潔的印象。"}, {"w": "immutable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Unchanging over time; unable to be changed.", "c": "不可改變的；永恆不變的", "s": "Early astronomers believed that the stars were immutable, fixed forever in their positions, until careful observations of a brilliant new star in 1572 suggested that even the heavens could change.", "t": "早期的天文學家相信星辰是永恆不變的，永遠固定在原本的位置上，直到一五七二年對一顆明亮新星的仔細觀測顯示，就連天體也可能改變。", "as": "The dogmatic professor treated his theories as immutable truths, and he would castigate any student who dared to question them, however cogent or judicious her objections.", "at": "那位武斷的教授把自己的理論視為不可動搖的真理，任何膽敢質疑的學生都會遭到他嚴厲斥責，無論她的反對意見多麼有說服力或明智審慎。"}, {"w": "declaim", "p": "v.", "d": "To speak dramatically and forcefully, as if giving a formal speech.", "c": "慷慨陳詞；朗誦", "s": "Standing on a wooden crate in the town square, the activist began to declaim against the new tax law, his loud, theatrical voice carrying across the market as a crowd gradually gathered to listen.", "t": "這名社運人士站在鎮上廣場的木箱上，開始慷慨激昂地抨擊新稅法，他宏亮而富戲劇性的聲音傳遍整個市集，人群也漸漸聚攏過來聆聽。", "as": "In ancient Rome, students learned to declaim on moral questions, and many teachers prized a sonorous voice and a grandiloquent style far above the simple clarity of an argument.", "at": "在古羅馬，學生學習就道德議題慷慨陳詞，許多老師重視宏亮的嗓音與華麗浮誇的文風，遠勝於論點本身的簡明清晰。"}, {"w": "thrall", "p": "n.", "d": "A state of being controlled or enslaved by someone or something.", "c": "束縛；奴役", "s": "For centuries, the peasants of the region lived in thrall to powerful landlords, unable to leave their villages, own land, or marry without permission from the masters who controlled every part of their lives.", "t": "數百年來，該地區的農民一直受制於有權勢的地主，未經掌控他們生活一切的主人允許，他們不能離開村莊、擁有土地，甚至不能結婚。", "as": "Held in thrall by the charismatic but nefarious cult leader, his devotees surrendered their savings and severed ties with relatives who tried to warn them.", "at": "被那位極具魅力卻邪惡的教主所控制，他的信徒交出了積蓄，並與試圖警告他們的親人斷絕往來。"}, {"w": "sate", "p": "v.", "d": "To satisfy an appetite or desire fully.", "c": "使滿足；使飽足", "s": "After hiking for eight hours without food, the climbers finally reached the mountain hut, where a huge pot of rice and vegetable stew was enough to sate even the hungriest members of the group.", "t": "登山客在沒有進食的情況下健行了八個小時，終於抵達山屋，那裡的一大鍋米飯和蔬菜燉菜足以讓團隊中最餓的人也吃得心滿意足。", "as": "No amount of praise could sate the actor's insatiable vanity; he craved constant adulation from fans and sulked for days whenever a review was less than effusive.", "at": "再多的讚美也滿足不了這位演員貪得無厭的虛榮心；他渴望影迷不斷的吹捧，只要劇評不夠熱烈，他就會悶悶不樂好幾天。"}, {"w": "gadfly", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who annoys others by persistent, provocative criticism.", "c": "愛找碴批評的人；牛虻", "s": "Socrates famously described himself as a gadfly sent to sting the city of Athens into action, constantly questioning its leaders and provoking citizens to examine their own beliefs, even though it made him many enemies.", "t": "蘇格拉底曾有名地自比為一隻被派來叮咬雅典城、促其奮起的牛虻，他不斷質問城邦的領袖，激發公民檢視自己的信念，即使這為他招來許多敵人。", "as": "A tireless gadfly, the journalist would importune officials with awkward questions, and her trenchant columns exposed the duplicity of politicians who preferred to avoid scrutiny.", "at": "這位記者是個不知疲倦的批評者，總是糾纏官員提出尷尬的問題，她犀利的專欄揭穿了那些寧願逃避監督的政客的兩面手法。"}, {"w": "hackneyed", "p": "adj.", "d": "Used so often that it has become dull and unoriginal.", "c": "陳腐的；老套的", "s": "The writing instructor urged students to avoid hackneyed phrases such as 'at the end of the day' and 'think outside the box,' explaining that overused expressions make even good ideas sound tired and unoriginal.", "t": "寫作老師勸學生避免使用像「說到底」和「跳脫框架思考」這類陳腔濫調，並解釋過度使用的說法會讓即使是好點子也顯得陳舊、缺乏原創性。", "as": "The film's hackneyed plot, a predictable tale of a callow hero who saves the world, was redeemed only by the director's droll humor and inventive visual effects.", "at": "這部電影老套的情節——一個涉世未深的英雄拯救世界的可預測故事——只靠導演冷面詼諧的幽默與富創意的視覺效果才得以挽救。"}, {"w": "iniquity", "p": "n.", "d": "Great injustice or immoral behavior; wickedness.", "c": "邪惡；極不公正", "s": "In his famous speeches, the abolitionist Frederick Douglass condemned the iniquity of slavery, describing in powerful detail the cruelty and injustice suffered by millions of people who were denied their basic freedom.", "t": "廢奴主義者弗雷德里克．道格拉斯在其著名演說中譴責奴隸制度的罪惡，以有力而詳盡的描述，道出數百萬被剝奪基本自由的人所承受的殘酷與不公。", "as": "The reformer's diatribe against the iniquity of child labor was so cogent that even callous factory owners could not refute her evidence of children toiling in squalid conditions.", "at": "這位改革者痛斥童工制度罪惡的激烈演說極具說服力，就連冷酷無情的工廠老闆也無法反駁她所提出的證據：孩童在骯髒惡劣的環境中辛苦勞動。"}, {"w": "whimsical", "p": "adj.", "d": "Playfully unusual or fanciful, often in an amusing way.", "c": "異想天開的；古怪有趣的", "s": "Children loved the author's whimsical picture books, in which teapots held tea parties, clouds went shopping, and a shy giraffe learned to ride a bicycle through a city made entirely of candy.", "t": "孩子們很喜歡這位作家充滿奇想的繪本：書中的茶壺舉辦茶會、雲朵去逛街，還有一隻害羞的長頸鹿學會騎著腳踏車穿越一座完全用糖果打造的城市。", "as": "The architect's whimsical designs, with their askew windows and variegated tiles, delighted tourists from around the world but nettled conservative neighbors who much preferred plain brick facades.", "at": "這位建築師的設計充滿奇想，有歪斜的窗戶與五彩斑斕的磁磚，令來自世界各地的觀光客驚喜不已，卻惹惱了偏好樸素紅磚外牆的保守鄰居。"}, {"w": "ensconce", "p": "v.", "d": "To settle someone or oneself firmly in a safe, comfortable place.", "c": "安頓；使安坐", "s": "On rainy afternoons, my grandmother liked to ensconce herself in the old armchair beside the window, wrapped in a wool blanket with a cup of tea and a mystery novel she had read many times before.", "t": "在下雨的午後，我祖母喜歡舒舒服服地窩在窗邊那張舊扶手椅上，裹著羊毛毯，手捧一杯茶，讀著一本她早已讀過許多遍的推理小說。", "as": "Once ensconced in his commodious office, the new director grew aloof, rarely leaving it to consult the hardworking staff whose ideas he had once so eagerly solicited.", "at": "新任主管一安坐在他寬敞的辦公室裡，就變得冷漠疏離，很少走出辦公室去徵詢那些勤奮員工的意見，而他過去曾如此熱切地向他們請益。"}, {"w": "plutocrat", "p": "n.", "d": "A person whose power comes from great wealth.", "c": "富豪統治者；財閥", "s": "Critics warned that the election had been effectively bought by a single plutocrat, a billionaire whose enormous campaign donations gave him more influence over national policy than millions of ordinary voters combined.", "t": "批評者警告，這場選舉實際上已被一名財閥收買；這位億萬富翁巨額的政治獻金，使他對國家政策的影響力超過數百萬名一般選民的總和。", "as": "In the novel, a ruthless plutocrat uses nepotism and machination to control the town, filling every important post with relatives eager to serve his rapacious ambitions.", "at": "在這部小說中，一名冷酷無情的財閥利用任人唯親與陰謀詭計掌控整座小鎮，把每一個重要職位都安插給急於為他貪婪野心效力的親戚。"}, {"w": "beatific", "p": "adj.", "d": "Showing great joy and peace; blissful.", "c": "洋溢幸福的；安詳喜悅的", "s": "In the famous Renaissance painting, the saint gazes upward with a beatific expression, her face glowing with a calm, heavenly happiness that seems to lift her far above the suffering around her.", "t": "在這幅著名的文藝復興畫作中，聖女帶著安詳喜悅的神情仰望天空，她的臉龐洋溢著平靜而神聖的幸福，彷彿使她超然於周遭的苦難之上。", "as": "After years of tribulation, the refugee's beatific smile upon reaching safety was an ineffable sight, too profound for any reporter to capture in mere words.", "at": "經歷多年苦難之後，這名難民抵達安全之地時臉上那抹幸福安詳的微笑，是一幅難以言喻的景象，深刻得讓任何記者都無法單憑文字捕捉。"}, {"w": "unfettered", "p": "adj.", "d": "Free from restrictions or controls.", "c": "不受束縛的；自由的", "s": "The new research institute gave its scientists unfettered access to its laboratories and funding, allowing them to pursue risky ideas without having to justify every experiment to a committee of cautious administrators.", "t": "這間新研究機構讓旗下科學家不受限制地使用實驗室與經費，使他們能追求高風險的構想，而不必向一群謹慎保守的行政人員交代每一項實驗。", "as": "Some economists argue that unfettered markets inevitably engender inequality, while others insist that excessive regulation would stymie the very innovation that lifts people out of poverty.", "at": "有些經濟學家認為，不受管制的市場必然會導致不平等，另一些人則堅持，過度的管制會阻礙那些讓人們擺脫貧窮的創新。"}, {"w": "estrange", "p": "v.", "d": "To cause someone to become unfriendly or distant from another.", "c": "使疏遠；使失和", "s": "A bitter argument over their late father's house threatened to estrange the two brothers permanently, and for several years they spoke only through lawyers and refused to attend the same family events.", "t": "一場為了亡父房產而起的激烈爭執，可能讓這對兄弟從此反目成仇；有好幾年，他們只透過律師溝通，並且拒絕出席同一場家族聚會。", "as": "Her intransigent refusal to compromise estranged her from longtime allies, and the long, obdurate feud eventually left her ostracized within the very movement she had founded.", "at": "她頑固地拒絕妥協，使她與多年的盟友疏遠，而這場長久僵持不下的爭執，最終讓她在自己一手創立的運動中遭到排擠。"}, {"w": "sibilant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Making or containing a hissing sound, like 's' or 'sh'.", "c": "發嘶嘶聲的；噝音的", "s": "In the poem, the writer repeats the letter 's' in nearly every line, creating a soft, sibilant sound that imitates the hiss of waves sliding back over the sand at night.", "t": "在這首詩中，作者幾乎每一行都重複使用發嘶擦音的字母，營造出一種輕柔的嘶嘶聲，模仿夜晚海浪滑回沙灘時的沙沙聲響。", "as": "The sibilant whispers of the conspirators filled the dim hall, a susurrus of secrets that made the anxious young prince suspect a cabal was forming against him.", "at": "密謀者嘶嘶的低語聲充斥著昏暗的大廳，那竊竊私語般的秘密耳語讓焦慮的年輕王子懷疑有一個陰謀集團正在策劃對付他。"}, {"w": "pundit", "p": "n.", "d": "An expert who frequently gives opinions in the media.", "c": "專家；名嘴", "s": "Although nearly every political pundit on television had confidently predicted a landslide victory, the challenger won by only a few hundred votes, forcing commentators to explain why their forecasts had been so wrong.", "t": "雖然幾乎每一位電視上的政治評論家都信心滿滿地預測會是壓倒性勝利，挑戰者卻只以幾百票之差勝出，迫使評論員解釋為什麼他們的預測錯得如此離譜。", "as": "The cable pundit was notorious for his glib pronouncements, and he would pontificate on everything from foreign policy to nutrition without any expertise in either.", "at": "這位有線電視名嘴以油腔滑調的發言惡名昭彰，從外交政策到營養學，他都能自以為是地高談闊論，卻對兩者都毫無專業可言。"}]}, {"unit": 34, "level": 7, "cards": [{"w": "redolent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Strongly suggestive or reminiscent of something; fragrant.", "c": "令人聯想的；芬芳的", "s": "The old harbor town, with its narrow stone lanes and faded shop signs, was redolent of the nineteenth century, so much so that visitors often felt as though they had stepped into a historical novel.", "t": "這座古老的港口小鎮有著狹窄的石板巷弄與褪色的店招，處處令人聯想到十九世紀，以至於遊客常覺得自己彷彿走進了一部歷史小說。", "as": "The kitchen was redolent of cinnamon and roasted chestnuts, a poignant evocation of the winters the author had spent at her grandmother's farmhouse as a child.", "at": "廚房裡瀰漫著肉桂與烤栗子的香氣，深刻動人地喚起作者童年時在祖母農舍度過的那些冬天。"}, {"w": "demagogue", "p": "n.", "d": "A leader who gains power by exploiting people's emotions and prejudices.", "c": "煽動家；蠱惑民心的政客", "s": "Historians warn that a demagogue often rises during times of economic hardship, winning popular support by blaming scapegoats, stirring up fear, and making grand promises that he has no realistic plan to keep.", "t": "歷史學家警告，煽動家往往在經濟困頓時期崛起，藉由歸咎代罪羔羊、煽動恐懼，以及做出毫無實際計畫可兌現的宏大承諾，來贏得民眾的支持。", "as": "The demagogue's tirades played on voters' xenophobia, yet his ostensible concern for ordinary factory workers merely masked a ruthless desire to consolidate power for himself.", "at": "這名煽動家的長篇激烈演說利用了選民的仇外心理，而他表面上對一般工廠勞工的關心，其實只是掩蓋了為自己鞏固權力的冷酷野心。"}, {"w": "maudlin", "p": "adj.", "d": "Excessively and foolishly sentimental, often tearfully so.", "c": "過度感傷的；多愁善感的", "s": "Critics complained that the film's final scene was maudlin, with swelling violins, slow-motion hugs, and a tearful ten-minute farewell speech that seemed designed to force emotion rather than earn it honestly.", "t": "評論家抱怨這部電影的最後一幕過於煽情，激昂的小提琴樂聲、慢動作的擁抱，加上長達十分鐘、淚眼婆娑的告別演說，似乎是刻意催淚，而非真誠地打動觀眾。", "as": "The memoir avoids maudlin self-pity; instead, the author recounts her years of privation with wry humor and a stoic refusal to blame anyone else for her misfortunes.", "at": "這本回憶錄避開了過度感傷的自憐；作者反而以帶點嘲諷的幽默，以及不怨天尤人的堅忍態度，回顧她那些困頓匱乏的歲月。"}, {"w": "begrudge", "p": "v.", "d": "To envy or resent someone for having something.", "c": "嫉妒；不情願給予", "s": "Although she had trained for years and lost the race by less than a second, the runner-up did not begrudge the winner her medal, instead congratulating her warmly and praising her remarkable final sprint.", "t": "雖然她苦練多年，卻以不到一秒之差落敗，這位亞軍並沒有嫉妒冠軍得到獎牌，反而熱情地向她道賀，並稱讚她最後那段驚人的衝刺。", "as": "Few colleagues begrudged the magnanimous professor her accolades, for she had always been generous with her time and quick to commend the work of younger scholars.", "at": "很少有同事嫉妒這位寬宏大量的教授所獲得的榮譽，因為她向來不吝付出時間，也總是樂於稱讚年輕學者的研究成果。"}, {"w": "avowal", "p": "n.", "d": "An open declaration or acknowledgment of something.", "c": "公開聲明；坦承", "s": "The president's public avowal of support for the climate treaty surprised many observers, who had expected him to remain silent, and it encouraged several other nations to announce their own commitments the following week.", "t": "總統公開聲明支持氣候條約，令許多原以為他會保持沉默的觀察家感到意外，此舉也促使其他數個國家在隔週宣布了各自的承諾。", "as": "His fervent avowal of innocence seemed sincere, but the jury found it hard to reconcile his tearful words with the incriminating evidence that the prosecutor presented.", "at": "他熱切地公開聲明自己清白，看似真誠，但陪審團難以將他含淚的說詞與檢察官提出的罪證相互調和。"}, {"w": "proselytize", "p": "v.", "d": "To try to convert someone to a religion, belief, or cause.", "c": "勸人改變信仰；傳教", "s": "Missionaries in the sixteenth century traveled thousands of miles to proselytize in Asia and the Americas, building schools and churches as they tried to persuade local people to adopt the Christian faith.", "t": "十六世紀的傳教士遠行數千英里到亞洲與美洲傳教，一邊興建學校與教堂，一邊試圖說服當地人接受基督教信仰。", "as": "An ardent devotee of veganism, my roommate never misses a chance to proselytize at dinner, though her didactic lectures rarely persuade anyone to give up cheese.", "at": "我的室友是素食主義的熱情信徒，她從不放過在晚餐時大力宣揚的機會，不過她那說教式的長篇大論，很少說服任何人放棄起司。"}, {"w": "guileless", "p": "adj.", "d": "Innocent and honest; free of deceit or cunning.", "c": "天真坦率的；不狡詐的", "s": "The young witness was so guileless and sincere that the jury believed every word of her testimony, convinced that a child so open and honest could not possibly have invented such a detailed story.", "t": "這名年輕證人如此天真坦率、真誠懇切，陪審團相信她證詞中的每一個字，深信一個如此坦白誠實的孩子不可能捏造出這麼詳細的故事。", "as": "The guileless farmer was easy prey for the charlatan, whose glib promises of miraculous crop yields persuaded him to invest his meager savings in worthless seeds.", "at": "這位天真單純的農夫很容易成為那名江湖騙子的獵物，騙子那些花言巧語、保證作物奇蹟豐收的承諾，說服他把微薄的積蓄投資在毫無價值的種子上。"}, {"w": "unconscionable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Unreasonable, excessive, and morally unacceptable.", "c": "不合情理的；昧著良心的", "s": "Consumer groups condemned the drug company's decision to raise the price of a life-saving medicine by five thousand percent as unconscionable, arguing that no business should profit so heavily from patients' desperation.", "t": "消費者團體譴責那家藥廠將救命藥物漲價五千％的決定毫無良知，認為任何企業都不應該從病患的絕望中牟取如此暴利。", "as": "The landlord's unconscionable rent increases forced dozens of indigent families from their homes, and the city council finally moved to proscribe such predatory practices for good.", "at": "房東昧著良心的漲租迫使數十個貧困家庭流離失所，市議會終於採取行動，永久明令禁止這類掠奪性的做法。"}, {"w": "conflate", "p": "v.", "d": "To combine two or more distinct things into one, confusing them.", "c": "合併；混為一談", "s": "Many students mistakenly conflate weather and climate, but the science teacher patiently explained that weather describes short-term conditions on a given day, whereas climate refers to long-term patterns measured over decades.", "t": "許多學生誤把天氣和氣候混為一談，但自然老師耐心地解釋，天氣描述的是某一天的短期狀況，而氣候指的則是以數十年為單位測量的長期型態。", "as": "The essay's fallacious argument conflates correlation with causation, an elementary error that seriously undermines the author's otherwise erudite and carefully researched analysis of urban crime.", "at": "這篇文章的謬誤論證把相關性與因果關係混為一談，這個基本錯誤嚴重削弱了作者原本學識淵博、考證周詳的城市犯罪分析。"}, {"w": "animus", "p": "n.", "d": "Strong hostility or ill will toward someone or something.", "c": "敵意；惡意", "s": "The judge removed herself from the case after lawyers revealed that she had once publicly expressed animus toward the defendant, arguing that her personal hostility might prevent her from ruling fairly.", "t": "律師揭露這名法官曾公開對被告表達敵意後，她便自行迴避此案，律師主張她個人的敵視態度可能使她無法公正裁決。", "as": "Despite years of bitter rivalry, the senator harbored no lasting animus toward his opponent, and he even delivered a laudable and effusive tribute at her retirement dinner.", "at": "儘管多年來激烈較勁，這位參議員對他的對手並未懷有長久的敵意，甚至還在她的退休晚宴上發表了一篇值得稱道、熱情洋溢的致敬詞。"}, {"w": "swath", "p": "n.", "d": "A long, broad strip or area of land or something else.", "c": "長條地帶；大片區域", "s": "The tornado cut a swath of destruction nearly a mile wide through the farming region, flattening barns, uprooting trees, and leaving a long path of debris across fields that had been ready for harvest.", "t": "龍捲風在農業區劃出一道寬近一英里的毀滅地帶，夷平穀倉、連根拔起樹木，並在原本即將收割的田野上留下一長條瓦礫。", "as": "Wildfires have destroyed vast swaths of forest, and scientists warn that the deleterious effects on wildlife may be far more pernicious than official estimates suggest.", "at": "野火已摧毀大片森林，科學家警告，這對野生動物的有害影響可能遠比官方估計的更加惡劣深遠。"}, {"w": "conflagration", "p": "n.", "d": "A large, destructive fire; also, a major violent conflict.", "c": "大火災；大規模衝突", "s": "The Great Fire of London in 1666 was a conflagration that burned for four days, destroying more than thirteen thousand houses and nearly ninety churches before it was finally brought under control.", "t": "一六六六年的倫敦大火是一場延燒了四天的大火災，在終於被控制住之前，摧毀了一萬三千多棟房屋和將近九十座教堂。", "as": "Diplomats feared that the border skirmish, if not quickly defused, could escalate into a regional conflagration, so they worked to mollify both governments and avert a cataclysm.", "at": "外交官擔心，這場邊境小衝突若不迅速化解，可能升級為區域性的大規模戰火，因此他們努力安撫兩國政府，以避免一場浩劫。"}, {"w": "rarefied", "p": "adj.", "d": "Exclusive and refined, understood by only a select few; also, thin (air).", "c": "高深的；稀薄的", "s": "Once limited to the rarefied world of elite universities and research laboratories, artificial intelligence has now entered ordinary homes, where millions of people use it daily to write emails and plan trips.", "t": "人工智慧過去只存在於頂尖大學與研究實驗室那個曲高和寡的圈子，如今已進入尋常百姓家，數百萬人每天用它來寫電子郵件和規劃旅行。", "as": "The poet's rarefied verse, full of esoteric allusions to medieval theology, delighted a small circle of devoted scholars but seemed hopelessly abstruse to most ordinary readers.", "at": "這位詩人的詩作曲高和寡，充滿引用中世紀神學的深奧典故，令一小群熱衷的學者為之著迷，對大多數一般讀者而言卻顯得艱澀難懂、無從理解。"}, {"w": "mendicant", "p": "n.", "d": "A beggar; someone who lives by asking for charity.", "c": "乞丐；托缽修士", "s": "In medieval Europe, a wandering mendicant might travel from town to town asking for food and coins, depending entirely on the charity of strangers for survival because he owned nothing at all.", "t": "在中世紀的歐洲，一名四處流浪的乞丐可能從一個城鎮走到另一個城鎮，討取食物和錢幣；由於他一無所有，只能完全仰賴陌生人的施捨過活。", "as": "The novel's hero, an itinerant mendicant clad in rags, supplicates the haughty nobles for alms, yet his austere wisdom eventually shames them into acts of charity.", "at": "小說的主角是一名衣衫襤褸、四處漂泊的乞丐，他向傲慢的貴族乞求施捨，然而他那簡樸清苦中蘊含的智慧，最終使貴族們羞愧地行善布施。"}, {"w": "recompense", "p": "v.", "d": "To pay or reward someone for effort, loss, or harm.", "c": "賠償；酬報", "s": "After the factory accidentally polluted the river, a court ordered the company to recompense the local fishermen for their lost income, requiring payments that covered three full years of missed catches.", "t": "工廠意外污染河川後，法院判令該公司賠償當地漁民所損失的收入，要求支付的金額須涵蓋整整三年的漁獲損失。", "as": "The government pledged to recompense families whose land had been seized, though critics derided the offer as a mere pittance compared with the true value of the property.", "at": "政府承諾賠償土地遭到徵收的家庭，不過批評者嘲諷這項補償與土地的真實價值相比，只是微不足道的一點錢。"}, {"w": "inundate", "p": "v.", "d": "To overwhelm with a great amount; to flood.", "c": "使應接不暇；淹沒", "s": "After the popular singer announced a free concert in the park, fans began to inundate the city's ticket website with requests, causing the system to crash within minutes and leaving thousands of people frustrated.", "t": "那位人氣歌手宣布將在公園舉辦免費演唱會後，歌迷的索票請求開始如潮水般湧入市府的售票網站，導致系統在幾分鐘內當機，數千人因此大失所望。", "as": "Inundated with a plethora of applications, the overwhelmed admissions committee resorted to a cursory review of each personal essay, a decision that many hopeful applicants found disheartening.", "at": "大量申請如潮水般湧至，不堪負荷的招生委員會只好對每篇個人自述草草審閱，這項決定讓許多滿懷希望的申請者感到灰心。"}, {"w": "aggrandize", "p": "v.", "d": "To increase the power, wealth, or importance of someone.", "c": "擴大（權勢）；吹捧抬高", "s": "Rather than serving the public, the governor seemed determined to aggrandize himself, building monuments in his own honor, renaming streets after his family, and steadily expanding the authority of his office.", "t": "這位州長非但沒有為民服務，反而似乎一心只想擴張自己的權勢：為自己建造紀念碑、以家族成員之名替街道重新命名，並不斷擴大其職權。", "as": "The megalomaniac emperor sought to aggrandize his reign with grandiose palaces, while his sycophantic courtiers dutifully praised every reckless extravagance as a sign of genius.", "at": "那位自大狂皇帝企圖以宏偉浮誇的宮殿來彰顯自己的統治，而他那些阿諛奉承的朝臣則盡責地把每一項魯莽的奢侈揮霍都讚頌為天才的象徵。"}, {"w": "outré", "p": "adj.", "d": "Highly unconventional, bizarre, or eccentric.", "c": "古怪的；離經叛道的", "s": "The designer's outré collection, featuring dresses made of bubble wrap, hats shaped like goldfish bowls, and shoes with built-in flowerpots, shocked traditional critics but delighted young audiences hungry for something new.", "t": "這位設計師的作品系列十分古怪，有用氣泡紙做成的洋裝、形似金魚缸的帽子，還有內建花盆的鞋子，令傳統評論家大為震驚，卻讓渴望新鮮事物的年輕觀眾欣喜不已。", "as": "What once seemed outré in the avant-garde gallery soon became mainstream, as every idiosyncrasy of the iconoclast's style was copied by designers eager to appear daring.", "at": "曾經在前衛藝廊裡顯得離經叛道的作品，很快便成為主流，因為這位打破傳統者風格中的每一項獨特癖好，都被急於顯得大膽的設計師紛紛仿效。"}, {"w": "quintessential", "p": "adj.", "d": "Representing the most perfect or typical example of something.", "c": "典型的；最具代表性的", "s": "With its crowded night markets, steaming bowls of beef noodle soup, and scooters weaving through narrow lanes, the neighborhood offers curious visitors the quintessential Taipei experience in a single evening.", "t": "這一帶有擁擠的夜市、熱騰騰的牛肉麵和穿梭於狹窄巷弄的機車，能讓好奇的遊客在一個晚上就體驗到最道地、最具代表性的台北風情。", "as": "The quintessential Renaissance man, Leonardo da Vinci was a prolific inventor and painter whose insatiable curiosity led him to study everything from anatomy to flight.", "at": "達文西是典型的文藝復興全才，他是一位多產的發明家與畫家，永不滿足的好奇心驅使他鑽研從解剖學到飛行的各種領域。"}, {"w": "pander", "p": "v.", "d": "To cater to people's lowest desires or prejudices for gain.", "c": "迎合；投其所好", "s": "The newspaper's editor refused to pander to readers' appetite for scandal, insisting that the paper would continue publishing serious investigative reports even if celebrity gossip attracted far more clicks and advertising money.", "t": "這家報紙的總編輯拒絕迎合讀者對醜聞的胃口，堅持即使名人八卦能吸引多得多的點閱與廣告收入，報社仍會繼續刊登嚴肅的調查報導。", "as": "Rather than pandering to the crowd with vacuous slogans, the candidate spoke with rare candor about the budget crisis facing the city, even though his frank assessment was unpopular.", "at": "這位候選人沒有用空洞的口號迎合群眾，而是以少見的坦率談論城市所面臨的預算危機，儘管他直言不諱的評估並不討喜。"}]}, {"unit": 35, "level": 7, "cards": [{"w": "sacrosanct", "p": "adj.", "d": "Too sacred or important to be criticized or changed.", "c": "神聖不可侵犯的；不容更改的", "s": "For decades the town's original charter was treated as sacrosanct, and any council member who proposed even minor changes to its wording was accused of disrespecting the community's history and the sacrifices of its earliest settlers.", "t": "數十年來，這座城鎮的原始憲章被視為神聖不可侵犯，任何提議對其措辭做出哪怕是微小修改的議員，都會被指責不尊重社區的歷史與早期移民所做的犧牲。", "as": "The scientist argued that no theory should be sacrosanct, insisting that even the most venerated models must remain open to revision whenever new data prove them fallacious.", "at": "這位科學家主張沒有任何理論應該神聖不可侵犯，並堅稱即使是最受尊崇的模型，只要新數據證明其謬誤，也必須保持可修正的空間。"}, {"w": "indomitable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Impossible to defeat or discourage.", "c": "不屈不撓的；不可征服的", "s": "Despite losing her sight at the age of nineteen, the composer kept writing symphonies for another forty years, and critics often praised her indomitable spirit, which no setback, illness, or rejection from orchestras could ever break.", "t": "儘管這位作曲家在十九歲時失明，她仍持續創作交響曲長達四十年；評論家常讚揚她不屈不撓的精神，任何挫折、疾病或樂團的拒絕都無法擊垮她。", "as": "Even after three failed attempts to reach the summit, the indomitable climber remained resolute, dismissing the gloomy jeremiads of pessimistic critics with characteristic equanimity and quietly planning a fourth ascent.", "at": "即使三度登頂失敗，這位不屈不撓的登山家依然堅定不移，以他一貫的沉著冷靜，對悲觀評論家陰鬱的哀嘆不予理會，並默默計畫第四次攀登。"}, {"w": "mettle", "p": "n.", "d": "Courage and strength of spirit in facing difficulty.", "c": "勇氣；毅力", "s": "The first winter at the remote Antarctic research station tested the mettle of every scientist on the team, as months of darkness, isolation, and temperatures below minus sixty degrees forced them to rely on sheer determination.", "t": "在偏遠南極研究站度過的第一個冬天，考驗了團隊中每位科學家的毅力，因為長達數月的黑暗、孤立與低於零下六十度的氣溫，迫使他們只能依靠堅定的決心撐下去。", "as": "The grueling debate tournament proved the young speaker's mettle; facing a pugnacious opponent, she never lost her composure and answered each tirade with a trenchant rebuttal.", "at": "這場艱苦的辯論賽證明了這位年輕辯士的勇氣；面對好鬥的對手，她始終保持沉著，並以犀利的反駁回應對方每一次的長篇抨擊。"}, {"w": "ellipsis", "p": "n.", "d": "The omission of words, or the mark (...) showing it.", "c": "省略；省略號", "s": "When quoting only part of the senator's long speech, the reporter used an ellipsis to show readers that several words had been removed from the middle of the sentence without changing its original meaning.", "t": "在只引用參議員冗長演說的一部分時，記者使用了省略號，讓讀者知道句子中間刪去了幾個字，但並未改變其原意。", "as": "Rather than writing a verbose explanation, the poet relied on a single ellipsis to suggest what remained unsaid, a subtle nuance that astute readers immediately noticed.", "at": "這位詩人沒有寫下冗長的解釋，而是只用一個省略號來暗示未說出口的部分，這種微妙的細微差異，敏銳的讀者立刻就察覺到了。"}, {"w": "petulant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Childishly bad-tempered and easily annoyed.", "c": "任性易怒的；使性子的", "s": "When the referee refused to overturn the call, the star player threw his racket onto the court and sulked on the bench like a petulant child, a display that embarrassed his coach and drew loud boos from the crowd.", "t": "當裁判拒絕推翻判決時，這位明星球員把球拍摔在場上，像個使性子的孩子般在場邊生悶氣，這番表現讓教練難堪，也引來觀眾大聲噓他。", "as": "The petulant heir, long accustomed to obsequious servants who granted his every wish, grew irascible and sulky whenever an adviser or relative dared to question his extravagant spending on cars and parties.", "at": "這位任性易怒的繼承人長久以來習慣了奴顏婢膝、事事順從的僕人，每當顧問或親戚膽敢質疑他在名車與派對上的揮霍無度，他就會勃然大怒、悶悶不樂。"}, {"w": "deign", "p": "v.", "d": "To do something one considers beneath one's dignity.", "c": "屈尊；俯就", "s": "The famous architect was so arrogant that she would not deign to answer questions from first-year students, insisting that only senior professors were worthy of discussing her award-winning designs with her.", "t": "這位知名建築師傲慢至極，不肯屈尊回答大一學生的問題，並堅稱只有資深教授才配與她討論她的得獎設計。", "as": "The supercilious critic rarely deigned to review local productions, dismissing them as banal entertainments unworthy of his erudite attention, yet he praised the same amateur actors once they became famous.", "at": "這位高傲的評論家很少屈尊評論本地的演出，將其貶為不值得他這種博學之人關注的陳腐娛樂，然而一旦同樣這批業餘演員成名，他卻又大加讚揚。"}, {"w": "berate", "p": "v.", "d": "To scold or criticize someone angrily.", "c": "嚴厲斥責；痛罵", "s": "Instead of calmly explaining the error in the lab report, the supervisor chose to berate the intern loudly in front of the entire research team, an outburst that left the young scientist humiliated and reluctant to ask questions.", "t": "主管沒有冷靜地說明實驗報告中的錯誤，而是選擇在整個研究團隊面前大聲斥責那名實習生，這番爆發讓這位年輕科學家感到羞辱，也不敢再提出問題。", "as": "Rather than berating the students for their callow mistakes, the judicious coach chose to edify them, patiently explaining how each error could be avoided in the next competition.", "at": "這位明智的教練沒有因學生們幼稚生澀的錯誤而斥責他們，而是選擇啟發教導，耐心說明在下一場比賽中如何避免每一個錯誤。"}, {"w": "harbinger", "p": "n.", "d": "A person or thing that signals something coming.", "c": "先兆；預兆", "s": "In many parts of Taiwan, the arrival of the first plum rains is a harbinger of the hot, humid summer, warning farmers that they must finish harvesting certain crops before the heavy downpours arrive.", "t": "在台灣許多地方，第一場梅雨的到來是炎熱潮濕夏季的先兆，提醒農民必須在豪雨來臨之前完成某些作物的收成。", "as": "Economists viewed the sudden plethora of shuttered storefronts as a harbinger of recession, though a few sanguine analysts dismissed the trend as a transitory fluctuation.", "at": "經濟學家將突然大量出現的歇業店面視為經濟衰退的前兆，不過少數樂觀的分析師認為這股趨勢只是短暫的波動而不以為意。"}, {"w": "corpulent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Large and fat in body.", "c": "肥胖的；臃腫的", "s": "In many seventeenth-century Dutch portraits, wealthy merchants appear corpulent, their round bellies and heavy chins proudly displayed as signs that they could afford rich food at a time when most people ate very little.", "t": "在許多十七世紀的荷蘭肖像畫中，富商們顯得體態肥胖，他們圓滾的肚子與厚重的雙下巴被自豪地展示出來，象徵他們在多數人食物匱乏的年代仍吃得起豐盛的美食。", "as": "The corpulent king, renowned for his voracious appetite, held lavish banquets that his indigent subjects could only imagine, a contrast that fueled growing animosity throughout the realm.", "at": "這位以食量驚人聞名的肥胖國王舉辦奢華的宴會，那是他貧困的子民只能想像的場面，這樣的對比在全國各地激起日益高漲的敵意。"}, {"w": "aggrieved", "p": "adj.", "d": "Feeling resentment at having been treated unfairly.", "c": "憤憤不平的；受委屈的", "s": "After being passed over for promotion in favor of a less experienced colleague, the aggrieved engineer filed a formal complaint, arguing that the company had ignored her years of loyal service and outstanding performance reviews.", "t": "在升遷機會被一位經驗較少的同事取代後，這位憤憤不平的工程師提出正式申訴，主張公司漠視了她多年來的忠誠服務與優異的績效評核。", "as": "The aggrieved villagers sought redress from the provincial court, alleging that the mining company had engaged in a surreptitious scheme to divert their water supply.", "at": "憤憤不平的村民向省級法院尋求補償，指控該礦業公司暗中策劃，企圖改道他們的水源。"}, {"w": "polyglot", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who knows and uses several languages.", "c": "通曉多種語言的人", "s": "Raised by a Japanese mother and a French father in Singapore, the diplomat became a true polyglot, speaking six languages fluently and switching effortlessly between them during international negotiations on trade and climate policy.", "t": "這位外交官由日籍母親與法籍父親在新加坡撫養長大，成為一位真正通曉多國語言的人，能流利地說六種語言，並在貿易與氣候政策的國際談判中輕鬆自如地切換。", "as": "A gifted polyglot, the translator could render the same diatribe into five languages, preserving every subtle nuance of the speaker's acerbic wit for an international audience.", "at": "這位精通多國語言的天才譯者能將同一篇抨擊演說譯成五種語言，為國際聽眾保留講者尖酸機智中的每一個細微差異。"}, {"w": "comport", "p": "v.", "d": "To behave or conduct oneself in a particular way.", "c": "舉止；表現", "s": "Before the students visited the national museum, their teacher reminded them to comport themselves with dignity, speaking quietly in the galleries and treating the fragile artifacts and the museum staff with respect.", "t": "在學生參觀國立博物館之前，老師提醒他們要舉止得體，在展廳內輕聲說話，並尊重脆弱的文物與博物館的工作人員。", "as": "Even when the pundits hurled invective at him during the televised debate, the senator comported himself with remarkable equanimity, refusing to stoop to their level.", "at": "即使在電視辯論中遭到名嘴們的謾罵，這位參議員仍表現得異常沉著冷靜，拒絕降低自己的格調與他們一般見識。"}, {"w": "revile", "p": "v.", "d": "To criticize someone or something in an abusive, angry way.", "c": "辱罵；痛斥", "s": "Although later generations would celebrate his paintings as masterpieces, critics of the time chose to revile the artist, calling his bold use of color an insult to tradition and urging galleries never to display his work.", "t": "儘管後世將他的畫作譽為傑作，當時的評論家卻選擇痛斥這位畫家，稱他大膽的用色是對傳統的侮辱，並呼籲畫廊永遠不要展出他的作品。", "as": "Once reviled as a dangerous iconoclast, the scientist was later lionized by the very institutions that had tried to ostracize her for her unconventional theories.", "at": "這位科學家曾被辱罵為危險的反傳統者，後來卻受到當初因她非傳統的理論而試圖排擠她的那些機構所推崇。"}, {"w": "perspicacious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having a keen ability to notice and understand things.", "c": "敏銳的；有洞察力的", "s": "A perspicacious reader will notice that the narrator's account contradicts itself in several small details, a clue that the author deliberately planted to suggest that the story we are hearing may not be entirely true.", "t": "敏銳的讀者會注意到，敘事者的陳述在幾個小細節上自相矛盾，這是作者刻意埋下的線索，暗示我們聽到的故事可能並不完全真實。", "as": "The perspicacious detective saw through the suspect's specious alibi at once, recognizing that its seemingly lucid timeline concealed a crucial gap on the night of the robbery.", "at": "這位明察秋毫的偵探立刻識破嫌犯似是而非的不在場證明，看出那條看似清楚明瞭的時間線，隱藏了搶案當晚一段關鍵的空白。"}, {"w": "triumvirate", "p": "n.", "d": "A group of three people sharing power or leadership.", "c": "三人執政；三巨頭", "s": "After the death of Julius Caesar, Octavian, Mark Antony, and Lepidus formed a triumvirate to rule Rome together, but the three men soon distrusted one another, and their alliance eventually collapsed into civil war.", "t": "凱撒死後，屋大維、馬克・安東尼與雷必達組成三人執政，共同統治羅馬，但三人很快便互不信任，他們的同盟最終瓦解，演變成內戰。", "as": "The company was run by a triumvirate of founders whose ambivalent relationship eventually culminated in a bitter schism that split the firm into two rival factions.", "at": "這家公司由三位創辦人共同掌管，他們之間愛恨交織的關係最終演變成激烈的分裂，使公司分裂為兩個敵對的派系。"}, {"w": "augury", "p": "n.", "d": "A sign or omen of what will happen in the future.", "c": "預兆；占卜", "s": "Ancient Roman priests studied the flight patterns of birds before major battles, believing that each augury revealed whether the gods favored their armies or were warning the generals to delay the attack.", "t": "古羅馬祭司在重大戰役前觀察鳥類的飛行模式，相信每一個預兆都能揭示眾神是否眷顧他們的軍隊，或是在警告將領延後進攻。", "as": "The record turnout at the first rally seemed an auspicious augury for the young candidate, though prudent advisers warned that early enthusiasm is often ephemeral.", "at": "首場造勢大會創紀錄的出席人數，對這位年輕候選人而言似乎是個吉祥的預兆，不過謹慎的顧問提醒，早期的熱情往往轉瞬即逝。"}, {"w": "pallid", "p": "adj.", "d": "Pale; lacking color or liveliness.", "c": "蒼白的；無生氣的", "s": "After spending three months indoors recovering from a serious illness, the patient looked thin and pallid, so his doctor encouraged him to take short walks in the sunshine to rebuild his strength and appetite.", "t": "在室內養病三個月後，這名病人看起來消瘦又蒼白，因此醫生鼓勵他在陽光下短暫散步，以恢復體力與食慾。", "as": "Critics found the sequel a pallid imitation of the original, its banal dialogue and lackluster performances lacking the ebullience that had made the first film so memorable.", "at": "評論家認為這部續集只是原作毫無生氣的模仿，陳腐的對白與平淡的演出，缺少了讓第一集令人難忘的那股熱情洋溢。"}, {"w": "indolent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Lazy; avoiding activity or effort.", "c": "懶惰的；怠惰的", "s": "The essay contest judges were disappointed by one indolent student who had clearly spent no more than ten minutes on his entry, copying sentences from the prompt rather than developing original arguments or doing any research.", "t": "作文比賽的評審對一名懶惰的學生感到失望，他顯然只花了不到十分鐘完成參賽作品，直接抄寫題目中的句子，而沒有發展原創論點或做任何研究。", "as": "The indolent clerk, who spent most afternoons dozing at his desk, held what was essentially a sinecure, yet he expected generous remuneration for his perfunctory efforts.", "at": "這名懶散的職員大多數下午都在辦公桌前打瞌睡，他的職位本質上是個閒差，但他卻期望自己敷衍了事的工作能換得優渥的報酬。"}, {"w": "utilitarian", "p": "adj.", "d": "Designed to be useful rather than beautiful.", "c": "實用的；功利的", "s": "Unlike the ornate palaces built for the aristocracy, the workers' housing was strictly utilitarian: plain concrete blocks with small windows, shared kitchens, and no decoration of any kind, built quickly to shelter as many families as possible.", "t": "不同於為貴族建造的華麗宮殿，工人住宅完全講求實用：簡樸的水泥建築、小小的窗戶、共用的廚房，毫無任何裝飾，迅速建成以盡可能安置更多家庭。", "as": "The architect rejected the utilitarian design of the old library, replacing its drab concrete walls with an opulent atrium that some critics called ostentatious and wasteful.", "at": "這位建築師否定了舊圖書館講求實用的設計，以富麗堂皇的中庭取代其單調的水泥牆，一些評論家則批評這種設計浮誇又浪費。"}, {"w": "salacious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Indecent or scandalous, especially about sexual matters.", "c": "淫穢的；下流的", "s": "During the nineteenth century, some cheap newspapers boosted their sales by printing salacious gossip about the private lives of celebrities, while more respected publications condemned such stories as indecent and harmful to public morals.", "t": "在十九世紀，一些廉價報紙藉由刊登名人私生活的下流八卦來提高銷量，而較受尊重的刊物則譴責這類報導不雅且有害公共道德。", "as": "Media historians argue that salacious tabloids pandered to readers' basest curiosity, while their sensational headlines often obfuscated the genuinely important political news of the day.", "at": "媒體史學者認為，低俗下流的小報迎合讀者最卑劣的好奇心，而其聳動的標題常常模糊了當時真正重要的政治新聞。"}]}, {"unit": 36, "level": 8, "cards": [{"w": "bereft", "p": "adj.", "d": "Deprived of something; lacking; sad from loss.", "c": "被剝奪的；喪失（親人）而悲傷的", "s": "After the flood swept away their homes, crops, and livestock in a single night, many villagers were left bereft of everything they owned and had to depend entirely on emergency aid from the government.", "t": "洪水在一夜之間沖走了他們的房屋、作物與牲畜之後，許多村民失去了所擁有的一切，只能完全依靠政府的緊急援助。", "as": "Bereft of the wealthy patrons who had once sustained him, the aging poet languished in penury for years, his once prolific output dwindling to a handful of short verses each winter.", "at": "失去了曾經支撐他的富有贊助者後，這位年邁的詩人多年來在貧困中日漸消沉，他曾經豐沛的創作量逐漸減少到每年冬天只寫得出寥寥幾首短詩。"}, {"w": "nemesis", "p": "n.", "d": "An enemy or rival who cannot be overcome; a downfall.", "c": "剋星；宿敵", "s": "For years the champion swimmer won almost every race she entered, but a younger rival from Australia became her nemesis, defeating her in three consecutive world championships and finally ending her remarkable winning streak.", "t": "多年來這位游泳冠軍幾乎贏得她參加的每一場比賽，但一位來自澳洲的年輕對手成了她的剋星，連續三屆世界錦標賽擊敗她，終結了她驚人的連勝紀錄。", "as": "Hubris proved to be the general's nemesis; convinced of his own omnipotence, he ignored the prudent counsel of his officers and led his army into catastrophe.", "at": "傲慢自大成了這位將軍的剋星；他深信自己無所不能，無視軍官們審慎的建議，率領軍隊走向災難。"}, {"w": "equivocate", "p": "v.", "d": "To use vague language to avoid giving a clear answer.", "c": "含糊其詞；支吾搪塞", "s": "When reporters asked whether the factory had polluted the river, the spokesperson continued to equivocate, offering vague statements about ongoing reviews instead of simply admitting or denying that toxic waste had been released.", "t": "當記者詢問工廠是否污染了河川時，發言人仍持續含糊其詞，只提供關於調查仍在進行中的模糊說法，而不直接承認或否認曾排放有毒廢棄物。", "as": "Instead of equivocating when asked about the controversial pipeline, the candidate gave an unequivocal answer, a display of candor that surprised voters long accustomed to politicians' habitual circumlocution.", "at": "被問到具爭議的輸油管計畫時，這位候選人沒有含糊其詞，而是給出了明確的答案，這種坦率令長久以來習慣政客慣用迂迴說法的選民大感意外。"}, {"w": "philistine", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who is hostile or indifferent to culture and the arts.", "c": "庸俗之人；不懂藝術的人", "s": "The mayor who proposed tearing down the historic opera house to build a parking lot was called a philistine by local artists, who accused him of caring only about money and nothing about the city's cultural heritage.", "t": "提議拆除歷史悠久的歌劇院改建停車場的市長，被當地藝術家稱為庸俗之人，他們指責他只在乎金錢，毫不關心城市的文化遺產。", "as": "Dismissing modern sculpture as worthless junk, the wealthy philistine nonetheless bought several expensive pieces for his lobby, hoping their ostentatious display would impress the cognoscenti who attended his lavish parties.", "at": "這位富有卻不懂藝術的人把現代雕塑貶為毫無價值的垃圾，卻仍為他的大廳買下了好幾件昂貴的作品，希望藉由炫耀展示，讓出席他奢華派對的行家們留下深刻印象。"}, {"w": "bacchanalian", "p": "adj.", "d": "Characterized by wild, drunken celebration.", "c": "狂歡作樂的；酗酒喧鬧的", "s": "Ancient Roman festivals honoring the god of wine were often bacchanalian affairs, with crowds drinking heavily, dancing through the streets, and celebrating so wildly that the Senate eventually passed laws to restrict them.", "t": "古羅馬為紀念酒神而舉行的節慶往往是狂歡作樂的場合，群眾豪飲、在街上跳舞，慶祝得極其放縱，以致元老院最終通過法律加以限制。", "as": "In her historical novel, the author contrasted the bacchanalian revels of the decadent court with the austere lives of the peasants, whose privation the dissolute nobles blithely ignored.", "at": "在她的歷史小說中，作者將墮落宮廷的狂歡宴樂與農民的清苦生活加以對比，而那些放蕩的貴族對農民的貧困竟漠不關心。"}, {"w": "schism", "p": "n.", "d": "A split or division within a group over beliefs.", "c": "分裂；派系分立", "s": "In 1054, a bitter disagreement over church authority and doctrine produced a lasting schism between the Eastern and Western branches of Christianity, dividing believers into two separate institutions that remain apart today.", "t": "1054年，一場關於教會權威與教義的激烈爭執，在基督教東西兩派之間造成長久的分裂，使信徒分屬兩個至今仍各自獨立的機構。", "as": "The contentious debate over how to spend the grant created a lasting schism within the student club, and no amount of friendly persuasion could reconcile the two factions' intransigent positions.", "at": "這場關於如何運用補助款的激烈爭論，在學生社團內部造成長久的分裂，無論多少友善的勸說都無法調和兩派毫不妥協的立場。"}, {"w": "lingua franca", "p": "n.", "d": "A common language used between speakers of different languages.", "c": "通用語；共同語言", "s": "At international scientific conferences, English has become the lingua franca, allowing researchers from Brazil, Korea, Germany, and Kenya to share their findings and debate ideas without needing an interpreter for every conversation.", "t": "在國際科學會議上，英語已成為通用語，讓來自巴西、韓國、德國與肯亞的研究人員無需為每次交談都配備口譯員，就能分享研究成果並討論想法。", "as": "For centuries Latin served as the lingua franca of European scholars, enabling an erudite monk in Spain to correspond with a polyglot professor in Poland.", "at": "數百年來，拉丁文是歐洲學者的通用語，使西班牙一位博學的修士能與波蘭一位通曉多國語言的教授通信往來。"}, {"w": "winsome", "p": "adj.", "d": "Attractive or appealing in a charming, innocent way.", "c": "迷人的；討人喜歡的", "s": "The children's book became a bestseller largely because of its winsome main character, a shy little hedgehog whose gentle smile and kind heart charmed readers of every age around the world.", "t": "這本童書之所以成為暢銷書，很大程度歸功於其討人喜歡的主角——一隻害羞的小刺蝟，牠溫柔的微笑與善良的心擄獲了世界各地各年齡層的讀者。", "as": "Her winsome manner and genuine warmth made the new ambassador a personable presence at every embassy reception, quickly mollifying the foreign diplomats who had deeply resented her predecessor.", "at": "她迷人的舉止與真誠的溫暖，讓這位新任大使在每場使館招待會上都備受歡迎，很快便安撫了那些曾對她前任深感不滿的外國外交官。"}, {"w": "patrician", "p": "adj.", "d": "Aristocratic; belonging to or typical of the upper class.", "c": "貴族的；上流社會的", "s": "Born into a wealthy patrician family that had governed the city for generations, the young senator spoke with refined manners and an elegant accent that made ordinary voters feel he could never understand their problems.", "t": "這位年輕參議員出身於世代統治這座城市的富裕貴族家庭，談吐舉止優雅、口音高雅，使一般選民覺得他永遠無法理解他們的困境。", "as": "Despite his patrician upbringing in a grand country estate, the young reformer eschewed the privileges of his class and devoted his fortune to improving the lives of plebeian factory workers.", "at": "儘管在宏偉的鄉間莊園中以貴族方式長大，這位年輕的改革者卻摒棄了所屬階級的特權，將財富投入改善平民工廠勞工的生活。"}, {"w": "redact", "p": "v.", "d": "To edit or revise text, often removing sensitive parts.", "c": "編輯；修訂（刪除機密內容）", "s": "Before releasing the military documents to the public, government officials had to redact them carefully, blacking out the names of informants and any details that might endanger soldiers still serving overseas.", "t": "在向大眾公開軍事文件之前，政府官員必須仔細修訂這些文件，塗黑線人的姓名以及任何可能危及仍在海外服役士兵的細節。", "as": "Working for nearly a year, the editor redacted the rambling manuscript into a single readable volume, removing repetitive chapters and tangential anecdotes while preserving the author's lucid central argument.", "at": "編輯花了將近一年，將這份雜亂冗長的手稿修訂成一部易讀的單冊，刪去重複的章節與離題的軼事，同時保留作者清晰明瞭的核心論點。"}, {"w": "précis", "p": "n.", "d": "A brief summary of the main points of a text.", "c": "摘要；大意", "s": "Because the committee members had no time to read the entire two-hundred-page report, the assistant prepared a one-page précis highlighting its main findings, key statistics, and final recommendations for the new transportation policy.", "t": "由於委員們沒有時間閱讀整份兩百頁的報告，助理準備了一頁摘要，重點列出主要發現、關鍵統計數據以及對新交通政策的最終建議。", "as": "Her précis of the abstruse philosophical treatise was so clear and well organized that even neophytes in the seminar could grasp the author's central argument without wading through the long original.", "at": "她對那部深奧哲學論著所寫的摘要清楚又條理分明，即使是研討課上的初學者，也無需費力讀完冗長的原文，就能掌握作者的核心論點。"}, {"w": "taxonomy", "p": "n.", "d": "The scientific system of classifying living things or ideas.", "c": "分類學；分類法", "s": "Carl Linnaeus developed a taxonomy that sorted every known plant and animal into groups such as kingdom, genus, and species, giving scientists a shared method for naming and organizing the natural world.", "t": "林奈發展出一套分類法，將所有已知的植物與動物分入界、屬、種等類群，讓科學家擁有命名與整理自然界的共同方法。", "as": "The biologist's revised taxonomy of tropical beetles proved controversial, as several eminent colleagues dismissed her new categories as arbitrary and her genetic evidence as far too tenuous to persuade them.", "at": "這位生物學家修訂的熱帶甲蟲分類法引發爭議，因為幾位傑出的同行認為她的新類別武斷任意，而她的基因證據也太過薄弱，難以說服他們。"}, {"w": "subliminal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Below the level of conscious awareness.", "c": "潛意識的；下意識的", "s": "Some psychologists have studied whether subliminal images, flashed on a screen too quickly for viewers to consciously notice them, can actually influence what people choose to buy or how they vote.", "t": "一些心理學家研究，那些在螢幕上一閃而過、快到觀眾無法有意識察覺的潛意識影像，是否真的會影響人們的購買選擇或投票方式。", "as": "Consumer groups alleged that the television advertisement contained subliminal messages designed to beguile gullible viewers into buying the drink, though the company's executives adamantly denied the charge.", "at": "消費者團體指控這支電視廣告含有潛意識訊息，意圖誘騙容易上當的觀眾購買這款飲料，不過該公司高層堅決否認此項指控。"}, {"w": "misanthropy", "p": "n.", "d": "A general hatred or distrust of humankind.", "c": "厭世；憎恨人類", "s": "Disappointed by years of war and betrayal, the aging writer slowly retreated from society, and his later novels reveal a deep misanthropy, portraying almost every human character as selfish, cruel, and untrustworthy.", "t": "多年的戰爭與背叛令這位年邁作家失望透頂，他逐漸遠離社會，而他後期的小說流露出深刻的厭世情懷，幾乎把每個人物都描寫成自私、殘忍且不可信賴的。", "as": "The old hermit's misanthropy was legendary in the valley; he rebuffed every curious visitor with acerbic insults and seemed to regard all human society as fundamentally odious.", "at": "這位老隱士的厭世在山谷中是出了名的；他以尖酸的辱罵拒絕每一位好奇的訪客，似乎認為整個人類社會從根本上就令人厭惡。"}, {"w": "imprimatur", "p": "n.", "d": "Official approval or sanction, especially to publish.", "c": "認可；出版許可", "s": "The new textbook could not be distributed to public schools until it received the imprimatur of the Ministry of Education, whose reviewers checked every chapter for accuracy before granting final approval.", "t": "這本新教科書必須獲得教育部的認可才能發放到公立學校，教育部的審查人員會逐章檢查內容是否正確，才給予最終核准。", "as": "Having finally received the imprimatur of the scientific establishment, the once heterodox theory quickly became accepted wisdom, and many of its former detractors hurried to acquiesce.", "at": "在終於獲得科學界主流的認可後，這個曾經離經叛道的理論迅速成為公認的定論，而它過去的許多批評者也紛紛急於默認接受。"}, {"w": "canard", "p": "n.", "d": "A false and unfounded report or story.", "c": "謠言；無稽之談", "s": "The old canard that people use only ten percent of their brains has been repeated in movies and advertisements for decades, even though neuroscientists have shown that nearly every region of the brain is active.", "t": "「人類只使用了大腦的百分之十」這個老掉牙的謠言數十年來不斷在電影與廣告中被重複，儘管神經科學家早已證明大腦幾乎每個區域都是活躍的。", "as": "The investigative journalist exposed the canard as a calumny fabricated by the candidate's political rivals, though the spurious story had already damaged her reputation beyond repair.", "at": "這位調查記者揭露該謠言是候選人的政敵捏造的誹謗，不過這則虛假的報導早已對她的名聲造成無法彌補的傷害。"}, {"w": "perfidious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Deliberately disloyal or treacherous.", "c": "背信棄義的；不忠的", "s": "Historians still debate why the trusted general made the perfidious decision to secretly open the city gates to the enemy, betraying the king who had rewarded him with land, wealth, and the highest military honors.", "t": "歷史學家至今仍在爭論，這位深受信任的將軍為何做出背信棄義的決定，祕密為敵軍打開城門，背叛了曾以土地、財富與最高軍事榮譽獎賞他的國王。", "as": "The perfidious minister, a master of duplicity and machination, secretly sold state secrets to rival powers for years while publicly professing unwavering loyalty to the crown.", "at": "這位背信棄義的大臣精於欺詐與陰謀，多年來暗中向敵對勢力出賣國家機密，一面卻公開宣稱對王室忠貞不二。"}, {"w": "epiphany", "p": "n.", "d": "A sudden, powerful realization or insight.", "c": "頓悟；靈光乍現", "s": "While watching an apple fall in his garden, Isaac Newton supposedly had an epiphany about gravity, suddenly realizing that the same force pulling the fruit downward might also keep the moon in its orbit.", "t": "據說牛頓在花園裡看著蘋果落下時，對重力有了頓悟，突然意識到把果實往下拉的那股力量，可能也讓月球維持在軌道上運行。", "as": "After months of fruitless conjecture, the mathematician experienced a sudden epiphany while hiking that resolved the conundrum, and her elegant proof was soon hailed as seminal.", "at": "經過數月徒勞的推測，這位數學家在健行時突然靈光乍現，解開了這道難題，她簡潔優雅的證明很快就被譽為開創性的成果。"}, {"w": "prattle", "p": "v.", "d": "To talk at length in a foolish or trivial way.", "c": "閒扯；喋喋不休", "s": "During the long train journey, the passenger beside me continued to prattle about his cat's favorite foods and the weather in his hometown, never noticing that I was trying to finish an important report.", "t": "在漫長的火車旅途中，坐在我旁邊的乘客不停閒扯他家貓咪最愛的食物和他家鄉的天氣，絲毫沒注意到我正努力完成一份重要的報告。", "as": "The garrulous host prattled on for hours about trivial neighborhood gossip while his guests, thoroughly sated after the lavish holiday meal, struggled politely to stay awake.", "at": "這位多話的主人連續數小時喋喋不休地談著鄰里間瑣碎的八卦，而他的客人在豐盛的節日大餐後早已吃飽喝足，只能禮貌地努力撐著不打瞌睡。"}, {"w": "plebeian", "p": "adj.", "d": "Of the common people; ordinary or unrefined.", "c": "平民的；粗俗的", "s": "The wealthy critic dismissed fried chicken and bubble tea as plebeian food, but the young chef proudly served both at her restaurant, arguing that simple dishes loved by ordinary people deserve as much respect as fine cuisine.", "t": "這位富有的評論家把炸雞和珍珠奶茶貶為平民食物，但這位年輕主廚卻自豪地在她的餐廳供應這兩樣，主張受一般大眾喜愛的簡單料理與高級料理同樣值得尊重。", "as": "The supercilious aristocrat disparaged the serialized novel as plebeian entertainment for factory workers, yet its everyday language and touching characters won the hearts of millions of readers across the empire.", "at": "這位高傲的貴族貶低這部連載小說是給工廠工人看的平民娛樂，然而其日常的語言與動人的角色卻擄獲了帝國各地數百萬讀者的心。"}]}, {"unit": 37, "level": 8, "cards": [{"w": "gull", "p": "v.", "d": "To trick or deceive someone, especially a trusting person.", "c": "欺騙；愚弄", "s": "The online scammers used fake charity websites and heartbreaking photos to gull thousands of kind but trusting people into donating money that never reached a single hospital, school, or family in need.", "t": "這些網路詐騙者利用假冒的慈善網站與令人心碎的照片，欺騙了數千名善良卻輕信他人的民眾捐款，而這些錢從未送達任何一家醫院、學校或需要幫助的家庭。", "as": "The charlatan managed to gull dozens of credulous investors with his specious promises of a miraculous panacea, until a sharp-eyed reporter finally exposed the entire scheme in a front-page article.", "at": "這名江湖騙子以神奇萬靈丹那似是而非的承諾，成功欺騙了數十名輕信的投資人，直到一位眼光敏銳的記者終於在頭版報導中揭穿了整場騙局。"}, {"w": "compendious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Containing much information in a concise, complete form.", "c": "簡明扼要的；內容完整而精簡的", "s": "Students preparing for the history exam relied on a compendious study guide that covered five centuries of European politics, art, and science in only sixty pages, with no important event left out.", "t": "準備歷史考試的學生仰賴一本簡明完整的讀書指南，它只用六十頁就涵蓋了歐洲五個世紀的政治、藝術與科學，沒有遺漏任何重要事件。", "as": "Unlike the prolix textbooks that preceded it, the compendious handbook offered a lucid overview of the entire field, making it indispensable for neophytes and experts alike.", "at": "不同於先前冗長的教科書，這本簡明扼要的手冊對整個領域提供了清晰明瞭的概述，使其成為初學者與專家都不可或缺的工具書。"}, {"w": "rhapsodize", "p": "v.", "d": "To speak or write about something with great enthusiasm.", "c": "狂熱地談論；熱情讚頌", "s": "Whenever her friends asked about her trip to Hualien, she would rhapsodize for an hour about the marble cliffs of Taroko Gorge, the turquoise ocean, and the most delicious bowl of noodles she had ever tasted.", "t": "每當朋友問起她的花蓮之旅，她就會熱情洋溢地講上一個小時，大談太魯閣峽谷的大理石峭壁、碧藍的海洋，還有她吃過最美味的一碗麵。", "as": "At the gala, the effusive critic rhapsodized about the young pianist's mellifluous playing, praising her technique as inimitable and confidently predicting a brilliant international career for the shy teenager.", "at": "在晚會上，這位熱情洋溢的評論家對這位年輕鋼琴家悅耳流暢的演奏讚不絕口，稱讚她的技巧無人能及，並自信地預言這位害羞的少女將有輝煌的國際演奏生涯。"}, {"w": "oxymoron", "p": "n.", "d": "A phrase combining two words with opposite meanings.", "c": "矛盾修飾法；矛盾語", "s": "In his famous balcony scene, Shakespeare has Juliet describe parting from Romeo as \"sweet sorrow,\" an oxymoron that joins two opposite feelings to show how love can bring pleasure and pain at once.", "t": "在著名的陽台場景中，莎士比亞讓茱麗葉形容與羅密歐分離是「甜蜜的哀愁」，這個矛盾修飾語結合了兩種相反的情感，表現出愛情如何同時帶來歡愉與痛苦。", "as": "Critics joked that the phrase \"military intelligence\" was an oxymoron, a droll remark that the irascible general, already furious about the leaked report, did not find amusing in the least.", "at": "評論家開玩笑說「軍事情報」這個詞是矛盾修飾語，這句詼諧的話讓那位早已為報告外洩而大發雷霆、脾氣暴躁的將軍一點也不覺得好笑。"}, {"w": "provenance", "p": "n.", "d": "The place of origin or history of ownership of something.", "c": "起源；出處", "s": "Before the museum agreed to buy the ancient bronze vase, experts spent months investigating its provenance, tracing every owner back to the excavation site to make sure it had not been stolen or illegally exported.", "t": "在博物館同意購買這只古代青銅瓶之前，專家們花了數月調查它的來源，追溯每一位持有者直到出土地點，以確保它並非贓物或非法出口的文物。", "as": "Doubts about the painting's provenance led scholars to question whether it was authentic or merely an apocryphal attribution concocted by an unscrupulous dealer hoping to sell it at auction for millions.", "at": "對這幅畫來源的疑慮，使學者們質疑它究竟是真跡，還是只是某個想在拍賣會上賣得數百萬元、不擇手段的畫商所捏造的可疑歸屬。"}, {"w": "laissez-faire", "p": "n.", "d": "A policy of noninterference, especially by government in business.", "c": "放任主義；自由放任政策", "s": "Supporters of laissez-faire argue that markets work best when the government stays out of business decisions, while critics point to the dangerous factory conditions of the 1800s as proof that some regulation is necessary.", "t": "放任主義的支持者主張，政府不干預商業決策時市場運作得最好；而批評者則以十九世紀危險的工廠環境為例，證明某些規範是必要的。", "as": "The economist's unwavering devotion to laissez-faire seemed quixotic to colleagues, who argued that such rigid dogma ignored the deleterious effects of unchecked monopolies on ordinary consumers and small businesses.", "at": "這位經濟學家對放任主義堅定不移的信奉，在同事眼中顯得不切實際，他們認為這種僵化的教條忽視了不受約束的壟斷對一般消費者與小型企業的有害影響。"}, {"w": "preternatural", "p": "adj.", "d": "Beyond what is normal or natural; extraordinary.", "c": "超乎尋常的；超自然的", "s": "Even as a young child, the chess prodigy displayed a preternatural ability to predict her opponents' moves, calculating ten steps ahead with a speed and accuracy that astonished grandmasters three times her age.", "t": "這位西洋棋神童從小就展現出超乎常人的能力，能預測對手的棋步，以令年紀大她三倍的特級大師都驚嘆的速度與準確度，計算出十步之後的局勢。", "as": "The detective's preternatural calm amid the chaos was uncanny; while others panicked, he methodically gathered evidence that would later corroborate his initial theory about the stolen jewels.", "at": "這位偵探在混亂中超乎尋常的冷靜令人不可思議；當其他人驚慌失措時，他有條不紊地蒐集證據，後來這些證據證實了他最初對失竊珠寶的推論。"}, {"w": "disabuse", "p": "v.", "d": "To free someone from a mistaken belief or idea.", "c": "使醒悟；糾正錯誤觀念", "s": "The science teacher began the lesson by trying to disabuse her students of the common belief that summer is hot because the Earth is closer to the sun, explaining that the tilt of the planet's axis is the real cause.", "t": "這位自然老師在課堂一開始就試圖糾正學生們普遍的錯誤觀念——認為夏天炎熱是因為地球離太陽較近——並解釋地軸傾斜才是真正的原因。", "as": "The candid mentor quickly disabused the callow intern at the firm of his naive belief that success would come without arduous effort, long hours, or the occasional humiliating rebuff.", "at": "這位直率的導師很快就糾正了公司裡那位涉世未深的實習生天真的想法，讓他明白成功不會在沒有艱苦努力、長時間工作或偶爾遭受難堪拒絕的情況下到來。"}, {"w": "courtesan", "p": "n.", "d": "A woman who was the paid companion of wealthy, powerful men.", "c": "交際花；（宮廷）名妓", "s": "In the history of Renaissance Venice, the educated courtesan occupied an unusual social position: although excluded from respectable society, she often studied poetry and music and moved among the city's most powerful political figures.", "t": "在文藝復興時期威尼斯的歷史中，受過教育的交際花處於特殊的社會地位：雖然被排除於體面社會之外，她卻常研習詩歌與音樂，並周旋於城中最有權勢的政治人物之間。", "as": "The opera's heroine, a celebrated courtesan in nineteenth-century Paris, renounces her opulent life for love, a poignant theme that made the work an enduring favorite.", "at": "這部歌劇的女主角是十九世紀巴黎一位著名的交際花，她為愛放棄奢華的生活，這個動人的主題使此作品歷久不衰、廣受喜愛。"}, {"w": "debauch", "p": "v.", "d": "To corrupt morally or lead away from virtue.", "c": "使墮落；敗壞", "s": "Moralists in eighteenth-century London warned that cheap gin would debauch the city's working people, arguing that the drink was destroying families, encouraging crime, and leading honest laborers away from a decent, sober life.", "t": "十八世紀倫敦的道德家警告，廉價的琴酒會敗壞城中勞工的品德，主張這種酒正在摧毀家庭、助長犯罪，並使誠實的勞工偏離正派、清醒的生活。", "as": "Ancient critics charged that luxury and flattery had debauched the young emperor, transforming a once abstemious and studious prince into a dissolute and capricious tyrant feared by the entire empire.", "at": "古代的評論者指責奢華與阿諛奉承使這位年輕皇帝墮落，讓一位曾經節制又好學的王子變成全帝國畏懼、放蕩又反覆無常的暴君。"}, {"w": "braggadocio", "p": "n.", "d": "Empty, exaggerated boasting; arrogant bragging.", "c": "吹噓；誇口", "s": "The young boxer's endless braggadocio before the match, including his loud claims that he would knock out the champion in the first round, made his quick defeat even more embarrassing.", "t": "這位年輕拳擊手在賽前沒完沒了的吹噓，包括他大聲宣稱會在第一回合就擊倒冠軍，讓他迅速落敗的結局顯得更加難堪。", "as": "Beneath the general's bombastic braggadocio lay a deep insecurity, and his grandiloquent speeches to the troops could not conceal the army's long string of humiliating defeats along the northern frontier.", "at": "在這位將軍浮誇的吹噓之下，藏著深刻的不安全感，而他對部隊發表的誇大演說，也掩蓋不了軍隊在北方邊境接連吃下的屈辱敗仗。"}, {"w": "flagellate", "p": "v.", "d": "To whip or flog; to criticize severely.", "c": "鞭打；嚴厲責備", "s": "In medieval Europe, some religious groups would flagellate themselves in public processions, striking their own backs with whips as a form of penance they believed would win forgiveness for their sins.", "t": "在中世紀歐洲，一些宗教團體會在公開遊行中鞭打自己，用鞭子抽打自己的背部，作為一種他們相信能換得罪過寬恕的懺悔方式。", "as": "Rather than flagellating herself over one embarrassing gaffe, the candidate offered a candid apology and moved on, displaying an equanimity that impressed even her harshest critics in the press.", "at": "這位候選人沒有因一次難堪的失言而嚴厲自責，而是坦率地道歉後繼續前進，展現出連媒體上最嚴厲的批評者都佩服的沉著。"}, {"w": "insurgent", "p": "n.", "d": "A rebel fighting against an established government.", "c": "叛亂者；起義者", "s": "During the long civil war, each insurgent who joined the movement against the military government had to hide in the mountains, avoid army patrols, and rely on villagers for food and information.", "t": "在漫長的內戰期間，每一位加入反軍政府運動的叛亂分子都必須藏身山中、躲避軍隊巡邏，並依靠村民提供食物與情報。", "as": "The government's draconian crackdown only fueled the insurgents' animosity, and within a year their clandestine network had spread through the remote rural provinces, recruiting thousands of disillusioned young farmers.", "at": "政府嚴酷的鎮壓反而助長了叛亂分子的敵意，不到一年，他們的祕密網絡就擴散到偏遠的鄉村省分，吸收了數千名幻想破滅的年輕農民。"}, {"w": "panache", "p": "n.", "d": "Bold, confident style that attracts attention.", "c": "神氣；瀟灑的氣派", "s": "The young conductor led the orchestra with remarkable panache, sweeping her arms dramatically, smiling at the musicians, and turning even a familiar Beethoven symphony into an exciting and stylish performance.", "t": "這位年輕指揮以非凡的瀟灑氣派帶領樂團，她大幅度地揮動雙臂、對樂手們微笑，即使是一首耳熟能詳的貝多芬交響曲，也被她詮釋成一場精彩又有型的演出。", "as": "With characteristic panache, the urbane diplomat defused the volatile meeting between the two rival delegations, deftly turning a potential imbroglio into a cordial and surprisingly productive discussion.", "at": "這位溫文儒雅的外交官以他一貫的瀟灑氣派，化解了兩個敵對代表團之間一觸即發的會議，巧妙地將一場可能的糾紛轉變為友好且出乎意料有成效的討論。"}, {"w": "omnibus", "p": "adj.", "d": "Including or dealing with many different items at once.", "c": "綜合的；包含多項的", "s": "Rather than voting on dozens of separate spending measures, the legislature combined them into a single omnibus bill that funded schools, highways, hospitals, and national parks all at once, saving weeks of debate.", "t": "立法機關沒有分別就數十項支出案逐一表決，而是將它們合併成一項綜合法案，一次為學校、公路、醫院與國家公園提供經費，省下了數週的辯論時間。", "as": "Critics complained that the omnibus legislation was so convoluted that few lawmakers had actually read it, allowing lobbyists to quietly insert gratuitous provisions benefiting their wealthy clients.", "at": "批評者抱怨這項綜合法案錯綜複雜，以致很少議員讀過全文，讓說客得以悄悄塞入有利於其富有客戶、毫無必要的條款。"}, {"w": "militate", "p": "v.", "d": "To have a strong effect or influence, usually against something.", "c": "產生作用；起反作用", "s": "The company's high prices, slow delivery times, and poor customer service all militate against its chances of winning the government contract, so few analysts expected it to beat its more efficient competitors.", "t": "這家公司的高價、緩慢的交貨時間與不佳的客戶服務，都對其贏得政府合約的機會不利，因此很少分析師預期它能擊敗效率更高的競爭對手。", "as": "The candidate's reputation for duplicity militated against her campaign from the start, and no amount of effusive praise from loyal allies could mollify the skeptical voters in rural districts.", "at": "這位候選人以表裡不一聞名，這從一開始就對她的競選活動十分不利，忠實盟友再多熱情洋溢的讚揚，也無法安撫鄉村選區裡心存懷疑的選民。"}, {"w": "nihilistic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Rejecting all moral principles and believing life is meaningless.", "c": "虛無主義的；否定一切的", "s": "Many readers found the novel deeply nihilistic, since its characters reject every moral value, believe that nothing in life has meaning, and see no reason to hope for a better future.", "t": "許多讀者認為這部小說充滿虛無主義色彩，因為書中人物否定一切道德價值，相信人生沒有任何意義，也看不出有任何理由對更美好的未來抱持希望。", "as": "The playwright's nihilistic vision, articulated through a series of lugubrious monologues, alienated many audiences who had expected the ebullience and warmth of her earlier, more popular comedies.", "at": "這位劇作家透過一連串陰鬱的獨白所表達的虛無主義觀點，疏遠了許多原本期待她早期較受歡迎的喜劇那般熱情洋溢、溫馨動人的觀眾。"}, {"w": "torpid", "p": "adj.", "d": "Sluggish, inactive, and lacking energy.", "c": "遲鈍的；懶散不活潑的", "s": "During the coldest months, many reptiles become torpid, hiding in burrows or under rocks, moving very little and slowing their breathing and heartbeat until warmer weather returns and gives them the energy to hunt again.", "t": "在最寒冷的月份，許多爬蟲類會變得遲鈍不活動，躲在洞穴或石頭底下，幾乎不動，並減緩呼吸與心跳，直到天氣回暖、牠們重新有力氣捕食為止。", "as": "After the lavish banquet, the guests grew torpid and somnolent, and even the garrulous host fell silent as the dull, humid afternoon slowly wore on toward evening.", "at": "豐盛的宴席之後，賓客們變得遲鈍又昏昏欲睡，隨著沉悶潮濕的午後慢慢走向黃昏，連平時多話的主人也安靜了下來。"}, {"w": "seminal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Highly original and strongly influencing later developments.", "c": "開創性的；影響深遠的", "s": "Rachel Carson's seminal book Silent Spring, published in 1962, inspired the modern environmental movement and led directly to new laws that banned dangerous pesticides and protected wildlife across the United States for generations.", "t": "瑞秋・卡森於1962年出版的開創性著作《寂靜的春天》，啟發了現代環保運動，並直接促成禁止危險殺蟲劑、在美國各地世代保護野生動物的新法律。", "as": "The physicist's seminal paper, initially dismissed by senior colleagues as abstruse speculation, eventually engendered an entirely new field of research and a plethora of practical inventions still used today.", "at": "這位物理學家的開創性論文起初被資深同事斥為深奧難解的臆測，最終卻催生出一個全新的研究領域，以及大量至今仍在使用的實用發明。"}, {"w": "craven", "p": "adj.", "d": "Shamefully lacking in courage; cowardly.", "c": "懦弱的；膽小的", "s": "When the bully began insulting a younger student, the craven boy who had promised to defend his friend simply walked away, too frightened to say a word or even ask a teacher for help.", "t": "當那個霸凌者開始辱罵一位年紀較小的學生時，那個曾答應保護朋友的懦弱男孩竟直接走開，嚇得一句話也不敢說，甚至不敢去找老師幫忙。", "as": "Historians have long censured the council's craven capitulation to the invaders, arguing that a more resolute stance might have saved the ancient city and its people from destruction.", "at": "歷史學家長久以來一直譴責議會對侵略者懦弱的投降，主張若採取更堅定的立場，或許能讓這座古城及其人民免於毀滅。"}]}, {"unit": 38, "level": 8, "cards": [{"w": "maladroit", "p": "adj.", "d": "Clumsy or awkward, especially in handling situations.", "c": "笨拙的；不圓滑的", "s": "The ambassador's maladroit handling of the trade negotiations, including a careless remark that insulted his hosts and a missed deadline for key documents, left both governments frustrated and forced his replacement within a month.", "t": "這位大使在貿易談判中處理得十分笨拙，包括一句冒犯東道主的輕率言論，以及錯過重要文件的截止期限，令兩國政府都大感挫折，並迫使他在一個月內被撤換。", "as": "The maladroit spokesman tried to placate the angry crowd at the press conference, but his rambling and convoluted apology only deepened their animosity toward the company and its leaders.", "at": "那位笨拙的發言人試圖在記者會上安撫憤怒的群眾，但他冗長而迂迴的道歉只加深了他們對公司及其領導階層的敵意。"}, {"w": "gormandize", "p": "v.", "d": "To eat greedily and in large amounts.", "c": "狼吞虎嚥；暴飲暴食", "s": "After weeks of strict training meals, the marathon runners were tempted to gormandize at the post-race buffet, piling their plates with pastries and fried chicken until several of them felt too sick to attend the awards ceremony.", "t": "經過數週嚴格的訓練餐之後，馬拉松跑者們在賽後自助餐上忍不住狼吞虎嚥，盤子裡堆滿糕點和炸雞，直到好幾個人撐得難受，無法出席頒獎典禮。", "as": "Critics of the food festival complained that visitors came only to gormandize, and that the voracious crowds treated the region's ancient culinary legacy as nothing more than an excuse for gluttony.", "at": "這個美食節的批評者抱怨，遊客來此只為了大吃大喝，而那些貪吃的人潮只把該地區古老的飲食傳統當成暴飲暴食的藉口。"}, {"w": "polemical", "p": "adj.", "d": "Strongly attacking or defending an opinion in debate.", "c": "爭論的；論戰性的", "s": "Rather than presenting a balanced overview of the climate debate, the author wrote a polemical essay that fiercely attacked her opponents' arguments, which delighted her supporters but convinced few readers who had not already agreed with her.", "t": "這位作者沒有對氣候辯論做出平衡的概述，而是寫了一篇論戰性的文章，猛烈抨擊對手的論點，這讓她的支持者大為讚賞，卻幾乎沒有說服任何原本就不認同她的讀者。", "as": "Her polemical pamphlet, essentially a long diatribe against the factory owners, was so acerbic that even sympathetic reformers feared it would alienate the moderate voters they desperately needed.", "at": "她那本論戰性的小冊子，基本上是對工廠老闆的一篇長篇抨擊，言詞尖酸到連同情她的改革者都擔心，這會疏遠他們迫切需要的溫和派選民。"}, {"w": "epochal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely significant; marking the beginning of a new era.", "c": "劃時代的；開創新紀元的", "s": "The invention of the printing press was an epochal event in European history, because it made books affordable, spread new ideas across the continent, and helped bring about the Reformation and the Scientific Revolution.", "t": "印刷術的發明是歐洲歷史上劃時代的事件，因為它讓書籍變得平價，使新思想傳遍整個歐洲大陸，並促成了宗教改革與科學革命。", "as": "The physicist's epochal discovery was initially dismissed by hidebound colleagues, but within a decade it had become the seminal work on which an entire field of research was built.", "at": "這位物理學家劃時代的發現起初遭到思想守舊的同僚否定，但不到十年，它就成為整個研究領域賴以建立的開創性著作。"}, {"w": "cognoscenti", "p": "n.", "d": "People with expert knowledge of a particular field.", "c": "行家；鑑賞家", "s": "Although the general public largely ignored the young painter's first exhibition, the cognoscenti of the Taipei art world—critics, collectors, and gallery owners—immediately recognized her talent and began competing to acquire her early works.", "t": "雖然一般大眾大多忽視了這位年輕畫家的首次展覽，但台北藝術界的行家們——評論家、收藏家與畫廊老闆——立刻看出她的才華，並開始競相收購她的早期作品。", "as": "While the hoi polloi flocked to the summer blockbuster, the cognoscenti preferred the director's earlier, more recherché films, which they praised as subtle masterpieces of the genre.", "at": "當一般大眾湧向那部暑期賣座大片時，行家們卻更偏愛這位導演早期較為講究冷僻的電影，稱讚它們是該類型中細膩的傑作。"}, {"w": "immolate", "p": "v.", "d": "To kill as a sacrifice, especially by burning.", "c": "獻祭；焚燒犧牲", "s": "In the ancient epic studied in our literature seminar, the king prepares to immolate his finest bull on the temple altar, hoping that the sacrifice will persuade the gods to end the drought that is destroying his kingdom.", "t": "在我們文學研討課研讀的古代史詩中，國王準備在神殿祭壇上獻祭他最好的一頭公牛，希望這場犧牲能說服眾神結束那場正在摧毀他王國的旱災。", "as": "The anthropologist explained that some ancient cultures would immolate animals to propitiate their gods, a practice later reformers condemned as cruel but which believers considered sacrosanct.", "at": "這位人類學家解釋，某些古代文化會以動物獻祭來平息神明的怒氣，這種做法後來被改革者譴責為殘忍，但信徒們卻視之為神聖不可侵犯。"}, {"w": "hidebound", "p": "adj.", "d": "Narrow-minded and stubbornly resistant to new ideas.", "c": "守舊的；墨守成規的", "s": "The young engineer's proposal for solar-powered classrooms was rejected by a hidebound school board whose members insisted that the old methods had always worked well enough and saw no reason to experiment with unfamiliar technology.", "t": "這位年輕工程師提出的太陽能教室計畫，被一個守舊的校董會否決了；那些董事堅稱舊方法一向夠用，看不出有任何理由去嘗試不熟悉的技術。", "as": "The hidebound bureaucrats remained intransigent, refusing every reform proposal and treating even modest change as a dangerous threat to the comfortable sinecures they had enjoyed for decades.", "at": "那些墨守成規的官僚始終不肯讓步，拒絕每一項改革提案，甚至把小幅度的改變也視為對他們享受了數十年的舒適閒差的嚴重威脅。"}, {"w": "molder", "p": "v.", "d": "To slowly decay or crumble into dust.", "c": "腐朽；崩解成塵", "s": "For nearly a century, the explorer's journals were left to molder in a damp basement, and by the time archivists discovered them, many pages had turned to brown dust that could no longer be read.", "t": "將近一個世紀以來，這位探險家的日記被擱在潮濕的地下室裡慢慢腐朽，等到檔案管理員發現它們時，許多頁面已化為無法辨讀的褐色碎屑。", "as": "While the priceless manuscripts moldered in the neglected archive, university officials squabbled over budgets, and their dilatory response caused irreversible damage to the school's literary legacy.", "at": "當那些無價的手稿在無人照管的檔案室中逐漸腐朽時，大學官員們卻在為預算爭吵不休，他們拖延的反應對學校的文學遺產造成了無法挽回的損害。"}, {"w": "fratricide", "p": "n.", "d": "The killing of one's own brother or sister.", "c": "殺害手足；手足相殘", "s": "In the Hebrew Bible, the story of Cain and Abel presents the first act of fratricide, as Cain, consumed by jealousy over his brother's favored offering, kills Abel and is condemned to wander the earth.", "t": "在希伯來聖經中，該隱與亞伯的故事呈現了第一樁手足相殘的事件：該隱因嫉妒弟弟的祭品蒙神悅納而心生怨恨，殺害了亞伯，並被判罰在地上流離飄蕩。", "as": "Historians describe the civil war as a national fratricide whose bitter enmity lingered for generations, and whose painful ramifications still shape the regional politics of the country today.", "at": "歷史學家把這場內戰形容為一場全國性的手足相殘，其深仇大恨延續了好幾代，而它痛苦的後果至今仍影響著區域政治。"}, {"w": "splenetic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Bad-tempered, irritable, and spiteful.", "c": "脾氣暴躁的；易怒的", "s": "The critic was famous for his splenetic reviews; whenever a film disappointed him, he would write furious, insulting paragraphs about the director, as though every weak movie were a personal attack on him.", "t": "這位影評人以脾氣暴躁的評論聞名；每當一部電影令他失望，他就會寫出憤怒而帶有侮辱性的段落來批評導演，彷彿每部差勁的電影都是對他的人身攻擊。", "as": "The splenetic old senator, notoriously cantankerous and irascible, delivered a long tirade against the new budget, insulting the colleagues who had dared to support it.", "at": "這位脾氣暴躁的老參議員出了名的愛找碴又易怒，他發表了一長篇反對新預算的激烈演說，辱罵那些膽敢支持預算的同僚。"}, {"w": "ineluctable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Impossible to avoid or escape; inevitable.", "c": "不可避免的；無法逃避的", "s": "Many Greek tragedies explore the theme of ineluctable fate: no matter how hard the heroes struggle to escape the prophecy, every choice they make seems to lead them closer to the disaster they have been trying to avoid.", "t": "許多希臘悲劇探討無法逃避的命運這一主題：無論英雄們多麼努力想逃脫預言，他們所做的每個選擇似乎都把他們帶向更接近那場一直試圖避免的災難。", "as": "The economist argued that the decline of the moribund coal industry was ineluctable, and that politicians who promised its renaissance were offering voters little more than a chimera.", "at": "這位經濟學家主張，奄奄一息的煤礦業走向衰退是不可避免的，而那些承諾讓它復興的政客，給選民的不過是一場空想罷了。"}, {"w": "moribund", "p": "adj.", "d": "Dying; near the end of existence or vitality.", "c": "垂死的；瀕臨消亡的", "s": "Once a busy port, the town had become moribund by the 1980s: its factories had closed, young people had moved away to find jobs, and the few remaining shops struggled to survive on a shrinking population.", "t": "這座小鎮曾是繁忙的港口，但到了1980年代已奄奄一息：工廠紛紛關閉，年輕人為了找工作遠走他鄉，僅存的幾家商店也只能靠著日漸減少的人口苦苦支撐。", "as": "Determined to revive the moribund theater company, the new director tried to vivify its stale repertoire with bold productions, but hidebound subscribers resisted every innovation.", "at": "新任導演決心振興這個奄奄一息的劇團，試圖用大膽的製作為陳腐的劇目注入活力，但守舊的訂票會員們抵制每一項創新。"}, {"w": "bellwether", "p": "n.", "d": "Something that leads or indicates future trends.", "c": "領頭羊；（趨勢的）指標", "s": "Political analysts watch the county closely because it has long been a bellwether of national elections; for decades, the candidate who wins there has almost always gone on to win the presidency.", "t": "政治分析家密切關注這個郡，因為它長久以來一直是全國選舉的指標；數十年來，在那裡勝選的候選人幾乎總是接著贏得總統大位。", "as": "Investors regard the chipmaker as a bellwether for the entire technology sector, so its unexpectedly listless sales figures provoked widespread misgiving about the industry's prospects.", "at": "投資人把這家晶片製造商視為整個科技業的指標，因此它出乎意料的疲軟銷售數字引發了外界對該產業前景的普遍疑慮。"}, {"w": "permutation", "p": "n.", "d": "One of the possible ways a set of things can be arranged.", "c": "排列；變換", "s": "The math teacher challenged students to list every possible permutation of the letters A, B, and C, and they soon discovered that the three letters could be arranged in exactly six different orders.", "t": "數學老師要學生列出字母A、B、C每一種可能的排列方式，他們很快就發現這三個字母恰好能排成六種不同的順序。", "as": "The novel's plot went through countless permutations during revision, and the author admitted that her final, labyrinthine structure owed more to serendipity than to careful planning.", "at": "這部小說的情節在修改過程中歷經無數次變換，作者坦承，她最終那錯綜複雜的結構與其說來自周密的規劃，不如說是出於意外的機緣。"}, {"w": "interlope", "p": "v.", "d": "To intrude or interfere in other people's affairs.", "c": "干涉；闖入（他人事務）", "s": "When the two neighboring villages were negotiating a water-sharing agreement, a powerful businessman tried to interlope in their discussions, hoping to secure the river rights for his own factory before either side noticed.", "t": "當兩個相鄰的村莊正在協商共享水資源的協議時，一位有權勢的商人試圖插手他們的討論，希望在雙方察覺之前，替自己的工廠取得河川使用權。", "as": "Accused of trying to interlope in the merger talks, the lobbyist offered a glib denial, but a leaked dossier soon revealed his clandestine meetings with both companies.", "at": "這名說客被指控試圖介入合併談判，他輕描淡寫地否認，但一份外洩的檔案很快就揭露了他與兩家公司的祕密會面。"}, {"w": "hector", "p": "v.", "d": "To bully or intimidate with loud, threatening talk.", "c": "威嚇；恐嚇", "s": "The new coach believed that she could motivate her players without shouting, unlike her predecessor, who would hector them for hours after every loss until several talented athletes quit the team in frustration.", "t": "新教練相信，她不必大吼大叫也能激勵球員，不像她的前任，那位教練每次輸球後都會連續數小時威嚇球員，導致好幾名有天分的運動員在挫折中退出球隊。", "as": "Rather than hector the reluctant witnesses, the judicious defense attorney tried to cajole them gently and patiently, knowing that intimidation would only make them more obstinate.", "at": "這位明智的律師沒有威嚇那些不情願作證的證人，而是試著溫和地勸誘他們，因為他知道恐嚇只會讓他們更加頑固。"}, {"w": "dissolute", "p": "adj.", "d": "Living an immoral life devoted to pleasure and excess.", "c": "放蕩的；生活糜爛的", "s": "In the novel, the dissolute young heir wastes his family's fortune on gambling, lavish parties, and expensive horses, until his reckless lifestyle finally leaves him penniless and abandoned by the friends who once flattered him.", "t": "在這部小說中，那位生活放蕩的年輕繼承人把家族財富揮霍在賭博、奢華派對和昂貴的馬匹上，直到他魯莽的生活方式終於讓他身無分文，並被那些曾經奉承他的朋友拋棄。", "as": "The dissolute prince's spendthrift habits and endless bacchanalian feasts so scandalized his subjects that his reputation never recovered, even after he finally ascended the throne years later.", "at": "這位放蕩王子揮金如土的習性與無止盡的狂歡宴飲令子民震驚不已，即使在他登基之後，名聲也始終未能挽回。"}, {"w": "lineaments", "p": "n.", "d": "The distinctive features or outlines, especially of a face.", "c": "面部輪廓；特徵", "s": "Studying the old photograph under a magnifying glass, the historian traced the lineaments of the woman's face—the high cheekbones, the narrow chin, the deep-set eyes—and concluded that she was the poet's long-lost sister.", "t": "這位歷史學家用放大鏡仔細端詳那張老照片，描摹著那名女子臉部的輪廓——高聳的顴骨、窄小的下巴、深邃的眼睛——並斷定她就是那位詩人失散多年的妹妹。", "as": "Even in her dotage, the actress retained the elegant lineaments that had once made her the cynosure of every gathering, though her voice had grown frail and soft.", "at": "即使已屆衰老之年，這位女演員仍保有那曾使她成為每場聚會焦點的優雅輪廓，儘管她的聲音已變得虛弱而輕柔。"}, {"w": "churlish", "p": "adj.", "d": "Rude, surly, and ill-mannered.", "c": "粗魯的；沒禮貌的", "s": "After the host had spent all day preparing a special dinner for him, it seemed churlish of the guest to complain about the food, check his phone throughout the meal, and leave without saying thank you.", "t": "主人花了一整天為他準備一頓特別的晚餐，這位客人卻抱怨食物、整頓飯都在看手機，而且連聲謝謝都沒說就離開，實在顯得很沒禮貌。", "as": "It would be churlish to begrudge the winning team its moment of glory, even if their coach's braggadocio during the post-game interview struck many fans as insufferable.", "at": "即使冠軍隊教練在賽後訪問中的大言不慚讓許多球迷覺得難以忍受，吝於給予獲勝隊伍屬於他們的榮耀時刻也未免太小氣無禮了。"}, {"w": "prepossessing", "p": "adj.", "d": "Attractive; creating a favorable first impression.", "c": "討人喜歡的；給人好印象的", "s": "The candidate's prepossessing manner—her warm smile, confident handshake, and easy humor—impressed the interview panel at once, though the members still wanted to examine her research record before making a final decision.", "t": "這位應徵者討人喜歡的舉止——溫暖的微笑、自信的握手與輕鬆的幽默——立刻讓面試委員留下好印象，不過委員們在做出最終決定前，仍想仔細審查她的研究紀錄。", "as": "The hotel's exterior was hardly prepossessing, with its peeling paint and drab gray walls, but inside, guests discovered commodious rooms and a remarkably congenial staff.", "at": "這間旅館的外觀實在不怎麼討喜，油漆剝落、灰牆單調，但走進裡面，客人卻發現寬敞的房間與格外親切友善的員工。"}]}, {"unit": 39, "level": 8, "cards": [{"w": "elegiac", "p": "adj.", "d": "Expressing sorrow or mourning, especially for something lost.", "c": "哀悼的；哀傷的", "s": "Written shortly after his mother's death, the composer's final symphony has an elegiac quality; its slow, mournful melodies seem to grieve not only for her but for the vanished world of his childhood.", "t": "這位作曲家的最後一首交響曲寫於他母親過世後不久，帶有一種哀悼的氣質；那緩慢而哀傷的旋律似乎不只是為她而悲，也是為他童年那個已消逝的世界而悲。", "as": "The documentary's elegiac tone suited its subject, the moribund fishing villages of the east coast, whose plaintive folk songs now survive mostly in fragile old recordings kept by local libraries.", "at": "這部紀錄片哀傷的基調與其主題十分相稱，也就是東海岸那些日漸凋零的漁村，而那些村落哀怨的民謠如今大多只保存在錄音之中。"}, {"w": "ukase", "p": "n.", "d": "An official order or decree issued by an authority.", "c": "敕令；命令", "s": "Without consulting any teachers, the principal issued a ukase banning phones from the entire campus, and the sudden order, posted on every classroom door the next morning, took students and parents completely by surprise.", "t": "校長沒有徵詢任何教師的意見，就頒布了一道禁止全校園使用手機的命令；這項隔天早上貼在每間教室門上的突然命令，讓學生和家長完全措手不及。", "as": "The despotic governor ruled by ukase, issuing arbitrary decrees that his servile ministers enforced without question, no matter how much hardship they caused ordinary citizens.", "at": "這位專制的總督以敕令治理，頒布種種專斷的法令，而他那些卑躬屈膝的大臣無論這些法令給百姓帶來多少苦難，都毫無異議地執行。"}, {"w": "asperity", "p": "n.", "d": "Harshness or sharpness of tone or manner.", "c": "（語氣）嚴厲；粗暴", "s": "The editor's comments on the draft were written with such asperity that the young reporter nearly cried, since every note was cold, sharp, and impatient rather than helpful or encouraging.", "t": "編輯在稿子上的評語寫得如此嚴厲，讓那位年輕記者差點哭出來，因為每一條批註都冷酷、尖銳又不耐煩，既無幫助也毫無鼓勵。", "as": "She answered the reporter's impertinent question with unusual asperity, and her terse reply made it clear that she would not tolerate further intrusions into her private life.", "at": "她以罕見的嚴厲語氣回答記者那個無禮的問題，她簡短的回覆清楚表明，她不會再容忍對她私生活的進一步侵擾。"}, {"w": "delectation", "p": "n.", "d": "Great pleasure and delight; enjoyment.", "c": "愉悅；享受", "s": "For the delectation of visiting guests, the museum café prepared an elaborate tea service featuring delicate pastries, fresh fruit tarts, and rare oolong teas grown in the misty mountains of central Taiwan.", "t": "為了讓來訪貴賓盡情享受，博物館咖啡廳準備了一套精緻的下午茶，有精巧的糕點、新鮮水果塔，以及產自台灣中部雲霧繚繞山區的珍稀烏龍茶。", "as": "For the delectation of the cognoscenti, the gallery displayed a recherché collection of Song dynasty ceramics whose subtle glazes had seldom been seen outside private homes.", "at": "為了讓行家們大飽眼福，這間畫廊展出一批講究冷僻的宋代陶瓷收藏，其細膩的釉色鮮少在私人宅邸之外展示。"}, {"w": "bootless", "p": "adj.", "d": "Useless; producing no result or benefit.", "c": "無用的；徒勞的", "s": "After three hours of bootless searching through the flooded basement, the volunteers finally admitted that the missing documents had been destroyed, and they stopped digging through the mud to wait for the insurance investigator.", "t": "在淹水的地下室裡徒勞地搜索了三個小時後，志工們終於承認遺失的文件已經被毀，於是停止在泥濘中翻找，等待保險調查員到來。", "as": "Arguing with the obstinate official proved bootless; no matter how cogently the residents presented their case, he refused to rescind the order closing the neighborhood library.", "at": "與那位固執的官員爭論結果證明是徒勞的；無論居民們如何有條理地陳述理由，他都拒絕撤銷關閉社區圖書館的命令。"}, {"w": "explicate", "p": "v.", "d": "To explain something in detail; to analyze its meaning.", "c": "詳細解釋；闡明", "s": "In her lecture, the professor took nearly an hour to explicate a single short poem, carefully explaining each image, allusion, and line break until students understood meanings they had completely missed on first reading.", "t": "在講課中，教授花了將近一個小時詳細闡釋一首短詩，仔細解說每一個意象、典故和斷行，直到學生理解了他們初讀時完全忽略的含義。", "as": "The philosopher's attempt to explicate his abstruse theory only made it more convoluted, and even devoted disciples admitted they could not follow his circuitous reasoning.", "at": "這位哲學家試圖闡明他深奧的理論，結果反而讓它更加複雜難解，就連忠實的門徒都承認無法跟上他迂迴的推理。"}, {"w": "pejorative", "p": "adj.", "d": "Expressing contempt or disapproval; belittling.", "c": "貶義的；輕蔑的", "s": "Linguists note that some words change their meanings over time: \"silly\" once meant \"blessed\" or \"happy,\" but it gradually acquired a pejorative sense and is now used to criticize people as foolish.", "t": "語言學家指出，有些字詞的意義會隨時間改變：「silly」原本意指「有福的」或「快樂的」，但逐漸帶上了貶義，如今被用來批評別人愚蠢。", "as": "The columnist used \"philistine\" as a pejorative label for anyone who disliked modern art, a glib epithet that only alienated readers who might otherwise have listened to her arguments.", "at": "這位專欄作家把「庸俗之人」當作貶義標籤，套在任何不喜歡現代藝術的人身上；這個輕率的稱號只疏遠了那些原本可能會聽她論點的讀者。"}, {"w": "labyrinthine", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely complicated and confusing, like a maze.", "c": "錯綜複雜的；迷宮般的", "s": "Applying for a work visa turned out to be a labyrinthine process, as the young engineer was sent from office to office, filling out overlapping forms and following rules that seemed to contradict one another.", "t": "申請工作簽證原來是一個錯綜複雜的過程，這位年輕工程師被支使著從一個辦公室跑到另一個辦公室，填寫內容重疊的表格，遵循彼此似乎互相矛盾的規定。", "as": "The novel's labyrinthine plot, full of tangential subplots and sudden shifts in time, frustrated many readers, though the cognoscenti praised its daring structure as a modern chef-d'œuvre.", "at": "這部小說錯綜複雜的情節充滿離題的支線與突然的時間跳躍，讓許多讀者感到挫折，不過行家們卻稱讚它大膽的結構是一部現代傑作。"}, {"w": "leonine", "p": "adj.", "d": "Resembling or characteristic of a lion.", "c": "獅子般的；威武的", "s": "With his thick mane of white hair and deep, commanding voice, the old conductor had a leonine presence on stage, and the orchestra seemed to respond to his slightest gesture like a pride following its leader.", "t": "這位年長的指揮家有著一頭濃密的白髮與低沉而威嚴的嗓音，在舞台上展現獅子般的氣勢，整個樂團似乎對他最細微的手勢都有所回應，就像獅群追隨著首領。", "as": "The leonine statue guarding the temple gate was carved by a prolific sculptor whose work, once dismissed by pedantic critics, is now considered quintessential Taiwanese folk art.", "at": "守護廟門的那座獅形雕像出自一位多產的雕刻家之手，他的作品曾被賣弄學問的評論家所否定，如今卻被視為最典型的台灣民間藝術。"}, {"w": "doctrinaire", "p": "adj.", "d": "Rigidly applying a theory without regard for practical realities.", "c": "教條主義的；空談理論的", "s": "The new mayor took a doctrinaire approach to economic policy, insisting on applying his party's theories in every situation even when local business owners showed him clear evidence that the rules were harming the city.", "t": "新市長在經濟政策上採取教條主義的做法，堅持在每種情況下套用他所屬政黨的理論，即使當地商家向他出示明確證據，證明那些規定正在傷害這座城市。", "as": "The doctrinaire ideologue refused to compromise with his colleagues, dismissing every pragmatic solution as a betrayal of principle and treating anyone who questioned his theories as a dangerous heretic.", "at": "這位教條主義的空想家拒絕妥協，把務實的解決方案斥為背叛原則，並把每一位批評者都當成危險的異端。"}, {"w": "prescience", "p": "n.", "d": "Knowledge of events before they happen; foresight.", "c": "先見之明；預知", "s": "Decades before smartphones existed, the science-fiction writer described pocket-sized devices that could connect people across the world, and readers today are genuinely amazed by the prescience of her early novels.", "t": "在智慧型手機問世數十年前，這位科幻作家就描寫過能將世界各地的人連結起來的口袋型裝置，如今的讀者對她早期小說中的先見之明深感驚嘆。", "as": "Her prescience about the coming financial crisis seemed almost uncanny, and the astute investor's warnings, once dismissed as alarmist, were later fully vindicated by the events of that terrible year.", "at": "她對即將來臨的金融危機的先見之明幾乎令人覺得不可思議，這位精明投資者的警告曾被斥為危言聳聽，後來卻被事實證明是正確的。"}, {"w": "locution", "p": "n.", "d": "A particular word, phrase, or style of expression.", "c": "措辭；說法", "s": "Students of British English are often puzzled by the locution \"I'm easy,\" which does not describe someone's personality at all but simply means that the speaker has no strong preference about a choice.", "t": "學習英式英語的學生常對「I'm easy」這個說法感到困惑，它根本不是在描述某人的個性，而只是表示說話者對某個選擇沒有特別的偏好。", "as": "The author's fondness for archaic locutions gave his prose a florid, anachronistic flavor that some readers found charming and others found merely pedantic and tiresome.", "at": "這位作者偏愛古雅的措辭，使他的文章帶有一種華麗而不合時宜的風味，有些讀者覺得迷人，另一些人則只覺得賣弄學問。"}, {"w": "olfactory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Relating to the sense of smell.", "c": "嗅覺的", "s": "Dogs can detect certain diseases in humans because their olfactory abilities are extraordinary; a single dog's nose contains hundreds of millions of scent receptors, far more than the roughly six million found in ours.", "t": "狗能夠察覺人類的某些疾病，因為牠們的嗅覺能力非凡；一隻狗的鼻子裡就有數億個氣味受體，遠多於人類鼻子中大約六百萬個。", "as": "The chef's olfactory memory was prodigious; a single redolent whiff of jasmine could transport her back to her grandmother's kitchen and its vanished evening rituals.", "at": "這位主廚的嗅覺記憶驚人；只要嗅到一絲濃郁的茉莉花香，就能把她帶回祖母的廚房與那些早已消逝的傍晚儀式。"}, {"w": "logophile", "p": "n.", "d": "A lover of words.", "c": "愛好字詞的人；字詞愛好者", "s": "A true logophile, my grandfather kept three dictionaries beside his reading chair and delighted in learning unusual terms, often surprising the family at dinner by using a rare word he had discovered that afternoon.", "t": "我祖父是個真正熱愛字詞的人，他在閱讀椅旁放了三本字典，喜歡學習罕見的詞彙，常在晚餐時用一個他當天下午才發現的冷僻字，讓全家人大吃一驚。", "as": "Only a dedicated logophile would relish Elster's book, cheerfully memorizing such recherché terms as quidnunc and sesquipedalian while classmates dismissed the whole effort as pedantic.", "at": "只有真正熱愛字詞的人才會喜愛埃爾斯特的這本書，開心地背誦像「quidnunc」和「sesquipedalian」這類冷僻的詞彙，而同學們卻認為這種努力是在賣弄學問。"}, {"w": "perturb", "p": "v.", "d": "To make someone anxious, worried, or upset.", "c": "使不安；使煩惱", "s": "The unexpected drop in test scores did not seem to perturb the principal, who calmly explained to anxious parents that the new exam was harder and that the results did not reflect weaker teaching.", "t": "考試成績意外下滑似乎並沒有讓校長感到不安，他冷靜地向焦慮的家長解釋，新考試比較難，而這些成績並不代表教學品質變差。", "as": "Though the stoic captain was not easily perturbed, the sudden, ominous silence of the radio filled him with misgiving as the storm grew more violent.", "at": "雖然這位堅忍的船長不容易心慌，但隨著暴風雨越來越猛烈，無線電突然傳來的不祥寂靜仍讓他心生疑慮。"}, {"w": "dissimulate", "p": "v.", "d": "To hide one's true feelings or intentions; to pretend.", "c": "掩飾；假裝", "s": "Although she was deeply disappointed not to win the scholarship, she managed to dissimulate her feelings during the ceremony, smiling warmly and applauding as the winner walked to the stage to accept the award.", "t": "雖然沒得到獎學金讓她深感失望，但她在典禮上設法掩飾自己的情緒，在得獎者走上台領獎時，她溫暖地微笑並鼓掌。", "as": "The spy had learned to dissimulate so skillfully that even his closest friends never suspected his duplicity, interpreting his guarded manner as mere shyness rather than deliberate subterfuge.", "at": "這名間諜學會了極其高明的掩飾功夫，就連最親近的朋友都從未懷疑他的兩面手法，只把他戒備的態度當成害羞，而非刻意的欺瞞。"}, {"w": "bauble", "p": "n.", "d": "A small, showy trinket of little value.", "c": "華而不實的小飾品；小玩意兒", "s": "The tourist paid nearly a thousand dollars for what the vendor called an antique jade pendant, but an expert later told her it was merely a cheap plastic bauble produced by the thousands in a factory.", "t": "這名遊客花了將近一千元買下攤販所說的古董玉墜，但一位專家後來告訴她，那只不過是工廠大量生產的廉價塑膠小飾品。", "as": "To the ascetic monk, the emperor's jeweled crown was merely a garish bauble, a tawdry symbol of the vanity and avarice he had renounced in his youth.", "at": "對那位苦行僧而言，皇帝鑲滿珠寶的王冠不過是個俗麗的小玩意兒，是他年輕時便已捨棄的虛榮與貪婪的庸俗象徵。"}, {"w": "contrarian", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who deliberately opposes popular opinion.", "c": "唱反調的人；反向操作者", "s": "A natural contrarian, the investor bought shares in the airline just as everyone else was selling them in panic, reasoning that public fear had pushed the price far below the company's true value.", "t": "這位天生愛唱反調的投資人，在其他人都恐慌拋售航空公司股票時反而買進，他的理由是大眾的恐懼已把股價壓到遠低於公司的實際價值。", "as": "The columnist cultivated a reputation as a contrarian, gleefully disparaging every popular trend, though critics suspected her iconoclasm was less a matter of principle than of attracting attention.", "at": "這位專欄作家刻意經營唱反調的形象，興高采烈地貶低每一種流行趨勢，不過批評者懷疑她破除傳統的姿態與其說出於原則，不如說是為了博取關注。"}, {"w": "lummox", "p": "n.", "d": "A clumsy, stupid, or awkward person.", "c": "笨手笨腳的人；蠢笨的大個子", "s": "In the comic play, the hero's loyal but clumsy servant is a lovable lummox who trips over furniture, drops trays of food, and misunderstands every order, yet somehow saves his master in the final act.", "t": "在這齣喜劇中，主角忠心卻笨拙的僕人是個討人喜歡的笨蛋，他被家具絆倒、打翻餐盤，誤解每一道命令，卻不知怎地在最後一幕救了他的主人。", "as": "The maladroit lummox knocked over the priceless vase at the gala, and his flustered attempts to apologize only compounded the embarrassment of the mortified hosts.", "at": "那個笨手笨腳的大個子在晚宴上撞倒了一只無價的花瓶，他慌亂的道歉反而讓羞愧難當的主人們更加尷尬。"}, {"w": "fecund", "p": "adj.", "d": "Highly fertile; very productive or inventive.", "c": "多產的；肥沃的", "s": "The volcanic soil of the region is extraordinarily fecund, and farmers there can harvest three crops of rice each year, producing far more food than villages in the rocky highlands only fifty kilometers away.", "t": "該地區的火山土壤極其肥沃，那裡的農民每年可以收成三季稻米，產量遠遠超過僅五十公里外岩石遍布的高地村莊。", "as": "Her fecund imagination produced a seemingly inexhaustible stream of stories, and the prolific novelist wrote with such alacrity that her publisher struggled to keep pace.", "at": "她豐富的想像力似乎能源源不絕地創造故事，這位多產的小說家寫作如此迅速，連她的出版商都難以跟上她的步伐。"}]}, {"unit": 40, "level": 8, "cards": [{"w": "hoi polloi", "p": "n.", "d": "The common people; the masses.", "c": "平民百姓；一般大眾", "s": "The exclusive club once prided itself on keeping out the hoi polloi, admitting only wealthy families, but declining membership eventually forced it to open its doors to ordinary townspeople who could pay a modest fee.", "t": "這家高級俱樂部曾以拒絕平民百姓入內為傲，只接納富裕家族，但會員人數日益減少，最終迫使它向付得起少許費用的普通鎮民敞開大門。", "as": "The patrician critic sneered that the hoi polloi could never appreciate opera, but the festival's free outdoor performances drew enormous, enthusiastic crowds that belied his condescending prediction.", "at": "那位出身貴族的評論家冷笑說一般大眾永遠無法欣賞歌劇，但藝術節的免費戶外演出吸引了大批熱情的觀眾，證明他那高高在上的預言並不正確。"}, {"w": "felicitous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Well chosen and suited to the occasion; apt.", "c": "（措辭）恰當的；巧妙的", "s": "The speechwriter's felicitous phrase \"a bridge between generations\" perfectly captured the spirit of the new community center, and local newspapers quoted it in nearly every article about the opening ceremony.", "t": "撰稿人那句恰到好處的「世代之間的橋梁」完美捕捉了新社區中心的精神，當地報紙幾乎在每篇關於開幕典禮的報導中都引用了這句話。", "as": "Her felicitous choice of words helped mollify the aggrieved employees, who had expected a hollow apology but instead heard a sincere acknowledgment of the company's mistakes.", "at": "她恰如其分的措辭有助於安撫那些滿腹委屈的員工，他們原本以為只會聽到空洞的道歉，結果卻聽到公司真誠承認自己的錯誤。"}, {"w": "paean", "p": "n.", "d": "A song or speech of enthusiastic praise or triumph.", "c": "讚歌；頌詞", "s": "The documentary is essentially a ninety-minute paean to the city's night markets, celebrating their food, their vendors, and their lively atmosphere with such enthusiasm that viewers immediately want to visit Taipei.", "t": "這部紀錄片基本上是一首長達九十分鐘獻給這座城市夜市的讚歌，以極大的熱情頌揚那裡的美食、攤販與熱鬧的氣氛，讓觀眾看完立刻想去台北一遊。", "as": "The biography reads less like scholarship than a paean to its subject, and its effusive adulation of the general ignores the many blunders that historians have documented.", "at": "這本傳記讀起來與其說是學術著作，不如說是一首對傳主的頌歌，它對這位將軍熱情洋溢的吹捧，忽略了歷史學家所記載的許多重大失誤。"}, {"w": "serendipity", "p": "n.", "d": "The fortunate discovery of something good by accident.", "c": "意外發現的好運；機緣巧合", "s": "Alexander Fleming's discovery of penicillin is a classic example of serendipity: he noticed by chance that mold growing on a forgotten dish had killed the surrounding bacteria, leading to one of medicine's greatest breakthroughs.", "t": "亞歷山大·弗萊明發現盤尼西林是機緣巧合的經典例子：他偶然注意到，一個被遺忘的培養皿上長出的黴菌殺死了周圍的細菌，因而促成醫學史上最偉大的突破之一。", "as": "Through sheer serendipity, the itinerant researcher stumbled upon a cache of letters in a provincial bookshop, a fortuitous find that transformed her understanding of the poet's juvenilia.", "at": "純屬機緣巧合，這位四處奔走的研究者在一家鄉間書店意外發現一批信件，這個幸運的發現徹底改變了她對這位詩人少年習作的理解。"}, {"w": "epistolary", "p": "adj.", "d": "Relating to or written in the form of letters.", "c": "書信的；書信體的", "s": "Mary Shelley's Frankenstein is partly an epistolary novel, since much of the story is told through letters that a ship captain writes to his sister in England while exploring the frozen Arctic.", "t": "瑪麗·雪萊的《科學怪人》部分是一部書信體小說，因為故事有很大一部分是透過一位船長在北極冰原探險時寫給遠在英國的姊姊的信件來講述的。", "as": "Their epistolary friendship lasted forty years, and the voluminous correspondence, full of poignant confessions and witty badinage, is now considered a seminal document of the period.", "at": "他們之間的書信友誼持續了四十年，這批數量龐大的往來信件充滿令人動容的告白與機智的打趣，如今被視為那個時代極具影響力的文獻。"}, {"w": "gustatory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Relating to the sense of taste.", "c": "味覺的", "s": "Food scientists study the gustatory effects of sugar substitutes, measuring how strongly volunteers perceive sweetness, bitterness, and aftertaste when they sample identical drinks made with several different kinds of artificial sweeteners.", "t": "食品科學家研究代糖對味覺的影響，測量志願者在品嚐以數種不同人工甜味劑製成的相同飲料時，對甜味、苦味和餘味的感受強度。", "as": "The banquet was a gustatory delight for the deipnosophists at the table, whose erudite conversation about wine and history proved almost as satisfying as the food itself.", "at": "這場宴會對席間那些善於餐桌清談的人而言是一場味覺饗宴，他們關於葡萄酒與歷史的博學談話，幾乎和食物本身一樣令人滿足。"}, {"w": "cosset", "p": "v.", "d": "To pamper or treat with excessive care and protection.", "c": "寵愛；嬌慣", "s": "Some educators worry that parents who cosset their children too much—doing their homework, solving every conflict, and shielding them from all disappointment—leave them unprepared for the challenges of university and adult life.", "t": "一些教育工作者擔心，過度嬌慣孩子的父母——替他們寫作業、解決每一場衝突、讓他們免於一切失望——會使孩子對大學與成人生活的挑戰毫無準備。", "as": "Cosseted by doting servants since infancy, the young aristocrat grew into a petulant, indolent adult who considered even the smallest inconvenience of daily life an intolerable privation.", "at": "這位年輕貴族從小就被溺愛他的僕人們百般嬌慣，長大後成了一個任性又懶惰的人，連日常生活中最小的不便都視為無法忍受的匱乏。"}, {"w": "riposte", "p": "n.", "d": "A quick, clever reply, especially to criticism.", "c": "機智的回擊；反駁", "s": "When a heckler shouted that the candidate knew nothing about farming, she delivered a swift riposte, reminding the audience that she had grown up on a rice farm and still helped with the harvest every year.", "t": "當一名鬧場者大喊這位候選人對農業一無所知時，她迅速機智地回擊，提醒聽眾她是在稻田農家長大的，而且至今每年仍會幫忙收割。", "as": "The wit was famous for his ripostes, and his droll, mordant replies could deflate even the most bombastic opponent in a single, perfectly timed sentence.", "at": "這位才子以機智的反擊聞名，他那詼諧又辛辣的回答，只用一句時機恰到好處的話就能讓最浮誇的對手洩氣。"}, {"w": "patois", "p": "n.", "d": "A regional dialect or local form of speech.", "c": "方言；土話", "s": "Although the villagers could speak the national language when necessary, at home they used a local patois so different from standard speech that visitors from the capital could hardly understand a single sentence.", "t": "雖然村民在必要時能說國語，但在家裡他們使用一種當地方言，它與標準語差異之大，讓來自首都的訪客幾乎一句話都聽不懂。", "as": "The novelist rendered her characters' patois with such verisimilitude that readers could almost hear their voices, though some critics found the dense vernacular hard to follow.", "at": "這位小說家把筆下人物的方言描寫得極為逼真，讀者幾乎能聽見他們的聲音，不過有些評論家覺得那密集的地方口語難以理解。"}, {"w": "animadversion", "p": "n.", "d": "A critical or censorious remark; harsh criticism.", "c": "批評；責難", "s": "The senator's speech was full of animadversion against the new tax plan, and he spent nearly an hour criticizing its authors, attacking its assumptions, and condemning what he called its unfair treatment of small businesses.", "t": "這位參議員的演說充滿了對新稅制方案的責難，他花了將近一個小時批評方案的起草者、抨擊其前提假設，並譴責他所謂對小型企業的不公平待遇。", "as": "The professor's animadversions on the sophomoric essay were harsh but not gratuitous, and the chastened student later admitted that the censure had made him a better writer.", "at": "教授對那篇幼稚論文的批評雖然嚴厲，卻並非無的放矢，那名受到教訓的學生後來承認，這番責難讓他成為更好的寫作者。"}, {"w": "exegesis", "p": "n.", "d": "A critical explanation or interpretation of a text.", "c": "（經文的）詮釋；註解", "s": "Scholars have produced volumes of exegesis on a single chapter of the Analects, carefully interpreting each line to determine exactly what Confucius meant and how his teachings should be applied.", "t": "學者們針對《論語》中的單一篇章就寫出了大量的詮釋，仔細解讀每一句話，以確定孔子的確切含義以及他的教誨應如何應用。", "as": "Her exegesis of the abstruse medieval text was so clear that even neophytes could follow it, and colleagues praised it as a model of how to elucidate difficult sources.", "at": "她對那部深奧中世紀文本的詮釋如此清晰，連初學者都能理解，同僚們讚譽它是闡明艱澀文獻的典範。"}, {"w": "doyenne", "p": "n.", "d": "The most respected and experienced woman in a field.", "c": "（某領域的）女元老；女前輩", "s": "Having designed costumes for more than two hundred films over sixty years, she was widely regarded as the doyenne of Taiwanese fashion, and young designers often traveled long distances just to learn from her.", "t": "她六十年來為兩百多部電影設計過戲服，被廣泛視為台灣時尚界的女元老，年輕設計師常常不遠千里而來，只為向她學習。", "as": "The doyenne of investigative journalism, renowned for her probity and her indefatigable research, had spent five decades writing exposés that toppled several venal officials and inspired a generation of young reporters.", "at": "這位調查報導界的女元老以正直與不屈不撓的研究聞名，五十年來所寫的揭弊報導扳倒了數名貪腐官員，並啟發了一整個世代的年輕記者。"}, {"w": "acidulous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Slightly sour in taste; sharp or biting in manner.", "c": "微酸的；尖酸刻薄的", "s": "The restaurant critic's acidulous review described the chef's dessert as \"a sad puddle of overpriced sugar,\" and the sharp, biting tone of the article caused bookings to drop sharply that month.", "t": "這位餐廳評論家尖酸刻薄的評論把主廚的甜點形容為「一灘價格過高、令人難過的糖水」，文章尖銳辛辣的語氣導致那個月訂位數大幅下滑。", "as": "The aging playwright's acidulous wit, once merely sardonic, grew increasingly splenetic in his final years, and even his most loyal former acolytes gradually began to avoid his company.", "at": "這位年邁劇作家尖酸的機智原本只是帶點嘲諷，在他晚年卻變得愈來愈暴躁易怒，連過去最忠誠的追隨者也漸漸開始避開他。"}, {"w": "geld", "p": "v.", "d": "To castrate an animal, especially a horse; to weaken.", "c": "閹割（牲畜）；削弱", "s": "Experienced ranchers often geld young stallions that are not intended for breeding, because the procedure makes the horses calmer, easier to train, and far less likely to fight with other animals in the herd.", "t": "有經驗的牧場主人常會閹割不打算用來配種的年輕公馬，因為這項處理能讓馬匹更溫馴、更容易訓練，也大大降低牠們與馬群中其他動物打鬥的可能。", "as": "Critics argued that the committee's revisions would geld the anticorruption law, leaving behind a toothless statute that venal officials across the country could flout with impunity.", "at": "批評者認為，委員會的修正會削弱這部反貪腐法，只留下一紙毫無約束力的法規，讓全國各地的貪腐官員可以肆無忌憚地加以藐視。"}, {"w": "bathos", "p": "n.", "d": "An abrupt, ludicrous shift from the serious to the trivial.", "c": "突降法；由莊嚴突轉平庸", "s": "The film's dramatic final scene collapses into bathos when the hero, after a moving speech about sacrifice and freedom, suddenly slips on a banana peel, and the audience laughs instead of crying.", "t": "這部電影戲劇性的最後一幕突然從莊嚴跌入荒謬：英雄發表了一段關於犧牲與自由的感人演說後，竟突然踩到香蕉皮滑倒，觀眾因此笑了出來，而不是落淚。", "as": "The eulogy began with genuine eloquence but descended into bathos, as the speaker's maudlin anecdotes about the deceased's favorite sandwich made the solemn occasion feel almost risible.", "at": "這篇悼詞開頭確實雄辯動人，卻逐漸墜入荒謬的突降：講者關於死者最愛的三明治的那些多愁善感的軼事，讓莊嚴的場合幾乎顯得可笑。"}, {"w": "overweening", "p": "adj.", "d": "Excessively arrogant, confident, or presumptuous.", "c": "傲慢的；過度自信的", "s": "The general's overweening confidence proved disastrous; certain that his army could never be defeated, he ignored his scouts' warnings, divided his troops, and marched his soldiers straight into an obvious trap.", "t": "這位將軍過度的自信證明是一場災難；他確信自己的軍隊永遠不會被擊敗，於是無視偵察兵的警告，分散兵力，帶著士兵直接走進一個明顯的陷阱。", "as": "His overweening ambition and megalomania alienated even his staunchest allies, and the hubris that drove him to seize power ultimately hastened his dramatic downfall from the presidency.", "at": "他過度膨脹的野心與自大狂，連最忠實的盟友都疏遠了他，而驅使他奪權的狂妄自大最終也加速了他從總統大位上戲劇性的垮台。"}, {"w": "febrile", "p": "adj.", "d": "Feverish; marked by intense, nervous excitement.", "c": "發燒的；狂熱的", "s": "In the febrile final days of the campaign, volunteers worked around the clock, phones rang constantly, and rumors spread so quickly through the office that no one could tell which reports were true.", "t": "在競選活動最後那幾天狂熱的氣氛中，志工們日以繼夜地工作，電話響個不停，謠言在辦公室裡傳得飛快，沒有人分辨得出哪些消息是真的。", "as": "The febrile atmosphere on the trading floor was palpable, as anxious brokers, fearing an ineluctable crash, made frantic and impetuous decisions they would later regret.", "at": "交易大廳狂熱的氣氛清晰可感，焦慮的經紀人擔心一場無可避免的崩盤，做出種種慌亂而衝動、日後令他們後悔的決定。"}, {"w": "benighted", "p": "adj.", "d": "Ignorant or unenlightened; in a state of intellectual darkness.", "c": "無知的；愚昧的", "s": "Early European travelers often described distant cultures as benighted, assuming that people without printed books knew nothing, when in fact those societies possessed sophisticated knowledge of medicine, astronomy, and agriculture.", "t": "早期的歐洲旅行者常把遙遠的文化描述為愚昧無知，認為沒有印刷書籍的人就一無所知，但事實上那些社會擁有精深的醫學、天文與農業知識。", "as": "The reformer believed that universal education could enlighten even the most benighted regions, but her quixotic campaign to build village schools faced obstinate resistance from hidebound local elites.", "at": "這位改革者相信普及教育能啟蒙即使是最蒙昧的地區，但她興建鄉村學校的理想主義運動卻遭到守舊的地方權貴頑固抵抗。"}, {"w": "turpitude", "p": "n.", "d": "Wickedness; depravity or shameful immorality.", "c": "卑鄙；墮落", "s": "The lawyer was disbarred for moral turpitude after investigators proved that he had stolen money from elderly clients, forged their signatures, and lied repeatedly to the court to cover up his crimes.", "t": "這名律師在調查人員證實他偷竊年長客戶的錢、偽造他們的簽名，並一再向法院說謊以掩蓋罪行之後，因道德敗壞而被吊銷律師資格。", "as": "The novel exposes the turpitude of a venal aristocracy whose perfidious schemes and endless greed ultimately destroy the very kingdom that its members had solemnly sworn to protect.", "at": "這部小說揭露了一個貪腐貴族階層的卑劣，他們背信棄義的陰謀與無止境的貪婪，最終毀掉了其成員曾莊嚴發誓要保護的王國。"}, {"w": "imprecation", "p": "n.", "d": "A spoken curse; a word or phrase calling down evil.", "c": "詛咒；咒罵", "s": "In the Greek tragedy, the banished king stands at the city gates and utters a terrible imprecation, calling on the gods to bring plague and ruin upon the citizens who drove him into exile.", "t": "在這齣希臘悲劇中，被放逐的國王站在城門口發出可怕的詛咒，祈求眾神降下瘟疫與毀滅，懲罰那些把他驅逐流亡的市民。", "as": "Muttering imprecations under his breath, the irascible captain berated his exhausted crew for their dilatory work on the damaged sails and vowed to dock their wages at the next port.", "at": "這位易怒的船長低聲咒罵著，斥責疲憊不堪的船員修補破損船帆時拖拖拉拉，並揚言到了下一個港口就要扣他們的工資。"}]}, {"unit": 41, "level": 9, "cards": [{"w": "simper", "p": "v.", "d": "To smile in a silly, affected, self-conscious way.", "c": "傻笑；矯揉造作地笑", "s": "Instead of answering the reporter's pointed question about the missing funds, the young celebrity would only simper at the cameras and toss her hair, a coy, affected response that left viewers convinced she was hiding something.", "t": "這位年輕名人沒有回答記者關於失蹤款項的尖銳問題，只是對著鏡頭矯揉造作地傻笑並甩甩頭髮；這種故作羞怯的回應讓觀眾確信她有所隱瞞。", "as": "In Regency-era satirical novels, obsequious suitors simper at wealthy patrons while privately disparaging them, a duplicity the narrator exposes with gentle but thoroughly unsparing irony.", "at": "在攝政時期的諷刺小說中，諂媚的追求者對富有的贊助人矯揉造作地傻笑，私下卻對他們百般貶低；敘事者以溫和卻毫不留情的反諷揭露了這種表裡不一。"}, {"w": "denude", "p": "v.", "d": "To strip something of its covering; to make bare.", "c": "剝光；使裸露", "s": "Decades of illegal logging and overgrazing helped denude the once-forested hillsides, leaving bare slopes that could no longer absorb heavy rainfall and making the villages below far more vulnerable to devastating mudslides.", "t": "數十年來的非法伐木與過度放牧使原本林木茂密的山坡變得光禿，留下再也無法吸收豪雨的裸露坡地，也讓山下的村莊更容易遭受毀滅性土石流的侵襲。", "as": "The voracious locust swarm denuded thousands of hectares of farmland within days, and the ensuing famine engendered a profound and lasting malaise throughout the impoverished agricultural region.", "at": "那群貪婪的蝗蟲在數日內啃光了數千公頃農田，隨之而來的饑荒在那個貧困的農業地區引發了深刻而持久的萎靡不振。"}, {"w": "sui generis", "p": "adj.", "d": "Unique; in a class by itself.", "c": "獨特的；自成一類的", "s": "Critics struggled to classify the novel, which blended memoir, botanical notes, and invented folklore; most eventually concluded that it was simply sui generis, a work so original that it belonged to no existing genre or literary tradition.", "t": "評論家難以為這部小說歸類，因為它融合了回憶錄、植物筆記與虛構的民間傳說；大多數人最後認定它完全自成一類，是一部原創到不屬於任何既有文類或文學傳統的作品。", "as": "The composer's eclectic style, which juxtaposed Baroque counterpoint with West African drumming, struck many seasoned reviewers as genuinely sui generis rather than merely derivative or imitative.", "at": "這位作曲家兼容並蓄的風格將巴洛克對位法與西非鼓樂並置，在許多資深樂評看來真正自成一格，而非只是衍生或模仿之作。"}, {"w": "jeremiad", "p": "n.", "d": "A long, mournful complaint or lament about society.", "c": "哀訴；悲嘆的長篇大論", "s": "The retired professor's commencement speech turned into a jeremiad about the decline of reading, as he spent nearly forty minutes lamenting shortened attention spans, shuttered libraries, and a generation that, he claimed, preferred screens to books.", "t": "這位退休教授的畢業典禮致詞變成一篇哀嘆閱讀衰落的長篇悲歌，他花了將近四十分鐘感嘆注意力變短、圖書館關閉，以及他所稱偏好螢幕勝於書本的一代人。", "as": "The columnist's weekly jeremiads against the city's modern architecture grew so lugubrious and repetitive that even loyal readers who largely shared his misgivings began quietly skipping them.", "at": "這位專欄作家每週抨擊城市現代建築的哀訴變得如此悲戚又重複，連大致認同他疑慮的忠實讀者也開始悄悄跳過不讀。"}, {"w": "sobriquet", "p": "n.", "d": "A nickname, often humorous or affectionate.", "c": "綽號；外號", "s": "Because of his unshakable calm during the most dangerous rescue missions, the veteran firefighter earned the sobriquet \"Iceman\" from his crew, a name that eventually appeared even in official newspaper reports about his career.", "t": "由於在最危險的救援任務中始終鎮定自若，這名資深消防員從隊友那裡得到「冰人」的綽號，這個名號後來甚至出現在報紙對他職業生涯的正式報導中。", "as": "The flamboyant impresario relished his sobriquet, 'the Showman of Broadway,' and for decades never missed a single chance to aggrandize his fame through lavish and ostentatious premieres.", "at": "那位浮誇的演出經紀人很得意自己「百老匯秀場之王」的綽號，數十年來從不放過任何機會，以奢華又張揚的首演來抬高自己的名聲。"}, {"w": "regnant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Reigning or ruling; dominant or widespread.", "c": "統治的；佔優勢的", "s": "For much of the twentieth century, behaviorism was the regnant theory in American psychology departments, so researchers who wanted to study inner mental states often struggled to find funding, publishers, or sympathetic colleagues.", "t": "二十世紀大部分時間裡，行為主義是美國心理學系中佔主導地位的理論，因此想研究內在心理狀態的學者常常難以找到經費、出版商或志同道合的同事。", "as": "When the elderly regnant queen died without an heir, a bitter schism divided the nobility, and rival factions began plotting machinations to seize the vacant throne.", "at": "那位年邁的在位女王駕崩且無子嗣，一場激烈的分裂撕裂了貴族階層，敵對派系開始密謀各種詭計，企圖奪取空懸的王位。"}, {"w": "hauteur", "p": "n.", "d": "Haughtiness; an arrogant, superior manner.", "c": "傲慢；高傲", "s": "The new manager treated the factory workers with such hauteur, refusing to learn their names and speaking to them only through his assistant, that within months several experienced employees had resigned in protest.", "t": "這位新經理對工廠員工如此傲慢，不肯記住他們的名字，只透過助理與他們說話，以致幾個月內就有數名資深員工憤而辭職。", "as": "The aristocrat's icy hauteur and supercilious remarks alienated the villagers, who privately mocked him as a pompous, strutting popinjay whenever he rode through their muddy streets.", "at": "那位貴族冰冷的傲慢與目中無人的言語疏遠了村民，每當他騎馬經過泥濘的街道，村民便私下嘲笑他是個自命不凡、趾高氣揚的紈褲子弟。"}, {"w": "paterfamilias", "p": "n.", "d": "The male head of a family or household.", "c": "家長；（男性）一家之主", "s": "In ancient Roman law, the paterfamilias held extraordinary authority over his household, controlling the property of his adult children and even deciding whom his sons and daughters would be permitted to marry.", "t": "在古羅馬法中，家長對其家族擁有極大的權威，掌控成年子女的財產，甚至決定兒女可以和誰結婚。", "as": "As the family's venerable paterfamilias, Grandfather Lin presided over the annual Lunar New Year reunion with avuncular warmth, though his final word on all matters of inheritance remained inviolable.", "at": "身為家族德高望重的大家長，林爺爺以慈祥長輩的溫暖主持每年的農曆新年團圓聚會，但在一切遺產問題上，他的最終決定仍不容違背。"}, {"w": "apogee", "p": "n.", "d": "The highest or farthest point; a peak or climax.", "c": "頂點；遠地點", "s": "Many historians describe the eighteenth century as the apogee of Qing power, a period when the empire's territory, wealth, and cultural achievements reached heights that later rulers would never manage to equal.", "t": "許多史學家將十八世紀形容為清朝國力的巔峰，那段時期帝國的疆域、財富與文化成就達到了後世統治者再也無法企及的高度。", "as": "At the apogee of her fame, the soprano was lionized by critics and adored by the cognoscenti, yet she remained remarkably shy and diffident whenever she stepped offstage.", "at": "在聲名巔峰時期，這位女高音受到樂評家的追捧與行家的喜愛，但她一走下舞台，卻依然出奇地害羞而缺乏自信。"}, {"w": "mien", "p": "n.", "d": "A person's appearance, bearing, or manner.", "c": "風度；神態", "s": "Even during the most heated moments of the trial, the elderly judge maintained a calm and dignified mien, so that lawyers on both sides felt that her composed expression and steady bearing gave the courtroom a sense of order.", "t": "即使在審判最激烈的時刻，這位年長的法官仍保持冷靜而莊重的神態，因此雙方律師都覺得，她沉著的表情與穩重的儀態為法庭帶來了秩序感。", "as": "Beneath the general's stern, imperious mien lay a surprisingly magnanimous temperament, as the many defeated enemy soldiers he quietly pardoned after the war would later attest.", "at": "在這位將軍嚴厲而專橫的神態之下，藏著出人意料的寬宏性情；戰後被他悄悄赦免的眾多敵軍士兵日後都能證明這一點。"}, {"w": "dyspeptic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Irritable and gloomy, as if suffering from indigestion.", "c": "消化不良的；脾氣乖戾的", "s": "The theater critic was famously dyspeptic, greeting nearly every new production with sour, grumbling reviews, so readers were astonished when he praised a student musical as the most joyful performance he had seen in years.", "t": "這位劇評家以脾氣乖戾出名，幾乎對每一部新作都給予尖酸、牢騷滿腹的評論，因此當他稱讚一齣學生音樂劇是他多年來看過最歡樂的演出時，讀者都大吃一驚。", "as": "The dyspeptic editor, perpetually irascible and censorious, scrawled caustic comments across every single manuscript that crossed his cluttered desk, sparing not even the work of his most gifted young writers.", "at": "那位脾氣乖戾的編輯總是易怒又愛挑剔，在每一份送到他凌亂桌上的稿件上潦草寫下尖刻的評語，連他最有才華的年輕作者的作品也不放過。"}, {"w": "anaphora", "p": "n.", "d": "Repetition of a word or phrase at the start of successive clauses.", "c": "首語重複法；首句重複", "s": "Martin Luther King Jr.'s repetition of \"I have a dream\" at the start of successive sentences is a famous example of anaphora, a rhetorical device that builds emotional momentum by returning again and again to the same opening words.", "t": "馬丁・路德・金恩在連續句子開頭重複「我有一個夢想」，是首語重複法的著名例子；這種修辭技巧藉由一再回到相同的開頭詞語來累積情感張力。", "as": "Churchill's sonorous anaphora—'we shall fight on the beaches, we shall fight on the landing grounds'—was anything but banal; it galvanized a nation facing imminent cataclysm.", "at": "邱吉爾那段鏗鏘有力的首語重複——「我們將在海灘上作戰，我們將在登陸地作戰」——絕非陳腔濫調；它激勵了一個面臨迫在眉睫之浩劫的國家。"}, {"w": "philander", "p": "v.", "d": "(Of a man) to have casual love affairs; to flirt.", "c": "拈花惹草；玩弄感情", "s": "In many Victorian novels, a charming aristocrat who continues to philander after his engagement is eventually exposed, and the narrator uses his downfall to criticize a society that excused men's broken promises while harshly judging women.", "t": "在許多維多利亞時代小說中，一名在訂婚後仍繼續拈花惹草的迷人貴族最終會被揭穿，敘事者藉他的垮台批判一個寬待男人背信、卻嚴厲評判女人的社會。", "as": "Biographers note that the king's tendency to philander provoked a scandal at the royal court, and his duplicitous excuses only deepened the animus of his estranged queen.", "at": "傳記作家指出，這位國王拈花惹草的習性在王室宮廷引發醜聞，而他虛偽的藉口只加深了與他疏遠的王后的敵意。"}, {"w": "missive", "p": "n.", "d": "A letter, especially a long or official one.", "c": "信件；公函", "s": "The museum's new exhibit displays a handwritten missive that the general sent to his commanders on the eve of battle, a four-page letter in which he outlined his strategy and urged his officers to show mercy toward civilians.", "t": "博物館的新展覽展出一封將軍在戰役前夕寄給各指揮官的親筆信函；在這封四頁長的信中，他概述了作戰策略，並敦促軍官們善待平民。", "as": "The ambassador's brief missive, devoid of the usual diplomatic euphemism, was construed by the suspicious rival government as a blunt ultimatum demanding the immediate withdrawal of troops.", "at": "大使那封簡短的公函毫無慣常的外交委婉說法，被心存疑慮的敵對政府解讀為要求立即撤軍的直截了當的最後通牒。"}, {"w": "penultimate", "p": "adj.", "d": "Next to last; second from the end.", "c": "倒數第二的", "s": "The runner held a comfortable lead until the penultimate lap of the race, but on that next-to-last circuit of the track she pulled a muscle, and two competitors passed her before the final lap even began.", "t": "這名跑者一路保持舒適的領先，直到比賽的倒數第二圈；她在那一圈拉傷了肌肉，最後一圈還沒開始就被兩名對手超越。", "as": "In the penultimate chapter, the novelist finally provides the long-awaited denouement, leaving the brief last chapter as a quiet, elegiac coda that reflects on loss and memory.", "at": "在倒數第二章，小說家終於揭開期待已久的結局，讓簡短的最後一章成為一段沉靜而哀婉的尾聲，反思失落與記憶。"}, {"w": "zeitgeist", "p": "n.", "d": "The spirit, mood, or outlook of a particular era.", "c": "時代精神；時代思潮", "s": "Novels such as The Great Gatsby captured the zeitgeist of the 1920s so vividly that historians still quote them, since their restless parties, new money, and quiet disillusionment reflect the mood and values of an entire generation.", "t": "像《大亨小傳》這樣的小說如此生動地捕捉了一九二〇年代的時代精神，因此歷史學家至今仍會引用；書中躁動的派對、新富階層與隱隱的幻滅，反映了整整一代人的情緒與價值觀。", "as": "The documentary argues that punk rock embodied the zeitgeist of disaffected youth in the 1970s, whose nihilistic lyrics expressed a profound ennui with mainstream consumer culture.", "at": "這部紀錄片主張，龐克搖滾體現了一九七〇年代心懷不滿的青年的時代精神，他們虛無主義的歌詞表達出對主流消費文化深沉的倦怠。"}, {"w": "sententious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Given to pompous moralizing; full of maxims.", "c": "好說教的；滿口格言的", "s": "Students grew tired of the guest speaker's sententious lecture, which offered little practical advice and instead strung together pompous moral sayings about hard work, humility, and gratitude, delivered in the tone of a disappointed preacher.", "t": "學生們對這位客座講者好說教的演講感到厭倦，因為演講沒提供什麼實用建議，反而串起一句句關於勤奮、謙遜與感恩的浮誇道德格言，語氣活像一位失望的傳道者。", "as": "Polonius's sententious advice to his son, a string of platitudes about thrift and loyalty, is often quoted reverently, though Shakespeare clearly intended it to sound rather pedantic.", "at": "波隆尼爾給兒子那番好說教的忠告——一連串關於節儉與忠誠的陳腔濫調——常被人恭敬地引用，但莎士比亞顯然有意讓它聽起來相當迂腐賣弄。"}, {"w": "interdict", "p": "v.", "d": "To prohibit or forbid officially.", "c": "禁止；制止", "s": "To protect the endangered coral reef, the government voted to interdict all commercial fishing within twenty kilometers of the island, and coast guard patrols now board any vessel suspected of violating the new ban.", "t": "為了保護瀕危的珊瑚礁，政府投票通過禁止在該島二十公里範圍內進行一切商業捕撈，海巡隊如今會登檢任何涉嫌違反這項新禁令的船隻。", "as": "The church council moved to interdict the heterodox sermons of the itinerant preacher, whose rapidly growing following the bishops regarded as the beginning of a dangerous schism.", "at": "教會議會著手禁止那位巡迴傳道者的異端講道，因為主教們認為他迅速增加的追隨者是一場危險分裂的開端。"}, {"w": "malaise", "p": "n.", "d": "A vague feeling of discomfort, unease, or decline.", "c": "不適；萎靡不振", "s": "Economists described a deep malaise spreading through the region after the factories closed: unemployment remained high, young people moved away, and those who stayed reported a vague but persistent sense that things would never improve.", "t": "經濟學家形容，工廠關閉後，一股深沉的萎靡不振蔓延整個地區：失業率居高不下，年輕人紛紛外移，留下來的人則說自己有種模糊卻揮之不去的感覺，認為情況永遠不會好轉。", "as": "The patient complained of a general malaise and persistent lassitude, symptoms so nebulous that the doctors initially dismissed them as minor until blood tests revealed a serious infection.", "at": "這名病患抱怨全身不適與持續的倦怠，這些症狀如此模糊，以致醫生起初認為無關緊要，直到驗血發現嚴重感染。"}, {"w": "progeny", "p": "n.", "d": "Offspring or descendants of a person, animal, or plant.", "c": "子孫；後代", "s": "The botanist carefully recorded the traits of the original rose and its progeny across five generations, noting that many of the plant's descendants inherited its deep red color but not its unusual resistance to disease.", "t": "這位植物學家仔細記錄了原始玫瑰及其五代後代的特徵，並指出這株植物的許多後代遺傳了它的深紅色，卻沒有遺傳它對病害罕見的抵抗力。", "as": "The aging plutocrat feared that his indolent progeny would squander within a single generation the vast fortune he had amassed through decades of parsimonious living and shrewd investment.", "at": "這位年邁的富豪擔心，他那些懶散的子孫會在一代之內揮霍掉他數十年來靠省吃儉用與精明投資累積的巨大財富。"}]}, {"unit": 42, "level": 9, "cards": [{"w": "belie", "p": "v.", "d": "To give a false impression of; to contradict.", "c": "掩飾；與……不符", "s": "The marathon runner's slight frame and quiet voice belie her extraordinary endurance; few spectators who see her at the starting line would ever guess that she has already won three ultramarathons across the desert.", "t": "這名馬拉松跑者纖瘦的身形與輕柔的嗓音，掩飾了她驚人的耐力；在起跑線上看到她的觀眾，很少有人猜得到她已經贏過三場橫越沙漠的超級馬拉松。", "as": "The senator's jovial public persona belied a vindictive streak, and aides who crossed him soon found themselves marginalized and quietly excluded from every important policy meeting.", "at": "這位參議員在公眾面前的開朗形象，掩蓋了他記仇的一面；得罪他的助理很快就發現自己被邊緣化，悄悄地被排除在每一場重要的政策會議之外。"}, {"w": "factotum", "p": "n.", "d": "A person employed to do all kinds of work.", "c": "雜役；打雜的人", "s": "At the tiny rural museum, the only paid employee served as a kind of factotum, selling tickets, repairing display cases, answering the phone, guiding tours, and even mowing the lawn before visitors arrived each weekend.", "t": "在這座小小的鄉間博物館裡，唯一的支薪員工就像個萬事包辦的雜役：賣票、修理展示櫃、接電話、導覽解說，甚至在每個週末遊客到來前修剪草坪。", "as": "The eccentric novelist relied entirely on his loyal factotum, a stalwart and indefatigable assistant who managed his correspondence, cooked his meals, and placated the angry publishers he constantly ignored.", "at": "這位古怪的小說家完全依賴他忠心的雜役——一位可靠又不知疲倦的助手，替他處理書信、為他煮飯，還安撫被他一再冷落而憤怒的出版商。"}, {"w": "jingoism", "p": "n.", "d": "Extreme, aggressive patriotism favoring a warlike foreign policy.", "c": "沙文主義；好戰的愛國主義", "s": "Historians argue that the wave of jingoism sweeping through European newspapers in 1914, with their boastful headlines promising a quick and glorious victory, made it far harder for diplomats to prevent the outbreak of war.", "t": "史學家認為，一九一四年席捲歐洲報紙的好戰愛國狂熱，以誇耀的標題承諾一場速戰速決的光榮勝利，使外交官更難阻止戰爭爆發。", "as": "The demagogue's strident jingoism, combined with xenophobia aimed at immigrant workers, inflamed the restless crowds and drowned out the few calm voices calling for patient negotiation.", "at": "那名煽動家刺耳的好戰愛國主義，加上針對移工的仇外心態，激怒了躁動的群眾，淹沒了少數呼籲耐心談判的冷靜聲音。"}, {"w": "gainsay", "p": "v.", "d": "To deny or contradict; to speak against.", "c": "否認；反駁", "s": "No one on the review panel could gainsay the importance of the young researcher's discovery, since her data had been confirmed by three independent laboratories and explained a puzzle that had baffled scientists for decades.", "t": "評審小組中沒有人能否認這位年輕研究者的發現的重要性，因為她的數據已經獲得三間獨立實驗室證實，並解開了困擾科學家數十年的難題。", "as": "Though critics may cavil about his methods, few would gainsay the senator's probity, for in thirty years of public office he never once accepted a single dubious perquisite.", "at": "雖然批評者可能對他的方法吹毛求疵，卻很少有人能否認這位參議員的正直，因為在三十年的公職生涯中，他從未接受過任何一項可疑的額外好處。"}, {"w": "neology", "p": "n.", "d": "The coining of new words; a newly coined word.", "c": "新詞創造；新詞", "s": "Shakespeare's gift for neology is legendary: words such as \"eyeball,\" \"swagger,\" and \"lonely\" first appear in his plays, suggesting that he invented, or at least popularized, many terms that English speakers still use every day.", "t": "莎士比亞創造新詞的天分眾所皆知：諸如「eyeball」、「swagger」和「lonely」等字最早出現在他的劇作中，顯示他發明或至少推廣了許多英語使用者至今仍天天使用的詞彙。", "as": "The ubiquitous jargon of the technology industry relies heavily on neology, coining terms like 'blog' so quickly that dictionary editors must constantly revise their nomenclature.", "at": "科技業隨處可見的行話高度依賴新詞創造，「blog」之類的詞造得如此之快，字典編輯必須不斷修訂他們的術語體系。"}, {"w": "excrescence", "p": "n.", "d": "An abnormal outgrowth; an ugly, unwanted addition.", "c": "贅生物；多餘的累贅", "s": "Preservationists called the glass parking tower an excrescence on the historic square, arguing that the ugly, oversized addition spoiled the harmony of the eighteenth-century buildings that surrounded it on every side.", "t": "古蹟保存人士稱這座玻璃停車塔是這座歷史廣場上的贅瘤，主張這個醜陋又過大的增建物破壞了四周十八世紀建築的和諧。", "as": "The dermatologist reassured the anxious patient that the small excrescence on his shoulder was benign, a harmless blemish that could be removed without any deleterious effects.", "at": "皮膚科醫師向焦慮的病患保證，他肩上的小贅生物是良性的，只是無害的瑕疵，可以切除而不會造成任何不良影響。"}, {"w": "corbel", "p": "n.", "d": "A projecting stone or wooden bracket supporting a structure.", "c": "（建築）托架；梁托", "s": "Looking up at the cathedral wall, the architecture students noticed that each stone corbel jutting from the masonry was carved into a grinning face, yet every one also served the practical purpose of supporting the heavy roof beams.", "t": "抬頭仰望大教堂的牆面，建築系學生注意到，每一個從石牆突出的石托架都雕成咧嘴笑的臉，但每一個同時也具有支撐沉重屋梁的實際功能。", "as": "The medieval castle's castellated towers rested on massive corbels, and guides explained that these ponderous stone brackets had remained virtually immutable for nearly eight centuries.", "at": "那座中世紀城堡的城垛塔樓建在巨大的托架上，導覽員解說，這些沉重的石托架近八個世紀以來始終紋風不動。"}, {"w": "sedulous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Diligent, persevering, and painstakingly careful.", "c": "勤勉的；孜孜不倦的", "s": "Through years of sedulous research, checking every census record and ship manifest by hand, the historian finally traced the immigrant family from a small fishing village in Fujian to a bustling neighborhood in San Francisco.", "t": "經過多年孜孜不倦的研究，親手核對每一份人口普查紀錄與船隻乘客名單，這位歷史學家終於追溯出這個移民家族從福建小漁村到舊金山熱鬧街區的足跡。", "as": "Only by sedulous effort did the young polymath master six languages, and her assiduous study habits became an exemplary model for the younger students in her dormitory.", "at": "這位年輕的博學者憑著孜孜不倦的努力才精通六種語言，她勤勉的讀書習慣成為宿舍裡學弟妹的典範。"}, {"w": "maunder", "p": "v.", "d": "To talk or move in a rambling, aimless way.", "c": "嘮叨；漫無目的地閒晃", "s": "The guest speaker began to maunder about his childhood, his favorite restaurants, and the weather in Europe, wandering from topic to topic so aimlessly that the students never learned anything about the engineering career he had been invited to discuss.", "t": "這位客座講者開始漫無邊際地嘮叨他的童年、喜歡的餐廳和歐洲的天氣，話題東拉西扯，以致學生始終沒聽到他受邀來談的工程職涯。", "as": "Instead of offering a lucid précis of the report, the flustered official maundered through a discursive and largely irrelevant account of the committee's internal disputes.", "at": "那位慌亂的官員沒有對報告做出清楚的摘要，反而嘮嘮叨叨地講了一大段東拉西扯、大多無關的委員會內部爭執。"}, {"w": "saltation", "p": "n.", "d": "Leaping or jumping; an abrupt evolutionary change.", "c": "跳躍；（演化上的）突變", "s": "Some early biologists believed that new species arose through saltation, a sudden leap from one form to another in a single generation, rather than through the slow accumulation of tiny changes that Darwin described.", "t": "一些早期生物學家相信，新物種是透過跳躍式突變產生的，也就是在一代之間從一種形態突然躍變為另一種，而不是達爾文所描述的微小變化緩慢累積。", "as": "Geologists explained that sand grains move across the desert by saltation, bouncing in short, sporadic hops, and that this ubiquitous process gradually reshapes even the largest dunes.", "at": "地質學家解釋，沙粒以跳躍的方式移動越過沙漠，斷斷續續地短距離彈跳，而這個無所不在的過程會逐漸改變最巨大沙丘的形狀。"}, {"w": "anodyne", "p": "n.", "d": "Something that relieves pain or soothes distress.", "c": "止痛藥；慰藉之物", "s": "Before modern medicine, many doctors prescribed opium as an anodyne for patients recovering from surgery, although they did not yet understand how dangerously addictive the drug that soothed their pain could become.", "t": "在現代醫學出現之前，許多醫生會開立鴉片給術後康復中的病患作為止痛藥，雖然他們當時還不了解這種能舒緩疼痛的藥物會有多危險的成癮性。", "as": "For the disconsolate poet, music became an anodyne, temporarily assuaging her grief, though it could never fully efface the memory of the brother she had lost.", "at": "對那位悲痛欲絕的詩人而言，音樂成了一種慰藉，暫時舒緩她的悲傷，卻永遠無法完全抹去她對失去的哥哥的記憶。"}, {"w": "autodidactic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Self-taught; having learned without formal instruction.", "c": "自學的；無師自通的", "s": "Benjamin Franklin's autodidactic approach to learning is remarkable: having left school at ten, he taught himself science, French, and several musical instruments by reading borrowed books late into the night.", "t": "班傑明・富蘭克林自學的學習方式相當了不起：十歲便離開學校的他，靠著深夜閱讀借來的書籍，自學了科學、法語和好幾種樂器。", "as": "The autodidactic inventor, who had never attended a university, was initially derided by erudite engineers, yet his seminal patents eventually transformed the entire telegraph industry.", "at": "這位自學成才的發明家從未上過大學，起初遭到博學的工程師們嘲笑，但他開創性的專利最終改變了整個電報產業。"}, {"w": "jocund", "p": "adj.", "d": "Cheerful, merry, and lighthearted.", "c": "歡樂的；快活的", "s": "Wordsworth's famous poem describes a field of golden daffodils dancing in the breeze, explaining that a poet could not help but be jocund in such cheerful company and remember the scene with joy for years.", "t": "華茲華斯的名詩描寫一片在微風中起舞的金黃水仙，說明詩人在如此歡快的陪伴下不禁心情愉悅，並且多年後回想起那景象仍滿懷喜悅。", "as": "The jocund festival, with its convivial feasts and lively music, offered villagers a welcome respite from the tribulations of a long and difficult harvest season.", "at": "這場歡樂的節慶有熱鬧的宴席和輕快的音樂，讓村民在漫長艱辛的收成季節磨難之後，獲得了難得的喘息。"}, {"w": "simulacrum", "p": "n.", "d": "An image or representation; a superficial imitation.", "c": "影像；虛有其表的模仿", "s": "Critics complained that the theme park's replica of a Venetian street was merely a simulacrum of Italy, a plastic imitation with painted canals and piped-in music that captured none of the real city's history or life.", "t": "評論家抱怨，主題樂園仿造的威尼斯街道只是義大利的虛假仿製品，一個有著彩繪運河與播放背景音樂的塑膠仿品，完全沒有捕捉到真實城市的歷史與生活。", "as": "The authoritarian regime staged a simulacrum of democracy, holding elections whose outcomes were preordained, and dissidents who exposed the travesty were swiftly ostracized or imprisoned.", "at": "那個威權政權上演一場民主的假象，舉行結果早已註定的選舉，揭露這場鬧劇的異議人士很快就遭到排擠或監禁。"}, {"w": "lambent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Softly glowing or flickering; lightly brilliant.", "c": "（光）柔和閃爍的；（才智）輕快靈動的", "s": "In the painting, a single candle casts a lambent light across the sleeping child's face, its soft, flickering glow creating a warm contrast with the deep shadows that fill the rest of the room.", "t": "在這幅畫中，一支蠟燭在熟睡孩子的臉上投下柔和閃爍的光，那輕柔搖曳的光芒與充滿房間其他角落的濃重陰影形成溫暖的對比。", "as": "The essayist's lambent wit, never acerbic or mean-spirited, illuminated even the most abstruse philosophical questions, which helped make her books surprisingly popular with ordinary readers.", "at": "這位散文家輕快靈動的機智從不尖酸刻薄，即使是最深奧的哲學問題也能被照亮，這使她的書在一般讀者間意外受歡迎。"}, {"w": "supervene", "p": "v.", "d": "To occur as an unexpected or interrupting development.", "c": "意外發生；接踵而來", "s": "The expedition had planned to reach the summit by noon, but the guides warned that violent storms often supervene without warning at that altitude, and indeed one struck an hour into the climb, forcing the team to descend.", "t": "探險隊原本計劃中午前登頂，但嚮導警告，在那樣的海拔，猛烈的暴風雪常會毫無預警地突然來襲；果然，攀登一小時後暴風雪就來了，迫使隊伍撤退下山。", "as": "The ambassador's peace mission seemed auspicious until a sudden military coup supervened, plunging the capital into chaos and rendering every one of the previous negotiations completely nugatory.", "at": "大使的和平任務起初看似前景樂觀，直到一場突如其來的軍事政變橫生枝節，讓首都陷入混亂，也使先前所有的談判變得毫無意義。"}, {"w": "vainglorious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Excessively proud and boastful of one's own achievements.", "c": "自負的；虛榮誇耀的", "s": "The vainglorious general erected enormous statues of himself in every conquered city and ordered poets to praise his victories, yet historians note that most of his battles were actually won by his more modest officers.", "t": "那位自負的將軍在每座被征服的城市都豎立巨大的自己雕像，並命令詩人歌頌他的勝利，但史學家指出，他的大多數戰役其實是由較謙遜的軍官打贏的。", "as": "The vainglorious mayor's bombastic speeches about his own brilliance alienated many voters, who eventually concluded that his hubris far exceeded his actual accomplishments in office.", "at": "那位自負市長誇誇其談自己才華的浮誇演說疏遠了選民，選民最終認定他的狂妄遠遠超過他在任內的實際成就。"}, {"w": "petrifaction", "p": "n.", "d": "The process of turning into stone; paralyzing fear.", "c": "石化（作用）；驚呆", "s": "In Arizona's famous forest, visitors can see ancient logs transformed by petrifaction, a process in which minerals in groundwater slowly replaced the wood over millions of years until the trees became solid stone.", "t": "在亞利桑那州著名的森林裡，遊客可以看到經過石化作用的古老樹幹；在這個過程中，地下水中的礦物經過數百萬年慢慢取代木質，直到樹木變成堅硬的石頭。", "as": "Paleontologists noted that petrifaction had preserved the fossil with uncanny detail, making the minute veins of leaves that grew nearly two hundred million years ago clearly discernible.", "at": "古生物學家指出，石化作用以不可思議的細節保存了這塊化石，使將近兩億年前生長的葉子上的細微葉脈清晰可辨。"}, {"w": "feculent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Foul with filth or waste; full of dregs.", "c": "污穢的；滿是糞便的", "s": "Before nineteenth-century cities built modern sewer systems, many urban rivers became feculent channels carrying human and animal waste, and doctors eventually linked the filthy, foul-smelling water to repeated, deadly outbreaks of cholera.", "t": "在十九世紀的城市興建現代下水道系統之前，許多城市河川成了運送人畜排泄物的污穢水道，醫生們後來將這些骯髒惡臭的河水與一再爆發的致命霍亂疫情聯繫起來。", "as": "Reformers described the squalid tenements and noisome, feculent alleys of the industrial city in harrowing detail, and their reports helped galvanize public support for long-overdue sanitary laws.", "at": "改革者以令人心驚的細節描述這座工業城市骯髒的廉價公寓和惡臭污穢的巷弄，他們的報告激起了大眾對遲來已久的衛生法規的支持。"}, {"w": "Solomonic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Showing great wisdom in judgment, like King Solomon.", "c": "像所羅門王般睿智的；明斷的", "s": "Faced with two departments demanding the same small budget, the principal reached a Solomonic decision, dividing the money so fairly and wisely that both teams praised her judgment and agreed to cooperate on a shared project.", "t": "面對兩個部門爭取同一筆少量預算，校長做出了所羅門王般睿智的決定，把經費分配得如此公正明智，以致兩個團隊都讚揚她的判斷，並同意合作推動一項共同計畫。", "as": "The judge's Solomonic ruling in the contentious custody case was praised as impartial and humane, mollifying both families who had expected an ugly, protracted legal battle.", "at": "法官在這件爭議性監護權案中做出的睿智裁決，被讚為公正而合乎人情，安撫了原本預期將有一場醜陋又冗長官司的兩個家庭。"}]}, {"unit": 43, "level": 9, "cards": [{"w": "leitmotif", "p": "n.", "d": "A recurring theme, image, or musical phrase in a work.", "c": "主導動機；反覆出現的主題", "s": "In Wagner's operas, each major character is associated with a short musical phrase that returns whenever that figure appears or is mentioned, and listeners soon learn to recognize this leitmotif as a kind of audible signature.", "t": "在華格納的歌劇中，每個主要角色都與一段簡短的樂句相連，每當該角色出場或被提及時，這段樂句就會再次出現，聽眾很快就學會把這個主導動機辨識為一種聽覺上的標誌。", "as": "The theme of exile recurs as a poignant leitmotif throughout the novelist's work, and even her most laconic short stories return to it with ineluctable force.", "at": "流亡的主題作為一個令人心酸的主導動機，貫穿這位小說家的作品；即使是她最精簡的短篇小說，也以無可避免的力量回到這個主題。"}, {"w": "scaramouch", "p": "n.", "d": "A boastful but cowardly buffoon; a rascal.", "c": "膽小又愛吹牛的小丑；無賴", "s": "The playwright's audience roared with laughter at the scaramouch who strutted across the stage bragging about his countless victories in battle, only to dive behind a curtain the moment a real soldier drew his sword.", "t": "劇作家的觀眾對那個膽小又愛吹牛的丑角哄堂大笑——他在舞台上大搖大擺，吹噓自己在戰場上無數的勝績，但真正的士兵一拔劍，他便立刻躲到簾幕後面。", "as": "Critics dismissed the bombastic senator as a mere scaramouch, noting that his grandiloquent threats always dissolved into pusillanimous retreats whenever an opponent actually challenged him in public.", "at": "評論家認為這位浮誇的參議員不過是個膽小又愛吹牛的小丑，並指出每當對手真正公開挑戰他時，他那些誇大其詞的威脅總會化為怯懦的退縮。"}, {"w": "effloresce", "p": "v.", "d": "To burst into bloom; to flourish or blossom.", "c": "開花；蓬勃發展", "s": "After decades of censorship ended, the country's long-suppressed literary culture began to effloresce, as dozens of new journals, independent publishers, and experimental poets appeared almost overnight in cities that had once seemed creatively barren.", "t": "數十年的審查制度結束後，該國長期受壓抑的文學文化開始蓬勃綻放，數十種新期刊、獨立出版社與實驗派詩人幾乎在一夜之間出現在那些曾經看似毫無創意的城市裡。", "as": "Under the patronage of magnanimous merchants, Florentine art effloresced during the fifteenth century, and the eclectic workshops of the era produced painters, sculptors, and architects of astonishing range.", "at": "在慷慨大度的商人贊助下，佛羅倫斯的藝術在十五世紀蓬勃綻放，那個時代兼容並蓄的工作室培養出才華涵蓋極廣、令人驚嘆的畫家、雕塑家與建築師。"}, {"w": "skein", "p": "n.", "d": "A coiled length of yarn; a tangled, complicated sequence.", "c": "（紗線的）一束；錯綜複雜的一連串", "s": "The detective spent weeks untangling the skein of lies, forged letters, and false alibis that the suspect had woven, and only after tracing every twisted strand back to its source could she finally reconstruct what had happened that night.", "t": "這位偵探花了數週時間，解開嫌犯所編織的那團由謊言、偽造信件與虛假不在場證明交纏而成的亂麻；直到她把每一條糾結的線索都追溯到源頭，才終於重建那晚發生的事。", "as": "Historians struggle to unravel the skein of clandestine alliances and perfidious betrayals that preceded the war, because many participants deliberately obfuscated their roles in later memoirs.", "at": "歷史學家難以理清戰爭爆發前那一連串錯綜複雜的秘密結盟與背信棄義，因為許多參與者在日後的回憶錄中刻意模糊了自己的角色。"}, {"w": "interstice", "p": "n.", "d": "A small, narrow space between things or parts.", "c": "空隙；縫隙", "s": "Botanists were surprised to find tiny ferns and mosses thriving in every interstice of the ancient stone wall, where pockets of moisture and windblown soil had collected between blocks that masons had set in place centuries earlier.", "t": "植物學家驚訝地發現，在那道古老石牆的每一處縫隙中，都有細小的蕨類與苔蘚茂盛生長；在數百年前石匠砌好的石塊之間，積聚了一處處濕氣與被風吹來的泥土。", "as": "The essayist argued that genuine creativity flourishes in the interstices of a schedule, in those ephemeral moments of ennui between obligations, rather than in hours assiduously reserved for inspiration.", "at": "這位散文家主張，真正的創造力往往在行程表的縫隙中蓬勃生長——在各項義務之間那些短暫而無聊的片刻——而不是在刻意為靈感保留的時段裡。"}, {"w": "commentariat", "p": "n.", "d": "Journalists and pundits who comment on current events, collectively.", "c": "評論界；媒體評論員群體", "s": "Within minutes of the presidential debate ending, the cable-news commentariat had already declared a winner, though weeks later polling data showed that ordinary voters had largely ignored the pundits' instant verdicts and judged the candidates quite differently.", "t": "總統辯論結束後才幾分鐘，有線新聞評論界就已宣布了贏家；然而數週後的民調資料顯示，一般選民大多無視這些名嘴的即時評斷，對候選人的評價也大不相同。", "as": "The commentariat greeted the policy with a jeremiad of predictions about economic ruin, yet the sagacious finance minister, displaying remarkable sangfroid, simply waited for the data to prove her right.", "at": "評論界以一連串預言經濟崩潰的悲嘆迎接這項政策，然而睿智的財政部長展現出非凡的沉著，只是靜待數據證明她的正確。"}, {"w": "peregrination", "p": "n.", "d": "A long, wandering journey from place to place.", "c": "遊歷；長途漫遊", "s": "During his three-year peregrination across Central Asia, the medieval scholar wandered from one caravan town to the next, recording local customs, languages, and recipes in notebooks that historians still consult today.", "t": "在橫越中亞長達三年的遊歷中，這位中世紀學者從一座商隊城鎮漫遊到另一座，將當地的風俗、語言與食譜記錄在筆記本裡，至今歷史學家仍會參考這些筆記。", "as": "Her peregrinations through remote mountain villages were arduous, yet the polyglot anthropologist remained sanguine, convinced that each difficult journey would yield insights unavailable to more sedentary scholars.", "at": "她在偏遠山村之間的遊歷十分艱辛，但這位通曉多種語言的人類學家始終保持樂觀，深信每段艱難的旅程都能帶來那些較少走動的學者無從獲得的洞見。"}, {"w": "filigree", "p": "n.", "d": "Delicate ornamental work made of fine twisted wire.", "c": "金銀絲細工；精緻的花飾", "s": "The museum's most admired artifact is a tiny silver box decorated with filigree so delicate that visitors need a magnifying glass to appreciate how the craftsman twisted hair-thin wires into curling vines and blossoms.", "t": "這間博物館最受讚賞的文物是一個小小的銀盒，盒上裝飾的金銀絲細工極為精緻，參觀者需要借助放大鏡，才能欣賞工匠如何把細如髮絲的金屬線扭轉成蜷曲的藤蔓與花朵。", "as": "Frost had etched a filigree of ice across the window, and the fastidious photographer, ignoring the insouciant chatter of passing students, spent an hour capturing its ephemeral patterns before sunrise melted them.", "at": "霜在窗上蝕刻出一片精緻的冰花，那位一絲不苟的攝影師不理會路過學生漫不經心的閒聊，在日出融化它們之前花了一小時捕捉那轉瞬即逝的圖案。"}, {"w": "gimcrack", "p": "n.", "d": "A showy but useless or cheaply made object.", "c": "華而不實的小玩意；廉價俗麗的東西", "s": "The souvenir stalls outside the cathedral were crammed with every imaginable gimcrack: plastic snow globes, flimsy keychains, and glittering miniature spires that broke apart before tourists even reached their hotels.", "t": "大教堂外的紀念品攤位塞滿了各種你想像得到的華而不實的小玩意：塑膠雪花球、一折就斷的鑰匙圈，以及閃閃發亮的迷你尖塔模型——遊客還沒回到飯店就已經散了架。", "as": "The ostentatious mansion was cluttered with gilded gimcracks, and its owner's voracious appetite for such baubles struck his more abstemious neighbors as a symptom of vanity rather than taste.", "at": "那棟炫富的豪宅裡堆滿了鍍金的俗麗小玩意，主人對這類小飾物貪得無厭的胃口，在較為節制的鄰居看來是虛榮而非品味的表現。"}, {"w": "immitigable", "p": "adj.", "d": "Impossible to soften, lessen, or make less severe.", "c": "無法緩和的；不可減輕的", "s": "The poet's later letters describe an immitigable grief following the death of her only child, a sorrow so profound that neither the passage of time nor the consolation of friends could lessen it in the slightest degree.", "t": "這位詩人晚年的信件描述了她在唯一的孩子去世後那無法緩解的悲痛——這份哀傷如此深沉，無論時間的流逝或朋友的安慰都無法使它稍減分毫。", "as": "The lugubrious documentary portrayed the famine's immitigable suffering with unflinching candor, refusing the specious comfort of a hopeful ending that many viewers had expected from the filmmakers.", "at": "這部陰鬱的紀錄片以毫不退縮的坦率呈現那場饑荒無法緩解的苦難，拒絕給予許多觀眾期待導演提供的那種虛假慰藉——一個充滿希望的結局。"}, {"w": "panoply", "p": "n.", "d": "An impressive, complete array or collection of things.", "c": "一整套；壯觀的陣列", "s": "Visitors to the new science center can explore a dazzling panoply of interactive exhibits, from a full-scale replica of a Mars rover to a planetarium dome, a robotics workshop, and a living coral reef tank.", "t": "新科學中心的參觀者可以探索一系列令人目不暇給的互動展品，從等比例的火星探測車複製品，到天象儀圓頂、機器人工作坊，以及活珊瑚礁水族缸，應有盡有。", "as": "The general arrived with the full panoply of military power, yet his imperious demands met the intransigent refusal of villagers who had already survived three previous invasions.", "at": "將軍帶著全套軍事武力抵達，然而他專橫的要求遭到村民毫不妥協的拒絕——這些村民早已熬過了先前的三次入侵。"}, {"w": "recherché", "p": "adj.", "d": "Exquisite and rare; also excessively refined or obscure.", "c": "精選罕見的；過分考究的", "s": "The chef's tasting menu was almost absurdly recherché, featuring white truffles flown in from Alba, a rare saffron harvested by hand in Kashmir, and an heirloom rice that only three farmers in the world still cultivate.", "t": "這位主廚的品嚐菜單考究得近乎荒謬，菜色包括從阿爾巴空運而來的白松露、在喀什米爾以手工採收的稀有番紅花，以及全世界只剩三位農民仍在種植的傳家米。", "as": "The professor's lectures were so recherché and abstruse that only a few cognoscenti in the back row could follow his allusions to forgotten Byzantine poets.", "at": "那位教授的講課如此過分考究又艱深難懂，只有後排少數幾位行家能理解他對那些被遺忘的拜占庭詩人所做的典故引用。"}, {"w": "vertiginous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Causing dizziness, especially because of great height.", "c": "令人暈眩的；高得令人頭暈的", "s": "Climbers hoping to reach the summit must cross a narrow ridge with vertiginous drops on both sides, and many admit that glancing down at the valley two thousand meters below made their knees tremble and their heads spin.", "t": "想登頂的登山者必須穿越一道兩側都是令人暈眩深谷的狹窄山脊，許多人坦言，往下瞥一眼兩千公尺下方的山谷，就讓他們雙膝發抖、頭暈目眩。", "as": "The stock market's vertiginous plunge left even jaded traders shaken, and the normally garrulous analysts on the trading floor fell uncharacteristically taciturn as the losses mounted.", "at": "股市令人暈眩的暴跌讓連見慣大風大浪的交易員都為之震驚；隨著虧損不斷擴大，交易大廳裡平時喋喋不休的分析師們也一反常態地沉默寡言。"}, {"w": "kismet", "p": "n.", "d": "Fate or destiny; what is meant to happen.", "c": "命運；天命", "s": "The two scientists, born on opposite sides of the world, met only because a snowstorm grounded their flights in the same airport; years later, after winning a shared prize, they jokingly credited their partnership to kismet.", "t": "這兩位出生在地球兩端的科學家，只因一場暴風雪讓他們的班機都滯留在同一座機場而相遇；多年後共同獲獎時，他們開玩笑地把兩人的合作歸功於命運。", "as": "The quixotic explorer insisted that kismet, not careful planning, had guided his expedition, a fatalistic claim his more prudent colleagues found both whimsical and dangerous.", "at": "這位不切實際的探險家堅稱，引導他遠征的是命運而非周詳的計畫；他那些較為謹慎的同事認為，這種宿命論的說法既異想天開又危險。"}, {"w": "temporize", "p": "v.", "d": "To delay or avoid committing oneself in order to gain time.", "c": "拖延時間；含糊其辭以觀望", "s": "When reporters pressed the mayor about the contaminated water supply, he chose to temporize, promising further studies and future committees rather than admitting the problem or committing to any concrete plan to fix it.", "t": "當記者追問市長關於供水遭污染的問題時，他選擇拖延時間，承諾會進行更多研究、成立未來的委員會，而不承認問題，也不承諾任何具體的解決方案。", "as": "Rather than temporize with dilatory half-measures, the resolute governor confronted the crisis directly, and her candor won the trust of citizens weary of evasive politicians.", "at": "這位果斷的州長沒有以拖延的權宜之計來敷衍拖時間，而是直接面對危機；她的坦率贏得了早已厭倦閃爍其詞政客的民眾的信任。"}, {"w": "pleonasm", "p": "n.", "d": "The use of more words than necessary to express an idea.", "c": "冗詞；贅述", "s": "The editor circled phrases such as \"free gift,\" \"past history,\" and \"end result\" in red ink, explaining to the young reporter that each was a pleonasm because one word already contained the full meaning of the other.", "t": "編輯用紅筆圈出「免費贈品」、「過去的歷史」和「最終結果」等詞語，並向年輕記者解釋，每一個都是贅詞，因為其中一個字已經包含了另一個字的完整意義。", "as": "The verbose committee report was riddled with pleonasms and platitudes, and the trenchant reviewer who summarized it noted that its forty pages contained barely four pages of actual substance.", "at": "那份冗長的委員會報告充斥著贅詞與陳腔濫調，負責摘要的那位犀利評論者指出，四十頁的報告裡真正有內容的還不到四頁。"}, {"w": "verisimilitude", "p": "n.", "d": "The quality of appearing true or real.", "c": "逼真；貌似真實", "s": "To give the historical film greater verisimilitude, the director hired linguists to reconstruct seventeenth-century accents, insisted on hand-stitched costumes, and banned any props that would not have existed in a colonial village of that period.", "t": "為了讓這部歷史電影更加逼真，導演聘請語言學家重建十七世紀的口音，堅持使用手工縫製的服裝，並禁用任何在當時殖民地村莊中不可能存在的道具。", "as": "The novel's verisimilitude was merely ostensible: beneath its careful period detail lay a specious argument that no erudite historian of the era would ever accept without serious reservations.", "at": "這部小說的逼真只是表面上的：在細膩的時代細節之下，隱藏著一個似是而非的論點，任何博學的該時代歷史學家都不會毫無保留地接受。"}, {"w": "cabal", "p": "n.", "d": "A small secret group of plotters.", "c": "陰謀集團；秘密小團體", "s": "Historians now believe that the emperor's assassination was planned not by a lone fanatic but by a cabal of senior advisers who met secretly in a palace storeroom for months, plotting to seize control of the treasury.", "t": "歷史學家如今相信，皇帝遇刺並非某個孤身狂熱分子所策劃，而是一群高級顧問組成的陰謀集團所為；他們連續數月在宮殿的儲藏室裡秘密集會，密謀奪取國庫的控制權。", "as": "The novel's villain leads a cabal of venal bankers whose secret machinations nearly bankrupt the kingdom before a perspicacious young clerk finally exposes their elaborate scheme.", "at": "小說中的反派率領一群貪腐的銀行家組成陰謀集團，他們的秘密詭計幾乎讓王國破產，直到一位目光敏銳的年輕職員終於揭穿他們精心策劃的陰謀。"}, {"w": "postprandial", "p": "adj.", "d": "Happening or done after a meal, especially dinner.", "c": "餐後的；飯後的", "s": "Researchers studying sleep patterns found that many office workers experience a postprandial slump around two o'clock, when the body diverts energy toward digesting lunch and concentration drops noticeably for about an hour.", "t": "研究睡眠模式的學者發現，許多上班族在下午兩點左右會出現餐後倦怠，此時身體將能量轉向消化午餐，專注力會明顯下降大約一小時。", "as": "After the convivial banquet, the elderly professor delivered a postprandial speech so prolix that half the somnolent audience was dozing before he reached his second point.", "at": "在歡樂的宴會之後，那位年邁的教授發表了一篇冗長至極的餐後演講，他還沒講到第二個重點，半數昏昏欲睡的聽眾就已經打起瞌睡了。"}, {"w": "onomatopoeia", "p": "n.", "d": "The use of words that imitate the sounds they describe.", "c": "擬聲；擬聲詞", "s": "In her lesson on poetic devices, the teacher asked students to find examples of onomatopoeia in the comic strip, and they quickly pointed out words like \"buzz,\" \"crash,\" and \"sizzle\" that mimic the very noises they name.", "t": "在講解詩歌修辭手法的課堂上，老師要學生在漫畫中找出擬聲的例子，他們很快就指出像「嗡嗡」、「砰」和「滋滋」這類模仿其所指聲音的詞語。", "as": "The poet's adroit use of onomatopoeia, from the hiss of the sea to the clatter of hooves, gives her ballads a vivid immediacy that more pedantic critics have inexplicably overlooked.", "at": "這位詩人巧妙地運用擬聲手法，從海浪的嘶嘶聲到馬蹄的噠噠聲，讓她的歌謠充滿生動的臨場感，而較為迂腐的評論家卻莫名地忽略了這一點。"}]}, {"unit": 44, "level": 9, "cards": [{"w": "dudgeon", "p": "n.", "d": "A feeling of offended resentment or indignation.", "c": "憤慨；生氣", "s": "When the committee rejected his proposal without even reading it, the veteran architect gathered his blueprints, announced that he would never work with the city again, and stormed out of the meeting in high dudgeon.", "t": "當委員會連看都沒看就否決了他的提案時，這位資深建築師收起藍圖，宣布再也不會與市政府合作，然後怒氣沖沖地衝出會議室。", "as": "The irascible novelist left the literary festival in high dudgeon after a trenchant critic described his latest book as a bombastic retread of his earlier work.", "at": "一位犀利的評論家將這位暴躁小說家的新書形容為對他早期作品浮誇的翻版，他因此怒氣沖沖地離開了文學節。"}, {"w": "hegemony", "p": "n.", "d": "Dominance or leadership of one group or nation over others.", "c": "霸權；支配地位", "s": "For nearly a century, Britain's naval hegemony allowed it to control the world's major shipping routes, but by the 1940s rising powers had built fleets strong enough to end its unchallenged dominance of the seas.", "t": "將近一個世紀以來，英國的海上霸權使其得以掌控全球主要航線，但到了1940年代，新興強權已建立起足以終結其稱霸海洋地位的艦隊。", "as": "The tech giant's cultural hegemony seemed inexorable until a small coterie of iconoclast programmers, ostracized by the industry, released free software that eroded its dominance with astonishing speed.", "at": "這家科技巨頭的文化霸權看似勢不可擋，直到一小群打破傳統的程式設計師推出免費軟體，以驚人的速度侵蝕了它的主導地位。"}, {"w": "premonitory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Giving a warning in advance; serving as an omen.", "c": "預兆的；預先警告的", "s": "Seismologists now study the faint premonitory tremors that sometimes occur days before a major earthquake, hoping that these early signals might someday give coastal residents enough warning to evacuate safely.", "t": "地震學家如今研究那些有時在大地震發生前數天出現的微弱前兆震動，希望這些早期訊號有朝一日能給沿海居民足夠的預警時間安全撤離。", "as": "Ignoring the premonitory rumbles from the volcano, the obstinate village elders refused to evacuate, dismissing the scientists' warnings as the alarmist jeremiads of overcautious outsiders.", "at": "頑固的村中長老不理會火山傳來的預兆性隆隆聲，拒絕撤離，並把科學家的警告斥為過度謹慎的外人危言聳聽的悲嘆。"}, {"w": "retronym", "p": "n.", "d": "A new term coined to distinguish an original thing from newer versions.", "c": "逆向詞；回溯詞", "s": "Before the invention of the electric guitar, nobody needed the phrase \"acoustic guitar\"; linguists call such a term a retronym because it was created only after newer technology made the original need a new name.", "t": "在電吉他發明之前，沒有人需要「木吉他」這個說法；語言學家把這種詞稱為逆向詞，因為它是在新科技出現、原本的事物需要新名稱之後才被創造出來的。", "as": "The lexicographer offered an erudite but lucid survey of retronyms such as \"landline\" and \"snail mail,\" showing how technological change quietly renders ordinary words ambiguous.", "at": "這位辭典編纂者對「市內電話」和「蝸牛郵件」等逆向詞做了一番博學而清晰的考察，說明科技變遷如何悄悄地使普通詞語變得含糊不清。"}, {"w": "recuse", "p": "v.", "d": "To withdraw from a decision because of a conflict of interest.", "c": "迴避（案件或決策）；自行退出", "s": "Because her brother-in-law owned one of the companies being investigated, the judge decided to recuse herself from the case, publicly explaining that the public must never doubt the court's impartiality.", "t": "由於她的姊夫擁有其中一家受調查的公司，這位法官決定自行迴避此案，並解釋說，絕不能讓大眾懷疑法院的公正性。", "as": "Critics argued that the official's refusal to recuse himself, despite obvious financial ties to the contractor, revealed a venal disregard for the probity expected of public servants.", "at": "批評者認為，儘管這位官員與承包商有明顯的財務關係，他卻拒絕迴避，這顯示他唯利是圖，無視公職人員應有的廉正操守。"}, {"w": "penury", "p": "n.", "d": "Extreme poverty; severe lack of money or resources.", "c": "赤貧；貧困", "s": "Although the composer's symphonies are now performed in concert halls around the world, he spent his final years in penury, selling his furniture to pay for bread and candles in a freezing rented room.", "t": "雖然這位作曲家的交響曲如今在世界各地的音樂廳演出，他卻在赤貧中度過晚年，在寒冷的租屋裡變賣家具，只為換取麵包和蠟燭。", "as": "The memoir describes the author's childhood penury without self-pity; even as an indigent student, she remained sanguine, convinced that education would eventually free her family.", "at": "這部回憶錄毫不自憐地描述作者童年的赤貧生活；即使身為貧困的學生，她依然樂觀，深信教育終將讓家人脫離困境。"}, {"w": "roué", "p": "n.", "d": "A pleasure-seeking man of dissolute, immoral habits; a rake.", "c": "浪子；放蕩者", "s": "In many nineteenth-century novels, the charming but unprincipled roué gambles away his family fortune, ignores every social obligation, and eventually ruins the reputation of everyone foolish enough to trust him.", "t": "在許多十九世紀的小說中，那個迷人卻毫無原則的浪子會把家產揮霍在賭桌上，無視一切社會責任，最終毀掉每一個愚蠢到信任他的人的名聲。", "as": "The aging roué in the comedy, ostentatious and utterly unscrupulous, squanders his inheritance on lavish parties while his long-suffering steward tries in vain to curb his excesses.", "at": "這部喜劇中那位年華老去的浪子，愛炫耀又毫無道德顧忌，把遺產揮霍在奢華的派對上，而他那位長期隱忍的管家則徒勞地試圖約束他的放縱。"}, {"w": "Luddite", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who opposes new technology or technological change.", "c": "反對新科技的人；守舊者", "s": "Although he writes all his novels by hand and refuses to own a smartphone, the author insists he is no Luddite; he simply finds that typing distracts him from the slow work of choosing words.", "t": "雖然這位作家所有小說都用手寫，也拒絕擁有智慧型手機，他卻堅稱自己並不是反對新科技的人；他只是覺得打字會讓他無法專心於推敲字詞這項慢工。", "as": "Dismissed as a Luddite by younger colleagues, the obstinate professor nonetheless proved prescient: his skepticism about the flashy software was vindicated when it corrupted the department's records.", "at": "這位固執的教授被年輕同事斥為反科技的守舊者，但事實證明他頗有先見之明：當那套花俏的軟體損毀系上的紀錄時，他的懷疑得到了證實。"}, {"w": "schadenfreude", "p": "n.", "d": "Pleasure derived from another person's misfortune.", "c": "幸災樂禍", "s": "Psychologists have found that sports fans often feel schadenfreude when a bitter rival loses a championship game, experiencing genuine delight not because their own team won but because a hated opponent suffered.", "t": "心理學家發現，體育迷在死敵輸掉冠軍賽時往往會幸災樂禍，他們真心感到高興，並不是因為自己的球隊贏了，而是因為痛恨的對手吃了苦頭。", "as": "The pundit's thinly veiled schadenfreude at his rival's downfall struck viewers as petty, and his sardonic jokes only deepened the animosity between their two networks.", "at": "這位名嘴對競爭對手的垮台幾乎毫不掩飾地幸災樂禍，觀眾認為他氣量狹小，而他那些譏諷的笑話只加深了兩家電視台之間的敵意。"}, {"w": "costive", "p": "adj.", "d": "Slow and sluggish; also stingy (literally, constipated).", "c": "遲緩的；吝嗇的", "s": "The once-prolific novelist became strangely costive in middle age, producing only a single slim volume in fifteen years, as if every sentence had to be forced out of him against his will.", "t": "這位曾經多產的小說家到了中年卻變得出奇地遲緩，十五年間只寫出一本薄薄的書，彷彿每一個句子都是違背他意願硬擠出來的。", "as": "The costive foundation, notoriously parsimonious with its grants, surprised everyone by funding the project, though its officials remained characteristically taciturn about why they had changed course.", "at": "這個出了名吝於撥款的基金會，出乎眾人意料地資助了這項計畫，不過基金會的主管們一如往常，對他們改變方針的原因三緘其口。"}, {"w": "gallimaufry", "p": "n.", "d": "A confused jumble or hodgepodge of different things.", "c": "大雜燴；混雜", "s": "The attic was a gallimaufry of forgotten objects: broken lamps, wartime letters, a dented trumpet, stacks of yellowed magazines, and a box of seashells collected by someone no one in the family could identify.", "t": "閣樓裡是一堆被遺忘物品的大雜燴：壞掉的檯燈、戰時的信件、一把凹陷的小號、成疊泛黃的雜誌，還有一盒家裡沒有人說得出是誰收集的貝殼。", "as": "The festival's program was an eclectic gallimaufry of jazz, puppetry, and poetry readings, a whimsical mix that delighted audiences but exasperated the more fastidious critics.", "at": "這個藝術節的節目是爵士樂、偶戲與詩歌朗讀兼容並蓄的大雜燴，這種異想天開的組合讓觀眾大為開心，卻讓較挑剔的評論家感到惱火。"}, {"w": "analects", "p": "n.", "d": "Selected passages or sayings from the writings of an author.", "c": "語錄；文選", "s": "The professor assigned a slim volume of analects rather than the philosopher's complete works, explaining that these carefully chosen passages captured his central ideas without overwhelming first-year students with thousands of pages.", "t": "教授指定學生閱讀一本薄薄的語錄選集，而非這位哲學家的全集，並解釋說，這些精心挑選的段落掌握了他的核心思想，又不會讓一年級學生被數千頁的篇幅壓垮。", "as": "Students often find Confucius's Analects deceptively simple, yet each laconic saying rewards assiduous study, gradually revealing a sagacious and coherent philosophy of ethics, government, and personal cultivation.", "at": "學生們常覺得孔子的《論語》看似簡單，但每一句簡潔的話語都值得勤勉研讀，從中可見一套關於倫理、治國與個人修養的睿智哲學。"}, {"w": "parturition", "p": "n.", "d": "The act or process of giving birth; childbirth.", "c": "分娩；生產", "s": "Veterinarians monitoring the endangered rhinoceros installed several cameras in her enclosure weeks before parturition, so that they could intervene immediately if any complication arose during the delivery of her calf.", "t": "負責照護這頭瀕危犀牛的獸醫在牠分娩前數週就在圍欄內裝設攝影機，以便在生產小犀牛的過程中一旦出現任何併發症能立即介入。", "as": "Medical historians note that before modern obstetrics, parturition was a perilous ordeal, and the benign practices of skilled midwives saved countless lives that physicians' arbitrary remedies endangered.", "at": "醫學史學者指出，在現代產科出現之前，分娩是一場危險的考驗，熟練助產士溫和的做法挽救了無數條性命，而醫師們武斷的療法卻常常危及生命。"}, {"w": "atrabilious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Gloomy and melancholy, or bad-tempered and irritable.", "c": "憂鬱的；暴躁易怒的", "s": "The old lighthouse keeper in the novel is an atrabilious figure who rarely speaks, scowls at visiting children, and spends long winter evenings brooding over the wife and son he lost at sea.", "t": "小說中的老燈塔看守人是個陰鬱暴躁的人物，他很少說話，對來訪的孩子們皺眉，並在漫長的冬夜裡為他在海上失去的妻兒沉思憂傷。", "as": "The atrabilious critic's reviews were so consistently morose and splenetic that readers came to regard his rare praise as an encomium of almost legendary value.", "at": "這位憂鬱暴躁的評論家的書評一貫陰沉又尖酸，以至於讀者把他難得的讚美視為價值近乎傳奇的頌詞。"}, {"w": "transmogrify", "p": "v.", "d": "To transform completely, often in a surprising or bizarre way.", "c": "使徹底變形（常指離奇地）；使改頭換面", "s": "In the children's story, a careless wizard's spell manages to transmogrify the king's dignified palace into a giant wobbling cake, complete with frosting towers and a moat of bubbling chocolate.", "t": "在這個童話故事中，一位粗心巫師的咒語竟把國王莊嚴的宮殿徹底變成一個搖搖晃晃的巨大蛋糕，還有糖霜塔樓和一條冒著泡的巧克力護城河。", "as": "Within a decade, the speculators had transmogrified the quiet fishing village into a garish resort, an ostentatious transformation that many longtime residents viewed with lugubrious resignation.", "at": "不到十年，投機客就把那座寧靜的漁村徹底改造成俗豔的度假勝地；對這種浮誇的轉變，許多老居民只能悲傷而無奈地接受。"}, {"w": "screed", "p": "n.", "d": "A long, tiresome piece of writing or speech, usually ranting.", "c": "冗長的激烈言論；長篇大論", "s": "Instead of a short letter explaining his resignation, the departing manager sent the entire staff a twelve-page screed attacking his colleagues, the company's founders, and nearly every decision made in the past decade.", "t": "離職的經理沒有寄一封簡短的信說明辭職原因，而是寄給全體員工一份長達十二頁的激烈長文，抨擊他的同事、公司創辦人，以及過去十年幾乎每一項決策。", "as": "The blogger's latest screed was a vitriol-soaked diatribe against modern architecture, so prolix and splenetic that even readers who shared his views abandoned it halfway through.", "at": "這位部落客最新的長篇大論是一篇充滿惡毒言辭、抨擊現代建築的謾罵文章，冗長又尖酸，連認同他觀點的讀者都讀到一半就放棄了。"}, {"w": "matutinal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Relating to or occurring in the early morning.", "c": "早晨的；清晨的", "s": "Birdwatchers who hope to hear the full chorus of forest songbirds must set out before sunrise, because most species are noisiest during their matutinal burst of activity and grow quiet by mid-morning.", "t": "想要聽到森林鳴禽完整大合唱的賞鳥人必須在日出前出發，因為大多數鳥類在清晨活動最旺盛時最吵鬧，到了上午過半就會安靜下來。", "as": "The poet's matutinal habit of writing before dawn was sacrosanct; nothing, not even the garrulous visits of her neighbors, could tempt her to abandon those quiet hours.", "at": "這位詩人在黎明前寫作的清晨習慣神聖不可侵犯；任何事物，即使是鄰居們喋喋不休的造訪，都無法誘使她放棄那些安靜的時光。"}, {"w": "crapulent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Sick or unwell from eating or drinking too much.", "c": "暴飲暴食而不適的；飲食過度的", "s": "Historians of ancient Rome describe banquets that lasted for hours, after which many crapulent senators, having consumed course after course of rich food, could barely stand and had to be carried home by servants.", "t": "研究古羅馬的歷史學家描述了持續數小時的宴會；宴後，許多吃下一道又一道油膩菜餚的元老院議員撐得幾乎站不起來，只能由僕人抬回家。", "as": "Dickens satirizes the crapulent aldermen who feast extravagantly while ignoring the indigent families outside, contrasting their voracious appetites with the hunger of the city's poor.", "at": "狄更斯諷刺那些暴飲暴食的市府議員，他們奢華地大吃大喝，卻無視門外貧困的家庭，以他們貪得無厭的胃口對比城市窮人的飢餓。"}, {"w": "ipso facto", "p": "adv.", "d": "By that very fact or act; as a direct result.", "c": "根據事實本身；當然地", "s": "The debate coach reminded her students that a claim repeated by many people is not ipso facto true; popularity is not evidence, and every assertion must still be supported by reliable data and sound reasoning.", "t": "辯論教練提醒學生，一個被許多人重複的說法並不因此就是真的；受歡迎不等於證據，每一項主張仍必須以可靠的數據和嚴謹的推理來支持。", "as": "The specious argument that an expensive treatment is ipso facto superior to a cheap one is a sophistry that perspicacious patients and doctors should learn to resist.", "at": "「昂貴的療法本身就必然優於便宜的療法」這種似是而非的論點是一種詭辯，有洞察力的病患與醫師都應該學會抵制。"}, {"w": "debouch", "p": "v.", "d": "To emerge from a narrow place into a wider, open area.", "c": "（從狹窄處）湧出；（河流）注入", "s": "After winding for hundreds of kilometers through steep, narrow canyons, the river finally begins to debouch onto a broad coastal plain, where it slows, spreads out, and deposits rich soil across the farmland.", "t": "這條河流在陡峭狹窄的峽谷間蜿蜒數百公里後，終於開始流出到廣闊的沿海平原，在那裡水流減緩、四散開來，把肥沃的土壤沉積在農田上。", "as": "When the crowd debouched from the narrow alley into the plaza, the normally taciturn police chief ordered his officers to remain impartial and to avoid any truculent display of force.", "at": "當人群從狹窄的巷子湧入廣場時，平時沉默寡言的警察局長命令部下保持中立，避免任何粗暴的武力展示。"}]}, {"unit": 45, "level": 9, "cards": [{"w": "immure", "p": "v.", "d": "To enclose within walls; to imprison or confine.", "c": "禁閉；監禁", "s": "In the legend recounted by medieval chroniclers, the jealous duke ordered his workers to immure his rival inside a sealed tower, leaving only a narrow slot through which guards could pass bread and water each day.", "t": "在中世紀編年史家所記述的傳說中，那位善妒的公爵命令工人把他的對手禁閉在一座封死的塔樓裡，只留下一道窄縫，讓守衛每天遞送麵包和水。", "as": "Immured for decades in a remote monastery, the erudite monk refused to languish in despair; instead, he copied fragile manuscripts so carefully that later scholars came to regard his versions as nearly sacrosanct.", "at": "這位博學的修士被禁閉在偏遠的修道院長達數十年，卻不願在絕望中萎靡不振；他反而細心抄寫脆弱的手稿，使後世學者將他的抄本視為近乎神聖不可侵犯。"}, {"w": "corrigendum", "p": "n.", "d": "An error to be corrected, especially in a printed book.", "c": "勘誤；（書中）需更正的錯誤", "s": "After a reviewer noticed that the textbook listed the boiling point of ethanol incorrectly, the publisher inserted a small slip in every remaining copy, noting the corrigendum and giving the accurate figure of 78 degrees Celsius.", "t": "一位審稿人發現教科書把乙醇的沸點寫錯之後，出版社在每本剩下的書中都夾入一張小紙條，註明這項勘誤，並列出正確的數值攝氏78度。", "as": "The pedantic editor, never one to be complacent, published a corrigendum for a single misplaced decimal in the census table, and his laconic note fixed the error without a word of excuse.", "at": "那位咬文嚼字、從不自滿的編輯，為人口普查表中一個放錯位置的小數點刊登了一則勘誤，他簡短的說明修正了錯誤，沒有一句辯解。"}, {"w": "latitudinarian", "p": "adj.", "d": "Tolerant of a wide range of views, especially in religion.", "c": "（尤指宗教上）寬容的；不拘泥教條的", "s": "Unlike his strict predecessor, who expelled any student questioning official doctrine, the new headmaster took a latitudinarian approach, welcoming debates about faith and allowing pupils of every religious background to express their beliefs openly.", "t": "不同於前任那位會開除任何質疑官方教義學生的嚴格校長，新校長採取寬容的作法，歡迎關於信仰的辯論，並允許各種宗教背景的學生公開表達自己的信仰。", "as": "The bishop's latitudinarian views made him a pariah among dogmatic clergy, yet his magnanimous treatment of dissenters helped ameliorate tensions that had divided the parish for generations.", "at": "這位主教寬容的宗教觀使他在固守教條的神職人員中成為被排擠的人，但他對異議者寬宏大量的態度，卻有助於緩和分裂教區數代的緊張關係。"}, {"w": "stentorian", "p": "adj.", "d": "Extremely loud and powerful in sound.", "c": "聲音洪亮的；大嗓門的", "s": "Without a microphone in the crowded stadium, the coach relied on her stentorian voice, which carried clearly across the entire field and allowed every player, even those at the far end, to hear her instructions.", "t": "在擁擠的體育場裡沒有麥克風，教練只能依靠她洪亮的嗓音，那聲音清楚地傳遍整個球場，讓每位球員，甚至遠在另一端的人，都能聽到她的指示。", "as": "The senator's stentorian delivery and bombastic rhetoric impressed the crowd, but one sagacious political journalist noted that beneath the vociferous display lay remarkably little genuine substance or evidence.", "at": "這位參議員洪亮的演說方式和浮誇的言辭讓群眾印象深刻，但一位睿智的政治記者指出，在那喧嚷的表演之下，幾乎沒有真正的內容或證據。"}, {"w": "abecedarian", "p": "n.", "d": "A beginner, especially one learning the alphabet.", "c": "初學者；學字母的人", "s": "Although she later became a celebrated linguist fluent in nine languages, Professor Lin admits that in her first Arabic class she was a mere abecedarian, struggling for weeks simply to recognize the letters and copy them neatly.", "t": "雖然林教授後來成為精通九種語言的知名語言學家，但她承認，在第一堂阿拉伯語課時，她只是個初學者，花了好幾週才勉強認得字母並把它們工整地抄寫下來。", "as": "No longer a diffident abecedarian, the young pianist now practiced with sedulous discipline, though her teacher warned that technical skill alone would never make her playing truly poignant.", "at": "這位年輕的鋼琴家不再是羞怯的初學者，如今她以孜孜不倦的紀律練習，但她的老師提醒她，光靠技巧永遠無法讓她的演奏真正動人。"}, {"w": "juvenilia", "p": "n.", "d": "Works produced by an author or artist while young.", "c": "少年時期的作品；早期習作", "s": "Scholars studying Jane Austen's juvenilia have found that the comic sketches she wrote as a teenager already display the sharp wit and keen social observation that would later distinguish mature novels such as Pride and Prejudice.", "t": "研究珍・奧斯汀少年時期作品的學者發現，她十幾歲時寫下的那些詼諧短篇，已展現出後來使《傲慢與偏見》等成熟小說與眾不同的犀利機智與敏銳社會觀察。", "as": "Critics once dismissed the painter's juvenilia as banal imitations, but a recent exhibition revealed that even those nascent works contained the lugubrious colors that define his celebrated later portraits.", "at": "評論家曾把這位畫家的少年作品斥為平庸的模仿，但最近的一場展覽顯示，即使是那些初期作品，也已帶有日後成為他著名晚期肖像畫特色的陰鬱色調。"}, {"w": "hidalgo", "p": "n.", "d": "A Spanish nobleman of the lower rank.", "c": "西班牙下級貴族；紳士", "s": "Cervantes made his famous hero a poor hidalgo from La Mancha, a minor nobleman who owned little more than an old horse and a library of romances, yet who proudly believed he belonged to an honorable class of knights.", "t": "塞萬提斯把他筆下的著名主角塑造成來自拉曼查的一位窮困西班牙下級貴族——一個除了一匹老馬和一屋子騎士小說外幾乎一無所有的小貴族，卻驕傲地相信自己屬於光榮的騎士階級。", "as": "Though impoverished, the proud hidalgo maintained an urbane manner and austere habits, refusing to ostracize the peasants who, in the eyes of his snobbish neighbors, were far beneath him.", "at": "這位驕傲的西班牙下級貴族雖然家道中落，卻依然保持文雅的舉止與簡樸的生活習慣，也拒絕排斥那些在他勢利的鄰居眼中地位遠低於他的農民。"}, {"w": "eleemosynary", "p": "adj.", "d": "Relating to or supported by charity; charitable.", "c": "慈善的；施捨的", "s": "Founded in 1890 to provide free meals and medical care to the city's poorest families, the hospital was an eleemosynary institution that depended entirely on donations from wealthy merchants rather than on fees from patients.", "t": "這家醫院於1890年創立，為城裡最貧困的家庭提供免費餐食與醫療照護，是一所完全仰賴富商捐款、而非向病患收費的慈善機構。", "as": "The foundation's eleemosynary mission was rooted in genuine altruism, yet its lucrative investments in tobacco companies made its generosity seem hollow, an irony that even its most sanguine supporters acknowledged.", "at": "這個基金會的慈善使命源於真誠的利他精神，但它在菸草公司的高獲利投資卻讓它的慷慨顯得空洞，連最樂觀的支持者都承認這種諷刺。"}, {"w": "plangent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Loud and resonant, with a mournful or melancholy tone.", "c": "（聲音）響亮而哀傷的；悲鳴的", "s": "As the funeral procession moved slowly through the village, the plangent tolling of the old church bell echoed across the valley, its deep, sorrowful notes seeming to express the grief that the silent mourners could not put into words.", "t": "送葬隊伍緩緩穿過村莊時，古老教堂鐘聲那響亮而哀傷的鐘鳴在山谷間迴盪，低沉悲切的音調彷彿道出了默默送行的人們無法言說的悲痛。", "as": "The cellist's plangent solo, with its plaintive, lugubrious phrases, moved even the stoic conductor to tears during the memorial concert for victims of the earthquake.", "at": "在為地震罹難者舉辦的追思音樂會上，大提琴家那響亮而哀傷的獨奏，帶著淒婉、悲戚的樂句，連一向沉著冷靜的指揮都感動落淚。"}, {"w": "lagniappe", "p": "n.", "d": "A small extra gift given with a purchase.", "c": "（購物時附送的）小贈品；額外的好處", "s": "In New Orleans, shopkeepers traditionally slipped a lagniappe into a customer's bag, such as an extra praline or a thirteenth doughnut, as a small thank-you that cost the store little but kept loyal buyers coming back.", "t": "在紐奧良，店家傳統上會在顧客的袋子裡偷偷放一份小贈品，例如多一顆胡桃糖或第十三個甜甜圈，作為一個花不了店家多少錢、卻能讓忠實顧客一再光顧的小小謝意。", "as": "Even the most frugal customers appreciated the bakery's lagniappe of a free cookie, a small boon that, unlike the ostentatious promotions of rival chains, felt personal and sincere.", "at": "即使是最節儉的顧客，也很喜歡這家麵包店附贈一塊免費餅乾的小禮物；這份小小的好處，不像競爭連鎖店那些浮誇的促銷活動，讓人感到親切而真誠。"}, {"w": "acolyte", "p": "n.", "d": "A devoted follower or assistant; an altar attendant.", "c": "追隨者；助手（教會的侍僧）", "s": "The famous architect rarely visited construction sites himself; instead, a loyal acolyte who had trained under him for fifteen years supervised the builders, faithfully carrying out every instruction and defending the master's ideas in meetings.", "t": "這位知名建築師很少親自到工地；取而代之的是一位在他門下受訓十五年的忠實追隨者負責監督工人，忠實執行每項指示，並在會議中捍衛大師的理念。", "as": "Surrounded by obsequious acolytes who echoed his every opinion, the aging philosopher grew complacent, until a former student's candor exposed how outdated many of his theories had become.", "at": "這位年邁的哲學家被一群對他每個觀點都隨聲附和、奉承諂媚的追隨者包圍，逐漸變得自滿，直到一位以前學生的坦率直言，揭露了他許多理論早已過時。"}, {"w": "chatoyant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having a changing, shimmering luster, like a cat's eye.", "c": "（如貓眼般）閃光變幻的；光彩閃爍的", "s": "Jewelers prize the gem known as tiger's eye for its chatoyant surface: when the polished stone is turned slowly under a lamp, a band of golden light seems to glide across it like the gleam in a cat's eye.", "t": "珠寶商十分珍視名為虎眼石的寶石，因為它的表面光彩變幻：當拋光的石頭在燈下緩緩轉動時，一道金色光帶彷彿像貓眼中的光芒般在表面滑過。", "as": "The designer's chatoyant silk gown was undeniably striking, but a fastidious critic dismissed it as garish, arguing that its shifting colors were a gratuitous distraction from the elegant tailoring.", "at": "這位設計師那件光澤變幻的絲綢禮服無疑十分搶眼，但一位挑剔的評論家卻斥之為俗豔，認為那些變幻的色彩是毫無必要的干擾，掩蓋了優雅的剪裁。"}, {"w": "doppelgänger", "p": "n.", "d": "A ghostly double of a living person; a look-alike.", "c": "（活人的）幽靈分身；長相酷似的人", "s": "In the eerie story studied in our German literature seminar, the narrator is horrified to meet his own doppelgänger, a stranger with his exact face and voice who seems to know every secret of his past.", "t": "在我們德國文學研討課上讀的那篇詭異故事中，敘事者驚恐地遇見了自己的分身——一個和他有著一模一樣臉孔和聲音、似乎知道他過去每個秘密的陌生人。", "as": "Edgar Allan Poe's tale \"William Wilson\" features a doppelgänger who acts as the conscience of the dissolute narrator, repeatedly thwarting his unscrupulous schemes until the reprobate finally destroys him.", "at": "愛倫・坡的短篇小說〈威廉・威爾森〉中有一個分身，扮演那位放蕩敘事者的良知，一再阻撓他不擇手段的詭計，直到這個無賴最終將他殺死。"}, {"w": "supernumerary", "p": "adj.", "d": "Exceeding the usual or required number; extra.", "c": "額外的；多餘的；編制外的", "s": "When the factory installed automated assembly lines, dozens of workers suddenly became supernumerary, and the company offered them retraining programs rather than keeping them on a payroll for jobs that no longer needed to be done.", "t": "工廠裝設自動化生產線後，數十名工人突然成了多餘的人力，公司於是提供他們再培訓課程，而不是讓他們繼續領薪做那些已不再需要的工作。", "as": "Biologists explain that the supernumerary toes on some cats result from a harmless mutation; far from being treated as a pariah, such a cat was considered a boon by sailors, who prized it as a skillful hunter.", "at": "生物學家解釋，有些貓多出來的腳趾源自無害的突變；這樣的貓非但沒有遭到排斥，反而被水手視為福星，因為他們看重牠是個捕獵高手。"}, {"w": "rebarbative", "p": "adj.", "d": "Unattractive and objectionable; tending to repel or irritate.", "c": "令人反感的；令人厭惡的", "s": "Although the scientist's research on vaccines was brilliant, his rebarbative personality, marked by constant sarcasm and contempt for colleagues, drove away collaborators and made it nearly impossible for him to secure funding for new projects.", "t": "雖然這位科學家的疫苗研究十分出色，但他那令人反感的個性——總是冷嘲熱諷、輕視同事——趕跑了合作者，也讓他幾乎不可能為新計畫爭取到經費。", "as": "The critic found the novel's narrator so rebarbative, an acerbic misanthrope who disparages everyone he meets, that she could barely finish the book despite its elegant prose.", "at": "這位評論家覺得小說的敘事者令人極為反感——一個尖酸刻薄、貶低身邊每個人的厭世者——儘管文筆優美，她仍幾乎讀不完這本書。"}, {"w": "louche", "p": "adj.", "d": "Disreputable or of questionable morality; shady.", "c": "不正派的；名聲不好的；可疑的", "s": "The novelist set her mystery in a louche waterfront district of 1920s Shanghai, where smugglers, swindlers, and corrupt officials met in smoky gambling halls that respectable citizens avoided after dark.", "t": "這位小說家把她的推理故事設定在1920年代上海一個名聲不佳的碼頭區，那裡的走私客、騙子和貪官在烏煙瘴氣的賭場聚會，體面的市民天黑後都避而遠之。", "as": "The once-genteel hotel had acquired a louche reputation, attracting dissolute gamblers and spendthrift heirs, until a new owner restored its dignity and dismissed the staff who had profited from the scandal.", "at": "這家曾經高雅的飯店漸漸聲名狼藉，吸引了放蕩的賭徒和揮霍無度的富家子弟，直到新業主恢復了它的尊嚴，並解雇了那些從醜聞中牟利的員工。"}, {"w": "interregnum", "p": "n.", "d": "A period between two reigns or governments; a pause.", "c": "（兩任君主或政府之間的）空位期；過渡期", "s": "During the seven-month interregnum that followed the king's sudden death, no one held the throne, and rival nobles competed fiercely for power until a council finally crowned his young nephew in a quiet ceremony.", "t": "國王猝逝後的七個月空位期間，無人繼承王位，敵對的貴族激烈爭權，直到一個議會終於在一場低調的儀式中為他年輕的姪子加冕。", "as": "During the brief interregnum between the two administrations, cautious officials avoided any unprecedented decisions, and the pragmatic interim director focused on keeping basic services running smoothly.", "at": "在兩屆政府交接的短暫空窗期，謹慎的官員避免做出任何史無前例的決定，而務實的代理主管則專注於維持基本服務順利運作。"}, {"w": "alembic", "p": "n.", "d": "A distilling apparatus; something that refines or transforms.", "c": "蒸餾器；淨化（或轉化）的工具", "s": "Medieval alchemists heated herbs and minerals in an alembic, a glass vessel with a long beaked spout, hoping that the vapors they collected and cooled would reveal the secret of turning ordinary metals into gold.", "t": "中世紀的煉金術士在蒸餾器——一種有著長長鳥嘴狀導管的玻璃容器——中加熱草藥和礦物，希望他們收集並冷卻的蒸氣能揭開把普通金屬變成黃金的秘密。", "as": "For the poet, grief became an alembic that distilled her mundane daily experiences into lucid, poignant verses admired by readers who had endured similar losses.", "at": "對這位詩人而言，悲傷成了一座蒸餾器，把她平凡的日常經驗提煉成清晰而動人的詩句，受到曾經歷類似喪痛的讀者推崇。"}, {"w": "oleaginous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Oily; falsely or excessively flattering.", "c": "油質的；油腔滑調的；諂媚的", "s": "The candidate's oleaginous manner at the fundraiser, with his exaggerated compliments, constant smiles, and eagerness to praise every wealthy donor, struck many guests as insincere and left them doubting his commitment to ordinary voters.", "t": "這位候選人在募款餐會上油腔滑調的態度——誇張的恭維、不斷的笑容，以及急於讚美每位富有捐款人的模樣——讓許多賓客覺得他虛情假意，也懷疑他對一般選民的承諾。", "as": "The oleaginous courtier was a consummate sycophant, cajoling the queen with endless flattery while secretly plotting against the few honest ministers who saw through his charm.", "at": "這位油腔滑調的朝臣是個十足的馬屁精，用無盡的奉承哄騙女王，同時暗中算計那幾位看穿他魅力的正直大臣。"}, {"w": "wastrel", "p": "n.", "d": "A wasteful person, especially one who squanders money.", "c": "揮霍者；浪費的人；敗家子", "s": "Within three years of inheriting his grandfather's fortune, the young wastrel had spent it all on racehorses, lavish parties, and luxury cars, leaving nothing for the family business that had taken decades to build.", "t": "繼承祖父的財產不到三年，這個年輕的敗家子就把錢全花在賽馬、奢華派對和豪華汽車上，讓那份花了數十年才建立起來的家族事業一無所剩。", "as": "Dismissed by his frugal father as an indolent wastrel, the young man surprised everyone by founding a lucrative software company and later donating much of his fortune to charity.", "at": "這個年輕人曾被節儉的父親斥為懶散的敗家子，卻出乎眾人意料地創辦了一家獲利豐厚的軟體公司，後來還把大部分財產捐給慈善機構。"}]}, {"unit": 46, "level": 10, "cards": [{"w": "sangfroid", "p": "n.", "d": "Composure and calmness under danger or pressure.", "c": "沉著；臨危不亂", "s": "When the engine failed shortly after takeoff, the pilot displayed remarkable sangfroid, calmly informing air traffic control, guiding the plane over the crowded city, and landing it safely on the river without a single passenger being seriously injured.", "t": "飛機起飛後不久引擎失靈，機長展現出非凡的沉著，冷靜地通知航管人員，駕駛飛機飛越人口稠密的城市，並安全降落在河面上，沒有任何一名乘客受重傷。", "as": "The surgeon's sangfroid during the crisis was legendary; while younger doctors panicked, she worked with stoic equanimity and adamant focus until the patient's heartbeat stabilized.", "at": "這位外科醫師在危急時刻的沉著鎮定堪稱傳奇；當年輕醫師驚慌失措時，她以堅忍的平靜與堅定不移的專注持續手術，直到病人的心跳穩定下來。"}, {"w": "desuetude", "p": "n.", "d": "A state of disuse or inactivity.", "c": "廢棄不用；廢止", "s": "The old law forbidding residents to keep goats within city limits had fallen into desuetude decades ago; no one had been fined under it since 1920, and most officials did not even know it still existed.", "t": "禁止居民在市區內飼養山羊的那條舊法律早在幾十年前就已廢棄不用；自1920年以來沒有人因此被罰款，大多數官員甚至不知道它依然存在。", "as": "After the railway closed, the station fell into desuetude, and the once-opulent waiting hall became a moribund relic until volunteers restored it as a nascent community arts center.", "at": "鐵路停駛後，車站便荒廢不用，昔日富麗堂皇的候車大廳成了奄奄一息的遺跡，直到志工將它修復，成為一座剛起步的社區藝術中心。"}, {"w": "shibboleth", "p": "n.", "d": "A word, custom, or belief that distinguishes a group.", "c": "（區分群體的）特定用語或習俗；陳腐的信條", "s": "For many years, the ability to quote Shakespeare from memory was a social shibboleth among the British elite, a test that quietly separated graduates of prestigious schools from those who had received an ordinary education.", "t": "多年來，能憑記憶背誦莎士比亞是英國菁英階層中的一種身分標記，這種考驗悄悄地把名校畢業生與只受過一般教育的人區分開來。", "as": "The economist challenged the old shibboleth that tax cuts always pay for themselves, offering lucid data that even her most obstinate critics found difficult to disparage.", "at": "這位經濟學家挑戰「減稅總能自行彌補財政」這條陳腐的信條，提出清晰的數據，讓即使是最頑固的批評者也難以貶低。"}, {"w": "cri de coeur", "p": "n.", "d": "A passionate cry of protest or appeal.", "c": "發自內心的吶喊；激動的呼籲", "s": "The young climate activist's speech at the United Nations was a genuine cri de coeur, an emotional appeal in which she begged world leaders to stop making empty promises and to act before her generation inherited a ruined planet.", "t": "這位年輕氣候運動人士在聯合國的演說是真正發自內心的吶喊，她在這場感性的呼籲中懇求世界領袖停止空洞的承諾，在她這一代繼承一個毀壞的星球之前採取行動。", "as": "Her novel is less a polished narrative than a cri de coeur against injustice, its plaintive passages giving voice to the pariahs whom society had long chosen to ostracize.", "at": "她的小說與其說是一部精雕細琢的敘事作品，不如說是對不公義發出的吶喊，書中淒婉的段落為那些長期遭社會排擠的邊緣人發聲。"}, {"w": "incunabula", "p": "n.", "d": "Books printed before 1501; the earliest stages of something.", "c": "古版書（1501年前印刷的書）；搖籃期", "s": "The university library's rare-book room holds several incunabula, including a copy of a Latin Bible printed in Mainz around 1460, which scholars may examine only while wearing gloves under the supervision of a librarian.", "t": "這所大學圖書館的珍本室收藏了數本古版書，包括一本約於1460年在美因茲印刷的拉丁文聖經，學者只能在館員監督下戴著手套翻閱。", "as": "Collectors pay lucrative sums for incunabula, yet one erudite curator argues that these fragile volumes are sacrosanct cultural treasures that belong in public libraries rather than private vaults.", "at": "收藏家願意花巨款購買古版書，但一位博學的館長主張，這些脆弱的典籍是神聖不可侵犯的文化瑰寶，應屬於公共圖書館，而非私人保險庫。"}, {"w": "chef-d'œuvre", "p": "n.", "d": "A masterpiece, especially in art or literature.", "c": "傑作；代表作", "s": "Although the composer wrote more than forty symphonies, critics agree that his final work, completed only weeks before his death, is his chef-d'œuvre, the piece that most fully reveals his genius and emotional depth.", "t": "雖然這位作曲家寫了四十多首交響曲，但評論家一致認為，他在去世前幾週才完成的最後一部作品是他的傑作，最能充分展現他的天才與情感深度。", "as": "Many critics consider the cathedral the architect's chef-d'œuvre, though some fastidious purists find its ornate towers ostentatious compared with the austere churches of his early career.", "at": "許多評論家認為這座大教堂是這位建築師的代表作，但一些挑剔的純粹主義者覺得，和他早期職業生涯中那些樸素的教堂相比，它華麗的尖塔顯得太過鋪張炫耀。"}, {"w": "iamb", "p": "n.", "d": "A metrical foot of one unstressed then one stressed syllable.", "c": "抑揚格（一輕一重的音步）", "s": "In our poetry unit, the teacher explained that each iamb contains an unstressed syllable followed by a stressed one, as in the word \"delight,\" and that five of these units form a single line of pentameter.", "t": "在我們的詩歌單元中，老師解釋說每個抑揚格音步都包含一個非重音節，後面接一個重音節，就像delight這個字一樣，而五個這樣的音步就組成一行五音步詩。", "as": "The pedantic professor insisted that every iamb be marked correctly, yet his didactic lectures on meter were so monotonous that even devoted students struggled to stay awake.", "at": "那位迂腐的教授堅持每個抑揚格音步都必須正確標記，但他講授格律的說教式課程極其單調乏味，連認真的學生都很難保持清醒。"}, {"w": "frisson", "p": "n.", "d": "A sudden thrill of excitement or fear.", "c": "（興奮或恐懼的）一陣戰慄；震顫", "s": "When the lights dimmed and the first notes of the famous overture filled the hall, a frisson of excitement passed through the audience, many of whom had waited years to hear the legendary orchestra perform live.", "t": "當燈光暗下、那首著名序曲的第一個音符響徹音樂廳時，觀眾之間湧起一陣興奮的戰慄，其中許多人已等了好幾年，只為現場聆聽這支傳奇樂團的演出。", "as": "Reading the explorer's laconic diary gave the historian a frisson of discovery, for its terse entries revealed a clandestine expedition that official records had never mentioned.", "at": "閱讀這位探險家言簡意賅的日記，讓這位歷史學家感受到一陣發現的興奮，因為那些簡短的記載揭露了一次官方紀錄從未提及的秘密探險。"}, {"w": "prelapsarian", "p": "adj.", "d": "Relating to the time before the Fall; innocent and unspoiled.", "c": "人類墮落前的；純真無邪的", "s": "The painter depicted the remote island as a prelapsarian paradise, with gentle animals, abundant fruit, and peaceful villagers, as if its inhabitants had never known greed, war, or any of the troubles of the modern world.", "t": "這位畫家把那座偏遠的小島描繪成人類墮落之前的樂園，有溫馴的動物、豐盛的果實和平和的村民，彷彿島上居民從未經歷過貪婪、戰爭或現代世界的任何煩惱。", "as": "Nostalgic novels often portray childhood as a prelapsarian world, but the author's candor about her own tenuous family life offered a far less sanguine view.", "at": "懷舊小說往往把童年描繪成純真無瑕的世界，但這位作者坦率寫出自己脆弱不穩的家庭生活，呈現出遠沒那麼樂觀的觀點。"}, {"w": "métier", "p": "n.", "d": "A person's trade, profession, or special area of skill.", "c": "專長；職業；擅長的領域", "s": "After years of struggling as a novelist, the writer discovered that her true métier was the short essay, a form in which her sharp observations and economical style allowed her to shine in a way longer fiction never had.", "t": "這位作家當了多年苦苦掙扎的小說家之後，才發現她真正的專長是短篇散文；在這種文體中，她敏銳的觀察和精簡的文風讓她大放異彩，這是長篇小說從未做到的。", "as": "The diffident engineer found her métier in designing accessible playgrounds for disabled children, work that perfectly suited both her assiduous attention to detail and her genuine altruism.", "at": "這位內向羞怯的工程師在為身心障礙兒童設計無障礙遊樂場中找到了自己的專長，這份工作完全符合她對細節孜孜不倦的關注，以及她真誠的利他精神。"}, {"w": "ablution", "p": "n.", "d": "The act of washing oneself, especially as a religious ritual.", "c": "沐浴；淨身（尤指宗教儀式）", "s": "Before entering the temple, worshippers performed a ritual ablution, using a wooden ladle to pour cool water over their hands and rinse their mouths as a symbol of purifying both body and mind.", "t": "進入神社前，參拜者會進行淨身儀式，用木杓把清涼的水淋在手上並漱口，象徵身心皆得到淨化。", "as": "The anthropologist's lucid account explained that the villagers' morning ablutions in the river were not mundane hygiene habits but sacrosanct rituals connecting each family to its ancestors.", "at": "這位人類學家清晰的描述說明，村民每天早晨在河中的沐浴淨身並非平凡的衛生習慣，而是將每個家庭與祖先連結起來、神聖不可侵犯的儀式。"}, {"w": "apostasy", "p": "n.", "d": "The abandonment of one's religious faith or political principles.", "c": "背教；變節；背棄信仰（或主義）", "s": "When the senator, who had spent thirty years championing free trade, suddenly voted for strict tariffs, members of his party condemned the move as an act of apostasy and accused him of betraying the principles they shared.", "t": "這位花了三十年倡導自由貿易的參議員突然投票支持嚴格關稅時，黨內成員譴責此舉是背棄理念的行為，並指控他背叛了他們共同的原則。", "as": "In the seventeenth century, apostasy could make a believer a pariah, yet the philosopher Spinoza endured excommunication with stoic calm and continued his erudite work in quiet poverty.", "at": "在十七世紀，背棄信仰可能使信徒成為人人排斥的對象，但哲學家史賓諾莎以堅忍的平靜承受被逐出教會的處分，並在清貧中默默繼續他淵博的著述。"}, {"w": "sumptuary", "p": "adj.", "d": "Regulating personal spending, especially on luxuries.", "c": "限制奢侈的；節制個人消費的", "s": "In Elizabethan England, sumptuary laws strictly controlled what people could wear, forbidding anyone below a certain social rank from dressing in purple silk, gold thread, or other fabrics reserved for the nobility.", "t": "在伊莉莎白時代的英格蘭，限制奢侈的法律嚴格規範人們的穿著，禁止某一社會階級以下的人穿著紫色絲綢、金線或其他專屬於貴族的布料。", "as": "Ancient Roman sumptuary laws tried to curb ostentatious banquets by limiting the number of guests and dishes, but wealthy spendthrifts usually found clever ways to evade them with impunity.", "at": "古羅馬限制奢侈的法律試圖藉由限制賓客人數和菜餚數量來遏止鋪張炫耀的宴會，但富有的揮霍者通常都能找到巧妙的辦法規避，且不受懲罰。"}, {"w": "tatterdemalion", "p": "n.", "d": "A person dressed in ragged, tattered clothing.", "c": "衣衫襤褸的人；破衣爛衫者", "s": "Charles Dickens often described the London streets as crowded with orphans and beggars, and in one scene a thin tatterdemalion in a torn coat and mismatched shoes asks a wealthy gentleman for a single coin.", "t": "狄更斯常描寫倫敦街頭擠滿孤兒和乞丐；在某一幕中，一個穿著破外套、腳上的鞋子不成對、骨瘦如柴的衣衫襤褸者向一位富有的紳士乞討一枚硬幣。", "as": "The tatterdemalion who wandered into the village was at first treated as a pariah, but his sagacious advice during the drought soon won him the gratitude of even the most obstinate farmers.", "at": "那個流浪到村裡、衣衫襤褸的人起初遭人排斥，但他在旱災期間提出的睿智建議，很快就贏得了連最固執的農夫都心存感激。"}, {"w": "abjure", "p": "v.", "d": "To solemnly renounce a belief, claim, or practice.", "c": "公開放棄；發誓棄絕", "s": "In 1633, under threat of imprisonment, Galileo was forced to abjure his belief that the Earth moves around the sun, publicly declaring before the court that he rejected the idea he had defended for years.", "t": "1633年，在監禁的威脅下，伽利略被迫公開放棄他「地球繞著太陽轉」的信念，在法庭上公開宣布他摒棄自己捍衛多年的觀點。", "as": "Though pressured to abjure his unorthodox theories, the adamant scientist refused, and his candor eventually won the admiration of colleagues who had once been quick to castigate him.", "at": "儘管被施壓要他公開放棄那些非正統的理論，這位堅定不移的科學家仍然拒絕，而他的坦率最終贏得了那些曾急於嚴厲批評他的同事的敬佩。"}, {"w": "noblesse oblige", "p": "n.", "d": "The duty of the privileged to act generously toward others.", "c": "貴族義務；位高則任重", "s": "Motivated by a sense of noblesse oblige, the wealthy family that owned the mill funded a free school and a clinic for workers' children, believing that their privileged position required them to help those with fewer advantages.", "t": "出於一種「位高則任重」的責任感，擁有這座工廠的富裕家族出資為工人子女興建了一所免費學校和一家診所，他們相信自己的特權地位要求他們幫助那些條件較差的人。", "as": "Critics dismissed the billionaire's donations as condescending noblesse oblige, but beneficiaries argued that his magnanimous gifts did more to ameliorate poverty than any government program.", "at": "批評者把這位億萬富翁的捐款斥為居高臨下的貴族施恩，但受惠者認為，他慷慨大方的捐贈在減輕貧困方面，比任何政府計畫都更有成效。"}, {"w": "primogeniture", "p": "n.", "d": "The right of the eldest son to inherit everything.", "c": "長子繼承制；長子繼承權", "s": "Under the system of primogeniture that governed many aristocratic families in medieval Europe, the eldest son inherited the entire estate, so younger brothers often had to seek their fortunes in the church or the army.", "t": "在中世紀歐洲許多貴族家庭所奉行的長子繼承制度下，長子繼承全部產業，因此弟弟們往往只能到教會或軍隊中另謀出路。", "as": "Primogeniture seemed sacrosanct to the old aristocracy, but reformers condemned it as arbitrary and argued that dividing estates more fairly would redress generations of inequality.", "at": "對舊貴族而言，長子繼承制似乎神聖不可侵犯，但改革者譴責它是武斷專橫的制度，並主張更公平地分配財產，才能矯正數代以來的不平等。"}, {"w": "xeric", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having or adapted to extremely dry conditions.", "c": "乾燥的；適應乾旱的；旱生的", "s": "To conserve water during the long drought, the city encouraged homeowners to replace thirsty lawns with xeric gardens filled with cacti, agaves, and other plants that thrive on very little rainfall.", "t": "為了在漫長的乾旱期間節約用水，市政府鼓勵屋主把耗水的草坪換成旱生植物花園，種滿仙人掌、龍舌蘭和其他只需極少雨量就能茂盛生長的植物。", "as": "Botanists once dismissed the xeric plateau as a barren wasteland, but recent fieldwork revealed an eclectic community of hardy shrubs and insects whose survival strategies are nothing short of uncanny.", "at": "植物學家曾把這片乾旱的高原視為貧瘠的荒地，但最近的田野調查發現，那裡有種類多元的耐旱灌木與昆蟲群落，牠們的生存策略簡直不可思議。"}, {"w": "uxorious", "p": "adj.", "d": "Excessively fond of or submissive to one's wife.", "c": "溺愛妻子的；過分順從妻子的", "s": "In the comic play, the uxorious merchant cannot make even the smallest decision without consulting his wife, and his friends tease him for agreeing to every one of her requests, no matter how unreasonable.", "t": "在這齣喜劇中，那位溺愛妻子的商人連最小的決定都要先徵詢太太的意見，他的朋友們取笑他對妻子的每個要求都言聽計從，無論多麼不合理。", "as": "Historians describe the emperor as uxorious, so devoted to his wife that he let her advisers make capricious decisions while obsequious courtiers flattered them both.", "at": "歷史學家形容這位皇帝溺愛妻子，他對皇后如此言聽計從，以致讓她的謀士做出反覆無常的決定，而諂媚的朝臣則對兩人極盡奉承。"}, {"w": "oppugn", "p": "v.", "d": "To call into question; to dispute or oppose.", "c": "質疑；反駁；抨擊", "s": "At the conference, a young researcher rose to oppugn the professor's widely accepted theory, presenting new fossil evidence that contradicted his claim about when birds first evolved from small dinosaurs.", "t": "在研討會上，一位年輕研究人員起身質疑那位教授廣為接受的理論，提出新的化石證據，反駁他關於鳥類何時最初從小型恐龍演化而來的主張。", "as": "Few dared to oppugn the venerated historian's conclusions, but one diffident graduate student, armed with tenacious research and lucid arguments, finally exposed the tenuous evidence behind them.", "at": "很少有人敢質疑這位德高望重的歷史學家的結論，但一位羞怯的研究生憑著鍥而不捨的研究與清晰的論證，終於揭露了那些結論背後薄弱的證據。"}]}, {"unit": 47, "level": 10, "cards": [{"w": "agnosia", "p": "n.", "d": "Inability to recognize objects, people, or sounds despite normal senses.", "c": "失認症；認知不能", "s": "After a minor stroke damaged part of his visual cortex, the retired professor could still see a cup, a key, and a pencil perfectly clearly, yet he could no longer name or recognize any of them, a puzzling condition neurologists diagnosed as agnosia.", "t": "一次輕微中風損傷了這位退休教授的部分視覺皮質後，他仍能清楚看見杯子、鑰匙和鉛筆，卻再也無法說出它們的名稱或辨認它們；神經科醫師將這種令人費解的狀況診斷為失認症。", "as": "Oliver Sacks's case studies of agnosia are hardly prosaic medical reports; with lucid prose and genuine compassion, he made esoteric neurological disorders understandable to ordinary readers.", "at": "奧利佛．薩克斯關於失認症的個案研究絕非平淡乏味的醫學報告；他以清晰的文筆和真誠的同理心，讓一般讀者也能理解深奧難懂的神經疾病。"}, {"w": "casuistry", "p": "n.", "d": "Clever but misleading reasoning, especially about moral questions.", "c": "詭辯；似是而非的道德推理", "s": "The philosophy professor warned her students against casuistry, explaining that clever arguments which twist moral principles to excuse obviously wrong behavior, such as justifying cheating on the grounds that everyone else does it, may sound persuasive but ultimately rest on deceptive reasoning.", "t": "這位哲學教授警告學生要提防詭辯，她解釋說，那些扭曲道德原則來為明顯錯誤的行為開脫的巧妙論證，例如以「別人也都這麼做」為由替作弊辯解，聽起來或許有說服力，但歸根究柢是建立在欺騙性的推理之上。", "as": "The lawyer's casuistry was so specious that even the jurors, initially impressed by his polished closing argument, soon recognized it as mere sophistry designed to obfuscate his client's guilt.", "at": "這位律師的詭辯似是而非，連起初對他精心修飾的結辯印象深刻的陪審員，很快也看穿那不過是為了混淆其當事人罪責的強詞奪理。"}, {"w": "parapraxis", "p": "n.", "d": "A slip of the tongue or pen thought to reveal hidden wishes.", "c": "失誤動作；佛洛伊德式口誤", "s": "When the nervous candidate accidentally called his campaign launch a farewell speech, commentators joked that the parapraxis revealed his secret doubts about winning the election, just as Sigmund Freud would have predicted.", "t": "這位緊張的候選人不小心把自己的競選造勢活動說成告別演說，評論員開玩笑說，這個口誤透露出他對勝選暗藏的疑慮，正如佛洛伊德會預料的那樣。", "as": "Freud contended that every parapraxis, however trivial it seemed, offered a revealing glimpse of repressed desires, but many modern psychologists regard this supposition as tenuous and impossible to test.", "at": "佛洛伊德主張，每一次失誤動作無論看似多麼微不足道，都能讓人一窺被壓抑的慾望；但許多現代心理學家認為這個假設站不住腳，而且無法檢驗。"}, {"w": "polymath", "p": "n.", "d": "A person with great knowledge in many different fields.", "c": "博學者；通才", "s": "Leonardo da Vinci is often described as the ultimate polymath, since he not only painted the Mona Lisa but also designed flying machines, dissected human bodies to study anatomy, and filled notebooks with observations about geology, optics, and engineering.", "t": "李奧納多．達文西常被譽為終極的博學通才，因為他不僅畫了《蒙娜麗莎》，還設計飛行器、解剖人體研究解剖學，並在筆記本中寫滿了對地質、光學和工程的觀察。", "as": "A true polymath, Benjamin Franklin was a prolific writer and printer, an adroit diplomat, and an inventor whose erudite experiments with electricity earned admiration throughout Europe.", "at": "班傑明．富蘭克林是一位真正的博學者：他是多產的作家兼印刷商、精明幹練的外交官，也是發明家，他對電學所做的淵博實驗贏得了全歐洲的讚賞。"}, {"w": "encomium", "p": "n.", "d": "A speech or piece of writing expressing warm, formal praise.", "c": "讚頌；頌詞", "s": "At the ceremony honoring the retiring principal, a former student delivered a heartfelt encomium, praising her decades of devotion, her unwavering kindness toward struggling pupils, and her remarkable talent for making every teenager feel valued and understood.", "t": "在表彰即將退休校長的典禮上，一位校友發表了一篇真摯的頌詞，讚揚她數十年來的奉獻、她對學習困難學生始終如一的善意，以及她讓每個青少年都感到被重視與理解的非凡才能。", "as": "The critic's effusive encomium for the debut novel struck some readers as hyperbole, yet the young author's poignant portrayal of rural poverty genuinely deserved high praise.", "at": "這位評論家對這部處女作小說熱情洋溢的讚頌，在部分讀者看來有些誇大，但這位年輕作家對鄉村貧困的動人描寫確實值得高度讚揚。"}, {"w": "charrette", "p": "n.", "d": "An intense, final burst of work to finish a project.", "c": "專案衝刺；密集協作設計會議", "s": "With the city council's deadline only three days away, the architecture students locked themselves in the studio for an intense charrette, sketching, debating, and rebuilding models around the clock until their redesign of the riverfront park was finally complete.", "t": "距離市議會的截止期限只剩三天，建築系學生把自己關在工作室裡展開密集的衝刺，夜以繼日地畫草圖、辯論並重做模型，直到河濱公園的重新設計終於完成。", "as": "During the weeklong charrette, residents, engineers, and planners managed to reconcile their disparate visions, and the collaborative plan that emerged was far more felicitous than any proposal drafted alone.", "at": "在為期一週的密集設計研討中，居民、工程師和規劃師成功調和了彼此迥異的願景，最後產出的合作方案遠比任何單獨擬定的提案都更為恰當。"}, {"w": "debride", "p": "v.", "d": "To remove dead or infected tissue from a wound.", "c": "清創；清除壞死組織", "s": "Before the surgeon could close the soldier's badly infected leg wound, she had to carefully debride it, cutting away the dead and contaminated tissue so that the healthy flesh underneath could heal properly and the infection would not spread.", "t": "外科醫師在縫合這名士兵嚴重感染的腿部傷口之前，必須先仔細清創，切除壞死及受污染的組織，好讓底下健康的組織得以正常癒合，感染也不會擴散。", "as": "Nurses must debride burn wounds meticulously, because leaving even a modicum of dead tissue behind can cause a serious infection and protract the patient's painful recovery for many weeks.", "at": "護理師必須一絲不苟地為燒傷傷口清創，因為即使殘留少量壞死組織，也可能引發嚴重感染，使病人痛苦的復原期延長好幾週。"}, {"w": "lapidary", "p": "adj.", "d": "Elegant, precise, and concise, as if engraved in stone.", "c": "簡潔精煉的；寶石雕刻的", "s": "Critics admired the poet's lapidary style, noting that each short line seemed chiseled with the precision of a stone engraver, so that not a single word was wasted and every phrase could be quoted on a monument.", "t": "評論家讚賞這位詩人簡潔精煉的文風，指出每一行短句彷彿都經石匠精準雕琢，沒有一個字是多餘的，每一句都足以刻在紀念碑上。", "as": "Lincoln's Gettysburg Address, with its lapidary phrasing and laconic eloquence, stands in stark contrast to the verbose, rambling two-hour oration that preceded it that afternoon.", "at": "林肯的蓋茲堡演說措辭精煉、言簡意賅，與當天下午在它之前那場長達兩小時、冗長散漫的演說形成鮮明對比。"}, {"w": "oviparous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Producing eggs that hatch outside the mother's body.", "c": "卵生的", "s": "Most reptiles and birds are oviparous, laying eggs that develop and hatch outside the mother's body, whereas nearly all mammals give birth to live young, with the platypus and the echidna being famous exceptions to that rule.", "t": "大多數爬蟲類和鳥類都是卵生的，牠們產下的蛋在母體外發育並孵化；而幾乎所有哺乳類都直接產下幼崽，鴨嘴獸和針鼴則是此規則中著名的例外。", "as": "The platypus, an oviparous mammal, seemed so anomalous to early European naturalists that some dismissed the first specimens as spurious creations stitched together by clever hoaxers.", "at": "鴨嘴獸是卵生的哺乳動物，牠在早期歐洲博物學家眼中顯得極為反常，有些人甚至認為最早送到的標本是狡猾的騙子縫合拼湊出來的假貨。"}, {"w": "marmoreal", "p": "adj.", "d": "Resembling marble, especially in being cold, smooth, or white.", "c": "大理石般的；冷峻的", "s": "Visitors to the museum gazed at the ancient Greek statue of Athena, whose marmoreal skin appeared so smooth, pale, and cold that it seemed less like carved stone than like a living goddess frozen in perfect stillness.", "t": "博物館的參觀者凝視著古希臘雅典娜雕像，她那大理石般的肌膚看起來如此光滑、蒼白又冰冷，與其說是雕刻的石頭，不如說像一位凝結在完美靜止中的活生生女神。", "as": "The aristocrat's marmoreal composure never wavered during the trial; she listened to every allegation with stoic indifference, as aloof as the statues lining her family's estate.", "at": "這位貴族在審判期間始終保持如大理石般冷峻的鎮定；她以堅忍淡漠的態度聆聽每一項指控，冷漠得就像她家族莊園裡排列的雕像。"}, {"w": "nugatory", "p": "adj.", "d": "Of no real value or importance; having no effect.", "c": "無價值的；無效的", "s": "The new regulation proved almost entirely nugatory, because the agency responsible for enforcing it had no inspectors, no budget, and no legal authority to fine companies that ignored its rules, so factories simply continued polluting as before.", "t": "這項新規定幾乎完全形同虛設，因為負責執行的機關既沒有稽查員、沒有預算，也沒有對違規企業開罰的法定權力，於是工廠照舊排放污染。", "as": "The committee dismissed his objections as nugatory, a pedantic catalog of trivial errors that did nothing to undermine the study's salient conclusions about air pollution and childhood asthma.", "at": "委員會認為他的反對意見毫無價值，不過是一份賣弄學問、羅列瑣碎錯誤的清單，絲毫動搖不了該研究關於空氣污染與兒童氣喘的重要結論。"}, {"w": "presbycusis", "p": "n.", "d": "Gradual loss of hearing that comes with old age.", "c": "老年性聽力喪失；老年重聽", "s": "Audiologists explain that presbycusis usually develops slowly after age sixty, as tiny hair cells in the inner ear wear out over decades, which is why many grandparents struggle to hear high-pitched voices and conversations in noisy restaurants.", "t": "聽力師解釋，老年性聽力喪失通常在六十歲以後慢慢出現，因為內耳中細小的毛細胞經過數十年逐漸耗損，這就是許多祖父母難以聽清高音調的聲音以及在吵雜餐廳中交談的原因。", "as": "Many elderly people with presbycusis feel marginalized at family gatherings, and some become taciturn or morose rather than repeatedly asking relatives to speak more loudly.", "at": "許多患有老年性聽力喪失的長者在家庭聚會中感到被邊緣化，有些人寧可變得沉默寡言或悶悶不樂，也不願一再請親戚說大聲一點。"}, {"w": "cicerone", "p": "n.", "d": "A guide who shows and explains sights to visitors.", "c": "導遊；嚮導", "s": "Our cicerone in Rome, a retired archaeology professor, led the group through the Forum for four hours, pointing out crumbling temples, explaining the history behind each ancient ruin, and answering every question with patience and humor.", "t": "我們在羅馬的導遊是一位退休的考古學教授，他帶領團員在古羅馬廣場走了四個小時，一一指出傾頹的神殿、講解每座古蹟背後的歷史，並以耐心和幽默回答每一個問題。", "as": "Acting as our cicerone through the labyrinthine streets of old Kyoto, the erudite monk patiently elucidated the long and fascinating history of every temple we passed that morning.", "at": "這位學識淵博的僧侶擔任我們的嚮導，帶我們穿梭於京都古城迷宮般的街道，並耐心闡明那天早上沿途每座寺廟悠久而迷人的歷史。"}, {"w": "pansophic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having or claiming universal knowledge of all subjects.", "c": "全知的；無所不通的", "s": "The encyclopedia's ambitious editors hoped to create a truly pansophic reference work, one that would gather all human knowledge, from astronomy and botany to music and law, into a single collection accessible to every curious reader.", "t": "這部百科全書雄心勃勃的編輯們希望打造一部真正無所不包的參考著作，將從天文學、植物學到音樂與法律的所有人類知識，匯集成一套每位好奇讀者都能取用的全集。", "as": "No scholar is truly pansophic, so the professor's supercilious claim that he could answer any question struck his students as a pretentious bit of braggadocio.", "at": "沒有任何學者是真正無所不知的，因此這位教授傲慢地宣稱自己能回答任何問題，在學生看來不過是一番自命不凡的吹噓。"}, {"w": "rubicund", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having a healthy, reddish complexion; ruddy.", "c": "紅潤的；面色紅潤的", "s": "After a brisk morning hike up the snowy mountain, the old farmer returned to the cabin with a rubicund face, his cheeks glowing bright red from the cold wind and vigorous exercise, looking healthier than he had in years.", "t": "在雪山上輕快健行一個早上之後，這位老農夫回到小屋時滿面紅光，他的雙頰因寒風和劇烈運動而泛著鮮紅的光澤，看起來比多年來都要健康。", "as": "The rubicund innkeeper was a jovial host, greeting each weary traveler with a convivial toast and a hearty meal beside the roaring fireplace before they had even removed their muddy boots.", "at": "這位面色紅潤的旅店老闆是個快活的主人，旅客們還沒脫下沾滿泥濘的靴子，他就在熊熊爐火旁以歡樂的祝酒和豐盛的餐點迎接每一位疲憊的旅人。"}, {"w": "picaresque", "p": "adj.", "d": "Relating to fiction about the adventures of a likable rogue.", "c": "流浪漢小說的；以無賴冒險為題材的", "s": "Mark Twain's Adventures of Huckleberry Finn borrows from the picaresque tradition, following a clever, rule-breaking boy through a loosely connected series of episodes as he drifts down the Mississippi River and meets swindlers, feuding families, and colorful scoundrels.", "t": "馬克．吐溫的《頑童歷險記》借鑒了流浪漢小說的傳統，描寫一個聰明又不守規矩的男孩沿密西西比河漂流，在一連串鬆散相連的情節中遇見騙子、世仇家族以及形形色色的無賴。", "as": "The anonymous author of Lazarillo de Tormes created the first great picaresque hero, a penniless boy whose adroit trickery and ingratiating charm help him survive a series of cruel masters.", "at": "《小癩子》的匿名作者塑造了第一位偉大的流浪漢小說主角——一個身無分文的男孩，他憑著靈巧的詐術和討好人的魅力，在一連串殘酷的主人手下存活下來。"}, {"w": "endogenous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Originating or produced from within an organism or system.", "c": "內生的；內源性的", "s": "Researchers discovered that the hormone was endogenous, produced naturally inside the body by specialized cells in the brain rather than absorbed from food or medicine, which explained why patients' levels rose and fell on a regular daily cycle.", "t": "研究人員發現這種荷爾蒙是內源性的，是由大腦中的特化細胞在體內自然產生，而非從食物或藥物中吸收，這解釋了為何患者體內的濃度會以規律的每日週期起伏。", "as": "Economists debated whether the recession was endogenous, caused by intrinsic flaws in the banking system, or an unforeseen ramification of a sudden political cataclysm abroad that rattled global markets.", "at": "經濟學家爭論這場衰退究竟是內生的，源於銀行體系本身的缺陷，還是海外一場突如其來的政治巨變所引發、震撼全球市場的意外後果。"}, {"w": "perorate", "p": "v.", "d": "To speak at great length in a grand, formal style.", "c": "長篇大論；（演說）作總結", "s": "Instead of answering the student's simple question about the homework deadline, the professor began to perorate on the decline of academic standards, speaking grandly and at tiresome length for nearly forty minutes while the class stared at the clock.", "t": "教授沒有回答學生關於作業截止日的簡單問題，反而開始長篇大論地談起學術水準的衰退，以浮誇的語氣冗長地講了將近四十分鐘，全班只能盯著時鐘看。", "as": "Every evening the demagogue would perorate for hours in a crowded stadium, delivering a vitriolic diatribe against immigrants that his loyal supporters cheered with fervent enthusiasm.", "at": "每天晚上，這位煽動家都會在擠滿人的體育場裡長篇大論好幾個小時，發表抨擊移民的惡毒長篇演說，而他忠實的支持者則報以狂熱的歡呼。"}, {"w": "onychophagy", "p": "n.", "d": "The habit of biting one's fingernails.", "c": "咬指甲癖", "s": "Dermatologists report that onychophagy often begins in childhood as a way of coping with stress or boredom, and that chronic nail-biting can damage the nail bed, spread germs from the fingers to the mouth, and even harm the teeth.", "t": "皮膚科醫師指出，咬指甲癖常在童年時期開始，作為應對壓力或無聊的方式，而長期咬指甲可能損傷甲床、將手指上的細菌帶入口中，甚至傷害牙齒。", "as": "His chronic onychophagy betrayed the anxiety beneath his urbane exterior; whenever negotiations reached an impasse, he would surreptitiously gnaw at his fingernails beneath the table.", "at": "他長期咬指甲的習慣洩漏了他溫文儒雅外表下的焦慮；每當談判陷入僵局，他就會在桌下偷偷啃咬指甲。"}, {"w": "déjà lu", "p": "n.", "d": "The feeling of having already read something before.", "c": "似曾讀過之感；讀過的舊東西", "s": "Halfway through the bestselling thriller, the literature professor experienced a strong sense of déjà lu, realizing that its plot twists, characters, and even several descriptions closely resembled a little-known mystery novel she had read decades earlier.", "t": "讀到這本暢銷驚悚小說的一半時，這位文學教授產生了強烈的似曾讀過之感，她發現書中的情節轉折、角色，甚至好幾段描寫，都與她數十年前讀過的一本冷門推理小說極為相似。", "as": "The reviewer complained that the hackneyed memoir offered nothing but déjà lu, a predictable rehash of banal anecdotes that readers had encountered in countless earlier celebrity autobiographies.", "at": "這位書評家抱怨，這本陳腔濫調的回憶錄只帶給人似曾讀過之感，不過是把讀者早已在無數名人自傳中看過的平庸軼事再炒一次冷飯。"}]}, {"unit": 48, "level": 10, "cards": [{"w": "verbigerate", "p": "v.", "d": "To repeat the same words or phrases meaninglessly and obsessively.", "c": "反覆唸叨；無意義地重複字句", "s": "Psychiatrists noted that during severe episodes the patient would verbigerate for hours, repeating the same three meaningless phrases over and over in a monotone, apparently unaware that the nurses beside him were trying to speak to him.", "t": "精神科醫師注意到，在嚴重發作期間，這名病人會一連好幾個小時反覆唸叨，以單調的語氣一遍又一遍重複同樣三句毫無意義的話，似乎完全沒察覺身旁的護理師正試著跟他說話。", "as": "Rather than offering a cogent rebuttal, the flustered candidate began to verbigerate, repeating the same hackneyed slogans until even his allies found the monotonous performance embarrassing.", "at": "這位慌亂的候選人沒有提出有力的反駁，反而開始反覆唸叨，一再重複同樣陳腔濫調的口號，直到連他的盟友都覺得這場單調的表演令人難堪。"}, {"w": "tenebrous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Dark, shadowy, or gloomy; also hard to understand.", "c": "陰暗的；晦澀難懂的", "s": "The explorers lit their lanterns before entering the tenebrous cave, where no sunlight had penetrated for thousands of years and the darkness was so complete that they could not see their own hands in front of their faces.", "t": "探險隊員在進入那座陰暗的洞穴前點亮了提燈；那裡數千年來從未有陽光照入，黑暗徹底得讓他們連眼前自己的手都看不見。", "as": "Eighteenth-century Gothic novelists especially delighted in tenebrous settings, filling their stories with crumbling castles, labyrinthine corridors, and lugubrious villains who lurked in dim, candlelit chambers.", "at": "十八世紀的哥德小說家尤其熱衷於陰暗的場景，在故事中填滿傾頹的城堡、迷宮般的走廊，以及潛伏在燭光幽微的密室裡、陰鬱哀戚的反派角色。"}, {"w": "agnate", "p": "adj.", "d": "Related through the father's side or male line of descent.", "c": "父系的；男系親屬的", "s": "Under the ancient Roman system of inheritance, only agnate relatives, those connected to the deceased through a continuous line of male ancestors, could claim his estate, while relatives on the mother's side received nothing.", "t": "在古羅馬的繼承制度下，只有父系親屬——也就是透過一脈相承的男性祖先與死者相連的人——才能主張繼承他的遺產，母系的親屬則一無所得。", "as": "In many traditional Chinese villages, agnate kinship determined who could worship in the ancestral hall, and the custom of primogeniture gave the eldest son an almost sacrosanct authority.", "at": "在許多中國傳統村落中，父系親屬關係決定誰能在祠堂祭祖，而長子繼承的習俗更賦予長子幾乎神聖不可侵犯的權威。"}, {"w": "ululate", "p": "v.", "d": "To howl or wail loudly, often in grief or celebration.", "c": "嚎叫；哀號", "s": "As the victorious runners crossed the finish line, women in the crowd began to ululate, filling the stadium with long, high-pitched, trilling cries that are a traditional expression of joy in many parts of North Africa and the Middle East.", "t": "當獲勝的選手衝過終點線時，人群中的婦女開始高聲歡呼，讓整座體育場充滿悠長、高亢、帶顫音的呼聲，這在北非與中東許多地區是表達喜悅的傳統方式。", "as": "At the funeral, the mourners began to ululate softly at first, and their plaintive cries grew louder until the whole disconsolate village seemed to share a single unbearable grief.", "at": "在葬禮上，送葬者起初輕聲哀號，哀傷的哭聲越來越響，直到整個悲痛欲絕的村莊彷彿共同承受著同一份難以忍受的哀慟。"}, {"w": "zucchetto", "p": "n.", "d": "A small round skullcap worn by Roman Catholic clergy.", "c": "（天主教神職人員的）無邊便帽；小圓帽", "s": "Visitors to the Vatican can identify a cardinal by his scarlet zucchetto, the small round skullcap perched on the back of his head, while the pope wears a white one and bishops wear one of purple silk.", "t": "到梵蒂岡參觀的遊客可以從猩紅色的小圓帽辨認出樞機主教——那是一頂戴在後腦上的小型圓形便帽；教宗戴白色的，主教則戴紫色絲質的。", "as": "The elderly bishop's purple zucchetto was the only ostentatious detail of his otherwise austere attire, a humble wardrobe that reflected his lifelong devotion to frugal living.", "at": "這位年邁主教的紫色小圓帽，是他一身樸素裝扮中唯一顯眼的細節；他簡樸的衣著反映了他一生崇尚節儉生活的信念。"}, {"w": "pseudandry", "p": "n.", "d": "A woman's use of a man's name as a pen name.", "c": "女性使用男性筆名", "s": "Because Victorian publishers often dismissed novels by women, Mary Ann Evans resorted to pseudandry, publishing Middlemarch under the name George Eliot so that critics would judge her work on its merits rather than on her gender.", "t": "由於維多利亞時代的出版商往往輕視女性寫的小說，瑪麗．安．艾凡斯便採用男性筆名，以喬治．艾略特之名出版《米德鎮的春天》，讓評論家依作品本身的價值而非她的性別來評斷。", "as": "The Brontë sisters' pseudandry was a pragmatic stratagem: writing as Currer, Ellis, and Acton Bell, they hoped to avoid the stigma attached to female authors in their era.", "at": "勃朗特姊妹使用男性筆名是一種務實的策略：她們以柯勒、艾利斯和艾克頓．貝爾之名寫作，希望避開當時加諸女性作家的污名。"}, {"w": "caesura", "p": "n.", "d": "A pause or break, especially within a line of poetry.", "c": "（詩行中的）停頓；中斷", "s": "In Old English poetry such as Beowulf, every line is divided into two halves by a strong caesura, a natural pause in the middle of the line that gives the verse its distinctive rhythm when read aloud.", "t": "在《貝奧武夫》等古英語詩歌中，每一行都被一個明顯的停頓分為前後兩半；這個位於詩行中間的自然停頓，使詩句在朗讀時具有獨特的節奏。", "as": "The pianist's dramatic caesura just before the final chord was so poignant that the entire audience held its breath, and the ensuing silence felt almost ethereal.", "at": "鋼琴家在最後一個和弦之前那戲劇性的停頓如此動人，全場觀眾都屏住了呼吸，隨之而來的寂靜幾乎有種空靈之感。"}, {"w": "philodox", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who loves and stubbornly clings to his own opinions.", "c": "固執己見者；自以為是的人", "s": "No amount of evidence could change the mind of the stubborn columnist, a lifelong philodox who loved his own opinions so dearly that he dismissed every contradicting study as biased and every critic as ignorant.", "t": "再多的證據也改變不了這位頑固專欄作家的想法；他一輩子固執己見，深愛自己的觀點，把每一項相反的研究都斥為偏頗，把每一位批評者都視為無知。", "as": "An obstinate philodox, the senator would pontificate on any subject and rebuff every expert who dared to question his opinions, however well-founded their objections were.", "at": "這位參議員是個頑固的自以為是者，他對任何主題都愛高談闊論，並斷然回絕每一位膽敢質疑他意見的專家，無論他們的反對理由多麼有根據。"}, {"w": "valetudinarian", "p": "n.", "d": "A sickly person who worries constantly about his health.", "c": "體弱多病者；過分擔心健康的人", "s": "Mr. Woodhouse in Jane Austen's Emma is a classic valetudinarian, constantly fretting about drafts, damp weather, and rich food, and urging his guests to eat thin gruel because he fears that cake might harm their health.", "t": "珍．奧斯汀《艾瑪》中的伍德豪斯先生是典型的過分擔心健康的人，他總是為穿堂風、潮濕的天氣和油膩的食物憂心忡忡，還力勸客人喝稀粥，因為他擔心蛋糕會傷害他們的健康。", "as": "The aging composer became a reclusive valetudinarian, so fastidious about his diet and so anxious about germs that he languished indoors for months, refusing to see even his closest friends.", "at": "這位年邁的作曲家變成一個離群索居、過度憂心健康的人；他對飲食極度挑剔，又非常害怕病菌，因此在室內萎靡了好幾個月，連最親近的朋友都拒絕見面。"}, {"w": "apotheosis", "p": "n.", "d": "The highest point or perfect example; elevation to divine status.", "c": "典範；神化", "s": "Many music historians regard Beethoven's Ninth Symphony as the apotheosis of the classical symphony, the supreme example of the form, in which centuries of musical development reached their most glorious and powerful expression.", "t": "許多音樂史學家把貝多芬的《第九號交響曲》視為古典交響曲的巔峰典範，是此一曲式的最高代表，數百年的音樂發展在其中達到最輝煌、最有力的表現。", "as": "The emperor's apotheosis after his death transformed a ruthless, despotic ruler into a god whom the Roman people were expected to venerate in lavish temples throughout the empire.", "at": "這位皇帝死後被神化，使一位冷酷專制的統治者搖身變成神祇，羅馬人民被要求在帝國各地富麗堂皇的神殿中崇敬他。"}, {"w": "chiaroscuro", "p": "n.", "d": "The dramatic use of contrasting light and shadow in art.", "c": "明暗對比法；明暗配置", "s": "Caravaggio was a master of chiaroscuro, placing brightly lit figures against deep black backgrounds so that the strong contrast between light and shadow made his religious scenes look startlingly three-dimensional and dramatic.", "t": "卡拉瓦喬是明暗對比法的大師，他把明亮的人物置於深黑的背景前，強烈的光影對比使他的宗教場景顯得驚人地立體而富戲劇性。", "as": "Rembrandt's chiaroscuro imbues his portraits with a pensive, almost mystical quality, as luminous faces emerge from the tenebrous background like memories surfacing from the dark.", "at": "林布蘭的明暗對比法讓他的肖像畫充滿沉思、近乎神祕的氣質，一張張明亮的臉龐從幽暗的背景中浮現，宛如從黑暗中湧現的記憶。"}, {"w": "contemn", "p": "v.", "d": "To treat or regard someone or something with contempt; scorn.", "c": "蔑視；藐視", "s": "The arrogant young aristocrat seemed to contemn anyone who worked with their hands, sneering at servants, farmers, and craftsmen as though they were beneath his notice and unworthy of even the most basic respect.", "t": "這位傲慢的年輕貴族似乎蔑視所有靠雙手勞動的人，他嘲笑僕人、農夫和工匠，彷彿他們不值一顧，連最基本的尊重都不配得到。", "as": "The young reformers openly contemned the corrupt officials who profited from nepotism, and they vowed to castigate publicly anyone whose greed betrayed the public trust.", "at": "年輕的改革者公開蔑視那些靠裙帶關係牟利的腐敗官員，並誓言要公開嚴厲譴責任何因貪婪而辜負公眾信任的人。"}, {"w": "apologia", "p": "n.", "d": "A formal written defense of one's beliefs or conduct.", "c": "辯護書；（為信念或行為的）正式辯解", "s": "After years of public criticism, the former general published a lengthy apologia explaining and justifying every controversial decision he had made during the war, hoping to persuade historians that his actions had been necessary.", "t": "在多年飽受公眾批評之後，這位前將軍出版了一部長篇辯護書，解釋並辯解他在戰爭期間所做的每一項爭議決定，希望說服歷史學家相信他的行動是必要的。", "as": "John Henry Newman's famous apologia was not an abject plea for forgiveness but a lucid, eloquent effort to vindicate his religious convictions against his detractors' scurrilous attacks.", "at": "約翰．亨利．紐曼著名的辯護書並非卑屈地乞求原諒，而是一部清晰而雄辯的著作，旨在駁斥批評者的惡意中傷，證明他宗教信念的正當性。"}, {"w": "gorgonize", "p": "v.", "d": "To paralyze or hypnotize someone, as if turning them to stone.", "c": "使呆若木雞；使石化", "s": "The strict headmistress could gorgonize an entire auditorium of noisy teenagers with a single icy stare, freezing them in their seats so completely that no one dared to whisper, move, or even breathe loudly.", "t": "這位嚴厲的女校長只要冷冷一瞪，就能讓整個禮堂吵鬧的青少年呆若木雞，把他們定在座位上，沒人敢竊竊私語、動一下，甚至大聲呼吸。", "as": "The prosecutor's minatory glare seemed to gorgonize the witness, who sat petrified in the stand, unable to equivocate any longer about where he had been that night.", "at": "檢察官帶有威脅意味的怒視彷彿讓證人石化了；他僵坐在證人席上，再也無法對那晚自己身在何處含糊其辭。"}, {"w": "scholia", "p": "n.", "d": "Explanatory notes written in the margins of ancient texts.", "c": "（古籍的）旁註；評註", "s": "Modern classicists depend heavily on the scholia that medieval scribes wrote in the margins of Homer's manuscripts, since these explanatory notes preserve valuable information from ancient commentaries that have otherwise been lost.", "t": "現代古典學者十分倚重中世紀抄寫員寫在荷馬手稿頁邊的旁註，因為這些解說性的註解保存了原本已失傳的古代注釋中的寶貴資訊。", "as": "The erudite scholia in the margins of the manuscript elucidate many abstruse passages, yet a few annotations are so cryptic that scholars still debate their meaning.", "at": "手稿頁邊那些博學的旁註闡明了許多深奧難懂的段落，但仍有少數註解極為隱晦，學者至今仍在爭論其含義。"}, {"w": "cathect", "p": "v.", "d": "To invest emotional energy in a person, object, or idea.", "c": "傾注情感；投注心力", "s": "Psychologists observe that lonely children often cathect their favorite stuffed animals, pouring so much emotional energy into these toys that losing one can feel as painful as losing a real friend.", "t": "心理學家觀察到，孤單的孩子常會把情感傾注在最喜愛的絨毛玩偶上，對這些玩具投入大量情感，以致失去其中一個可能就像失去真正的朋友一樣痛苦。", "as": "Some fans cathect so intensely on a celebrity that their adulation becomes almost obsessive, and they may feel genuinely aggrieved when their idol disappoints them.", "at": "有些粉絲在名人身上投注極其強烈的情感，使他們的崇拜幾近痴迷；當偶像令他們失望時，他們可能會真心感到受傷委屈。"}, {"w": "sortilege", "p": "n.", "d": "Fortune-telling by drawing lots; sorcery or magic.", "c": "抽籤占卜；巫術", "s": "In ancient times, priests sometimes practiced sortilege to make important decisions, drawing marked stones or sticks at random from a container and interpreting the results as messages revealing the will of the gods.", "t": "在古代，祭司有時會以抽籤占卜來做出重要決定，從容器中隨機抽出做了記號的石頭或木籤，並將結果解讀為揭示神明旨意的訊息。", "as": "Temple visitors who seek guidance through sortilege are rarely gullible; most regard drawing lots as a comforting ritual rather than an infallible augury of the future.", "at": "透過抽籤占卜尋求指引的廟宇信眾很少是輕信之人；多數人把抽籤視為一種安心的儀式，而非對未來萬無一失的預兆。"}, {"w": "terpsichorean", "p": "adj.", "d": "Relating to dancing or the art of dance.", "c": "舞蹈的；與舞蹈有關的", "s": "The ballet company's newest production showcased remarkable terpsichorean skill, as dancers leaped, spun, and glided across the stage with such grace that the audience gave them a standing ovation after every scene.", "t": "這個芭蕾舞團最新的作品展現了非凡的舞蹈技巧，舞者們在台上跳躍、旋轉、滑行，姿態優美得讓觀眾在每一幕結束後都起立鼓掌。", "as": "Fred Astaire's terpsichorean genius always seemed completely effortless; his lissome movements and impeccable timing made even the most arduous routines look as natural as walking.", "at": "佛雷．亞斯坦的舞蹈天才總是看似完全毫不費力；他輕盈柔軟的動作和無懈可擊的節奏感，讓即使最艱難的舞步看起來都像走路一樣自然。"}, {"w": "esprit de l'escalier", "p": "n.", "d": "Thinking of the perfect reply too late to use it.", "c": "事後才想到的妙語；馬後炮式的機智", "s": "Hours after the debate ended, the student suddenly thought of the perfect response to her opponent's argument, a frustrating case of esprit de l'escalier that left her wishing she could return to the podium and deliver it.", "t": "辯論結束數小時後，這名學生突然想到如何完美回應對手的論點，這種事後才想到妙語的情況令人懊惱，讓她恨不得能回到講台上說出來。", "as": "Plagued by esprit de l'escalier, the diffident clerk spent the evening composing a devastating riposte to his boss's insult, a retort he would never have the temerity to deliver.", "at": "這位缺乏自信的職員飽受事後才想到妙語之苦，整晚都在構思一句能狠狠回擊老闆侮辱的話，但他永遠不會有膽量真的說出口。"}, {"w": "popinjay", "p": "n.", "d": "A vain, overdressed person who talks too much.", "c": "自負又愛打扮的人；花花公子", "s": "The other officers mocked the young lieutenant as a popinjay, a vain, chattering show-off who spent more time admiring his polished boots and gold buttons than learning how to lead soldiers in battle.", "t": "其他軍官嘲笑這位年輕中尉是個愛打扮又自負的花花公子，一個虛榮又多嘴的愛現者，花在欣賞自己擦亮的靴子和金鈕扣上的時間，比學習如何帶兵作戰還多。", "as": "The vainglorious popinjay strutted through the gala in a garish velvet suit, boasting about his wealth to anyone who would listen and oblivious to the derision of the other guests.", "at": "那個自負虛榮的花花公子穿著一身俗豔的天鵝絨西裝在晚會上大搖大擺，向任何願意聽的人炫耀他的財富，對其他賓客的嘲笑渾然不覺。"}]}, {"unit": 49, "level": 10, "cards": [{"w": "catachresis", "p": "n.", "d": "The incorrect use of a word, or a strained figure of speech.", "c": "詞語誤用；牽強的比喻", "s": "The editor circled the phrase \"a mute point\" in red ink, explaining in the margin that writing \"mute\" for \"moot\" is a classic catachresis that careful readers will notice immediately and that may undermine the author's credibility.", "t": "編輯用紅筆圈出「a mute point」這個片語，並在頁邊說明，把「moot」寫成「mute」是典型的詞語誤用，細心的讀者會立刻察覺，而且可能損害作者的可信度。", "as": "The professor, notoriously pedantic, devoted an entire lecture to a single catachresis in the student's essay, though classmates felt his censure was far harsher than such a minor slip warranted.", "at": "這位以賣弄學問出名的教授，竟為了學生論文中的一處詞語誤用而花了一整堂課講解，但同學們覺得他的責難遠比這種小失誤應得的嚴厲得多。"}, {"w": "etiology", "p": "n.", "d": "The cause or origin of a disease or condition.", "c": "病因；病源學", "s": "Although doctors can now treat the symptoms of the illness quite effectively, its etiology remains a mystery, and researchers are still debating whether genetic factors, environmental toxins, or a combination of both actually trigger the disease.", "t": "雖然醫生現在已能相當有效地治療這種疾病的症狀，但其病因仍然是個謎，研究人員仍在爭論究竟是遺傳因素、環境毒素，還是兩者共同引發了這種疾病。", "as": "Early theories about the etiology of the plague were largely conjecture, and many physicians, hidebound by ancient teachings, refused to consider that fleas carried by rats might be the culprit.", "at": "早期關於鼠疫病因的理論大多是臆測，許多醫生受古代學說束縛、思想守舊，拒絕考慮老鼠身上的跳蚤可能才是元兇。"}, {"w": "demimonde", "p": "n.", "d": "A marginal social group of doubtful respectability or legality.", "c": "社會邊緣階層；聲名可疑的圈子", "s": "In his novels about nineteenth-century Paris, Balzac moved easily between elegant aristocratic salons and the demimonde of gamblers, swindlers, and struggling actors, a shadowy world that respectable society officially ignored but secretly found fascinating.", "t": "在描寫十九世紀巴黎的小說中，巴爾札克在優雅的貴族沙龍與由賭徒、騙子和潦倒演員組成的邊緣社會之間自如穿梭，那是一個體面社會表面上忽視、私下卻深感著迷的灰暗世界。", "as": "The journalist spent months in the city's demimonde of unlicensed boxing clubs and clandestine card games, and her exposé revealed a nefarious network that the police had long ignored.", "at": "這位記者花了數個月深入該城市由無照拳擊俱樂部和秘密牌局構成的地下社會，她的揭發報導揭露了一個警方長期忽視的邪惡網絡。"}, {"w": "numinous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having a mysterious, spiritual quality suggesting a divine presence.", "c": "神聖的；超自然而令人敬畏的", "s": "Visitors who enter the ancient cathedral at dawn often describe a numinous atmosphere, as shafts of colored light fall silently across the stone floor and even lifelong skeptics feel they are standing in the presence of something sacred.", "t": "黎明時分走進這座古老大教堂的訪客，常形容那裡有一種神聖莊嚴的氛圍：一道道彩色光束靜靜灑落在石砌地板上，連一輩子抱持懷疑態度的人都覺得自己正身處某種神聖事物的面前。", "as": "The ineffable silence of the redwood forest struck the hikers as almost numinous, and even the most garrulous member of the group fell quiet, lost in pensive reflection.", "at": "紅杉林中難以言喻的寂靜讓健行者覺得近乎神聖，連團體中最多話的成員也安靜下來，陷入沉思。"}, {"w": "lexiphanic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Using pretentious, showy words to appear learned.", "c": "賣弄詞藻的；咬文嚼字的", "s": "The judges praised the student's research but criticized her lexiphanic writing style, noting that phrases like \"the utilization of multifarious methodologies\" only obscured her ideas, and they urged her to choose plain words whenever possible.", "t": "評審讚賞這名學生的研究，但批評她賣弄詞藻的寫作風格，指出像「the utilization of multifarious methodologies」這類措辭只會模糊她的想法，並敦促她盡可能選用淺白的字詞。", "as": "The politician's lexiphanic speeches, full of bombastic phrases and needless circumlocution, impressed few voters, who wanted plain, simple answers rather than an exhibition of his vocabulary.", "at": "這位政治人物賣弄詞藻的演說充滿浮誇的措辭和不必要的拐彎抹角，幾乎打動不了選民，他們要的是直白簡單的答案，而不是他的詞彙展示。"}, {"w": "brachiate", "p": "v.", "d": "To swing from branch to branch using the arms.", "c": "（以手臂）擺盪攀援；臂行", "s": "Gibbons are the acrobats of the rain forest: rather than walking along branches, they brachiate through the canopy with astonishing speed, swinging hand over hand and sometimes covering ten meters in a single graceful leap.", "t": "長臂猿是雨林中的特技演員：牠們不是沿著樹枝行走，而是以驚人的速度在樹冠層間擺盪前進，雙手交替抓握，有時一次優雅的躍動就能跨越十公尺。", "as": "Watching the young orangutans brachiate with such alacrity, the primatologist marveled at how their long arms, honed over millions of years of evolution, made such a prodigious feat look effortless.", "at": "看著幼年紅毛猩猩如此敏捷地擺盪攀援，這位靈長類學家驚嘆於牠們歷經數百萬年演化磨練而成的長臂，竟讓如此驚人的壯舉看起來毫不費力。"}, {"w": "quidnunc", "p": "n.", "d": "A nosy person eager to know the latest gossip.", "c": "好管閒事的人；愛打聽八卦的人", "s": "Every small town seems to have at least one quidnunc who sits by the front window all day, noting who visits whom and then eagerly spreading the latest rumors to anyone willing to stop and listen.", "t": "每個小鎮似乎都至少有一個好管閒事的人，整天坐在前窗旁，記下誰去拜訪了誰，然後迫不及待地把最新傳聞散播給任何願意停下來聽的人。", "as": "The office quidnunc, ever officious and garrulous, somehow learned about the CEO's resignation before the board did, and by noon the rumor had become ubiquitous throughout the building.", "at": "辦公室裡那個愛打聽八卦的人，一向愛多管閒事又喋喋不休，竟比董事會還早得知執行長辭職的消息，到了中午，這個傳聞已傳遍整棟大樓。"}, {"w": "catechumen", "p": "n.", "d": "A person receiving basic instruction, especially in Christian doctrine.", "c": "慕道者；（任何領域的）初學者", "s": "In the early church, a catechumen often studied for as long as three years before baptism, attending lessons on prayer, scripture, and moral conduct but leaving the service before the most sacred rituals began.", "t": "在早期教會中，慕道者往往要在受洗前學習長達三年，參加有關禱告、經文與道德行為的課程，但在最神聖的儀式開始之前就必須離開禮拜。", "as": "As a mere catechumen in the world of jazz, the young pianist was reluctant to opine on improvisation, preferring to sit quietly and learn from the cognoscenti who gathered at the club.", "at": "身為爵士樂界的初學者，這位年輕鋼琴家不願對即興演奏發表意見，寧可安靜地坐著，向聚集在俱樂部裡的行家學習。"}, {"w": "sybarite", "p": "n.", "d": "A person devoted to luxury and pleasure.", "c": "酷愛奢華享樂的人；縱情逸樂者", "s": "The emperor was a true sybarite who spent his days lounging on silk cushions, sampling rare delicacies imported from distant provinces, and listening to musicians, while the affairs of the empire were left almost entirely to his ministers.", "t": "這位皇帝是個十足貪圖享樂的人，終日倚臥在絲綢軟墊上，品嚐從遙遠省分進貢的珍饈美饌，聆聽樂師演奏，而帝國的政務幾乎全交給了大臣處理。", "as": "Though critics derided him as a sybarite who squandered his fortune on opulent banquets, the merchant was also remarkably philanthropic, funding hospitals and schools throughout the city.", "at": "雖然批評者嘲笑他是個把財富揮霍在奢華宴席上的享樂主義者，但這位商人也非常樂善好施，資助了全市各地的醫院和學校。"}, {"w": "quisling", "p": "n.", "d": "A traitor who collaborates with an occupying enemy.", "c": "賣國賊；通敵的叛徒", "s": "After the war ended, the citizens demanded that the mayor be put on trial, calling him a quisling who had helped the invading army round up resistance fighters in exchange for power and protection during the occupation.", "t": "戰爭結束後，市民要求將市長送上法庭審判，稱他是個賣國賊，在占領期間為了換取權力與保護而協助入侵軍隊圍捕反抗軍。", "as": "History has been unequivocal in its judgment of the quisling governor, whose perfidious alliance with the invaders made his name a lasting stigma for his descendants.", "at": "歷史對這位通敵總督的評斷毫不含糊，他與侵略者背信棄義的結盟，使他的名字成為子孫永遠的汙名。"}, {"w": "catholicon", "p": "n.", "d": "A universal remedy believed to cure all ills.", "c": "萬靈藥；萬應靈丹", "s": "Medieval apothecaries sold a sticky herbal syrup advertised as a catholicon capable of curing everything from fevers and coughs to melancholy and gout, although modern chemists have found that it contained little more than honey and wine.", "t": "中世紀的藥劑師販售一種黏稠的草藥糖漿，宣稱它是能治癒從發燒、咳嗽到憂鬱和痛風等各種病症的萬靈藥，但現代化學家發現它所含的不過是蜂蜜和葡萄酒而已。", "as": "The economist warned that tax cuts were no catholicon for the nation's ills, dismissing the minister's promises as specious sophistry designed merely to placate anxious voters.", "at": "這位經濟學家警告，減稅並非解決國家弊病的萬靈藥，並駁斥部長的承諾只是似是而非的詭辯，目的不過是安撫焦慮的選民。"}, {"w": "discalced", "p": "adj.", "d": "Barefoot or wearing only sandals, as certain religious orders.", "c": "赤足的；（修士）只穿涼鞋的", "s": "The discalced friars walked the rocky mountain paths in nothing but simple leather sandals, even in winter, because their religious order required them to give up shoes as a sign of humility and poverty.", "t": "這些赤足修會的修士即使在冬天，也只穿著簡單的皮涼鞋走在崎嶇的山路上，因為他們的修會要求他們捨棄鞋子，以表謙卑與清貧。", "as": "The discalced nuns led an austere life of privation, and their abstemious diet of bread and vegetables astonished visitors accustomed to the comforts of the city.", "at": "這些赤足修女過著刻苦清貧的生活，她們只吃麵包和蔬菜的節制飲食，讓習慣城市舒適生活的訪客大為驚訝。"}, {"w": "incondite", "p": "adj.", "d": "Poorly constructed; crude and unpolished in composition.", "c": "（文章）結構拙劣的；粗糙的", "s": "The first draft of the novel was so incondite, with scenes appearing in random order and characters vanishing for no reason, that the editor spent nearly a year helping the author shape it into a coherent story.", "t": "這部小說的初稿結構極為拙劣，場景隨意排列，角色無緣無故消失，以致編輯花了將近一年協助作者把它打磨成一個連貫的故事。", "as": "Although the poet's juvenilia were admittedly incondite, scholars find in those clumsy early verses the nascent themes that would eventually flower in her seminal poetry collection.", "at": "雖然這位詩人的少作確實粗糙拙劣，但學者在那些笨拙的早期詩句中，發現了日後在她那部影響深遠的詩集中開花結果的初萌主題。"}, {"w": "afflatus", "p": "n.", "d": "A sudden creative inspiration, as if from a divine source.", "c": "靈感；神來之筆", "s": "The composer claimed that the entire symphony came to him in a single night of divine afflatus, as melodies poured into his mind so quickly that he could barely write them down before the sun rose.", "t": "這位作曲家聲稱，整部交響曲是在一夜的神聖靈感中降臨於他的，旋律如泉湧般湧入腦海，快得讓他幾乎來不及在日出前寫下來。", "as": "Waiting for afflatus, the novelist argued, was a recipe for lethargy; she preferred assiduous daily work, believing that inspiration rewards those who show up at the desk.", "at": "這位小說家主張，枯等靈感降臨只會讓人陷入怠惰；她偏好每天勤奮不懈地寫作，相信靈感會眷顧那些每天坐到書桌前的人。"}, {"w": "flaneur", "p": "n.", "d": "A person who strolls idly, observing city life.", "c": "（城市）閒逛者；漫遊觀察者", "s": "Like a true flaneur, the poet Baudelaire wandered the boulevards of Paris for hours with no destination in mind, watching shoppers, street vendors, and passing carriages and recording his impressions of modern urban life.", "t": "詩人波特萊爾就像一位真正的城市漫遊者，毫無目的地在巴黎的林蔭大道上閒逛數小時，觀察購物者、街頭小販與往來的馬車，並記錄下他對現代都市生活的印象。", "as": "A peripatetic flaneur by temperament, the photographer would simply meander through Taipei's crowded night markets for hours, capturing candid moments that more hurried visitors never noticed.", "at": "這位攝影師天生就是個四處遊走的城市漫遊者，他會在臺北擁擠的夜市裡閒逛好幾個小時，捕捉那些步履匆忙的遊客從未注意到的自然瞬間。"}, {"w": "quomodocunquize", "p": "v.", "d": "To make money by any means possible.", "c": "不擇手段地賺錢；想盡辦法撈錢", "s": "During the gold rush, many shopkeepers chose to quomodocunquize rather than mine for gold themselves, charging desperate prospectors ten times the normal price for shovels, flour, and boots and growing far richer than most of their customers.", "t": "淘金熱期間，許多店主選擇不擇手段地賺錢，而不是親自去挖金，他們向走投無路的淘金客收取十倍於平常的價格購買鏟子、麵粉和靴子，結果比大多數顧客都富有得多。", "as": "Driven by sheer cupidity, the unscrupulous landlord would quomodocunquize however he could, charging even his poorest tenants spurious fees for repairs he never actually made.", "at": "在純粹的貪婪驅使下，這個無良房東想盡一切辦法撈錢，甚至向最貧困的房客收取他根本沒做過的維修費用，巧立名目。"}, {"w": "pasquinade", "p": "n.", "d": "A satire or lampoon, especially one posted publicly.", "c": "（張貼於公共場所的）諷刺文；諷刺詩", "s": "In sixteenth-century Rome, citizens who feared punishment for criticizing the pope would secretly attach a witty pasquinade to an ancient statue at night, so that by morning crowds could gather to read the anonymous mockery.", "t": "在十六世紀的羅馬，害怕因批評教宗而受罰的市民，會在夜裡偷偷把一篇詼諧的諷刺文貼在一座古代雕像上，到了早上，人群便會聚集過來閱讀這些匿名的嘲諷。", "as": "The anonymous pasquinade nailed to the town hall door was a scathing invective against the corrupt mayor, and its mordant wit soon made it the talk of the entire province.", "at": "釘在市政廳門上的匿名諷刺文是對這位貪腐市長的猛烈抨擊，其辛辣的機智很快就讓它成為全省熱議的話題。"}, {"w": "Xanthippe", "p": "n.", "d": "A bad-tempered, scolding woman; a shrew.", "c": "潑婦；悍婦", "s": "In the comedy, the long-suffering innkeeper is married to a Xanthippe who scolds him from dawn to dusk, criticizing his cooking, his clothes, and his friends so fiercely that customers flee whenever she enters the dining room.", "t": "在這部喜劇中，飽受折磨的旅店老闆娶了一個潑婦，她從早到晚數落他，批評他的廚藝、衣著和朋友，兇得每當她走進餐廳，客人就紛紛逃離。", "as": "Literary scholars note that Xanthippe, wife of Socrates, may have been unfairly maligned, since the irascible temper ascribed to her comes largely from apocryphal anecdotes written long after her death.", "at": "文學學者指出，蘇格拉底的妻子贊西佩可能遭到不公平的詆毀，因為她那易怒的脾氣大多來自她死後很久才寫成、真偽可疑的軼事。"}, {"w": "pococurante", "p": "adj.", "d": "Indifferent or unconcerned; caring little about anything.", "c": "漠不關心的；滿不在乎的", "s": "Despite the coach's passionate speech before the championship game, the team's star player remained pococurante, scrolling through his phone and shrugging as though the outcome of the season made no difference to him at all.", "t": "儘管教練在冠軍賽前發表了慷慨激昂的演說，球隊的明星球員卻依然漠不關心，一邊滑手機一邊聳肩，彷彿這個球季的結果對他毫無影響。", "as": "The critic's pococurante attitude toward contemporary art struck many as a pose; beneath his jaded, insouciant manner, friends insisted, lay a deep and fervent love of painting.", "at": "這位評論家對當代藝術漠不關心的態度，在許多人看來只是故作姿態；朋友們堅稱，在他那厭倦而滿不在乎的外表下，其實藏著對繪畫深沉而熾熱的熱愛。"}, {"w": "homunculus", "p": "n.", "d": "A very small human; a miniature, fully formed person.", "c": "小矮人；（舊說中精子內的）微型人", "s": "Some seventeenth-century scientists believed that each sperm cell contained a tiny, fully formed homunculus that simply grew larger in the womb, a theory that seems absurd today but was taken seriously before microscopes improved.", "t": "一些十七世紀的科學家相信，每個精子細胞內都含有一個發育完整的微型小人，只是在子宮裡逐漸長大；這個理論如今看來荒謬，但在顯微鏡技術進步之前卻曾被認真看待。", "as": "In the alchemist's laboratory, the novel's protagonist attempts to create a homunculus in a glass alembic, an act of hubris that ultimately leads to his ruin.", "at": "在煉金術士的實驗室裡，小說主角試圖在玻璃蒸餾器中造出一個小矮人，這種狂妄自大之舉最終導致了他的毀滅。"}]}, {"unit": 50, "level": 10, "cards": [{"w": "morganatic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Describing a marriage where a lower-ranked spouse gains no royal title.", "c": "貴賤通婚的；（婚姻）不繼承爵位的", "s": "Because Archduke Franz Ferdinand insisted on marrying a countess considered beneath his rank, the Austrian court allowed only a morganatic marriage, which meant that his wife could never become empress and their children could never inherit the throne.", "t": "由於斐迪南大公堅持迎娶一位被認為身分低於他的伯爵夫人，奧地利宮廷只允許這是一樁貴賤通婚，這意味著他的妻子永遠無法成為皇后，他們的子女也永遠無法繼承王位。", "as": "The prince's morganatic union with a commoner caused a schism within the royal family, and the patrician elders, ever hidebound, refused to attend the modest ceremony.", "at": "王子與平民的貴賤通婚在王室內部引發分裂，那些一向墨守成規的貴族長輩拒絕出席這場簡樸的婚禮。"}, {"w": "paraleipsis", "p": "n.", "d": "Emphasizing something by claiming to pass over it.", "c": "陽否陰述法；假省筆法", "s": "When the candidate declared, \"I will not even mention my opponent's failed businesses,\" he was using paraleipsis, a clever rhetorical trick that draws attention to a topic precisely by pretending to leave it out.", "t": "當這位候選人宣稱「我甚至不會提到我對手那些失敗的生意」時，他正是在使用陽否陰述法，這種巧妙的修辭技巧正是藉由假裝略過某個話題來引起人們對它的注意。", "as": "The senator's paraleipsis was transparent and disingenuous: by saying he would never stoop to discuss his rival's alleged peccadilloes, he made sure every reporter wrote about them.", "at": "這位參議員的陽否陰述手法既明顯又虛偽：他說自己絕不會自貶身價去談論對手被指控的小過失，卻確保了每位記者都會報導這些事。"}, {"w": "mumpsimus", "p": "n.", "d": "A stubbornly held error or outdated custom, even after correction.", "c": "明知錯誤仍固守的習慣；冥頑不靈", "s": "Even after the new study proved that cracking knuckles does not cause arthritis, my grandfather clung to his old mumpsimus, insisting that the scientists were wrong and continuing to scold anyone who cracked their fingers at the table.", "t": "即使新研究已證明扳指關節不會導致關節炎，我祖父仍固守他那錯誤的舊觀念，堅稱科學家錯了，並繼續責罵任何在餐桌上扳手指的人。", "as": "The editor's insistence on an obsolete spelling was pure mumpsimus; though dictionaries had long ago changed the entry, he remained intransigent and obstinate, rejecting every correction.", "at": "這位編輯堅持使用過時的拼法，純粹是冥頑不靈；儘管字典早已修改了該詞條，他仍不肯讓步、固執己見，拒絕所有的更正。"}, {"w": "bibliophagic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Devouring books; reading eagerly and constantly.", "c": "嗜書如命的；啃書的", "s": "As a bibliophagic child, Marie Curie read every volume in her father's library, from physics textbooks to poetry collections, and her sisters joked that she consumed books faster than the family could buy them.", "t": "身為一個嗜書如命的孩子，瑪麗·居禮讀遍了她父親書房裡的每一本書，從物理教科書到詩集都不放過，她的姊妹們還開玩笑說，她讀書的速度比家人買書的速度還快。", "as": "Her bibliophagic appetite was truly insatiable; a polymath by habit, she read history, chemistry, and philosophy in a single week and still begged the librarian for more.", "at": "她嗜書如命的胃口真是永不滿足；她習慣廣泛涉獵，一週內就讀完歷史、化學和哲學書籍，卻仍央求圖書館員再給她更多書。"}, {"w": "corybantic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Wild, frenzied, and unrestrained, as in a frantic dance.", "c": "狂熱的；狂亂奔放的", "s": "When the final whistle confirmed their first championship in forty years, the fans erupted into corybantic celebrations, leaping over seats, beating drums, and dancing wildly in the stadium until security finally cleared the stands after midnight.", "t": "當終場哨聲確認他們四十年來首座冠軍時，球迷們爆發出狂熱的慶祝，跳過座椅、敲打鼓、在體育場內瘋狂舞動，直到午夜過後保全人員才終於清空看台。", "as": "The festival's corybantic revelry struck some observers as bacchanalian, yet anthropologists argued that these vociferous, all-night dances served a solemn ritual purpose for the entire community.", "at": "這個節慶狂熱的狂歡在一些觀察者看來簡直是縱酒狂歡，但人類學家主張，這些喧鬧、通宵達旦的舞蹈對整個社群具有莊嚴的儀式意義。"}, {"w": "aubade", "p": "n.", "d": "A song or poem greeting or lamenting the dawn.", "c": "晨歌；破曉詩", "s": "In Romeo and Juliet, the famous scene in which the young couple argue over whether they hear a lark or a nightingale is a classic aubade, a poem in which lovers lament the arrival of morning.", "t": "在《羅密歐與茱麗葉》中，那對年輕戀人爭論他們聽到的是雲雀還是夜鶯的著名場景，就是一首典型的晨歌，也就是戀人哀嘆早晨來臨的詩歌。", "as": "Philip Larkin's bleak aubade, written in a mood of elegiac melancholy, reflects on mortality in the gray matutinal hours, when the poet lies awake contemplating death.", "at": "菲利普·拉金那首淒涼的晨歌，以哀傷憂鬱的心境寫成，描寫詩人在灰濛濛的清晨時分醒著躺在床上思索死亡，反思人終將一死。"}, {"w": "lycanthropy", "p": "n.", "d": "The supposed transformation of a human into a wolf.", "c": "變狼術；變狼妄想症", "s": "Medieval European folklore is filled with tales of lycanthropy, in which ordinary villagers were believed to transform into wolves under the full moon, and some historians link these legends to fears about wild animals and disease.", "t": "中世紀歐洲民間傳說中充滿了人變狼的故事，人們相信普通村民會在滿月時化身為狼，一些歷史學家將這些傳說與人們對野獸和疾病的恐懼聯繫在一起。", "as": "Psychiatrists describe clinical lycanthropy as a rare and anomalous delusion, and they caution that the lurid legends of folklore should not be conflated with this genuine and serious condition.", "at": "精神科醫師將臨床變狼妄想症描述為一種罕見而反常的妄想，並提醒民間傳說中聳人聽聞的故事不應與這種真實而嚴重的病症混為一談。"}, {"w": "nullipara", "p": "n.", "d": "A woman who has never given birth.", "c": "未產婦；未曾生育的女性", "s": "The medical textbook explains that the first stage of labor usually lasts longer for a nullipara than for a woman who has already delivered a child, so doctors adjust their expectations according to each patient's history.", "t": "這本醫學教科書解釋，未產婦的第一產程通常比已生育過的女性來得長，因此醫生會根據每位病患的病史調整預期。", "as": "The epidemiologists' seminal study found that a nullipara faced a slightly different health profile than other women, a finding that was later corroborated by several larger trials.", "at": "流行病學家那項影響深遠的研究發現，未產婦的健康狀況與其他女性略有不同，這項發現後來獲得數項規模更大的試驗證實。"}, {"w": "weltschmerz", "p": "n.", "d": "Sadness about the world's unavoidable suffering; world-weariness.", "c": "厭世感；悲世情懷", "s": "After reading news about wars, floods, and famines every morning for a month, the young journalist sank into a deep weltschmerz, feeling that no matter how hard anyone tried, the world would always remain full of pain.", "t": "連續一個月每天早上閱讀有關戰爭、洪水和饑荒的新聞後，這位年輕記者陷入了深深的厭世感，覺得無論任何人如何努力，這個世界永遠都會充滿痛苦。", "as": "The Romantic poets' weltschmerz often bordered on the maudlin, yet their melancholy reflections on human misery and loss remain surprisingly poignant to many readers more than two centuries later.", "at": "浪漫主義詩人的厭世情懷常近乎多愁善感，但他們對人類苦難的憂鬱沉思，兩個多世紀後仍令許多讀者深受感動。"}, {"w": "noetic", "p": "adj.", "d": "Relating to the mind or intellect.", "c": "智力的；理性認知的", "s": "The philosophy course focused on the noetic side of human experience, asking students to analyze how we form concepts, judge truth, and gain knowledge rather than how our emotions or physical senses shape our daily lives.", "t": "這門哲學課著重於人類經驗中的理智層面，要求學生分析我們如何形成概念、判斷真理以及獲得知識，而非我們的情感或身體感官如何影響日常生活。", "as": "The professor's lectures were noetic feasts for the erudite, but younger and less experienced students found his abstruse arguments about consciousness and perception nearly impossible to follow.", "at": "這位教授的講課對學識淵博的人而言是理智的饗宴，但較年輕、經驗較少的學生覺得他關於意識與知覺的深奧論點幾乎無法理解。"}, {"w": "quiddity", "p": "n.", "d": "The essential nature that makes something what it is.", "c": "本質；（事物的）實質", "s": "In her award-winning essay, the art critic tried to capture the quiddity of traditional Taiwanese puppet theater, the special combination of music, craft, and storytelling that makes it unlike any other form of performance in the world.", "t": "在她那篇得獎的文章中，這位藝評家試圖捕捉臺灣傳統布袋戲的本質，也就是那種結合音樂、工藝與說故事的獨特組合，使它不同於世界上任何其他表演形式。", "as": "Medieval scholastics debated the quiddity of ordinary objects such as stones and chairs with tireless, pedantic zeal, and their abstruse disputations still fascinate many philosophers today.", "at": "中世紀經院哲學家以孜孜不倦、咬文嚼字的熱忱辯論石頭、椅子等日常物品的本質，而他們深奧的論辯至今仍令許多哲學家著迷。"}, {"w": "resistentialism", "p": "n.", "d": "The humorous belief that inanimate objects actively work against humans.", "c": "物體反抗論（戲稱物品故意與人作對）", "s": "When the printer jammed, the stapler broke, and the laptop crashed just minutes before her presentation, Ms. Huang joked that resistentialism was clearly real, since every machine in the office seemed determined to defeat her.", "t": "就在她簡報前幾分鐘，印表機卡紙、釘書機壞掉、筆電當機，黃老師開玩笑說，物體反抗論顯然是真的，因為辦公室裡的每台機器似乎都決心要打敗她。", "as": "The engineer's droll lecture on resistentialism, complete with examples of umbrellas that vanish only on rainy days, provided welcome levity during an otherwise monotonous conference.", "at": "這位工程師關於物體反抗論的詼諧演講，舉出了雨傘只在下雨天才會不見等例子，為原本單調乏味的研討會帶來了令人歡迎的輕鬆氣氛。"}, {"w": "nullibiquitous", "p": "adj.", "d": "Existing nowhere; not to be found anywhere.", "c": "無處存在的；遍尋不著的", "s": "Although the brochure promised friendly staff, quiet rooms, and free breakfast, guests soon discovered that all three were nullibiquitous; the hotel was noisy, the clerks were rude, and no meal was ever served.", "t": "雖然簡介承諾有親切的員工、安靜的房間和免費早餐，但房客很快就發現這三樣東西根本不存在；飯店吵雜、櫃台人員無禮，而且從未供應過任何餐點。", "as": "The miracle cure that the charlatan had sold to the gullible villagers proved nullibiquitous, and once they realized it, their eager hopes quickly gave way to bitter recrimination.", "at": "那名江湖郎中賣給輕信村民的神奇療法根本不存在，村民們一明白這點，熱切的希望很快就轉為激烈的相互指責。"}, {"w": "flocculent", "p": "adj.", "d": "Fluffy and woolly, like loose tufts of wool.", "c": "羊毛狀的；絮狀的；毛茸茸的", "s": "In the chemistry lab, students watched closely as a soft, flocculent precipitate began to form in the beaker, its white clumps drifting slowly through the liquid like tiny tufts of cotton before settling at the bottom.", "t": "在化學實驗室裡，學生們仔細觀察燒杯中開始形成一種柔軟的絮狀沉澱物，白色的團塊像一小簇一小簇的棉花般緩緩在液體中漂浮，最後沉澱在底部。", "as": "The flocculent clouds drifting slowly over the verdant hills gave the landscape an ethereal, dreamlike quality that the painter labored for weeks to capture on canvas.", "at": "緩緩飄過青翠山丘的團團絮雲，賦予這片風景一種空靈而夢幻的氣質，畫家花了數週苦心想把它描繪在畫布上。"}, {"w": "boustrophedon", "p": "n.", "d": "Writing alternate lines in opposite directions, right-to-left then left-to-right.", "c": "牛耕式轉行書寫法", "s": "Some of the oldest Greek inscriptions were written in boustrophedon, so readers moved from right to left along one line and then from left to right along the next, much as an ox plows a field.", "t": "一些最古老的希臘銘文是以牛耕式轉行書寫法寫成的，讀者沿著一行由右讀到左，再沿著下一行由左讀到右，就像牛犁田一樣。", "as": "The archaeologist's exegesis of the weathered stone tablet hinged on recognizing its boustrophedon, an esoteric pattern of alternating script direction that had confounded generations of earlier scholars.", "at": "這位考古學家對這塊風化石碑的詮釋，關鍵在於辨識出它的牛耕式轉行書寫法，這種書寫方向交替的冷僻模式曾讓好幾代早期學者困惑不已。"}, {"w": "clinquant", "p": "adj.", "d": "Glittering with gold or tinsel; showily bright.", "c": "金光閃閃的；俗麗耀眼的", "s": "The opera's costumes were so clinquant, covered in gold sequins, metallic thread, and sparkling fake jewels, that when the stage lights struck them the singers seemed to shimmer like moving statues of polished brass.", "t": "這齣歌劇的戲服金光閃閃，綴滿金色亮片、金屬絲線和閃亮的假珠寶，當舞台燈光照在上面時，演唱者彷彿化身為閃閃發亮、會移動的拋光黃銅雕像。", "as": "The ballroom's clinquant decorations seemed garish to the austere critic, who dismissed the gilded chandeliers and glittering tinsel garlands as tawdry displays of newly acquired wealth.", "at": "舞廳那些金光閃閃的裝飾在這位樸素的評論家眼中顯得俗豔，他把鍍金吊燈和閃亮的金箔花環斥為新近致富者俗不可耐的炫富。"}, {"w": "castellated", "p": "adj.", "d": "Having battlements or turrets like a castle.", "c": "有城垛的；城堡式的", "s": "The castellated walls of the old university library, with their notched stone tops and corner turrets, make it look more like a medieval fortress than a place where students quietly study for their final exams.", "t": "這座老大學圖書館有城垛的牆壁，頂端是鋸齒狀的石砌城齒，四角還有塔樓，使它看起來更像一座中世紀堡壘，而不是學生安靜準備期末考的地方。", "as": "The eccentric millionaire built a castellated mansion, complete with a moat and drawbridge, so ostentatious and grandiose that his neighbors derided it as a monument to vanity rather than taste.", "at": "這位古怪的富翁蓋了一棟有城垛的城堡式豪宅，還附有護城河和吊橋，極盡炫耀、浮誇之能事，以致鄰居嘲笑它是虛榮的紀念碑，而非品味的展現。"}, {"w": "ultracrepidarian", "p": "adj.", "d": "Giving opinions on matters beyond one's knowledge.", "c": "對外行事妄加評論的；越界發言的", "s": "The famous actor's ultracrepidarian comments on vaccine safety alarmed doctors, who pointed out that starring in a hospital drama does not give anyone the medical training needed to advise millions of viewers about their health.", "t": "這位知名演員對疫苗安全性妄加評論，令醫生們憂心，他們指出，主演醫療劇並不會讓任何人具備為數百萬觀眾提供健康建議所需的醫學訓練。", "as": "The ultracrepidarian pundit would pontificate on economics, astronomy, and medicine with equal confidence, though his glib pronouncements revealed only a superficial grasp of each field.", "at": "這位愛對外行事妄加評論的名嘴，能以同樣的自信對經濟學、天文學和醫學高談闊論，但他那些油嘴滑舌的論斷只暴露出他對每個領域的膚淺理解。"}, {"w": "thersitical", "p": "adj.", "d": "Loud, abusive, and scurrilous in speech.", "c": "粗聲謾罵的；出言不遜的", "s": "The town meeting turned ugly when one thersitical resident began shouting insults at the council members, calling them fools and thieves until the chairperson finally asked security to escort him out of the hall.", "t": "鎮民大會在一名出言不遜的居民開始對議員大聲辱罵、稱他們為蠢蛋和小偷後變得難堪，直到主席終於請保全人員將他護送出會場。", "as": "The columnist's thersitical rants against his political rivals, filled with scurrilous invective and personal insults, eventually alienated even his most loyal readers, who canceled their subscriptions in protest.", "at": "這位專欄作家對政敵粗聲謾罵的長篇抨擊充滿下流的惡言和人身攻擊，最終連他最忠實的讀者也離他而去，紛紛取消訂閱以示抗議。"}, {"w": "perendinate", "p": "v.", "d": "To put off until the day after tomorrow.", "c": "拖延到後天", "s": "Whenever his mother asked him to clean his room, Kevin would perendinate, promising to do it not tomorrow but the day after, and somehow that day after tomorrow never seemed to arrive.", "t": "每當母親要他整理房間時，凱文總會拖延到後天，答應不是明天而是後天再做，而不知怎麼的，那個「後天」似乎永遠不會到來。", "as": "The dilatory committee chose to perendinate its vote yet again, and the activists, exasperated by such endless temporizing, began a noisy protest outside the city hall building.", "at": "這個拖拖拉拉的委員會再次決定把投票延到後天，那些被這種無止境的拖延戰術激怒的社運人士，開始在市政廳大樓外大聲抗議。"}]}];
